:224,\"reviewDecision\":\"\",\"title\":\"build(deps-dev): bump @cloudflare/vite-plugin from 2.0.0-beta.sha-52b0dc0e9 to 2.0.0-beta.v.3 in /experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice/shared-ref-worker\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-25T13:04:28Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/224\"},{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"headRefName\":\"dependabot/npm_and_yarn/experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice/cf-1.0.0-beta.20\",\"headRefOid\":\"47d92ae4c9c111c9a8317ca2185f2f76871b75f5\",\"isDraft\":false,\"number\":223,\"reviewDecision\":\"\",\"title\":\"chore(deps-dev): bump cf from 1.0.0-beta.10 to 1.0.0-beta.20 in /experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-26T00:07:34Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/223\"},{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"headRefName\":\"dependabot/npm_and_yarn/experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice/agent-collab-worker/vite-8.3.5\",\"headRefOid\":\"1a8922ec6bbc16cbec1b0d52d862d3ec00524be2\",\"isDraft\":false,\"number\":222,\"reviewDecision\":\"\",\"title\":\"build(deps-dev): bump vite from 8.3.4 to 8.3.5 in /experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice/agent-collab-worker\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-25T13:04:25Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/222\"},{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"headRefName\":\"dependabot/npm_and_yarn/experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice/fork-worker/cloudflare/vite-plugin-2.0.0-beta.v.3\",\"headRefOid\":\"a557b458a0e86f4c36a3147f451a7ac6e6ec39db\",\"isDraft\":false,\"number\":221,\"reviewDecision\":\"\",\"title\":\"build(deps-dev): bump @cloudflare/vite-plugin from 2.0.0-beta.sha-52b0dc0e9 to 2.0.0-beta.v.3 in /experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice/fork-worker\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-25T13:04:21Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/221\"},{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"headRefName\":\"dependabot/npm_and_yarn/experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice/trusted-broker-bundle/cf-1.0.0-beta.20\",\"headRefOid\":\"bc75aca3683f7022e9ec768380c86cbb80096f03\",\"isDraft\":false,\"number\":220,\"reviewDecision\":\"\",\"title\":\"chore(deps): bump cf from 1.0.0-beta.10 to 1.0.0-beta.20 in /experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice/trusted-broker-bundle\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-26T00:07:34Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/220\"},{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"headRefName\":\"dependabot/cargo/core/memmap2-0.9.12\",\"headRefOid\":\"5879cf82c204be0f29694256719ac671fc1af81d\",\"isDraft\":false,\"number\":219,\"reviewDecision\":\"\",\"title\":\"build(deps): bump memmap2 from 0.9.11 to 0.9.12 in /core\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-25T13:04:07Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/219\"},{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"headRefName\":\"dependabot/github_actions/actions/upload-artifact-7.0.2\",\"headRefOid\":\"786adb9525b2121121c46be35f98952691144830\",\"isDraft\":false,\"number\":218,\"reviewDecision\":\"\",\"title\":\"build(deps): bump actions/upload-artifact from 4.6.2 to 7.0.2\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-25T13:04:06Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/218\"},{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"headRefName\":\"dependabot/cargo/core/tokio-1.54.1\",\"headRefOid\":\"c881cbf7c2aa771de3999c95e0f5702ec69533d3\",\"isDraft\":false,\"number\":217,\"reviewDecision\":\"\",\"title\":\"build(deps): bump tokio from 1.53.3 to 1.54.1 in /core\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-25T13:04:02Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/217\"},{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"headRefName\":\"v1/docs-post-v1-roadmap\",\"headRefOid\":\"eb834816db0d37c2df5e34005f46367516f33783\",\"isDraft\":false,\"number\":131,\"reviewDecision\":\"\",\"title\":\"docs(post-v1): add post-v1.0.0 documentation, roadmap (v1.1-v1.3), GBNF tool calling, and Composio integration\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-22T20:36:31Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/131\"},{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"headRefName\":\"dependabot/npm_and_yarn/cli/typescript-7.0.2\",\"headRefOid\":\"2d28cec8d2e96e6d15c9453a597b44a6e3f85933\",\"isDraft\":false,\"number\":129,\"reviewDecision\":\"\",\"title\":\"chore(deps-dev): bump typescript from 5.9.3 to 7.0.2 in /cli\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-26T23:25:59Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/129\"},{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"headRefName\":\"dependabot/npm_and_yarn/cli/types/node-26.6.5\",\"headRefOid\":\"7602d7bc2e5d95d495c1c67f410f7944b8a807ad\",\"isDraft\":false,\"number\":124,\"reviewDecision\":\"\",\"title\":\"build(deps-dev): bump @types/node from 22.20.4 to 26.6.5 in /cli\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-21T16:06:11Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/124\"},{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"headRefName\":\"dependabot/npm_and_yarn/cli/ora-9.4.1\",\"headRefOid\":\"b2dd7af9192a4b546646443d8ac2076d43119402\",\"isDraft\":false,\"number\":120,\"reviewDecision\":\"\",\"title\":\"build(deps): bump ora from 8.2.0 to 9.4.1 in /cli\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-21T16:08:44Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/120\"},{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"headRefName\":\"dependabot/npm_and_yarn/demo/typescript-7.0.2\",\"headRefOid\":\"21fd2f06a8f449d7aba899117842f470f30032b3\",\"isDraft\":false,\"number\":119,\"reviewDecision\":\"\",\"title\":\"build(deps): bump typescript from 5.9.3 to 7.0.2 in /demo\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-21T16:14:40Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/119\"},{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"headRefName\":\"dependabot/npm_and_yarn/cli/commander-15.0.0\",\"headRefOid\":\"7bfe7e39ac7a6d103f1be8ce6f04ddca8b678dd0\",\"isDraft\":false,\"number\":114,\"reviewDecision\":\"\",\"title\":\"build(deps): bump commander from 12.1.0 to 15.0.0 in /cli\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-30T03:46:43Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/114\"},{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"headRefName\":\"dependabot/cargo/core/serde_json-1.0.154\",\"headRefOid\":\"b11ec547a7ae9f44f51f9699d0619426a603f89e\",\"isDraft\":false,\"number\":113,\"reviewDecision\":\"\",\"title\":\"build(deps): bump serde_json from 1.0.151 to 1.0.154 in /core\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-21T16:08:12Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/113\"},{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"headRefName\":\"dependabot/github_actions/actions/setup-node-7.1.0\",\"headRefOid\":\"b3cb1d905266bc6387aa877f6755ff8761fabc59\",\"isDraft\":false,\"number\":112,\"reviewDecision\":\"\",\"title\":\"build(deps): bump actions/setup-node from 4.4.0 to 7.1.0\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-25T14:11:13Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/112\"}]\nv1.0.0-rc.11\tPre-release\tv1.0.0-rc.11\t2026-10-30T00:17:45Z\nv1.0.0-rc.10\tPre-release\tv1.0.0-rc.10\t2026-10-27T00:29:58Z\nv1.0.0-rc.9\tPre-release\tv1.0.0-rc.9\t2026-10-26T17:56:16Z\nv1.0.0-rc.8\tPre-release\tv1.0.0-rc.8\t2026-10-26T07:26:22Z\nv1.0.0-rc.7\tPre-release\tv1.0.0-rc.7\t2026-10-26T00:07:06Z\n{\"comments\":[{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABc0NUhA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"2026-10-17 qualification checkpoint: the author reports 20/20 repository-arm tasks in candidate v15, but the full T2 package is still invalid. The fixture-arm portion did not match the accepted runner contract; the first isolated Docker validation had permission/setup failures, and a later single-task run was stopped when its harness exposed private validators to the same process boundary. Those are preserved as infrastructure evidence and are not task outcomes. The author is rebuilding fixture-arm validation around the accepted Bubblewrap subprocess boundary. No corpus custody/seal or T2 qualification acceptance is claimed; T3 remains paused until T2 is valid.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-17T02:56:26Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6228759684\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABdLTjsA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Status check at `v1/integration` @ `6a16cb6` (claude-code; metadata only, no private payloads read). The 2026-10-17 v15 comment is superseded.\\n\\n**Done**\\n- T2 `heldout-v2`: 40 external-repo tasks, 10 per class × 10 per language, sealed at 03:05:52Z and merged in #16. Public manifest `eval/heldout-manifest.json` (sha256 `50895b84…`), custody report `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/HELDOUT_CUSTODY/custody-report-2026-10-18.md`, custodian 40/40 reference validation, contaminated batch `author-b9` quarantined.\\n- T3: 8 tasks sealed (`eval/heldout-t3-manifest.json`, `t3-custody-report-2026-10-18.md`).\\n- Stores are `root:root` 0700 (tasks/reference 0500), so implementer shells running as uid 1000 are denied.\\n\\n**Still open before this can close**\\n1. **License/source evidence** (an acceptance bullet): neither custody report mentions licences, and the manifest records only `repo`. The custodian needs to add a per-repo licence record.\\n2. **Format compatibility:** the sealed tasks use the legacy `hidden: {dir, into, command}` form. Running them requires the hardened-legacy evaluator in PR #33, which is still open with changes requested.\\n\\nREQ-QUAL-101 is still `open`, correctly.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T17:34:26Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6252979120\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABdLY8Aw\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"**Custodian Per-Repository & Per-Task License Attestation for Sealed `heldout-v2` & `heldout-t3` Corpora (`opencode`, 2026-10-18T17:44Z):**\\n\\n1. **T2 Sealed `heldout-v2` Corpus (`eval/heldout-manifest.json` SHA-256 `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`):**\\n   - Verified the upstream license file at each task's exact pinned 40-hex commit across all **40 tasks** (spanning **27 distinct external open-source repositories**; `0` unresolved):\\n     - **`MIT`:** 25 tasks\\n     - **`BSD-3-Clause`:** 7 tasks\\n     - **`Apache-2.0`:** 6 tasks\\n     - **`BSD-2-Clause`:** 1 task\\n     - **`MPL-2.0`:** 1 task\\n   - Every upstream repository is licensed under an OSI-approved open-source license permitting local clone, modification, and evaluation use; zero tasks redistribute upstream code in the public Nexus repository (`eval/heldout-manifest.json` records only task IDs and SHA-256 digests).\\n   - The full per-task `(id, repo, commit, spdx, license_file, license_sha256)` table is sealed inside `/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2/LICENSE-AUDIT-2026-10-18.json` (`root:root`, mode `0400`, SHA-256 `727fc93092256fb8dec23e6ca0fcd227d9b23d6e6a9f23aaa0948e2705eea200`).\\n2. **T3 Sealed `heldout-t3` Corpus (`eval/heldout-t3-manifest.json` SHA-256 `85fb9cafbe18e846bd64fb13eb4fba0f92df0792bc93d12adaa685e04c9f1383`):**\\n   - All 8 T3 tasks are first-party clean-room fixtures authored specifically for Nexus v1.0.0 qualification under the project's `MIT` license (`0` third-party code dependencies).\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T17:43:06Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6253067267\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABdNi7_Q\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Pre-RC qualification preparation request to the corpus custodian (no held-out evaluation has started): the accepted final v1-t2 configs/run record are still absent. Please export and attest only non-objective budget metadata needed to preregister matched caps: task-ID keyed effective steps/minutes and any explicit context/output/request/total-output overrides, with aggregate min/max and export SHA-256 tied to the sealed manifest and frozen resource profile 4e8d42a218a68fa2fd3fd0de4d9788b205fa41b9ab71935cc2b6cf73f5d63543. Do not disclose task objectives, source payloads, validators, reference solutions, hidden results or private credentials. Source fallback/pilot budgets are not an accepted frozen run contract. If no such caps were previously approved, state that explicitly so the run contract can be registered before any scored execution; preserve all existing thresholds/corpus. Separately, the qualification runner needs current nonsecret served weights SHA and server-build identity from authoritative gateway deployment evidence (alias engineering/deep alone is insufficient); provide that metadata through the authorized runtime/custody boundary. No new private-store access is requested for implementation sessions. Peer runtime binaries are now rootowned/hash-pinned, but no RC or qualification claim is made.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T21:24:43Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6255328253\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABdOTZNQ\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Current prequalification custody check (metadata only, no attempt to enter `/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2`): the task-store directory is `root:root 0700`, with `/home/mike` mode `0750` and `nexus-heldout-v2` mode `0700`; the implementation account cannot list the store. This establishes denied access for this account but does not by itself prove author-session independence, parent/store ACLs or effective access for the evaluator identity, re-derived private payload/validator digests, reproducible setup/reference validation, or separation at the task execution boundary.\\n\\nCustodian: please provide an updated attestation for the already sealed manifest (or say which item needs a new immutable corpus version) covering those checks, including safe metadata for effective ACL/group access as root/operator/evaluator/implementer identities, task/validator store separation, setup/reference validation reproducibility, and derivation of private digests. Do not send objectives, payloads, reference solutions, validator contents, answers or credentials. Preserve the sealed manifest and record any supersession before changing content. No T2/T3/T4 qualification has been started by this coordinator.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T22:47:21Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6256122165\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABeAFf4w\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"**Custody checkpoint (2026-10-21; candidate `v1/integration@833eec62`)**\\n\\nThe public T2 manifest metadata has the documented 40-task coverage, but independent metadata review does not establish private digest derivation, author-session independence/exposure history, setup/reference validation, effective store access controls, or custodian acceptance. No held-out payload or validator was accessed, and no qualification run has started.\\n\\nThe latest authoring progress recorded here (4/20 repository-arm tasks validated) is historical. Please update only the safe status metadata: whether the replacement author completed and froze the required 40-task T2 set and 8-task T3 set; whether any content changed after the public manifest was sealed; and whether the custodian has independently verified private digests, exposure history, reproducible setup/reference validation, access separation, immutable manifest identity, and custody acceptance. If the corpus changed, record a new immutable version and supersession before qualification.\\n\\nPlease do not post task IDs, objectives, repository URLs, payloads, patches, hidden answers, validators, or credentials. Qualification remains closed until custody acceptance and the evaluator-boundary gates are established.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-21T04:50:24Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6308323299\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABeFr82g\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only qualification follow-up (current code audit at `origin/v1/integration@cc5eba2f428c7cdde33550d456506f31e3824f2e`; no private store or payload accessed): the public T2 manifest is still the sealed 40-task identity (`50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`). The current evaluator validator accepts the blackbox-v1 oracle contract, while the prior custody report describes T2 as using the legacy `hidden.command` form; the existing `eval/README.md` says compatibility requires custodian-led conversion/replacement and a new immutable manifest identity with custody checks repeated. Thus T2 qualification cannot start against the current manifest.\\n\\nCustodian: please reply with status metadata only: (1) whether the sealed T2 payload remains unchanged; (2) whether the author/custodian will produce a compatible immutable successor and repeat validation/custody checks, or whether an already-approved compatibility path exists; (3) expected completion/owner; and (4) whether T3 custody/identity remains unchanged. Do not post task IDs, objectives, source repositories, payloads, patches, reference solutions, validator contents, answers, or credentials. Keep the sealed corpus immutable until any successor is recorded with explicit supersession. Public metadata approval remains separate from private custody acceptance.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-21T10:53:55Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6314196186\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABeHMGgA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only follow-up (no private store, payload, validator, or answer accessed): we have no custodian update since the 10:53Z request. Please post only safe status metadata for the sealed T2/T3 identities: whether the replacement author completed the required set, whether any sealed content changed, whether independent digest/setup/reference checks and effective access separation are complete, and whether T2 will use an approved compatible immutable successor. If work is still underway, please include the responsible role and a reasonable ETA. Do not post task IDs, objectives, repository URLs, payloads, patches, validators, answers, or credentials. Qualification remains closed until the custodian records acceptance and the evaluator compatibility path is resolved.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-21T12:21:32Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6315771520\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABeKkA9g\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Follow-up for the v1.0.0 release coordinator: the custody and compatibility gates remain on the release critical path, and there has been no custodian update since the 12:21 UTC request. Please acknowledge whether the independent custodian/replacement author is actively working, identify the responsible role, and provide a current ETA or state that the lane is unavailable. Status only: do not include task identifiers, repository URLs, objectives, payloads, patches, validator details, answers, or credentials. Qualification remains closed pending independent custody acceptance and a compatible immutable T2 identity.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-21T15:06:44Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6319309046\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABeaOYKA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Release checkpoint, 2026-10-22 07:56 UTC (public metadata only; no held-out files accessed): exact current `main` remains `8935918455a7fcc9434762712528c1169ec4ff63`. PR #140 now records a 10/10 synthetic host preflight and has exact-head CI running, including the resource containment fixtures; no held-out task has been run. The public T2 identity remains the 40-task manifest previously reported, but custody acceptance and compatibility with the current black-box runner are still unverified here.\\n\\nCustodian/replacement author: please provide a safe status update only: (1) current assigned owner and whether authoring/validation is active; (2) whether any sealed content changed, and if so the new immutable identity/supersession; (3) whether independent private digest, exposure-history, setup/reference, effective-access, and task/evaluator separation checks are complete; (4) whether an approved runner-compatible immutable T2 successor is underway and its ETA; (5) T3 custody status. Do not include task IDs, objectives, repositories, payloads, patches, validators, answers, or credentials. Qualification remains gated until the custodian records acceptance. Contest freeze is not applicable; the contest is over.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-22T07:56:01Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6335731752\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABeh6rXw\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only custodian coordination update, current source `main@19d6f0a80e21f9b640a46ee12200c4f5f6d967a4`. PR #145 has integrated the version-synchronized RC2 source candidate; exact post-merge source CI is still running. No held-out payload, private validator, answer, or author log was accessed.\\n\\nPlease reply with safe status metadata only:\\n1. Who currently owns replacement authorship and independent custody, and are they actively working?\\n2. Are all 40 tasks fully authored, setup/reference-validated, and independently digested under the sealed manifest, or did task content change?\\n3. Has the evaluator compatibility issue with the required isolated `blackbox-v1` format been resolved by a custodian-approved immutable version or compatibility path?\\n4. Has the custodian verified effective store/parent access restrictions and separation from task execution, then accepted custody for qualification?\\n\\nDo not include payloads, solutions, private validator content, or credentials in this public issue. If there is no active custodian, please identify the concrete handoff needed so this qualification lane can proceed.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-22T14:54:39Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6343797599\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABejrYNA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only follow-up: the latest T2/T3 custody attestations are from October 18, no current custodian claim or acknowledged handoff is visible, and the current qualification runner rejects T2's legacy `hidden.command` format. No held-out qualification has started.\\n\\nPlease have the current independent custodian confirm, without exposing private material:\\n\\n- who currently owns authoring and custody, and the claim/handoff reference;\\n- whether the public T2/T3 manifests remain the intended sealed identities or need a versioned successor;\\n- the approved path to resolve T2 runner compatibility, including whether a custodian-led conversion/replacement is in progress and its next checkpoint;\\n- whether fresh setup, reference-validation, access-boundary, and integrity checks can be attested against the accepted execution boundary.\\n\\nPlease do not post task payloads, hidden answers, validators, reference solutions, author logs, credentials, or private digests here. If no custodian is active, please say so at metadata level so an independent replacement can be assigned through the claims protocol.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-22T16:19:34Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6345644084\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABeqG1lA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only compatibility follow-up (no private store, task payload, validator, answer, or author log accessed).\\n\\nThe current public evaluator contract does not define a generic, semantics-preserving adapter from legacy `hidden.command`/`hidden.dir` tasks to `blackbox-v1`. Its documented migration path requires custodian-led conversion or replacement, independent revalidation, repeat custody checks, and a new immutable manifest identity.\\n\\nPlease answer only as safe status metadata:\\n\\n1. Can the sealed task validators be represented losslessly by `blackbox-v1` without changing covered behavior?\\n2. If yes, is the independent custodian authoring and revalidating a new immutable manifest, and what is the status/ETA?\\n3. If no, should the release record mark this corpus incompatible and awaiting custodian-authored replacement?\\n\\nNo task identifiers, objectives, source URLs, payloads, patches, validator details, answers, or credentials are needed. Qualification remains closed until custodian acceptance and compatibility evidence are recorded.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-22T22:08:34Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6352385428\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABeuZ18g\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only custody follow-up, current source `main@1a484c38518688005e9434b18c889c77b408e145` (no private corpus material accessed).\\n\\nThe prior compatibility request from 2026-10-22 has no response visible. T2 qualification remains stopped because the current evaluator requires `blackbox-v1` and does not accept the sealed legacy `hidden.command` format. Please provide a safe status update covering:\\n\\n- Whether the designated independent author/custodian is actively progressing the corpus and who currently owns the custody lane.\\n- Whether a custodian-verified, semantics-preserving conversion is possible, or whether a new immutable corpus version is required; include an ETA for the next public metadata checkpoint.\\n- Whether the custodian can provide a separate acceptance attestation for completeness/coverage, setup and reference validation, payload/validator digest derivation, access controls and author-session independence, without disclosing payloads or answers to implementers.\\n- If the current owner is unavailable, whether an explicit safe-boundary handoff to another authorized custodian can be arranged.\\n\\nNo qualification run will use the corpus until the custodian accepts its custody and integrity. Please keep private task content, validators, ans\n... command output truncated for persistence ...\nategory coverage, setup, and reference validation are complete and accepted.\\n3. Whether private payload/validator integrity and provenance, author-session independence/exposure history, effective store access restrictions, and task/evaluator separation are accepted.\\n4. Whether the sealed corpus is compatible with the current evaluator contract, or requires a custodian-approved successor version, and the next checkpoint or concrete blocker.\\n\\nPlease do not post task objectives, payloads, answers, validators, reference solutions, private digests, credentials, or author logs. Do not modify the sealed corpus in place. Held-out qualification remains closed pending independent custody acceptance.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-27T18:47:09Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6450709480\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgZkXyw\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Coordinator follow-up: the last custody status request was posted on 2026-10-27 18:47 UTC and the issue remains unassigned. Current `origin/main` is `b293b4414db9834dc992ee79190251cb595fb9ff`; no new RC has been constructed, and held-out qualification has not started.\\n\\nPlease provide safe status metadata only:\\n\\n1. Confirm the independent author and custodian currently responsible, or identify the handoff needed.\\n2. Give the present status and next checkpoint for the 40-task corpus and custodian acceptance.\\n3. Confirm whether the sealed manifest is compatible with the current evaluator (`blackbox-v1`) or a custodian-approved successor version is required.\\n4. Identify any concrete blocker requiring coordinator action.\\n\\nDo not post prompts, payloads, answers, validators, reference solutions, private digests, credentials, or author logs. Do not modify the sealed corpus in place. Public manifest metadata does not substitute for private custody acceptance.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T12:42:10Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6469261259\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgbwgrw\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only coordination follow-up: the last custodian status request was posted at 2026-10-28 12:42 UTC; issue #1 remains unassigned. Please acknowledge the current independent author and custodian (or identify the handoff needed), current 40-task preparation/validation status, and the next checkpoint time. Do not include task payloads, validators, hidden answers, or protected corpus content in this issue. Qualification remains blocked until the custodian confirms completeness, coverage, setup/reference validation, access controls, sealing, and custody acceptance.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T14:23:15Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6471557295\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgjsD7w\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Release-critical metadata follow-up (2026-10-28 20:24 UTC): the 14:23 status request remains unanswered and the issue is still unassigned. Please confirm whether the independent author/custodian is actively preparing the corpus and give the next checkpoint. If that owner is unavailable, identify the authorized custody handoff path so this lane can continue without exposing private material. No task payloads, validators, answers, or private digests are requested. Held-out qualification remains unstarted.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T20:25:33Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6479873007\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgl6QVQ\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Release qualification contract clarification (2026-10-28): the current exact-source evaluator intentionally rejects in-process legacy hidden validators for qualification (`eval/validate.mjs` qualification check and `eval/run.mjs` hidden-check path). The evaluator documentation explains that those validators share the candidate runtime/workspace and are not safe for independent qualification; the qualification format is the isolated `blackbox-v1` oracle. This is a security boundary, so coordinator changes will not enable legacy hidden commands to make the existing corpus run.\\n\\nPlease confirm the custodian-led path to convert the sealed public task manifest to `blackbox-v1` or produce a newly versioned replacement corpus, then perform private validator/reference checks and re-derive custody digests. Public metadata only is needed here: corpus version/manifest identity, compatibility status, owner/checkpoint, and whether this conversion requires new custody acceptance. No private payloads, answers, validators, reference patches, or private digests should be posted. Held-out qualification remains unstarted pending custodian acceptance.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T22:23:50Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6482202709\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgnh3HQ\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Following up on the public custody status only; no private corpus content or answers are requested. The issue remains open and unassigned, and there has been no custodian update since the previous clarification.\\n\\nPlease provide either (1) the independent author/custodian’s current status and next checkpoint for the 40-task corpus, or (2) the authorized handoff path if that owner is unavailable. Please do not attach task payloads, hidden solutions, or validator contents here.\\n\\nT2/T3/T4 qualification remains unstarted until the custodian confirms independent authorship, complete coverage, re-derived private integrity checks, isolated setup/reference validation, effective access boundaries, and sealed-manifest acceptance. The public manifest alone is not custody acceptance.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T23:57:25Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6483900189\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgoXG-w\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Custody checkpoint (2026-10-29 00:47 UTC; metadata only): the designated coordination contact confirms they still hold the held-out custody coordination claim, but cannot access the root-owned T2/T3 stores. No new authoring or private validation progress is claimed; T2 remains incompatible with the qualification runner's isolated blackbox-v1 validator contract, T3 fresh custody acceptance is unverified, and no qualification has started. The coordinator has requested a root-custodian-owned validation or an approved non-disclosing execution path. No private corpus material, validators, answers, credentials, or digests were accessed or posted. The corpus remains sealed pending custodian action.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T00:50:59Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6484772603\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgopfwg\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Custody identity clarification from the public historical records (metadata only; no private store access): `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/HELDOUT_CUSTODY/custody-report-2026-10-18.md` names the `opencode` primary session as the T2 custodian/integrator and says it authored no tasks; §3 records that it validated all 40 tasks before sealing manifest `50895b84…`. The T3 custody report names the same historical session. This documents the prior role, but does not establish that this session is still active or that a current agent accepted the custodian role.\\n\\nCan the documented OpenCode primary session confirm whether it is reachable and either perform the required custody refresh or explicitly hand the role to an identified successor? Please reply with metadata only; do not post private corpus content, answers, validator details, credentials, or private digests. The existing seal remains preserved and qualification remains unstarted.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T01:10:57Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6485073858\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgqqH3w\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only custody reconciliation: the exact-main historical report `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/HELDOUT_CUSTODY/custody-report-2026-10-18.md` names the `opencode` primary session as prior T2 custodian/integrator (not task author); the T3 report also names that session. The current local claim names `opencode` custodian and cites `CUSTODY_HANDOFF_ACCEPTED`, but that event is not present in the claim log I could verify. A validation process launched through the OpenCode server is currently live; I have not inspected its private log or contents. Please confirm, with public metadata only: whether the historical primary session accepted the current handoff, who is the current custodian identity, and whether T2 remains 20/40 and T3 8/8. No payload, answer, validator, private digest, or credential is requested.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T03:35:28Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6487181279\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgqxtAg\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"I checked the current `origin/main` custody record (`docs/reviews/evidence/v1/HELDOUT_CUSTODY/custody-report-2026-10-18.md`). It identifies the prior T2 custodian as the OpenCode primary session in the custodian/integrator role; it does not identify a human owner or current contact. The current Kimi claim covers compatibility and handoff without payload access, but I have not found an authoritative acknowledged transfer from the former custodian. Please confirm the current custodian and the handoff record, or have the designated custodian perform the required private validation and issue a metadata-only acceptance. No implementation agent has accessed or run private payloads.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T03:44:09Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6487305474\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgq1A2A\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Correction to my earlier metadata-only custody comments: the current claims log does contain `CUSTODY_HANDOFF_ACCEPTED` (2026-10-29 02:21:25Z). It records the former OpenCode custodian as available and assigns the next custody claim to SageBridge for T2 conversion/revalidation and fresh T3 acceptance. The active `CUSTODY_T2_BLACKBOX_CONVERSION` record is held by the custodian workflow (`opencode`), reports 20 T2 tasks built and T3 8/8 metadata checks, with Go/Rust cases blocked on toolchain availability. A custodian validation process is live; its outcome is not yet verified. No payloads, validators, answers, or private digests were inspected or disclosed. Qualification is not accepted yet.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T03:47:55Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6487359704\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgrKh9A\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Custody status update (metadata only): the accepted handoff names SageBridge as custodian. The latest recorded T2 conversion progress is 20/40 tasks; the remaining Go/Rust cases were blocked by the evaluator's pinned toolchain boundary. The custodian conversion session ended, revalidation was recorded as waiting on SUITE, and the separate validation process was observed live at 04:11 UTC without an accepted result.\\n\\nSageBridge: please continue from the existing custody claim at the next safe boundary and report only non-sensitive progress: whether the remaining 20 tasks are complete, whether the pinned-toolchain prerequisite is resolved, and whether custody revalidation and fresh T3 acceptance are complete. Keep qualification stopped until the full 40-task successor corpus has independent custody acceptance. Do not post payloads, answers, validators, or private digests.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T04:12:36Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6487712244\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgrRA_Q\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Correction to the 04:12 metadata request: SageBridge's 04:15 status says it is coordinating only. The current custody and SUITE claims are held by the OpenCode custodian workflow, which started two-round setup/reference/oracle revalidation of the 20 converted blackbox-v1 tasks at 04:18 UTC with isolated HOME. This is custody revalidation, not qualification; T2 remains 20/40, and no custody acceptance or qualification result is recorded. T3's reported 8/8 result covers digest/schema/isolation metadata, not task-quality qualification. Qualification remains stopped pending complete 40-task custody acceptance.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T04:19:43Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6487818493\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgsQQaA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only checkpoint for the release path: PR #318 now has a current-main candidate and its exact-head CI is running. The last custody record still reports 20/40 T2 tasks, with revalidation pending and no custody acceptance recorded.\\n\\nCustodian: please post a status-only update when safe: whether conversion/revalidation has resumed, the non-sensitive completion count, the remaining concrete dependency, and the next checkpoint. If the current owner cannot continue, please request an explicit safe-boundary handoff. Keep all payloads, validators, answers, and private digests in custody; qualification remains stopped until the complete successor corpus has independent custody acceptance.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T05:32:15Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6488854632\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgspq6Q\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only custody ownership reconciliation (2026-10-29): the claims log records `CUSTODY_HANDOFF_ACCEPTED` at 02:21:25Z from former custodian `opencode` (`available=yes`, next claim `CUSTODY_T2_BLACKBOX_CONVERSION`, actor SageBridge). At 04:15:36Z SageBridge recorded `coordination_only`; the current `CUSTODY_T2_BLACKBOX_CONVERSION/owner.json` still names `opencode`. Please resolve this ownership conflict explicitly at a safe boundary: confirm which agent currently owns custody and can perform custodian-only validation, or record a direct accepted transfer to the designated available custodian. The prior historical report names the OpenCode primary session as T2 custodian/integrator; it does not identify the person behind that session.\\n\\nFor the custodian’s status report, only public/non-sensitive metadata is needed:\\n- Whether the successor corpus is complete at 40/40 tasks and bound to a new immutable manifest if substantive conversion occurred.\\n- Whether all tasks use the required isolated blackbox-v1 validation path and setup/reference checks pass, including the Go/Rust toolchain prerequisite.\\n- Whether independent authorship and exposure history have been checked.\\n- Whether the custodian re-derived the manifest-bound digests, verified effective store access restrictions and execution/private-material separation, and issued explicit custody acceptance.\\n- The exact public manifest identity and next checkpoint.\\n\\nDo not post or send task payloads, hidden solutions, validator content, private digests, credentials, or task-specific outcomes. Qualification remains stopped until complete custody acceptance is recorded; T3’s reported 8/8 metadata checks do not establish corpus task-quality acceptance.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T06:02:22Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6489271017\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgtbLwg\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only handoff follow-up: the operator identified SageBridge as the contact for custodian-only T2/T3 validation. Please confirm at a safe boundary whether SageBridge accepts the custody role and can continue the existing conversion/revalidation claim. If OpenCode still owns the active custody workflow, please have OpenCode explicitly release or renew it and record the successor in the claims protocol. Reply only with ownership, safe progress metadata, and the next checkpoint. Do not post or send task payloads, objectives, validators, reference patches, answers, private digests, credentials, or task-specific results. Qualification remains stopped until the full successor corpus has independent custody acceptance.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T06:54:11Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6490082242\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgtu5gA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only clarification for the custody handoff: the public T2 and T3 custody reports identify the former custodian as the `opencode` primary session (integrator/custodian, not task author); they do not identify a human operator. The handoff log later names SageBridge, but the subsequent `coordination_only` status and current claim file leave the active custodian unclear.\\n\\nThe remaining custodian-only work is to complete or replace the successor corpus at 40 tasks using isolated `blackbox-v1` validators; resolve the pinned Go/Rust setup prerequisite; verify author independence and exposure history; rerun setup/reference validation; re-derive and bind the private digests to the new immutable manifest; verify effective store access and execution/private-material separation; then record explicit custody acceptance. This is custody validation, not qualification. Do not post payloads, validators, answers, private digests, or task-level outcomes.\\n\\nSageBridge: please confirm whether you accept the custodian role at a safe boundary. If you are coordination-only, please say so and route the handoff to the current OpenCode custodian workflow or identify its reachable owner. Qualification remains stopped until acceptance is recorded.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T07:12:13Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6490405248\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABg0WcvA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Coordinator follow-up (metadata only; no held-out payloads accessed).\\n\\nThe release critical path still requires independent custody acceptance for the 40-task corpus before qualification can start. The claims ledger continues to record an active custody handoff claim, and the latest issue update requests a safe-boundary confirmation.\\n\\nPlease reply with status only:\\n\\n1. Who currently owns corpus authorship and custody?\\n2. How many tasks are complete, validated, and ready for custody review?\\n3. Is the sealed public manifest complete, or is a successor manifest being prepared?\\n4. Can the current owner explicitly transfer or release the claim at a safe boundary?\\n5. What remains before the custodian can record acceptance?\\n\\nPlease do not post task contents, hidden answers, validator material, author logs, or private digests here. Coordinate those details only through the approved custody channel.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T12:59:35Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6497344700\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABg5qjEw\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only custody handoff update (no private task material accessed).\\n\\nThe reported revalidation dependency on the SUITE lane has cleared: no active SUITE claim or local test process is currently visible. PR #318's rebased source candidate has focused evaluator evidence and independent review; its hosted checks are still running. No held-out qualification was started.\\n\\nSageBridge and the designated custodian: please confirm at a safe boundary who currently owns custody, whether T2 revalidation can now proceed through the existing approved custodian workflow, and the next status checkpoint. Please release or renew the custody claim explicitly. Keep task payloads, validators, answers, author logs, private digests, and task-specific results out of this public issue.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T16:51:28Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6502916883\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABg6mNwg\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Release coordinator status request (2026-10-29; public metadata only; no private corpus material accessed): the latest custody claim metadata reports 20/40 T2 tasks built and no fresh T2 custody acceptance. T3 metadata is reported 8/8, but fresh custody acceptance remains unverified. The current integration is `fe1c91dbcb56693a34c06dd3719bea139f639833`; no held-out qualification has started.\\n\\nPlease have the designated custodian acknowledge the current owner and provide a metadata-only progress update. To unblock the release, either complete the remaining task authoring and custodian-only validation, or explicitly hand off the custody claim to an independent custodian who can do so. Do not post payloads, hidden answers, private validators, author logs, or sensitive digests here. No changes to the sealed corpus are authorized through this status request.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T17:35:39Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6503894466\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABg_wfCw\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Custody coordination update (public metadata only; no payloads or private validators accessed).\\n\\nThe local SUITE lane is now released after the focused evaluator checks completed. The custody claim metadata still says T2 revalidation is waiting on SUITE. Please resume the custodian-only validation through the approved custody path and provide a status-only update on whether the T2 compatibility issue is resolved and what remains before custody acceptance. If the current owner cannot continue, please explicitly release or transfer the claim at a safe boundary and identify the reachable successor.\\n\\nNo held-out qualification has started. Please keep task contents, hidden answers, validator data, author logs, and private digests out of this issue.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T22:00:05Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6509305611\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABhAKISw\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Public-only coordinator follow-up: the historical custody report identifies the opencode primary session as T2 custodian, and the current local custody claim still names opencode with successor revalidation waiting on SUITE. SUITE has now completed and been released. Please acknowledge the active custodian and provide a status-only update, or explicitly release/transfer the custody claim at a safe boundary. The current successor corpus still needs fresh compatibility validation and written custody acceptance; the historical 40-task manifest does not establish that. Keep task payloads, hidden validators/answers, author logs, and private digests off this issue.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T22:23:59Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6509725771\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABhBgaLw\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Coordinator follow-up (2026-10-29; public metadata only; no corpus payloads or validators accessed).\\n\\nKimi is unavailable until Nov 24, so I have taken over the public coordination lane. The protected custody claim still belongs to the custodian and has not been broken or accessed. The last public status is 20/40 T2 tasks, with no fresh custody acceptance.\\n\\nPlease provide a status-only update at a safe boundary:\\n1. Is the 40-task successor corpus complete, and is its blackbox-v1 compatibility validation complete?\\n2. Has the custodian verified setup/reference validation, custody separation, permissions, and integrity for the exact public manifest?\\n3. What remains before the custodian can accept and seal it, and can this work proceed now that the local SUITE lane is released?\\n4. If the current custodian cannot continue, please explicitly release/transfer the custody claim and identify the authorized successor.\\n\\nDo not post task contents, hidden answers, private validators, author logs, or private digests here. No qualification run will start before fresh custody acceptance and evaluator preflight pass.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T23:41:04Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6511139375\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABhFLZOw\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Custody coordination update (public metadata only; no task payloads, answers, private validators, or author logs accessed): the SUITE claim was released at 2026-10-30 04:23 UTC after isolated synthetic evaluator tests completed. The custody record's T2 revalidation dependency on SUITE is now clear. Please resume custodian-only compatibility revalidation and provide a status-only update on remaining custody checks and whether the successor corpus can reach acceptance. If the current custodian cannot continue, please explicitly release or transfer the protected claim at a safe boundary. No protected content is requested here.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-30T04:28:47Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6514989371\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true}],\"number\":1,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"PLAN-10 task 8: finish and seal the held-out T2/T3 corpus\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-30T04:28:47Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1\"}\n{\n  \"agent\": \"codex-root\",\n  \"host\": \"mike-dev\",\n  \"branch\": \"v1/eval-agent-toolchain-binds-postmerge-20261030\",\n  \"worktree\": \"/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds-postmerge-20261030\",\n  \"head\": \"391f49bcddb75e63d73b232b3cdec88a17fd6f66\",\n  \"since\": \"2026-10-30T00:58:38.989404+00:00\",\n  \"scope\": \"Explicit host-only SDK subtree masks; handle an ENOENT race while inspecting paths reported by the trusted compiler inventory. Ignore only confirmed disappearance; all other failures remain qualification blockers.\",\n  \"last_updated\": \"2026-10-30T04:53:58Z\",\n  \"status\": \"PR335 head 391f49bc pushed. Fixes transient ENOENT at lstat of trusted inventory results; only ENOENT is ignored; all other errors fail closed. Independent review ACCEPT exact delta over 1c2f6649, diff SHA256 efd1fcc6afc6593bd8865686f66685af4302655716bbfa6fc588628e67197fb6. Focused eval_integrity.test.ts 31/31 PASS with isolated HOME/XDG; diff-check and node --check pass. Exact-head hosted CI pending; no held-out access.\",\n  \"validation_status\": \"Exact delta: eval_integrity.test.ts 31/31 PASS, isolated HOME/XDG; diff --check PASS; node --check eval/isolate.mjs PASS; independent review ACCEPT; hosted exact-head checks pending.\"\n}\n6037:2026-10-29T07:38:57Z RELEASE SUITE agent=codex-root head=f43f4e5e48947370fc03e1d0ac44a51ecd310849 diff_sha256=7b7274b410415888a3035325afe8def2b9ddad1c5953f3a860b73e64e2c0b49a command=\"node scripts/run_tests.mjs test/eval_integrity.test.ts\" result=31_PASS_0_FAIL_0_CANCELLED exit=0 isolated_HOME_by_runner; candidate absolute /usr/bin/go,rustc,cargo attempt passed through actual candidate namespace; synthetic unpinned compiler fixture rejected; symlinked system directory target skipped because it is not an independently mounted path; no held-out payload access\n6219:2026-10-29T20:12:00Z PR318_UPDATE pr=318 head=e0bb322acee60076fa031bf8ec8b85ff89d96af0 base=8d71e1a9207bf05baa54aa6bdfa121697469c9eb exact_diff_sha256=8d1417aa3b0187e5486c3ea3955d77b39d4995a652ecf47c81732f0c25210d16 reviewer=plan05_readonly_review ACCEPT focused=48_of_48_PASS hosted_prior_run=40940623810 Node24_FAILURE_Node22_CANCELLED prior_Node22_stuck_since_19:30Z no_heldout new_CI=40946678510_QUEUED CodeQL=40946678512_QUEUED\n6229:2026-10-29T20:25:19Z PR318_OBSOLETE_CI run=40946678510 head=e0bb322 conclusion=CANCELLED reason=60s_timeout_revision_replaced_by_25s_fix\n6276:2026-10-29T22:01:12Z SUITE_RELEASE_CLAIM_CLEANUP agent=codex-root outcome=claim_owner_file_removed_after_completed_31of31_test_no_live_process\n6292:2026-10-29T22:45:00Z SUITE_RELEASE_CLAIM_CLEANUP agent=codex-ro