{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T04:59:01.075Z","ordinal":517027,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18b23-4d83-7030-a9f6-1c2205929058","session_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","root_turn_id":"01a18b23-4d83-7030-a9f6-1c2205929058","response_id":"resp_0db389702a7164cc016ae424129838819f9597838ace7537ec","usage":{"input_tokens":90633,"cached_input_tokens":89088,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":282,"reasoning_output_tokens":265,"total_tokens":90915},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":13934804,"cached_input_tokens":13831936,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":36684,"reasoning_output_tokens":23060,"total_tokens":13971488},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":9722964066,"cached_input_tokens":9619767168,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":27975334,"reasoning_output_tokens":16453945,"total_tokens":9750939400}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T04:59:01.189Z","ordinal":517028,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a18b2c-f2c5-7060-93cc-19b7c041833c","call_id":"call_b9a116beacd54c1e9608173123f66580","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/pr311_draft_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** — reviewed `534e21b7e5292a2f85ae1e3586e6051652e87ce6` against base `38a875ccfeb89f926d2bcf3cc12a37a0cbe40ff5`. Diff SHA-256: `bca120887e117401fa90cbbacc6cf539f52ac5ffeea0bd7fa2512f5042ff8b7b`.\\n\\nThe release job installs Go, materializes the pinned Go/Rust toolchains, trims hosted-runner SDK trees, and sets the evaluator sandbox roots before the CLI suite ([release.yml](/home/mike/nexus-wt/claude-release-parity/.github/workflows/release.yml:27), [release.yml](/home/mike/nexus-wt/claude-release-parity/.github/workflows/release.yml:36), [release.yml](/home/mike/nexus-wt/claude-release-parity/.github/workflows/release.yml:102)). These steps match CI’s evaluator setup ([ci.yml](/home/mike/nexus-wt/claude-release-parity/.github/workflows/ci.yml:20), [ci.yml](/home/mike/nexus-wt/claude-release-parity/.github/workflows/ci.yml:89)). The new parity test checks that the setup agrees and precedes the release CLI suite ([release_workflow_parity.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/claude-release-parity/cli/test/release_workflow_parity.test.ts:13)).\\n\\nNo findings. Source review only; I did not run tests. The release notes describe RC12 as unpublished and RC13 as its replacement; this review does not establish RC qualification.\\n\\n\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/review_pr300_readiness\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** — reviewed the uncommitted delta over `1c2f6649ffdead6d7d32c7fd9b1c57ee735a17b4`. The fixture removes the compiler when `lstatSync` first inspects the path returned by inventory, so it exercises the intended post-inventory ENOENT race. Only ENOENT is ignored; other errors still reach the outer fail-closed handler. Existing symlink detection and masking behavior remain unchanged.\\n\\nDiff SHA-256: `efd1fcc6afc6593bd8865686f66685af4302655716bbfa6fc588628e67197fb6`. I did not edit files or run tests.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/review_pr302\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT.** The lockfile-only change resolves the cited RUSTSEC-2026-0418: it upgrades `libz-sys` to the stated fixed version, 1.1.31. The locked `cc` is 1.5.1, below the advisory’s affected `cc >= 1.6.0` condition. The new checksum matches the local crates.io index entry, and the diff changes no other dependencies.\\n\\nI could not retrieve RUSTSEC-2026-0418 through the available advisory lookup, so that applicability assessment relies on the exact advisory details you supplied from main CI. No tests or suites were run.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18b23-4d83-7030-a9f6-1c2205929058","create_time":1793336341.1895182}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
