{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T04:59:07.709Z","ordinal":517036,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18b23-4d83-7030-a9f6-1c2205929058","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-abebd7c4-f8b3-4036-b6c7-81f3881c0323","process_id":"24701","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -l '420aa7e1|PR341|claude/release-eval-setup-parity' /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims --glob 'owner.json' | xargs -r -n1 sh -c 'echo --- $0; cat \"$0\"'; gh pr view 341 --repo mikeholownych/nexus-code --json comments,latestReviews --jq '{comments: [.comments[-3:][]|{author:.author.login,createdAt,body}],reviews: [.latestReviews[]|{author:.author.login,state,submittedAt,body}]}'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rg -l '420aa7e1|PR341|claude/release-eval-setup-parity' /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims --glob 'owner.json' | xargs -r -n1 sh -c 'echo --- $0; cat \"$0\"'; gh pr view 341 --repo mikeholownych/nexus-code --json comments,latestReviews --jq '{comments: [.comments[-3:][]|{author:.author.login,createdAt,body}],reviews: [.latestReviews[]|{author:.author.login,state,submittedAt,body}]}'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\"comments\":[{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Follow-up with merge-tree evidence: I computed a clean synthetic merge of current PR #335 head `1c2f6649ffdead6d7d32c7fd9b1c57ee735a17b4` and PR #341 head `420aa7e1a6d42480c0ec0d3b9bbec21066c27d60`, both based on `38a875ccfeb89f926d2bcf3cc12a37a0cbe40ff5`. The resulting tree is `b308db0ca827e56b812ec41296a2588239a4ac03`. In that merged tree, release.yml invokes `bash scripts/ci-trim-runner-image.sh`, the script is absent, and the parity test still asserts that CI has that invocation. This confirms a clean-merge integration defect. Please update #341 against the current evaluator setup and rerun exact-head checks/review.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-30T04:29:59Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Exact-head CI update for PR #341 head `420aa7e1a6d42480c0ec0d3b9bbec21066c27d60`: Node 22 passed; Node 24 failed only at `test/eval_t3.test.ts:246` because the synthetic T3 run refused to qualify with `compiler exposure could not be checked; refusing qualification`. PR #335's scanner candidate at `1c2f6649` has now passed both Node 22 and Node 24. This confirms PR #341 needs to be rebased/updated after #335 integration, in addition to removing the retired runner-trim command and strengthening the parity assertions. The existing release-workflow review blocker still applies; no merge or RC tag should proceed until the updated exact head has independent review and all exact-head checks pass.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-30T04:46:29Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"test-matrix (24) at 420aa7e1 failed one test: eval_t3.test.ts:246, after 430 ms, with `compiler exposure could not be checked; refusing qualification`. That is the same qualification-tooling flake that hit main at f7a394f5. #341 doesn't touch the evaluator or its tests. I re-ran the failed job once; merge still requires every exact-head check to be completed/success. Diagnosis posted on #335.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-30T04:46:43Z\"}],\"reviews\":[]}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":455809270}},"started_at_ms":1793336347252,"completed_at_ms":1793336347709}}
