{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T05:00:07.619Z","ordinal":517102,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18b23-4d83-7030-a9f6-1c2205929058","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae42455ba90819f9b24d53b0978e31b","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"**PR335’s scanner fix is complete and independently reviewed, but the exact-head checks are still running.** I’m keeping the release acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`; no RC is accepted and no stable release is verified.\n\n- PR335 is at `391f49bcddb75e63d73b232b3cdec88a17fd6f66` on `main`, against `origin/main` `38a875ccfeb89f926d2bcf3cc12a37a0cbe40ff5`.\n- CodeQL and JS/TS checks passed. Node 22 and Node 24 test matrices and Entire Gates remain pending. The earlier CI run was canceled and does not count as passing evidence.\n- The targeted evaluator regression passed **31/31** with isolated HOME/XDG. Independent review accepted the delta; only `ENOENT` for inventory paths that disappear during inspection is ignored, and other errors remain fail-closed.\n- PR341 still has unresolved evaluator/setup and release-workflow findings. Its owner’s worktree remains present, so I have not taken over the claimed changes.\n- Held-out custody still has no fresh acceptance; qualification has not started.\n\nNext, I’ll use PR335’s exact-head results to decide whether it can integrate, then revalidate dependent PRs and continue the release gates. Neither the RC11 evidence PRs nor the current pending checks establish v1.0.0 acceptance."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1793336405755,"completed_at_ms":1793336407619}}
