{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T05:02:14.754Z","ordinal":517199,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a18b2f-e6e2-78e0-91b1-0fd09377fa43","call_id":"call_08bded3835e945238154098bffe2c6f9","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/pr311_draft_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** — reviewed `534e21b7e5292a2f85ae1e3586e6051652e87ce6` against base `38a875ccfeb89f926d2bcf3cc12a37a0cbe40ff5`. Diff SHA-256: `bca120887e117401fa90cbbacc6cf539f52ac5ffeea0bd7fa2512f5042ff8b7b`.\\n\\nThe release job installs Go, materializes the pinned Go/Rust toolchains, trims hosted-runner SDK trees, and sets the evaluator sandbox roots before the CLI suite ([release.yml](/home/mike/nexus-wt/claude-release-parity/.github/workflows/release.yml:27), [release.yml](/home/mike/nexus-wt/claude-release-parity/.github/workflows/release.yml:36), [release.yml](/home/mike/nexus-wt/claude-release-parity/.github/workflows/release.yml:102)). These steps match CI’s evaluator setup ([ci.yml](/home/mike/nexus-wt/claude-release-parity/.github/workflows/ci.yml:20), [ci.yml](/home/mike/nexus-wt/claude-release-parity/.github/workflows/ci.yml:89)). The new parity test checks that the setup agrees and precedes the release CLI suite ([release_workflow_parity.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/claude-release-parity/cli/test/release_workflow_parity.test.ts:13)).\\n\\nNo findings. Source review only; I did not run tests. The release notes describe RC12 as unpublished and RC13 as its replacement; this review does not establish RC qualification.\\n\\n\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/review_pr300_readiness\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/review_pr302\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT.** The lockfile-only change resolves the cited RUSTSEC-2026-0418: it upgrades `libz-sys` to the stated fixed version, 1.1.31. The locked `cc` is 1.5.1, below the advisory’s affected `cc >= 1.6.0` condition. The new checksum matches the local crates.io index entry, and the diff changes no other dependencies.\\n\\nI could not retrieve RUSTSEC-2026-0418 through the available advisory lookup, so that applicability assessment relies on the exact advisory details you supplied from main CI. No tests or suites were run.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18b2e-6bb9-7ca2-be18-28c72b70147e","create_time":1793336534.7543526}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
