{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T05:02:39.277Z","ordinal":517217,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a18b30-46ad-7bd2-a287-ba68e8963ed8","author":"/root/review_pr300_readiness","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/review_pr300_readiness\nPayload:\n**ACCEPT** — PR #337 is still open at head `ba72d2cbfb8f446254cf829ac5990148fed82500`, based on `5c516476e8dfcaf9cdd59eaa204134e25d2be673`. Diff SHA-256 from that base: `bab1c8e8c846201646e048e969ff42423b2e6740e2cd53ff26f6df78bd9f0037`.\n\n- **Artifact binding:** The README records RC11’s source commit, installed version, and archive digest (`providers/README.md:5–11`). The archived provenance and compatibility metadata agree on RC11, source commit, build time, and archive digest (`providers/install/.provenance.json:5–13`, `compatibility.json:4–12`). The source commit is the RC11 tag target, and GitHub’s release asset reports the same archive digest.\n- **Receipts and outcomes:** ChatGPT has three passing verify steps and matching request IDs in its receipts (`chatgpt/verify.json:2–24, 26–70`). OpenRouter attempts 1 and 2 are explicitly failed as `TEMPORARILY_UNAVAILABLE`; attempt 3 records the three passing steps (`openrouter-attempt-1/verify.json:2–14`, `attempt-2/verify.json:2–14`, `attempt-3/verify.json:2–16`). The README preserves those failures and does not claim E5 or overall RC acceptance (`providers/README.md:21–26`).\n- **Hash integrity and disclosure:** All 22 entries in `SHA256SUMS` matched their archived file contents. Receipts contain provider/request metadata, not message bodies. The synthetic task files disclose that raw transcripts were not retained and label the task outcome as unverified/operator-reported (`openrouter-live-task/README.md:9–17`, `retry.md:9–15`); I found no credentials or raw prompt payloads in the packet.\n- **Current-main drift:** `origin/main` is `38a875cc`, two commits beyond the PR base: the RC12 candidate and installer durability fix. They do not invalidate this explicitly RC11-bound historical evidence. Rebase PR #337 onto current main before integration and exact-head checks; this packet cannot serve as RC12 qualification."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18b2e-6bb9-7ca2-be18-28c72b70147e","create_time":1793336559.277404,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":23821}}
