{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T05:06:55.710Z","ordinal":517385,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18b33-8176-74a3-9ae0-b741cc1afe98","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-bd3f5e15-5225-465a-ad98-0d2f3e36560b","process_id":"92032","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -l 'synthetic standalone OpenRouter|installed-RC11 synthetic|OpenRouter verification' /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims --glob 'owner.json' | while read f; do echo \"--- $f\"; cat \"$f\"; done; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc11-provider-evidence diff --stat; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc11-provider-evidence diff -- docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.11/providers/README.md docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.11/providers/SHA256SUMS | head -100"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rg -l 'synthetic standalone OpenRouter|installed-RC11 synthetic|OpenRouter verification' /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims --glob 'owner.json' | while read f; do echo \"--- $f\"; cat \"$f\"; done; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc11-provider-evidence diff --stat; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc11-provider-evidence diff -- docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.11/providers/README.md docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.11/providers/SHA256SUMS | head -100"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":" .../evidence/v1-qualification/rc.11/providers/README.md    | 14 ++++++++++++++\n .../evidence/v1-qualification/rc.11/providers/SHA256SUMS   |  3 ++-\n 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)\ndiff --git a/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.11/providers/README.md b/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.11/providers/README.md\nindex 1bbf480b..dbdd7a39 100644\n--- a/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.11/providers/README.md\n+++ b/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.11/providers/README.md\n@@ -24,3 +24,17 @@ Each verification ran from a new empty temporary workspace through the installed\n After attempt 3 passed, an authorized synthetic live task and a repeat ran in fresh temporary fixtures containing only `math.js` and its two-case Node test. The first task run made the intended one-line fix, but its completion was not established: the operator-configured verifier binding treated the imported source as verifier support because the fixture had no package manifest or declared deliverable. The test command passed in-run and independently after that attempt. In the repeat, `math.js` was declared with `--deliverable-file`; the operator observed Nexus report `VERIFIED`, and an independent post-run invocation was reported to pass 2/2 tests. The raw task transcript, flightlog, and fixture were not retained, so these task outcomes and post-run result are not independently reproducible from this packet. The first run requested a maximum of 8 total steps but recorded 13; the repeat records no step cap or observed step count. Therefore this packet does not establish step-limit compliance or provide acceptance evidence for task completion. Both attempts, including the first verifier refusal, remain described; the original `TEMPORARILY_UNAVAILABLE` outcomes from provider attempts 1 and 2 are preserved as historical failures; attempt 3 does not erase them.\n \n This packet covers installed-RC provider verification and records two synthetic task attempts with the reproducibility and step-limit limitations above. It does not establish standalone, held-out, T3/T4, or overall RC acceptance.\n+\n+## Additional bounded OpenRouter task (2026-10-30)\n+\n+A fresh, synthetic task was run against the installed RC11 artifact using the pinned OpenRouter model above. The isolated workspace contained only `math.js` and `test/math.test.js`; `math.js` was declared with `--deliverable-file`, and the trusted verifier was `node --test test/math.test.js`. No repository, user, or held-out files were present.\n+\n+Three attempts are preserved in order:\n+\n+1. Review mode made no changes because headless execution could not obtain tool approval. This is an incomplete attempt.\n+2. Auto mode without an authoritative verifier changed the deliverable, but Nexus correctly ended `UNVERIFIED (NO_APPLICABLE_VERIFIER)`. An independent test run passed 2/2; this does not change Nexus's failed completion disposition.\n+3. Auto mode with the explicit authoritative verifier ended `TASK COMPLETED - VERIFIED (node --test test/math.test.js)`. A separate post-run invocation of that same test command passed 2/2. The final `math.js` is exactly one changed deliverable and has SHA-256 `4a55def8b436bfbdad6298095c1398a43c04500f69ee7d7a7630ea809dac7441`; `test/math.test.js` has SHA-256 `ed07216490a7a47d91fc7d14c7f7e1770c36a72d449a335e795b7eadf43c8d2d`.\n+\n+For attempt 3, the retained flight log SHA-256 is `dfd1ba34fbe98e9e030b923f9b94217b997456155f564157497f993a1488ca89`, and the inference-receipt file SHA-256 is `b7388e212cebde84b8218ee439cea03431a9d464dc9fc5ef32d682ae47f6936d`. The raw files remain on the qualification host and are not copied into this repository. The run records the task, commands, artifact identity, completion disposition, independent result, hashes, and evidence-retention boundary in `openrouter-live-task-20261030.md`.\n+\n+This is one small standalone task, not corpus-based qualification or overall E5/RC acceptance. The failed/incomplete attempts remain part of the evidence; no claim is made that they passed.\ndiff --git a/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.11/providers/SHA256SUMS b/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.11/providers/SHA256SUMS\nindex c93aa188..9da4c21a 100644\n--- a/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.11/providers/SHA256SUMS\n+++ b/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.11/providers/SHA256SUMS\n@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@\n-46af8e2a78aafaa08e2d32630a8bb842089995b13485705146758ffab0432b78  ./README.md\n+b12cd3899b3e9b9c0b78ffb5abeee389a28ae3091d6fecb1959bf248da9fd58f  ./README.md\n 6b54366f6b6e27008a9a2b4b3f5dfd3d4adde9575e21f76215e964b854dd599a  ./chatgpt/inference_receipts.jsonl\n 57ee85739349cac77a2b4adcd75271c6c40339ba2793184f6b77a8c0112873aa  ./chatgpt/verify.json\n 2f4ebd1e0907b84b69c99a2b31ba79b64a46a10fc244eb8c0cb0d16070223ba2  ./chatgpt/verify.stderr\n@@ -18,5 +18,6 @@ fa0519924bbc21c8f724cc3b72a21f2f246efd8a91f8f34ed1fd9509cb865cc2  ./openrouter-a\n d24d97e45d4ccb7e1f46c8fc2537697623feed6e6e88d9476ef211856e06140a  ./openrouter-attempt-3/verify.json\n 70edc78a133e5d798bda280c9ba70b2f80a5eaf52e9e27fcecca0e1093f38281  ./openrouter-attempt-3/verify.stderr\n fa0519924bbc21c8f724cc3b72a21f2f246efd8a91f8f34ed1fd9509cb865cc2  ./openrouter-attempt-3/version.txt\n+58315ec6b5986c3c8a27f6a4813770ce7d7b4bbe25c0180f3ba0f2a07ac41497  ./openrouter-live-task-20261030.md\n e56d621dfdff4f16a4b0d1141b9dab1d50298eb5124d3ebfb05896cdf583d79f  ./openrouter-live-task/README.md\n af32e2061706f61405c7d94c048a0321504ce9ce18f5df78ba5fa072c367dddb  ./openrouter-live-task/retry.md\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":52334}},"started_at_ms":1793336815710,"completed_at_ms":1793336815710}}
