{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T05:07:31.685Z","ordinal":517447,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a18b34-bce4-7aa0-9622-7581e97cf37c","author":"/root/review_pr300_readiness","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/review_pr300_readiness\nPayload:\n**ACCEPT** — reviewed the uncommitted delta over `ba72d2cbfb8f446254cf829ac5990148fed82500`. The new report binds the task to RC11’s source revision, archive digest, installed version, OpenRouter model, declared deliverable, and explicit verifier (`openrouter-live-task-20261030.md:5–11`). It preserves the incomplete and unverified attempts, records the final verified disposition and reported independent 2/2 rerun, and limits the claim to one synthetic task rather than E5 or RC acceptance (`:15–19, :29–39`; `README.md:32–40`).\n\n`sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS` passed for all 23 entries; `git diff --check` passed. The new report contains no credentials or raw prompt transcript. Its hashes for source, test, flight log, and receipts are documented, but those raw files are not included, so those hashes and run details remain operator-reported rather than independently reproducible (`:29–35`).\n\nDiff SHA-256: `db79879f51989668a8b6367b78329df9584114e34abe53d0fa564eeeffd8d09f`. I did not edit files or run qualification."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18b33-8176-74a3-9ae0-b741cc1afe98","create_time":1793336851.6847591,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":23835}}
