{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T05:11:57.486Z","ordinal":517738,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a18b38-cb2e-7aa1-ae05-b9ca1c0683f4","author":"/root/pr311_draft_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/pr311_draft_review\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUIRED**\n\nGitHub confirmed PR #334’s head is still `bb335de6d943e54ff97f3fa03442dc267a91aa9b`; the actual merge base is `38a875ccfeb89f926d2bcf3cc12a37a0cbe40ff5`. Diff SHA-256: `f1b0017cd8bb0aa58d199153ba7605cabec75a974bfdfe94f4ffa427871e37ae`.\n\n- The packet manifest lists checksums for two RC11 power-loss logs that are absent at this exact head: [SHA256SUMS](/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/SHA256SUMS:66). GitHub returns 404 for those paths. The new RC11 failure claims link to the missing logs in [platform README](/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/README.md:73) and [power-loss README](/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/lifecycle/powerloss/README.md:74). Add the referenced logs with matching checksums, or remove the unsupported RC11 claims and manifest entries.\n\nThe RC10 logs and newly added scripts/docs match their recorded hashes. The RC10 failure disposition is explicit, and the fixed-CLI run is labeled a fix demonstration rather than release qualification. This was a read-only source review; I did not run tests or qualification.\n\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18b36-b9ed-7bf3-88e9-b2dec9ee7bb0","create_time":1793337117.4862332,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":23846}}
