{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T05:18:12.159Z","ordinal":518058,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18b3d-3c3f-73c2-85d3-8d368e2725dd","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-380b7c82-5e37-45b6-93e8-c320d71f5319","process_id":"55038","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","cat /home/mike/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md | sed -n '580,620p'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"cat /home/mike/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md | sed -n '580,620p'","name":"MEMORY.md","path":"/home/mike/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"# Task Group: Nexus v1 CI prerequisite integration and release qualification handoff\nscope: Integrate reviewed CI prerequisites and accurately track Nexus v1 release gates, claims, and held-out boundaries; use for `v1/integration` readiness work, not as a substitute for exact-RC qualification.\napplies_to: cwd=/home/mike/nexus-code (worktree used: /home/mike/nexus-wt/p10g-rebased); reuse_rule=recheck integration HEAD, claim ownership/staleness, exact CI, acceptance documents, and release state; recorded alpha.2 status and blockers are time-specific.\n\n## Task 1: Monitor exact-head CI/reviews and merge PR #10 without calling it a release, success for integration; partial for qualification\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-10-16T01-45-07-stRS-t5820_assessment_and_nexus_v1_release_monitoring.md (cwd=/home/mike/Projects/aihost, rollout_path=/home/mike/.codex/sessions/2026/10/16/rollout-2026-10-16T01-45-07-01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-18T01:41:41+00:00, thread_id=01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0, PR #10 integrated; qualification blocked)\n\n### keywords\n\n- Nexus v1, PR #10, bdc705e593def11ee5e44a6ebd0703b57e5953a0, CI 39085388798, v1/integration, 2c70d39ad4f9c29cff04c909eef9de6d2a29bdb2, check_requirements.mjs --enforce, REQ-QUAL-101, ACCEPTANCE.md, CONCURRENCY.md\n\n## Task 2: Record readiness status while the claim is active, success\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-10-16T01-45-07-stRS-t5820_assessment_and_nexus_v1_release_monitoring.md (cwd=/home/mike/Projects/aihost, rollout_path=/home/mike/.codex/sessions/2026/10/16/rollout-2026-10-16T01-45-07-01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-18T01:41:41+00:00, thread_id=01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0, held-out payload preserved; readiness files untouched)\n\n### keywords\n\n- FILE_docs_v1.0.0_READINESS.md, PLAN-10_READINESS_T2, nexus-claims, stale claim, 24-hour threshold, PR #9, held-out, fresh branch CI\n\n## User preferences\n\n- reviewers and the release workflow distinguish source/CI acceptance from RC/product qualification -> never call a green CI run a release. [Task 1]\n- when shared readiness/governance files are claimed, coordinate claim release or wait for the documented stale threshold; do not access held-out payloads or edit the artifact meanwhile. [Task 2]\n\n## Reusable knowledge\n\n- PR #10 exact head `bdc705e593def11ee5e44a6ebd0703b57e5953a0` passed CI run `39085388798` (contest contract, Node 20/22/24, Linux package/reproducibility) and three independent reviews accepted the code diff. It merged normally to `v1/integration` as `2c70d39ad4f9c29cff04c909eef9de6d2a29bdb2`; the candidate is an ancestor. [Task 1]\n- At handoff the version remained `0.1.0-alpha.2`; there was no RC, release tag, publication, or qualification run. `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` failed 12 rows: `REQ-AGT-002`, `REQ-AGT-010`, `REQ-PRV-003`, `REQ-REL-005`, `REQ-AGT-118`, `REQ-AGT-110`, `REQ-PRV-111`, `REQ-REL-114`, `REQ-QUAL-101`, `REQ-QUAL-107`, `REQ-QUAL-108`, `REQ-QUAL-109`. [Task 1]\n- Exact-head CI is necessary but insufficient: acceptance requires an installed exact RC, sealed held-out corpus, T2/T3/T4, provider/standalone matrices, human terminal acceptance, package/install/reproducibility checks, and owner-supplied independent RC acceptance. [Task 1]\n- `docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md` requires one worktree per slice, isolated `HOME`, claims for hot/shared files, no `pkill -f`, no concurrent gateway/full-suite runs, and owner-controlled tag/publish actions. [Task 1]\n- The readiness claims were `FILE_docs_v1.0.0_READINESS.md/owner.json` and `PLAN-10_READINESS_T2/owner.json`; at handoff the owner PID was absent but the claim was younger than 24 hours. Resume after release or the documented stale-claim procedure, update against `2c70d39`, and rerun fresh branch CI. [Task 2]\n\n## Failures and how to do differently\n\n- Symptom: GitHub merge-tool schema validation fails. Cause: `repository_full_name` was omitted. Fix: provide `repository_full_name: \"mikeholownych/nexus-code\"`. [Task 1]\n- Symptom: PR #9 readiness evidence is canceled/skipped or stale. Cause: it was based on the old integration head. Fix: acquire/release the readiness claim, refresh against current integration, then run fresh CI; never infer qualification from its prior checks. [Task 1][Task 2]\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":43839}},"started_at_ms":1793337492158,"completed_at_ms":1793337492159}}
