12.9 s.\\n- **Generic error:** the catch at eval/isolate.mjs:333 turns every cause into the same message. The causes are a spawn error, a nonzero helper exit, any helper stderr (any find stderr; scan-compiler-exposure.mjs fails on the first byte), and an lstatSync of a found path that vanished between the scan and the check.\\n- **Likely cause:** a fast failure is consistent with a find stderr or ENOENT race on a path mutated during the suite. Note /usr/local is runner-writable on hosted images.\\n- **Suggestion:** keep the refusal fail-closed, but include the cause in the problem string (timedOut/status/first stderr line/ENOENT path). Then the next occurrence names the root cause.\\n- **#341:** I re-ran its failed job once and disclosed the re-run there. The release workflow carries the same risk.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-30T04:46:42Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/335#issuecomment-6515206926\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABhFgNYQ\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"claude-code independent delta review: 1c2f6649..391f49bcddb75e63d73b232b3cdec88a17fd6f66 (eval/isolate.mjs +14/-2, eval_integrity.test.ts +24). **ACCEPT for this delta.** Earlier commits on this PR are covered by the other reviewers' ACCEPTs, not by this review.\\n- `inspectInventoryPath` ignores ENOENT only from the post-inventory lstat. That matches the existing semantics in `inspectExecutable` (isolate.mjs:270-272: stat/realpath ENOENT is no exposure).\\n- Every other lstat error still throws into the fail-closed catch.\\n- A path that no longer exists can't be bound into the sandbox, so ignoring it doesn't widen exposure.\\n- The new fixture deletes a mode-755 `go` between enumeration and inspection, and asserts both that the deletion happened and that the result is `{paths:[], problem:null}`.\\n\\nNon-blocking:\\n1. **The fix may not match the observed failure.** It covers only a disappearance after the scan. A path that disappears *during* GNU find's traversal still makes find write `No such file or directory` to stderr, and the helper still fails closed. The 430 ms failure on #341 might be that case, so the classified problem strings from 71e674bc/684fa9f4 should name the cause if it recurs. Please don't widen the stderr handling without that evidence.\\n2. **Merge order with #341.** If #341 merges first, this PR must also delete the trim step from release.yml, or `release_workflow_parity.test.ts` fails. If this PR merges first, #341 must drop its trim line. I'll rebase whichever lands second.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-30T04:56:47Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/335#issuecomment-6515330401\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true}],\"commits\":[{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-10-30T01:02:38Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"mike@holownych.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-10-30T03:56:41Z\",\"messageBody\":\"\",\"messageHeadline\":\"fix(eval): mask host SDK trees without trimming runners\",\"oid\":\"e76b3b47d8bc691f6b1ecca5f51cef5429d4fd72\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-10-30T02:23:34Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"mike@holownych.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-10-30T03:56:42Z\",\"messageBody\":\"\",\"messageHeadline\":\"fix(eval): classify compiler inventory failures\",\"oid\":\"71e674bcbf1d50363a4917ce77c60f3e8541153f\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-10-30T02:45:01Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"mike@holownych.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-10-30T03:56:43Z\",\"messageBody\":\"\",\"messageHeadline\":\"fix(eval): identify compiler helper exit failures\",\"oid\":\"df10d9d7bf99427c65dc51878c35ed9baac0ed88\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-10-30T03:02:13Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"mike@holownych.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-10-30T03:56:43Z\",\"messageBody\":\"\",\"messageHeadline\":\"fix(eval): bound expanded compiler scan roots\",\"oid\":\"19e35649ce4c01295929eeb366338c32aad6e0fe\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-10-30T03:05:33Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"mike@holownych.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-10-30T03:56:44Z\",\"messageBody\":\"\",\"messageHeadline\":\"fix(eval): report nonzero inventory helper exits\",\"oid\":\"07b07fad2e5cedd84788d0d4778e8be8de8ff1f8\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-10-30T03:56:34Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"mike@holownych.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-10-30T03:56:44Z\",\"messageBody\":\"\",\"messageHeadline\":\"fix(eval): retain safe inventory exit details\",\"oid\":\"684fa9f42c8c54a797a66c7053d9a0b627076ff6\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-10-30T04:23:09Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"mike@holownych.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-10-30T04:23:09Z\",\"messageBody\":\"\",\"messageHeadline\":\"perf(eval): batch compiler inventory roots\",\"oid\":\"1c2f6649ffdead6d7d32c7fd9b1c57ee735a17b4\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-10-30T04:53:41Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"mike@holownych.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-10-30T04:53:41Z\",\"messageBody\":\"\",\"messageHeadline\":\"fix(eval): ignore compiler paths removed after inventory\",\"oid\":\"391f49bcddb75e63d73b232b3cdec88a17fd6f66\"}],\"reviews\":[]}\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"### 2\nWarning: truncated output (original token count: 3506)\nTotal output lines: 1\n\n{\"comments\":[{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABhFIz-g\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"coderabbitai\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"NONE\",\"body\":\"<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\\n\\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai -->\\n\\n> [!IMPORTANT]\\n> - [ ] <!-- {\\\"checkboxId\\\":\\\"e9bb8d72-00e8-4f67-9cb2-caf3b22574fe\\\"} --> 🔍 Trigger review\\n> \\n> This repository does not receive automatic reviews because it has fewer than 10 stars.\\n> \\n> <details>\\n> <summary><strong><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/cog-dark.svg\\\"><img src=\\\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/cog.svg\\\" width=\\\"16\\\" height=\\\"16\\\" align=\\\"absmiddle\\\" alt=\\\"\\\"></picture> Run configuration</strong></summary>\\n> <dl>\\n> <dd>\\n> \\n> - **Source mode**: Auto\\n> - **Repository**: Unavailable\\n> - **Branch**: Unavailable\\n> - **File**: No configuration file from this repository applied\\n> - **Commit**: Unavailable\\n> - **Layers**: defaults\\n> - **Review profile**: CHILL\\n> - **Plan**: Advanced\\n> - **Run ID**: `cfd3cd76-77b2-47c1-b29b-9161cfcffa28`\\n> \\n> </dd>\\n> </dl>\\n> </details>\\n\\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai -->\\n\\n<!-- autopilot:start -->\\n- [ ] <!-- {\\\"checkboxId\\\":\\\"2708ad07-9f24-4260-9c11-7dc76a49f2e3\\\"} --> <strong title=\\\"Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\\\">Autofix</strong> · Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\\n<!-- autopilot:end -->\\n<!-- tips_start -->\\n\\n\\n\\nThanks for using [CodeRabbit](https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=oss&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=mikeholownych/nexus-code&utm_content=341)! It's free for OSS, and your support helps us grow. If you like it, consider giving us a shout-out.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary><strong>❤️ Share</strong></summary>\\n<dl>\\n<dd>\\n\\n- [X](https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A&url=https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\\n- [Mastodon](https://mastodon.social/share?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai)\\n- [Reddit](https://www.reddit.com/submit?title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit&text=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\\n- [LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/sharing/share-offsite/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai&mini=true&title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit&summary=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code)\\n\\n</dd>\\n</dl>\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands.</sub>\\n\\n<!-- tips_end -->\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-30T04:25:21Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":true,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/341#issuecomment-6514947066\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":false},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABhFJ0dg\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Coordination note from PR #335: its exact-head source review now ACCEPTs the bounded 64-root/64-KiB compiler inventory batching, but its Node22/Node24 CI is still running. PR #341 adds setup-go, pinned evaluator toolchains, runner-trim parity, and the parity test; its current trim step must remain consistent with PR #335’s final CI/release workflow shape. Please coordinate merge/rebase order against the exact main head before merging either workflow change. No tag or release publication is being performed here.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-30T04:26:41Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/341#issuecomment-6514963574\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABhFJ4oQ\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Independent review (fresh-context read-only reviewer subagent, not the author) of head 534e21b7e5292a2f85ae1e3586e6051652e87ce6: **ACCEPT**. There are 0 blocking findings.\\n- Step order matches both ci.yml jobs.\\n- The trim removes nothing that release.yml uses later.\\n- install-evaluator-toolchains.sh assumes nothing that differs from CI.\\n- The parity test passes on head and fails on base.\\n- sync-version --check and requirements --enforce both pass; the rc.13 notes file is present.\\n- No product code changed since the rc.12 tag.\\n\\nNon-blocking findings:\\n1. The notes asserted a scan 'timeout' that the log doesn't show. Fixed in 420aa7e1 by quoting the logged message; this is pending the reviewer's delta confirmation.\\n2. The provider_robustness timing failure (test 634) could recur on the release run.\\n3. The parity test is a substring check and doesn't enforce step order.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-30T04:26:46Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/341#issuecomment-6514964641\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABhFKJkA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Independent delta review (the same fresh-context, read-only reviewer) of head 420aa7e1a6d42480c0ec0d3b9bbec21066c27d60: **ACCEPT**. The diff from 534e21b7 …506 tokens truncated…d its parity test will fail. Please rebase/update #341 to match the current mask-only CI setup, then rerun exact-head tests and request a fresh review. The prior ACCEPT reviewed #341 before this cross-PR integration conflict was identified; it does not clear this blocker.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-30T04:28:09Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/341#issuecomment-6514981520\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABhFLCIA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Clarification to my previous comment: the exact obsolete command is `bash scripts/ci-trim-runner-image.sh`. My shell quoting removed the literal from the earlier comment. PR #335 deletes this script and its two CI invocations, so #341 must remove the release invocation and align its parity test with the mask-only setup before merge.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-30T04:28:18Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/341#issuecomment-6514983456\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABhFMRgA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Follow-up with merge-tree evidence: I computed a clean synthetic merge of current PR #335 head `1c2f6649ffdead6d7d32c7fd9b1c57ee735a17b4` and PR #341 head `420aa7e1a6d42480c0ec0d3b9bbec21066c27d60`, both based on `38a875ccfeb89f926d2bcf3cc12a37a0cbe40ff5`. The resulting tree is `b308db0ca827e56b812ec41296a2588239a4ac03`. In that merged tree, release.yml invokes `bash scripts/ci-trim-runner-image.sh`, the script is absent, and the parity test still asserts that CI has that invocation. This confirms a clean-merge integration defect. Please update #341 against the current evaluator setup and rerun exact-head checks/review.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-30T04:29:59Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/341#issuecomment-6515003776\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABhFYgMw\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Exact-head CI update for PR #341 head `420aa7e1a6d42480c0ec0d3b9bbec21066c27d60`: Node 22 passed; Node 24 failed only at `test/eval_t3.test.ts:246` because the synthetic T3 run refused to qualify with `compiler exposure could not be checked; refusing qualification`. PR #335's scanner candidate at `1c2f6649` has now passed both Node 22 and Node 24. This confirms PR #341 needs to be rebased/updated after #335 integration, in addition to removing the retired runner-trim command and strengthening the parity assertions. The existing release-workflow review blocker still applies; no merge or RC tag should proceed until the updated exact head has independent review and all exact-head checks pass.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-30T04:46:29Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":true,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/341#issuecomment-6515204147\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABhFYr8w\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"test-matrix (24) at 420aa7e1 failed one test: eval_t3.test.ts:246, after 430 ms, with `compiler exposure could not be checked; refusing qualification`. That is the same qualification-tooling flake that hit main at f7a394f5. #341 doesn't touch the evaluator or its tests. I re-ran the failed job once; merge still requires every exact-head check to be completed/success. Diagnosis posted on #335.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-30T04:46:43Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/341#issuecomment-6515207155\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true}],\"commits\":[{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-10-30T04:23:56Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"mike@holownych.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Opus 5.5\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-10-30T04:23:56Z\",\"messageBody\":\"The v1.0.0-rc.12 release run failed in npm --prefix cli test: release.yml\\nhad no setup-go, pinned evaluator toolchain install, or hosted-runner SDK\\ntrim, so evaluator tests hit 'go: command not found' and the compiler\\nexposure scan timed out. Add the three steps in ci.yml's order and a test\\nthat fails when the two workflows disagree on evaluator setup.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"ci(release): prepare the evaluator environment CI uses before the suite\",\"oid\":\"90fd7412a7430d0fe4298c645f782aa948575679\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-10-30T04:24:35Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"mike@holownych.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Opus 5.5\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-10-30T04:24:35Z\",\"messageBody\":\"RC12 was tagged but its release workflow failed before publishing, so\\ncut RC13 from the fixed workflow instead of moving the pushed RC12 tag.\\nNo product code changed since the RC12 tag.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"release: cut the 1.0.0-rc.13 candidate\",\"oid\":\"534e21b7e5292a2f85ae1e3586e6051652e87ce6\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-10-30T04:26:31Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"mike@holownych.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Opus 5.5\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-10-30T04:26:31Z\",\"messageBody\":\"Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"docs(release): quote the RC12 compiler-exposure failure as logged\",\"oid\":\"420aa7e1a6d42480c0ec0d3b9bbec21066c27d60\"}],\"reviews\":[]}\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"### 3\n{\"comments\":[{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABhCYj5w\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"coderabbitai\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"NONE\",\"body\":\"<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\\n\\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai -->\\n\\n> [!IMPORTANT]\\n> - [ ] <!-- {\\\"checkboxId\\\":\\\"e9bb8d72-00e8-4f67-9cb2-caf3b22574fe\\\"} --> 🔍 Trigger review\\n> \\n> This repository does not receive automatic reviews because it has fewer than 10 stars.\\n> \\n> <details>\\n> <summary><strong><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/cog-dark.svg\\\"><img src=\\\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/cog.svg\\\" width=\\\"16\\\" height=\\\"16\\\" align=\\\"absmiddle\\\" alt=\\\"\\\"></picture> Run configuration</strong></summary>\\n> <dl>\\n> <dd>\\n> \\n> - **Source mode**: Auto\\n> - **Repository**: Unavailable\\n> - **Branch**: Unavailable\\n> - **File**: No configuration file from this repository applied\\n> - **Commit**: Unavailable\\n> - **Layers**: defaults\\n> - **Review profile**: CHILL\\n> - **Plan**: Advanced\\n> - **Run ID**: `409a3fb5-ea24-42a8-852a-5be8cdbc0667`\\n> \\n> </dd>\\n> </dl>\\n> </details>\\n\\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai -->\\n\\n<!-- autopilot:start -->\\n- [ ] <!-- {\\\"checkboxId\\\":\\\"2708ad07-9f24-4260-9c11-7dc76a49f2e3\\\"} --> <strong title=\\\"Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\\\">Autofix</strong> · Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\\n<!-- autopilot:end -->\\n<!-- tips_start -->\\n\\n\\n\\nThanks for using [CodeRabbit](https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=oss&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=mikeholownych/nexus-code&utm_content=334)! It's free for OSS, and your support helps us grow. If you like it, consider giving us a shout-out.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary><strong>❤️ Share</strong></summary>\\n<dl>\\n<dd>\\n\\n- [X](https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A&url=https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\\n- [Mastodon](https://mastodon.social/share?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai)\\n- [Reddit](https://www.reddit.com/submit?title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit&text=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\\n- [LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/sharing/share-offsite/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai&mini=true&title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit&summary=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code)\\n\\n</dd>\\n</dl>\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands.</sub>\\n\\n<!-- tips_end -->\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-30T00:43:34Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":true,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/334#issuecomment-6512059367\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":false},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABhFMbsQ\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"CI triage for exact head ee1d8f33d1f9b5dbbee4b0f67d6f7832d2fae6ba: Node24’s npm test failure is the existing evaluator fixture `resource contract: candidate memory, processes, storage and CPU are kernel-bounded and every process is reaped`, which exits at `eval/isolate.mjs:551` because compiler exposure could not be checked. It is unrelated to the E2 evidence files, but it means this PR is not green. PR #335 carries the separately reviewed root-batching fix for that scanner path and is still running exact CI. After #335 is integrated, this evidence PR needs a fresh exact-head run; do not treat this current failure as passing evidence or merge on it.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-30T04:30:12Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/334#issuecomment-6515006385\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true}],\"commits\":[{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-10-30T00:43:15Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"mike@holownych.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-10-30T04:08:32Z\",\"messageBody\":\"Add the QEMU/KVM power-loss harness and its logs, and record the result\\nhonestly: the published RC10 artifact does not survive a power cut during an\\nupgrade.\\n\\nThe cell builds an ext4 image with rc.9 installed, starts the upgrade to rc.10,\\nand SIGKILLs the VM when the durable journal reaches `switched` (package in\\nplace, launcher switched, runtime unverified). Nothing is synced first and the\\nimage is mounted cache=none, so dirty page cache is lost as in a real power cut.\\n\\nOn RC10 the extracted package's data never reached the disk: after reboot\\n`v1.0.0-rc.10/bin/nexus` is 0 bytes, `nexus --version` prints nothing, and\\n`nexus upgrade --recover` cannot start because the launcher is the broken one.\\nThe installation cannot repair itself. Root cause: safeExtractTar never fsynced\\nthe extracted tree before the rename and launcher switch (fixed in PR #333).\\n\\nWith a CLI containing the fix the same cut leaves a working launcher, recovery\\nrolls back to rc.9, staging is removed, the stale lock is reclaimed, a second\\nrecovery is a no-op, and the retry completes to rc.10. That demonstrates the\\nfix; it is not qualification, and the cell stays failed for RC10.\\n\\nREADME row and section updated; 65 manifest entries verify.\",\"messageHeadline\":\"evidence(e2): record the power-loss durability cell, which fails on RC10\",\"oid\":\"d65153aeeb93d9369a7965198cca94a3b6bc70d9\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-10-30T00:59:20Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"mike@holownych.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-10-30T04:08:33Z\",\"messageBody\":\"Address review findings on the power-loss cell:\\n\\n- The BASELINE_CLI_DIST marker was written before `boot` truncated the log, so\\n  it never survived. Pass the dist digest on the kernel command line and have\\n  the guest print it, so the fixed-CLI run identifies itself in its own log.\\n- Add `NEXUS_POWERLOSS_LOG_SUFFIX` so the fixed demonstration writes its\\n  `-fixed-cli` logs directly instead of requiring a manual rename.\\n- Print the `bin/nexus` size for each package, list the package directory after\\n  recovery, and record `RECOVER_RC`. A 0-byte launcher is an empty shell script,\\n  so RC10's recovery exits 0 while doing nothing; the README now says that\\n  instead of \\\"cannot run\\\", which hides the hazard.\\n- Strip serial CR bytes and trailing padding on copy, so the committed logs\\n  produce clean diffs.\\n- Document the real prerequisites (root/sudo for loop mounts, mkfs.ext4, cpio,\\n  qemu-img, gzip, ldd).\\n\\nRe-ran both cells: RC10 still fails with `payload v1.0.0-rc.10: 0 bytes`,\\n`NEXUS=` empty and `RECOVER_RC=0`; the fixed CLI (dist sha256 08f3970b…) still\\nrecovers to rc.9 and completes the retry. 65 manifest entries verify.\",\"messageHeadline\":\"docs(e2): make the power-loss evidence self-identifying\",\"oid\":\"bbee4f8c89d847ae61dcf71d20cfb6b1a8c82b72\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-10-30T01:09:27Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"mike@holownych.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-10-30T04:08:33Z\",\"messageBody\":\"The fix demonstration recorded sha256 of `cli/dist/index.js`, but the fix lives\\nin `durable_tree.js`, which `index.js` imports dynamically. Record the SHA-256 of\\nthe dist's sorted file manifest instead, so the marker covers every module that\\nran.\\n\\nRe-ran both cells: RC10 still shows `payload v1.0.0-rc.10: 0 bytes` and\\n`RECOVER_RC=0`; the fixed CLI (manifest sha256 recorded in the log) still rolls\\nback to rc.9 and completes the retry. 65 manifest entries verify.\",\"messageHeadline\":\"docs(e2): pin the whole patched dist, not just its entry point\",\"oid\":\"ee1d8f33d1f9b5dbbee4b0f67d6f7832d2fae6ba\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-10-30T04:38:59Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"mike@holownych.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-10-30T04:38:59Z\",\"messageBody\":\"… too\\n\\nThe owner tagged v1.0.0-rc.11 at 8d4e5319, before the fsync fix landed, so RC11\\ncarries the same defect as RC10. Run the cell for rc.10 -> rc.11: the cut at\\n`switched` leaves `v1.0.0-rc.11/bin/nexus` at 0 bytes, `nexus --version` empty,\\nand `nexus upgrade --recover` exiting 0 without doing anything.\\n\\nParameterize the harness by base/target tag and archive digest so the same\\nscripts cover both transitions (rc.9 -> rc.10 and rc.10 -> rc.11), and record\\nthe RC11 row and log. 67 manifest entries verify.\",\"messageHeadline\":\"evidence(e2): the published RC11 artifact fails power-loss durability…\",\"oid\":\"bb335de6d943e54ff97f3fa03442dc267a91aa9b\"}],\"reviews\":[]}\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18b3d-3c3f-73c2-85d3-8d368e2725dd","create_time":1793337518.708538}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
