{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T05:18:58.272Z","ordinal":518135,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a18b3f-36e0-72d0-9005-140229215aa9","author":"/root/pr311_draft_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/pr311_draft_review\nPayload:\nPR #334 remains at exact head `bb335de6d943e54ff97f3fa03442dc267a91aa9b`; its GitHub-reported merge base remains `38a875ccfeb89f926d2bcf3cc12a37a0cbe40ff5`. The PR diff SHA-256 is still `f1b0017cd8bb0aa58d199153ba7605cabec75a974bfdfe94f4ffa427871e37ae`.\n\nThe RC11 evidence gap is unchanged:\n\n- [SHA256SUMS](/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/SHA256SUMS:66) lists the RC11 write and verify log hashes, but both paths return 404 at this head and neither appears in the PR’s changed-file list.\n- [platform README](/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/README.md:73) and [power-loss README](/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/lifecycle/powerloss/README.md:74) still claim RC11 failed and refer to the missing logs.\n- The PR body says “`SHA256SUMS` has 65 entries and verifies,” while the file has 67 entries, including those two missing paths. The only recent PR comment is CI triage; it does not address this evidence gap.\n\n**Disposition: CHANGES_REQUIRED.** The logs were not restored and the claims were not corrected, so the previous blocker remains. This refresh was read-only; no tests or qualification were run."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18b3d-3c3f-73c2-85d3-8d368e2725dd","create_time":1793337538.2726078,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":23867}}
