{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T05:27:40.525Z","ordinal":518490,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18b3d-3c3f-73c2-85d3-8d368e2725dd","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae42ac8d5b4819f9cf77eb9331843f6","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"## Checkpoint\n\n**Campaign:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`  \n**Acceptance:** `IN_PROGRESS`\n\n- `origin/main` is still `38a875ccfeb89f926d2bcf3cc12a37a0cbe40ff5`. The shared checkout remains dirty and untouched.\n- I rebased the PR #341 work onto PR #335’s exact head `391f49bcddb75e63d73b232b3cdec88a17fd6f66`. The corrected release workflow removes the retired runner-trim step, and the parity test checks that it is absent. The candidate is local commit `b2b9ac825c2e3d5a4961d91f020b2a0d1c1f7e45`; its [release workflow](/home/mike/nexus-wt/pr341-release-workflow-fix/.github/workflows/release.yml:27) and [parity test](/home/mike/nexus-wt/pr341-release-workflow-fix/cli/test/release_workflow_parity.test.ts:37) received an independent **ACCEPT**.\n- The focused parity test passed 1/1; syntax, diff, version-sync, and requirements checks passed. The requirements report is 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, and 7 open. The corrected PR #341 candidate still needs an exact-head CI run after PR #335 clears.\n- PR #335 has passing Node 22, Node 24, CodeQL, and JavaScript/TypeScript checks. Its Linux packaging job is still running the CLI suite; Entire Gates is also pending. PR #341’s original remote head has its Linux job and Entire Gates pending.\n- PR #334 remains blocked: its RC11 power-loss logs are listed in the manifest and cited in documentation, but absent from its exact head. Independent review remains **CHANGES_REQUIRED**. No logs were fabricated.\n- GitHub’s latest published release is still RC11. RC12 is tagged but has no published release; no accepted RC or stable v1.0.0 is verified.\n\nThe next executable step is to finish PR #335’s exact-head gates, then rebase/update and run exact-head checks for PR #341. The existing evidence and requirements distinctions remain in force: green source checks do not establish installed-RC or release acceptance. No new operator action is needed at this checkpoint.\n\n"}],"phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":{"entries":[{"path":"MEMORY.md","lineStart":580,"lineEnd":620,"note":"release convergence context and distinction between source CI and RC acceptance"}],"rolloutIds":["01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0"]}},"started_at_ms":1793338056846,"completed_at_ms":1793338060525}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T05:27:40.535Z","ordinal":518491,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","status":"completed","id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae42ac8d5b4819f9cf77eb9331843f6","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"## Checkpoint\n\n**Campaign:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`  \n**Acceptance:** `IN_PROGRESS`\n\n- `origin/main` is still `38a875ccfeb89f926d2bcf3cc12a37a0cbe40ff5`. The shared checkout remains dirty and untouched.\n- I rebased the PR #341 work onto PR #335’s exact head `391f49bcddb75e63d73b232b3cdec88a17fd6f66`. The corrected release workflow removes the retired runner-trim step, and the parity test checks that it is absent. The candidate is local commit `b2b9ac825c2e3d5a4961d91f020b2a0d1c1f7e45`; its [release workflow](/home/mike/nexus-wt/pr341-release-workflow-fix/.github/workflows/release.yml:27) and [parity test](/home/mike/nexus-wt/pr341-release-workflow-fix/cli/test/release_workflow_parity.test.ts:37) received an independent **ACCEPT**.\n- The focused parity test passed 1/1; syntax, diff, version-sync, and requirements checks passed. The requirements report is 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, and 7 open. The corrected PR #341 candidate still needs an exact-head CI run after PR #335 clears.\n- PR #335 has passing Node 22, Node 24, CodeQL, and JavaScript/TypeScript checks. Its Linux packaging job is still running the CLI suite; Entire Gates is also pending. PR #341’s original remote head has its Linux job and Entire Gates pending.\n- PR #334 remains blocked: its RC11 power-loss logs are listed in the manifest and cited in documentation, but absent from its exact head. Independent review remains **CHANGES_REQUIRED**. No logs were fabricated.\n- GitHub’s latest published release is still RC11. RC12 is tagged but has no published release; no accepted RC or stable v1.0.0 is verified.\n\nThe next executable step is to finish PR #335’s exact-head gates, then rebase/update and run exact-head checks for PR #341. The existing evidence and requirements distinctions remain in force: green source checks do not establish installed-RC or release acceptance. No new operator action is needed at this checkpoint.\n\n<oai-mem-citation>\n<citation_entries>\nMEMORY.md:580-620|note=[release convergence context and distinction between source CI and RC acceptance]\n</citation_entries>\n<rollout_ids>\n01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0\n</rollout_ids>\n</oai-mem-citation>","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"final_answer","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18b3d-3c3f-73c2-85d3-8d368e2725dd","create_time":1793338056.83614,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae42ac8d5b4819f9cf77eb9331843f6","turn_id":"01a18b3d-3c3f-73c2-85d3-8d368e2725dd","role":"assistant"},"revision":"retained_01a18b47-2ef6-7fe0-a7f4-e199a4e762a2","complete":true},"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":23880}}
