{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T05:29:30.244Z","ordinal":518579,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18b47-a54b-7cb0-a56a-8243423701cb","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-99c746a0-2274-45fe-b1ae-accf761cee0d","process_id":"31034","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git grep -n -i 'rc.11\\|rc.12\\|67 entries\\|rc11' origin/pr/334 -- docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/README.md docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/SHA256SUMS docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/lifecycle/powerloss/README.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"git grep -n -i \"rc.11\\\\|rc.12\\\\|67 entries\\\\|rc11\" origin/pr/334 -- docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/README.md docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/SHA256SUMS docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/lifecycle/powerloss/README.md","query":"rc.11\\|rc.12\\|67 entries\\|rc11","path":"334"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"origin/pr/334:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/README.md:58:| Power-loss durability (RC11) | **FAIL on the published RC11 artifact** (tag `8d4e5319`, which predates the fix). The same cut during rc.10 → rc.11 leaves `v1.0.0-rc.11/bin/nexus` at 0 bytes, `nexus --version` empty, and `nexus upgrade --recover` exiting 0 without doing anything. Any release built before #333 carries this defect | [log](ubuntu-22-04-node22-power-loss-durability-rc11-verify.log) |\norigin/pr/334:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/README.md:73:On the published RC10 artifact the cell **fails**: the extracted package's file data was never fsynced, so the rename and launcher switch survived while the payload did not. `v1.0.0-rc.10/bin/nexus` is 0 bytes, `nexus --version` prints nothing, and `nexus upgrade --recover` exits 0 without doing anything, because a 0-byte launcher is an empty shell script. The upgrade is performed by the installed rc.9 CLI, and the missing flush is in that running CLI. The published RC11 artifact (tag `8d4e5319`) reproduces the same failure for rc.10 → rc.11, because the tag predates the fix.\norigin/pr/334:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/README.md:94:- This covers the fresh-install / doctor / Node-preflight matrix plus the lifecycle cells (Ubuntu 22.04, Debian 12, Fedora 40 / Node 22) for E2 (ACC-PLAT) on RC10: install, installer-driven version switch and rollback, reinstall, repair and uninstall; checksum tamper; broken-candidate self-test; backup restore; updater process-crash recovery with staging cleanup; incompatible downgrade from a synthetic state-schema-1 release; synthetic-journal recovery from early transaction states and a malformed journal; and provenance-attestation verification. An ordinary successful `nexus upgrade` from alpha.2 is not executable because alpha.2 has no updater command; the alpha.2 row is installer-driven. Power-loss durability is now tested rather than assumed, and it **fails on both RC10 and RC11** (RC11 predates the fix): see the rows and section below.\norigin/pr/334:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/SHA256SUMS:66:b0afaa282f96f2c8d78421ed393cc8f7024a5f3d61989904473f409b481ddb21  ubuntu-22-04-node22-power-loss-durability-rc11-write.log\norigin/pr/334:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/SHA256SUMS:67:69a96131328e9fb0c20761d356bdc847496b758b7c881f130405a6dae0f54786  ubuntu-22-04-node22-power-loss-durability-rc11-verify.log\norigin/pr/334:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/lifecycle/powerloss/README.md:69:## Result on the published RC11 artifact: FAIL\norigin/pr/334:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/lifecycle/powerloss/README.md:71:`v1.0.0-rc.11` (tag `8d4e5319`) predates the fix, so rc.10 → rc.11 reproduces the\norigin/pr/334:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/lifecycle/powerloss/README.md:72:same failure: `v1.0.0-rc.11/bin/nexus` is 0 bytes, `nexus --version` is empty, and\norigin/pr/334:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/lifecycle/powerloss/README.md:74:(`...-power-loss-durability-rc11-verify.log`). Any release built before #333\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":28933}},"started_at_ms":1793338170243,"completed_at_ms":1793338170244}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T05:29:30.486Z","ordinal":518580,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18b48-dc76-74b0-a556-4047374aeb75","call_id":"call_4363c4392f57497db9be2d420e0dd7a0","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.6 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"origin/pr/334:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/README.md:58:| Power-loss durability (RC11) | **FAIL on the published RC11 artifact** (tag `8d4e5319`, which predates the fix). The same cut during rc.10 → rc.11 leaves `v1.0.0-rc.11/bin/nexus` at 0 bytes, `nexus --version` empty, and `nexus upgrade --recover` exiting 0 without doing anything. Any release built before #333 carries this defect | [log](ubuntu-22-04-node22-power-loss-durability-rc11-verify.log) |\norigin/pr/334:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/README.md:73:On the published RC10 artifact the cell **fails**: the extracted package's file data was never fsynced, so the rename and launcher switch survived while the payload did not. `v1.0.0-rc.10/bin/nexus` is 0 bytes, `nexus --version` prints nothing, and `nexus upgrade --recover` exits 0 without doing anything, because a 0-byte launcher is an empty shell script. The upgrade is performed by the installed rc.9 CLI, and the missing flush is in that running CLI. The published RC11 artifact (tag `8d4e5319`) reproduces the same failure for rc.10 → rc.11, because the tag predates the fix.\norigin/pr/334:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/README.md:94:- This covers the fresh-install / doctor / Node-preflight matrix plus the lifecycle cells (Ubuntu 22.04, Debian 12, Fedora 40 / Node 22) for E2 (ACC-PLAT) on RC10: install, installer-driven version switch and rollback, reinstall, repair and uninstall; checksum tamper; broken-candidate self-test; backup restore; updater process-crash recovery with staging cleanup; incompatible downgrade from a synthetic state-schema-1 release; synthetic-journal recovery from early transaction states and a malformed journal; and provenance-attestation verification. An ordinary successful `nexus upgrade` from alpha.2 is not executable because alpha.2 has no updater command; the alpha.2 row is installer-driven. Power-loss durability is now tested rather than assumed, and it **fails on both RC10 and RC11** (RC11 predates the fix): see the rows and section below.\norigin/pr/334:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/SHA256SUMS:66:b0afaa282f96f2c8d78421ed393cc8f7024a5f3d61989904473f409b481ddb21  ubuntu-22-04-node22-power-loss-durability-rc11-write.log\norigin/pr/334:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/SHA256SUMS:67:69a96131328e9fb0c20761d356bdc847496b758b7c881f130405a6dae0f54786  ubuntu-22-04-node22-power-loss-durability-rc11-verify.log\norigin/pr/334:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/lifecycle/powerloss/README.md:69:## Result on the published RC11 artifact: FAIL\norigin/pr/334:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/lifecycle/powerloss/README.md:71:`v1.0.0-rc.11` (tag `8d4e5319`) predates the fix, so rc.10 → rc.11 reproduces the\norigin/pr/334:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/lifecycle/powerloss/README.md:72:same failure: `v1.0.0-rc.11/bin/nexus` is 0 bytes, `nexus --version` is empty, and\norigin/pr/334:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/lifecycle/powerloss/README.md:74:(`...-power-loss-durability-rc11-verify.log`). Any release built before #333\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18b47-a54b-7cb0-a56a-8243423701cb","create_time":1793338170.486704}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
