{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T05:29:46.124Z","ordinal":518600,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18b47-a54b-7cb0-a56a-8243423701cb","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae42b496760819f92429c6f3275b62c","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The live Entire check explains the remaining review gate: PR #335’s trail reports no reviewer approval, with CI still running; PR #341’s trail also has no reviewer approval. Separately, I found an actionable evidence correction on PR #334: the RC11 logs are absent, so its RC11 failure claim cannot stay in an evidence package. I’m preparing a documentation-only correction in a fresh worktree, preserving the existing dirty worktree."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1793338185415,"completed_at_ms":1793338186124}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T05:29:46.128Z","ordinal":518601,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","status":"completed","id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae42b496760819f92429c6f3275b62c","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The live Entire check explains the remaining review gate: PR #335’s trail reports no reviewer approval, with CI still running; PR #341’s trail also has no reviewer approval. Separately, I found an actionable evidence correction on PR #334: the RC11 logs are absent, so its RC11 failure claim cannot stay in an evidence package. I’m preparing a documentation-only correction in a fresh worktree, preserving the existing dirty worktree.","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18b47-a54b-7cb0-a56a-8243423701cb","create_time":1793338185.4051101,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae42b496760819f92429c6f3275b62c","turn_id":"01a18b47-a54b-7cb0-a56a-8243423701cb","role":"assistant"},"revision":"retained_01a18b49-198f-7751-bd30-a969b366f935","complete":true},"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":23884}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T05:29:52.512Z","ordinal":518602,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0db389702a7164cc016ae42b4a1c94819fa912daa3890900ec","status":"completed","call_id":"call_524d18766d754260b3541c7d9cd460e4","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/pr334-evidence-correction/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/README.md\\n@@\\n-| Power-loss durability (RC11) | **FAIL on the published RC11 artifact** (tag `8d4e5319`, which predates the fix). The same cut during rc.10 → rc.11 leaves `v1.0.0-rc.11/bin/nexus` at 0 bytes, `nexus --version` empty, and `nexus upgrade --recover` exiting 0 without doing anything. Any release built before #333 carries this defect | [log](ubuntu-22-04-node22-power-loss-durability-rc11-verify.log) |\\n+| Power-loss durability (RC11) | **NOT VERIFIED in this evidence package.** A prior draft named RC11 write/verify logs, but those files are absent here; no RC11 result is asserted | — |\\n@@\\n-On the published RC10 artifact the cell **fails**: the extracted package's file data was never fsynced before the rename and launcher switch. `v1.0.0-rc.10/bin/nexus` is 0 bytes, `nexus --version` prints nothing, and `nexus upgrade --recover` exits 0 without doing anything, because a 0-byte launcher is an empty shell script. The upgrade is performed by the installed rc.9 CLI, and the missing flush is in that running CLI. The published RC11 artifact (tag `8d4e5319`) reproduces the same failure for rc.10 → rc.11, because the tag predates the fix.\\n+On the published RC10 artifact the cell **fails**: the extracted package's file data was never fsynced before the rename and launcher switch. `v1.0.0-rc.10/bin/nexus` is 0 bytes, `nexus --version` prints nothing, and `nexus upgrade --recover` exits 0 without doing anything, because a 0-byte launcher is an empty shell script. The upgrade is performed by the installed rc.9 CLI, and the missing flush is in that running CLI. No RC11 result is asserted in this evidence package because the two log artifacts named by the prior draft are absent.\\n@@\\n-- This covers the fresh-install / doctor / Node-preflight matrix plus the lifecycle cells (Ubuntu 22.04, Debian 12, Fedora 40 / Node 22) for E2 (ACC-PLAT) on RC10: install, installer-driven version switch and rollback, reinstall, repair and uninstall; checksum tamper; broken-candidate self-test; backup restore; updater process-crash recovery with staging cleanup; incompatible downgrade from a synthetic state-schema-1 release; synthetic-journal recovery from early transaction states and a malformed journal; and provenance-attestation verification. An ordinary successful `nexus upgrade` from alpha.2 is not executable because alpha.2 has no updater command; the alpha.2 row is installer-driven. Power-loss durability is now tested rather than assumed, and it **fails on both RC10 and RC11** (RC11 predates the fix): see the rows and section below.\\n+- This covers the fresh-install / doctor / Node-preflight matrix plus the lifecycle cells (Ubuntu 22.04, Debian 12, Fedora 40 / Node 22) for E2 (ACC-PLAT) on RC10: install, installer-driven version switch and rollback, reinstall, repair and uninstall; checksum tamper; broken-candidate self-test; backup restore; updater process-crash recovery with staging cleanup; incompatible downgrade from a synthetic state-schema-1 release; synthetic-journal recovery from early transaction states and a malformed journal; and provenance-attestation verification. An ordinary successful `nexus upgrade` from alpha.2 is not executable because alpha.2 has no updater command; the alpha.2 row is installer-driven. Power-loss durability is tested rather than assumed and **fails on RC10**; the RC11 result is not verified in this evidence package because its log artifacts are absent.\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/pr334-evidence-correction/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/lifecycle/powerloss/README.md\\n@@\\n-## Result on the published RC11 artifact: FAIL\\n-\\n-`v1.0.0-rc.11` (tag `8d4e5319`) predates the fix, so rc.10 → rc.11 reproduces the\\n-same failure: `v1.0.0-rc.11/bin/nexus` is 0 bytes, `nexus --version` is empty, and\\n-`nexus upgrade --recover` exits 0 without doing anything\\n-(`...-power-loss-durability-rc11-verify.log`). Any release built before #333\\n-carries the defect.\\n+## RC11 disposition: not verified in this evidence package\\n+\\n+A prior draft named RC11 write and verify logs, but those log files are absent\\n+from this evidence package. This package therefore makes no RC11 pass or failure\\n+claim. The RC10 failure and fixed-CLI demonstration below are supported by their\\n+included logs and remain distinct from RC11 qualification.\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/pr334-evidence-correction/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/SHA256SUMS\\n@@\\n-b0afaa282f96f2c8d78421ed393cc8f7024a5f3d61989904473f409b481ddb21  ubuntu-22-04-node22-power-loss-durability-rc11-write.log\\n-69a96131328e9fb0c20761d356bdc847496b758b7c881f130405a6dae0f54786  ubuntu-22-04-node22-power-loss-durability-rc11-verify.log\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18b47-a54b-7cb0-a56a-8243423701cb","create_time":1793338186.1128185}}}
