-e2-matrix.sh: OK\nrun-rc10-lifecycle.sh: OK\nlifecycle/backup-restore-run.sh: OK\nlifecycle/prepare-lifecycle-fixtures.sh: OK\nlifecycle/process-crash-server.js: OK\nlifecycle/run-checksum-tamper.sh: OK\nlifecycle/run-process-crash-recovery.sh: OK\nlifecycle/run-self-test-failure.sh: OK\nlifecycle/static-fixture-server.js: OK\nREADME.md: OK\nattestation-rc10.log: OK\nlifecycle/debian-12-node22-lifecycle.log: OK\nlifecycle/debian-12-node22-lifecycle.sh: OK\nlifecycle/fedora-40-node22-lifecycle.log: OK\nlifecycle/fedora-40-node22-lifecycle.sh: OK\nlifecycle/prepare-incompatible-fixture.sh: OK\nlifecycle/incompatible-server.js: OK\nlifecycle/run-incompatible-downgrade.sh: OK\nlifecycle/ubuntu-22-04-node22-incompatible-downgrade.log: OK\nlifecycle/run-synthetic-journal-recovery.sh: OK\nubuntu-22-04-node22-synthetic-journal-recovery.log: OK\nlifecycle/powerloss/README.md: OK\nlifecycle/powerloss/fetch-assets.sh: OK\nlifecycle/powerloss/guest-init: OK\nlifecycle/powerloss/run-power-loss-durability.sh: OK\nlifecycle/powerloss/serve-release.cjs: OK\nubuntu-22-04-node22-power-loss-durability-write.log: OK\nubuntu-22-04-node22-power-loss-durability-verify.log: OK\nubuntu-22-04-node22-power-loss-durability-fixed-cli-write.log: OK\nubuntu-22-04-node22-power-loss-durability-fixed-cli-verify.log: OK\nlifecycle/powerloss/README.md:69:## RC11 disposition: not verified in this evidence package\nlifecycle/powerloss/README.md:71:A prior draft named RC11 write and verify logs, but those log files are absent\nlifecycle/powerloss/README.md:72:from this evidence package. This package therefore makes no RC11 pass or failure\nlifecycle/powerloss/README.md:74:included logs and remain distinct from RC11 qualification.\nREADME.md:58:| Power-loss durability (RC11) | **NOT VERIFIED in this evidence package.** A prior draft named RC11 write/verify logs, but those files are absent here; no RC11 result is asserted | — |\nREADME.md:73:On the published RC10 artifact the cell **fails**: the extracted package's file data was never fsynced, so the rename and launcher switch survived while the payload did not. `v1.0.0-rc.10/bin/nexus` is 0 bytes, `nexus --version` prints nothing, and `nexus upgrade --recover` exits 0 without doing anything, because a 0-byte launcher is an empty shell script. The upgrade is performed by the installed rc.9 CLI, and the missing flush is in that running CLI. No RC11 result is asserted in this evidence package because the two log artifacts named by the prior draft are absent.\nREADME.md:94:- This covers the fresh-install / doctor / Node-preflight matrix plus the lifecycle cells (Ubuntu 22.04, Debian 12, Fedora 40 / Node 22) for E2 (ACC-PLAT) on RC10: install, installer-driven version switch and rollback, reinstall, repair and uninstall; checksum tamper; broken-candidate self-test; backup restore; updater process-crash recovery with staging cleanup; incompatible downgrade from a synthetic state-schema-1 release; synthetic-journal recovery from early transaction states and a malformed journal; and provenance-attestation verification. An ordinary successful `nexus upgrade` from alpha.2 is not executable because alpha.2 has no updater command; the alpha.2 row is installer-driven. Power-loss durability is tested rather than assumed and **fails on RC10**; the RC11 result is not verified in this evidence package because its log artifacts are absent.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":511583940}},"started_at_ms":1793338228025,"completed_at_ms":1793338229537}}
