idence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/lifecycle/powerloss/README.md\n .../evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/README.md     |  6 +++---\n .../evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/SHA256SUMS    |  6 ++----\n .../rc.10/platform-e2/lifecycle/powerloss/README.md           | 11 +++++------\n 3 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)\n65 docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/SHA256SUMS\nccf8bb25b351307e34b8fdaddd740eab7eb5854d8e1691667b894a866fd65f19  -\ndiff --git a/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/README.md b/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/README.md\nindex bc878b46..914eb3f6 100644\n--- a/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/README.md\n+++ b/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/README.md\n@@ -55,7 +55,7 @@ Fixtures were generated from the published RC10 archive (SHA-256 `444d0812ad583b\n | Incompatible downgrade | A synthetic release (`prepare-incompatible-fixture.sh`) declares state schema 1; `nexus upgrade --version v1.0.0-rc.4 --allow-downgrade --yes` was refused with `uses state schema version 1, which cannot read current state schema version 2`. Installed version, launcher target and package hash were unchanged and no target directory was created | [log](ubuntu-22-04-node22-incompatible-downgrade.log) |\n | Synthetic journal recovery | `run-synthetic-journal-recovery.sh` writes a valid `staged` journal with a staging directory, then a `preparing` journal without one: `nexus upgrade --recover` reports `cleaned_up`, removes staging, keeps the launcher and version, and creates no target directory; a malformed journal is refused with `failed schema or path validation`; the script verifies the installed version string and launcher symlink target are unchanged and that the target install directory remains absent (it does not compare package contents or user state); a second recovery is a no-op | [log](ubuntu-22-04-node22-synthetic-journal-recovery.log) |\n | Power-loss durability | **FAIL on the published RC10 artifact.** Power was cut (QEMU SIGKILL, ext4, `cache=none`) at the durable `switched` journal state. After reboot `v1.0.0-rc.10/bin/nexus` is 0 bytes, `nexus --version` prints nothing, and `nexus upgrade --recover` does nothing and exits 0 (a 0-byte launcher is an empty shell script), so the installation cannot repair itself. Cause: the extracted package was never fsynced before the rename and launcher switch. With a CLI containing the fix (PR #333) the same cut leaves a working launcher, recovery rolls back to rc.9, staging is removed, the stale lock is reclaimed, a second recovery is a no-op, and a retry completes to rc.10 | [RC10](ubuntu-22-04-node22-power-loss-durability-verify.log) · [fixed CLI](ubuntu-22-04-node22-power-loss-durability-fixed-cli-verify.log) |\n-| Power-loss durability (RC11) | **FAIL on the published RC11 artifact** (tag `8d4e5319`, which predates the fix). The same cut during rc.10 → rc.11 leaves `v1.0.0-rc.11/bin/nexus` at 0 bytes, `nexus --version` empty, and `nexus upgrade --recover` exiting 0 without doing anything. Any release built before #333 carries this defect | [log](ubuntu-22-04-node22-power-loss-durability-rc11-verify.log) |\n+| Power-loss durability (RC11) | **NOT VERIFIED in this evidence package.** A prior draft named RC11 write/verify logs, but those files are absent here; no RC11 result is asserted | — |\n | Provenance attestation | `gh attestation verify nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.0.0-rc.10.tar.gz -R mikeholownych/nexus-code` exited 0 on the published archive (SHA-256 `444d0812…b3e7`) with a Sigstore bundle; `--format json` returned a 13,989-byte verification result | [log](attestation-rc10.log) |\n \n The other additional lifecycle scripts do not set `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION`; their installer calls use the installer's default `auto` mode. The incompatible-downgrade and synthetic-journal-recovery scripts set it to `0` explicitly. Provenance is verified separately by the attestation cell. Provenance attestation is verified independently by the attestation cell above.\n@@ -70,7 +70,7 @@ Per-cell logs and results: `results.tsv`; image names and IDs: `prepared-images.\n \n `lifecycle/powerloss/` builds a 2 GiB ext4 image with rc.9 installed, boots a minimal QEMU/KVM guest, starts the upgrade to rc.10, and `SIGKILL`s the VM when the durable journal reaches `switched` — package in place and launcher switched, runtime verification not yet run. Nothing is synced first, and the image is mounted `cache=none`, so dirty page cache is lost exactly as in a power cut. The second boot dumps the journal, upgrade log and package directories, parses every JSON state file, runs `nexus upgrade --recover`, and asserts the rollback, staging removal, stale-lock reclamation and idempotence, then retries the upgrade to completion.\n \n-On the published RC10 artifact the cell **fails**: the extracted package's file data was never fsynced, so the rename and launcher switch survived while the payload did not. `v1.0.0-rc.10/bin/nexus` is 0 bytes, `nexus --version` prints nothing, and `nexus upgrade --recover` exits 0 without doing anything, because a 0-byte launcher is an empty shell script. The upgrade is performed by the installed rc.9 CLI, and the missing flush is in that running CLI. The published RC11 artifact (tag `8d4e5319`) reproduces the same failure for rc.10 → rc.11, because the tag predates the fix.\n+On the published RC10 artifact the cell **fails**: the extracted package's file data was never fsynced, so the rename and launcher switch survived while the payload did not. `v1.0.0-rc.10/bin/nexus` is 0 bytes, `nexus --version` prints nothing, and `nexus upgrade --recover` exits 0 without doing anything, because a 0-byte launcher is an empty shell script. The upgrade is performed by the installed rc.9 CLI, and the missing flush is in that running CLI. No RC11 result is asserted in this evidence package because the two log artifacts named by the prior draft are absent.\n \n The fix (PR #333) flushes every extracted file and directory before the switch. `NEXUS_POWERLOSS_BASELINE_DIST` runs the same published artifacts through a CLI containing the fix (the guest records the SHA-256 of the dist's sorted file manifest); that cut leaves a working launcher, recovery rolls back to rc.9, and the retry completes to rc.10. This demonstrates the fix; it is not qualification. The cell can only pass for a release whose own artifact contains the fix.\n \n@@ -91,6 +91,6 @@ The positive cells use Docker `--network bridge` to download the published RC10\n \n ## Scope and residuals\n \n-- This covers the fresh-install / doctor / Node-preflight matrix plus the lifecycle cells (Ubuntu 22.04, Debian 12, Fedora 40 / Node 22) for E2 (ACC-PLAT) on RC10: install, installer-driven version switch and rollback, reinstall, repair and uninstall; checksum tamper; broken-candidate self-test; backup restore; updater process-crash recovery with staging cleanup; incompatible downgrade from a synthetic state-schema-1 release; synthetic-journal recovery from early transaction states and a malformed journal; and provenance-attestation verification. An ordinary successful `nexus upgrade` from alpha.2 is not executable because alpha.2 has no updater command; the alpha.2 row is installer-driven. Power-loss durability is now tested rather than assumed, and it **fails on both RC10 and RC11** (RC11 predates the fix): see the rows and section below.\n+- This covers the fresh-install / doctor / Node-preflight matrix plus the lifecycle cells (Ubuntu 22.04, Debian 12, Fedora 40 / Node 22) for E2 (ACC-PLAT) on RC10: install, installer-driven version switch and rollback, reinstall, repair and uninstall; checksum tamper; broken-candidate self-test; backup restore; updater process-crash recovery with staging cleanup; incompatible downgrade from a synthetic state-schema-1 release; synthetic-journal recovery from early transaction states and a malformed journal; and provenance-attestation verification. An ordinary successful `nexus upgrade` from alpha.2 is not executable because alpha.2 has no updater command; the alpha.2 row is installer-driven. Power-loss durability is tested rather than assumed and **fails on RC10**; the RC11 result is not verified in this evidence package because its log artifacts are absent.\n - `endpoint.reachable` failing is expected in the isolated containers and is not a product failure; the same doctor run on a host with a configured gateway is the installed-RC provider evidence path.\n - Images were prepared for the RC9 matrix (`prep-182e8addeee0`). `prepared-images.json` records each cell label, image reference and image ID; it does not store separate base-distribution or Node-version fields. Positive-cell logs print the container's `node --version`; Node 24 cells mount the host Node v24.11.1 runtime into the Node 22 image.\ndiff --git a/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/SHA256SUMS b/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/SHA256SUMS\nindex fa38489a..33b0faaf 100644\n--- a/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/SHA256SUMS\n+++ b/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/SHA256SUMS\n@@ -42,7 +42,7 @@ fd4ec10b831834eb7060df9dbd311b6e716f716415f6a1f4c516856f61590c14  run-rc10-lifec\n a118090c486e0fe6b79b10b0bb64be604480c2ff37634ebee7cd999dfde37c36  lifecycle/run-process-crash-recovery.sh\n c7f9f273e0435e81b96171264428ccb94f2d354ba6324026d189d65b54f706f6  lifecycle/run-self-test-failure.sh\n 5095b0a681535ea8ac0c0f2870686f8937ef1b60980f2b76febf49bdd387dbb9  lifecycle/static-fixture-server.js\n-70e1c7ebdcda7d3ae4b7e4c3b29679c609166b265fd3540fd1285b2b205311c5  README.md\n+b93ae290fdd070cbd9c8c81d87dbf11aeadbb81d687549cdb494b82bcaafbb87  README.md\n 1303d3d78985349a02e262aab00b1119e038c839eb68a5c7c1f2ddf2048d83a2  attestation-rc10.log\n 59d7aa850450c96da19a0ba01d8ae172086115a6f89549fa229124cbad3e37a9  lifecycle/debian-12-node22-lifecycle.log\n d593020f8db817e76a7ab324570ec7c62997fdec4078447cf9a9c80d82ddb839  lifecycle/debian-12-node22-lifecycle.sh\n@@ -54,7 +54,7 @@ b05b014eb2284617b0331bb39ee8fb62b3c43e1767ba4ebccc9b03c949c42ec9  lifecycle/inco\n 39fc76c7d13d449ab4c8aae0241fb5759be6022b2e309c00e64b3841c94b4178  lifecycle/ubuntu-22-04-node22-incompatible-downgrade.log\n 56e99638a943e10f2e58d4386d0173eb2f3413ad76df6e198de57ac86a899420  lifecycle/run-synthetic-journal-recovery.sh\n f9ecd23acc4171fc77cf600a4cd15abc667908a714ad934c78c014ed000632c8  ubuntu-22-04-node22-synthetic-journal-recovery.log\n-ba4bf5d83097f04d46c9a0fd3ebcb83e5d87875f9f3e49825b00fbc6f3b7bc3e  lifecycle/powerloss/README.md\n+bf651c835784ca21c74e4e7d35ecb453bf0c77f68267f5853d1e66820dc6c169  lifecycle/powerloss/README.md\n 7a6094fd01a5cd392d3488eb790132d97709071415d7b6e3e14110ed12330c0f  lifecycle/powerloss/fetch-assets.sh\n 842fce3418bef41be4adb2ca5f15fea0c6e8c96496a58c2e45df4e121897172a  lifecycle/powerloss/guest-init\n 18f19fa27e480e299661faa3b89c7fcbe685452ad6248f62b656ef8554d6a682  lifecycle/powerloss/run-power-loss-durability.sh\n@@ -63,5 +63,3 @@ aa645ed28ed24c40a0274521c3b8c38330c007ba99a564ce5df9f1851c79d3d6  ubuntu-22-04-n\n 0501008ea1588bab704b741f88eb53722328ef70619323e8c462970bf677e0c2  ubuntu-22-04-node22-power-loss-durability-verify.log\n 7d96e2ebcc55b758bd2ac6047e2a770a28130d30b7b08250875b186f5c19caa0  ubuntu-22-04-node22-power-loss-durability-fixed-cli-write.log\n 8fa6c9ee6392434e4c90cecbcbe7b07775cc15b9dae07c7f01dccacd20e6a142  ubuntu-22-04-node22-power-loss-durability-fixed-cli-verify.log\n-b0afaa282f96f2c8d78421ed393cc8f7024a5f3d61989904473f409b481ddb21  ubuntu-22-04-node22-power-loss-durability-rc11-write.log\n-69a96131328e9fb0c20761d356bdc847496b758b7c881f130405a6dae0f54786  ubuntu-22-04-node22-power-loss-durability-rc11-verify.log\ndiff --git a/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/lifecycle/powerloss/README.md b/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/lifecycle/powerloss/README.md\nindex 57f3c8e1..5aa4bcb7 100644\n--- a/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/lifecycle/powerloss/README.md\n+++ b/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/lifecycle/powerloss/README.md\n@@ -66,13 +66,12 @@ The fix is in `cli/src/durable_tree.ts` (PR #333): `safeExtractTar` flushes ever\n file and directory of the extracted tree before the caller renames it and\n switches the launcher.\n \n-## Result on the published RC11 artifact: FAIL\n+## RC11 disposition: not verified in this evidence package\n \n-`v1.0.0-rc.11` (tag `8d4e5319`) predates the fix, so rc.10 → rc.11 reproduces the\n-same failure: `v1.0.0-rc.11/bin/nexus` is 0 bytes, `nexus --version` is empty, and\n-`nexus upgrade --recover` exits 0 without doing anything\n-(`...-power-loss-durability-rc11-verify.log`). Any release built before #333\n-carries the defect.\n+A prior draft named RC11 write and verify logs, but those log files are absent\n+from this evidence package. This package therefore makes no RC11 pass or failure\n+claim. The RC10 failure and fixed-CLI demonstration below are supported by their\n+included logs and remain distinct from RC11 qualification.\n \n ## Fix demonstration\n \n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":300758890}},"started_at_ms":1793338234041,"completed_at_ms":1793338235342}}
