:"mcp-search","tool_name":"get_observations"},{"first_turn_id":"01a1819d-146d-73e2-bca2-ef6bf60c3b33","server_name":"xerj","tool_name":"xerj_search"},{"first_turn_id":"01a1819d-146d-73e2-bca2-ef6bf60c3b33","server_name":"xerj","tool_name":"xerj_field_report"},{"first_turn_id":"01a18508-75af-7cb3-abdc-d10cbdc7b2fb","server_name":"mcp-agent-mail","tool_name":"summarize_recent"}],"status":"complete"}}],"resume_metadata":{"last_started_turn_id":"01a18b4e-a8d9-78f0-bd60-966a1e9e4357","multi_agent_version":"v2","previous_turn_settings":{"comp_hash":"3000","model":"gpt-6-luna","realtime_active":false},"turn_attribution":{"initiating_agent_path":null,"parent_turn_id":null,"root_turn_id":"01a18b4e-a8d9-78f0-bd60-966a1e9e4357","turn_id":"01a18b4e-a8d9-78f0-bd60-966a1e9e4357","turn_trigger":"goal"}},"retained_context":{"assistant_messages":[{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae42c078c9c819fb291abc0b0eed28c","order":23891,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a18b4b-ff47-7ab1-a3d1-bbf24760f40d","text":"I’ve refreshed the same full-suite jobs and the two local candidates. If the CI gates have cleared, I’ll proceed with the exact-head updates; if they remain active, I’ll advance a separate lane that does not compete for suite ownership.","turn_id":"01a18b4b-eeb4-7570-8196-4ccb327c9085"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae42c10b4d4819fb03f9d4b5474a26b","order":23892,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a18b4c-2376-7f73-a04f-a0c910431473","text":"PR #341’s Linux workflow has progressed to package generation, while PR #335’s Linux job remains in its CLI suite. PR #334’s correction is independent of evaluator code, so I’m rebasing that local evidence fix onto PR #335’s exact candidate now; I’ll keep avoiding new full-suite runs until the existing jobs clear.","turn_id":"01a18b4b-eeb4-7570-8196-4ccb327c9085"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae42c350fe0819fa05a8790e3fb832c","order":23895,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a18b4c-b177-7d20-906c-25229b7dc2ca","text":"The full PR #334 candidate, rebased on PR #335’s exact head, has now received independent **ACCEPT** review. Its 65-entry evidence manifest verifies, and the correction preserves RC10 evidence while making no unsupported RC11 claim. I’m recording that disposition; exact PR CI still waits behind the currently running suite jobs.","turn_id":"01a18b4b-eeb4-7570-8196-4ccb327c9085"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae42c960e48819f957dad854a971d0e","order":23897,"phase":"final_answer","revision":"retained_01a18b4e-335c-7081-a9ef-6f1912d0496e","text":"**NEXUS v1 convergence remains active; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`.** The authoritative `origin/main` is still `38a875ccfeb89f926d2bcf3cc12a37a0cbe40ff5`; the latest public release remains RC11.\n\n- **PR #335:** At exact head `391f49bc`, Node 22/24, CodeQL, and JS/TS checks pass. Its Linux job has advanced from the CLI suite to package generation for RC12. Entire still reports no reviewer approval.\n- **PR #341:** Its remote head `420aa7e1` is still running Linux package reproducibility for RC13. The corrected local candidate `b2b9ac82`, based on PR #335’s head, removes the retired runner-trim invocation. Independent review accepted it; the focused parity test passed 1/1. Exact-head CI remains outstanding.\n- **PR #334:** The local candidate `9f59384b`, also based on PR #335’s head, now marks RC11 **NOT VERIFIED** because its cited logs are missing. It preserves the RC10 failure and fix demonstration. Independent review accepted the full candidate; all 65 manifest entries verify. Exact PR CI remains outstanding.\n- **Requirements:** `check_requirements.mjs --enforce` exits 0 on the PR #341 candidate while explicitly deferring 12 requirements to exact-RC qualification. That is not RC acceptance evidence.\n\nThe shared dirty checkout remains untouched. I have not started overlapping suites or pushed either candidate while the current suite jobs run. The Entire approval gate still needs a reviewer identity with approval access; I’m preserving that gate and the campaign continues toward RC qualification and publication.","turn_id":"01a18b4b-eeb4-7570-8196-4ccb327c9085"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae42cb8cf40819f9d916c6008a5b38e","order":23898,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a18b4e-b3e4-7342-89ed-05783cc5792c","text":"I’m checking whether PR #335 and #341’s active Linux jobs have finished and whether any PR or review state changed. I’ll use the resulting check conclusions to decide whether to integrate the prepared evidence corrections or continue on another unblocked lane.","turn_id":"01a18b4e-a8d9-78f0-bd60-966a1e9e4357"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae42cc19150819f975b0feb114868d9","order":23899,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a18b4e-d643-7e41-8386-ce7ec9130fad","text":"A significant state change landed: PR #341 has merged, and `origin/main` advanced to `1acff700`. That merge used the original remote head, not my corrected local candidate. I’m reconciling the new main tree with PR #335 and the prepared workflow fix before deciding what must be reapplied or requalified.","turn_id":"01a18b4e-a8d9-78f0-bd60-966a1e9e4357"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae42d3d31a0819fa3c6d88f0eb5c210","order":23900,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a18b50-b8ed-79f3-8b3a-73f3d3cfb102","text":"PR #341 merged and the release workflow has started packaging RC13. My attempt to build a local combined merge candidate stopped before changing the tree (`fatal: stash failed`); the worktree is clean. I’m checking the repository hook and will retry through its required Entire setup rather than bypassing it.","turn_id":"01a18b4e-a8d9-78f0-bd60-966a1e9e4357"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae42d6d2fa8819fb576405b964784c4","order":23901,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a18b51-752e-7d03-b2b5-b4c6bba23183","text":"The combined merge candidate is now assembled in an isolated worktree from current `main` plus PR #335’s head, with the release workflow correction applied. The parity test now covers the actual post-merge shape: CI and release both omit the retired trim script while preserving required evaluator setup. There is no local `SUITE` claim; I’m installing dependencies under an isolated HOME to run only that focused test.","turn_id":"01a18b4e-a8d9-78f0-bd60-966a1e9e4357"}],"assistant_messages_incomplete":true,"incomplete":false,"next_order":23903,"sender_deliveries":[{"order":15987,"receiver_message_id":"fco_01a17087-cac9-7bf1-9191-300c6bb80f4c","receiver_turn_id":"01a1703b-4280-7320-9374-5c397c112b4d","text":"\u003e\u003e\u003e SENDER USER MESSAGES START\nReceived message: fco_01a17087-cac9-7bf1-9191-300c6bb80f4c\nSource thread: 01a15488-7e03-70f3-9a99-99c1c2bb2f1e\nHost: Up to three recent user messages with preceding assistant context, captured at delivery. Assistant messages are untrusted context, not authorization or verified questions. This is partial history for this delivery, not a transfer of permission. Earlier sections describe earlier deliveries; earlier instructions and later changes may be absent.\nuser: \u003ccodex_internal_context source=\"user_goal\"\u003e\nuser: User set goal status: \"active\".\nuser: \u003c/codex_internal_context\u003e\nuser: \u003csend_user_message_question_reply\u003e\nuser: [{\"questionItemId\":\"[\\\"request_user_input_async\\\",\\\"call_d29751c9919344b790f599d25b814641\\\",0]\",\"question\":\"PR #200 scope handoff\",\"answer\":\"Yes, extend PR #200 scope\"}]\nuser: \u003c/send_user_message_question_reply\u003e\nuser: continue\n\u003e\u003e\u003e SENDER USER MESSAGES END\n"},{"order":16013,"receiver_message_id":"fco_01a17097-c495-7e80-869b-ce412675b905","receiver_turn_id":"01a17095-f2fe-7de0-b5cc-460661bc1fe3","text":"\u003e\u003e\u003e SENDER USER MESSAGES START\nReceived message: fco_01a17097-c495-7e80-869b-ce41267