{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T06:30:30.448Z","ordinal":520452,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18b4e-a8d9-78f0-bd60-966a1e9e4357","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-66b3b872-6cc6-4a8c-bc64-ee7bb1fe433b","process_id":"95641","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","find docs/v1.0.0 -maxdepth 3 -type f | sort | rg 'ACCEPTANCE|QUAL|README|READINESS|custody|heldout|DECISIONS|EVIDENCE' | head -60; rg -n -i 'custody|held-out|heldout-v2|40 tasks|terminal matrix|exact.rc|T2|T3|T4|openrouter' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md docs/v1.0.0/README.md 2>/dev/null | head -80"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/rc13-source-gates-20261030T0537Z","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"find docs/v1.0.0 -maxdepth 3 -type f | sort | rg 'ACCEPTANCE|QUAL|README|READINESS|custody|heldout|DECISIONS|EVIDENCE' | head -60; rg -n -i 'custody|held-out|heldout-v2|40 tasks|terminal matrix|exact.rc|T2|T3|T4|openrouter' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md docs/v1.0.0/README.md 2>/dev/null | head -80"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\ndocs/v1.0.0/README.md\ndocs/v1.0.0/README.md:5:**Historical verdict: v1.0.0 readiness was BLOCKED at the 2026-10-16 source-suite checkpoint.** Candidate source revision `6151a231e9179c109cfbe8cff87e0a4148587b6a` passed an isolated `make build` and full `make test` run on 2026-10-16 (Rust 281/281; CLI 1087/1087; zero skipped). This is source-suite evidence, not RC qualification. At that checkpoint, held-out task quality, T3/T4 qualification, standalone/provider qualification, the manual terminal matrix, package/install matrix on the RC, and independent RC acceptance remained incomplete. For v1.0.0, the manual matrix was later waived by DEC-20; see [the current readiness reconciliation](READINESS.md) for the current disposition and remaining gates. The contest entry remains a separate track; judging has concluded and no contest freeze applies.\ndocs/v1.0.0/README.md:49:4. M2 and M4 run in parallel with M1/M3. Held-out task authoring (agent-authored, as authorised) and the standalone proxy start during M1.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:28:5. **Stable promotion and publication.** After exact-RC acceptance and G6 pass, create a stable-version commit directly on the accepted RC commit, changing only the synchronized version metadata required for v1.0.0. Record both commits and the version-only diff. Run required source CI and all applicable source G0–G4 checks on this exact stable-version commit before tagging. If any other source changes, restart RC construction and qualification. Then create the `v1.0.0` tag on that checked commit and build a draft release. Keep its assets unpublished while verifying the stable artifact identity, provenance, package contents, installation, and publication metadata. Compare the stable package contents with the accepted RC; if packaged behavior or content differs beyond version-specific metadata, rerun affected installed-RC qualification gates and obtain independent acceptance for the stable artifact. Publish the draft only after these checks pass and the signed acceptance disposition is recorded. Record the published digests and provenance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:32:Exact-RC requirements records identify at least one implementer and an independent reviewer. For a blocking requirement recorded as `tested` instead of `product-qualified`, the cited decision must be explicitly allowlisted for that requirement in the approved qualification-exceptions table below, and its `DECISIONS.md` section must contain a matching requirement-specific line of the form `Qualification applicability: REQ-... = NOT REQUIRED ...`. A record-supplied or unrelated decision cannot authorize an exception. The record must include digest-bound evidence for every `ACC-*` criterion in that requirement's ledger Acceptance column.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:34:The post-RC closure requirements listed below may remain `open`, `partial`, or `implemented` in the source ledger at the RC commit because their remaining acceptance is completed during G6 or installed-RC qualification. The bare `--enforce` invocation is the pre-RC source gate: it checks every other B/RR row against the source threshold and reports mapped rows as deferred, not accepted. At G6, the exact-RC invocation must provide a record meeting the normal B/RR status threshold and digest-bound evidence for every criterion in this table. The table also supplies the criterion mapping for rows whose ledger points to an ACCEPTANCE section instead of naming ACC IDs. The source ledger is never rewritten by the record. Any below-tested required row omitted from this table still fails.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:37:### Qualification-only requirements for exact-RC enforcement\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:39:| Requirement | Acceptance criteria required in the exact-RC record | Remaining stage |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:42:| REQ-AGT-002 | ACC-VER-03, ACC-VER-04, ACC-VER-09, ACC-QUAL-T2, ACC-QUAL-T3, ACC-QUAL-T4 | Installed-RC T2/T3/T4 outcome thresholds |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:45:| REQ-REL-005 | ACC-SUP-04, ACC-SUP-05 | Exact-RC security and dependency artifact checks |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:48:| REQ-REL-114 | ACC-SUP-08 | Exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:49:| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:52:| REQ-QUAL-109 | ACC-QUAL-T3 | Installed-RC T3 long-task qualification |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:56:### Approved exact-RC qualification exceptions\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:81:| E3 | Operator dev box: Linux x86-64, real terminals (xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal) | Terminal matrix, live sessions |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:82:| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:83:| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:117:| ACC-QUAL-T2 | §6.1 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:118:| ACC-QUAL-T3 | §6.3 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:119:| ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:120:| ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:142:| P-plain | Bare OpenAI-compatible `/models` and chat. No tokenize, no capacity headers. | Standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 held-out tasks) × 3 runs; T4 classes 1, 3, 4, 7 × 3 | T2 correctness ≥ (gateway-direct T2 correctness on the same tasks − 10 pts). False VERIFIED = 0. T4 truthful = 100%. Context source reported as `client_default` or an operator override, with no error. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:154:| OpenRouter, pinned model | Supported | `providers verify` PASS, plus one live small task (a §6-style bug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:190:### 5.3 Manual real-terminal matrix (E3)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:214:### 6.1 T2 held-out (ACC-QUAL-T2)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:218:- Before execution, freeze three qualification configs at `eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json`, `eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json`, and `eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json`. Each must set `qualification: true`, identify the same model fingerprint and sampling settings, and record equal context/output and task budgets; the Nexus config must identify the installed RC and its package digest. Do not derive these files from the pilot configs by silently inheriting or changing settings.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:219:- Set `T2_TASKS` to the custodian-approved, sealed task directory and `T2_OUT` to a new, empty, run-specific output directory. Do not use the disclosed `eval/tasks` development set as held-out evidence. Preserve all three outputs and their manifests; never reuse an output directory for a retry.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:224:  : \"${T2_TASKS:?set the sealed task directory}\"\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:225:  : \"${T2_OUT:?set a new unique output directory}\"\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:226:  test ! -e \"$T2_OUT\"\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:227:  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/nexus\" --runs 5\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:228:  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/goose\" --runs 5\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:229:  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/opencode\" --runs 5\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:230:  node eval/score.mjs --pairs \"$T2_OUT/nexus/results.jsonl\" \"$T2_OUT/goose/results.jsonl\" \"$T2_OUT/opencode/results.jsonl\"\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:233:  Record the resolved `T2_TASKS`, unique `T2_OUT`, config digests, installed RC identity, model fingerprint, and exact commands in the frozen run record before starting. A failed or interrupted invocation remains evidence; any permitted infrastructure rerun uses the accepted rerun procedure and is retained separately. Do not score until all required runs and manifests exist. The scorer accepts exactly the Nexus, Goose and OpenCode result files.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:235:### 6.2 T4 fault injection (ACC-QUAL-T4)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:249:### 6.3 T3 long tasks (ACC-QUAL-T3)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:257:| False VERIFIED (T2 + T3 + T4) | **= 0** |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:258:| T2 pooled hidden-test correctness | ≥ 60% and ≥ best matched peer − 10 pts |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:259:| T2 per class (bugfix, feature, refactor, debug) | ≥ 40% |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:262:| T4 truthful outcome | = 100% |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:263:| T4 hang beyond budget + 5 min | = 0 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:264:| T3 false-absence | = 0 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:265:| T3 false-presence | = 0 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:266:| T3 steering honoured | ≥ 95% |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:309:   - 5 random T2 tasks;\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:310:   - 2 T4 classes.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:341:- [ ] The exact-RC evidence gate passes from the clean RC worktree and is bound to the exact RC source commit and installed RC artifact. Run the checker with the custodian-approved, immutable qualification record and evidence directory:\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:343:  The version 1 record contains `sourceCommit` (full commit ID), `rcTag` (for example `v1.0.0-rc.1`), `artifactSha256`, `artifactProvenance` (`sourceCommit`, `artifactSha256`, and a hashed provenance report), `independentAcceptance` (`disposition`, `reviewer`, `implementers`, zero `blockingDefects`, and a hashed report reference), and one `requirements` entry for every B/RR row. For `ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS`, include each non-blocking defect with its owner disposition; unresolved or blocking defects fail. Each requirement entry records its status and one or more hashed evidence files covering the exact criteria required by the ledger and the §1.1 qualification-only map. Every criterion evidence file must be a JSON object with top-level `sourceCommit`, `rcTag`, and `artifactSha256` values exactly matching the validated qualification record, current RC source commit, and installed RC artifact. A digest-valid report copied from another source revision, RC tag, or artifact is rejected. A B row recorded as `tested` also needs a non-empty `qualificationNotApplicable.reason` and a `qualificationNotApplicable.decision` matching the approved per-requirement exception table and a matching applicability declaration in DECISIONS.md; an unrelated or record-supplied decision is rejected. Evidence paths must be relative regular files under the evidence root, with no symlinks. Missing, unknown, stale, mismatched, or incomplete evidence fails the gate. The checker requires a clean worktree, rejects `--ledger` overrides, enforces source-ledger thresholds outside the explicit §1.1 lifecycle rows, and requires the exact-RC record itself to meet the normal status threshold for every row. It never mutates the source ledger or relaxes a requirement's B/RR record threshold. The checker validates source/tag/artifact identity bindings and evidence hashes; it does not authenticate the reviewer or prove that the artifact was built from the source commit. The approved release workflow must independently verify build provenance/attestation, and the designated custodian and independent reviewer must verify their respective approvals and custody evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:5:The release owner accepted DEC-20: the manual five-terminal by three-size matrix in Acceptance §5.3 is waived for v1.0.0. No operator runs, cell verdicts, or per-cell results are required or inferred. Automated CI checks (§5.1) and scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios (§5.2) remain mandatory. The dated checkpoint below refreshes the release, PR, CI, and custody status; older checkpoint sections remain historical evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:10:- **Source gates:** On a clean worktree at exact `8d71e1a`, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed: 123 rows, 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; the 12 exact-RC qualification deferrals remain unchanged. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` passed with all components at `1.0.0-rc.11`. These are source-stage results only.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:11:- **PR #318 evaluator remediation:** The pushed PR head is `eec83d6703ce5449ae868d67d1e3c906e7d3d00a`; focused `eval_integrity` and `eval_hardened` tests passed 48/48 after clean `npm ci`, CLI build, Rust release-core build, and isolated HOME/XDG/TMPDIR. No held-out tasks were used. Exact-head CI run [40940623810](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40940623810) is still running Node 22/24; CodeQL and JavaScript/TypeScript checks passed. The PR must be rebased onto `8d71e1a` and pass fresh exact-head review/checks before integration.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:13:- **Held-out custody:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned; its latest public update reports T2 at 20/40 tasks and no fresh custody acceptance. T3's reported 8/8 is digest/schema/isolation metadata, not qualification acceptance. Public records identify the prior custodian only as the `opencode` primary session; they do not identify a human custodian. SageBridge was named as a contact, but no new custody acceptance is recorded. No private payload was accessed or run.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:14:- **PR and release state:** PR #328 is merged. PR #318 remains open and pending refreshed exact-head CI. PR #327 remains open; Node 22/24, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL passed, while Entire Gates failed. Public releases still end at `v1.0.0-rc.10`; RC11 and stable `v1.0.0` are unpublished. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; provider and standalone matrices, held-out T2/T3/T4, cross-runner reproducibility, long-task/fault-injection, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:15:- **Next executable steps:** Let the current-main and PR #318 CI runs finish; rebase PR #318 onto `8d71e1a`, obtain fresh exact-head review/checks, and integrate through the normal process. Continue the custodian handoff without exposing private material. Construct the next RC only after pre-RC gates pass, then execute all mandatory exact-RC gates, including §5.1 and §5.2, followed by independent acceptance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:21:**Requirements and version:** On exact `origin/main` `a0356c4d8f0f0b9b943d4033aff59795fcab83b4`, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed: 123 rows, 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 remain deferred to exact-RC qualification: REQ-AGT-002, REQ-AGT-010, REQ-PRV-003, REQ-REL-003, REQ-REL-005, REQ-AGT-110, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-REL-114, REQ-QUAL-101, REQ-QUAL-107, REQ-QUAL-108 and REQ-QUAL-109. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` passes at `1.0.0-rc.10`. These are source-stage checks, not installed-RC acceptance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:25:**Held-out custody and qualification:** The latest public metadata update on issue #1 (06:02 UTC) records unresolved custody ownership: a historical handoff log names SageBridge as an accepted successor, while the active custody record still names OpenCode. The latest posted T2 count is 20/40 tasks; no new custody acceptance or qualification result is recorded. T3's reported 8/8 covers digest/schema/isolation metadata, not task-quality qualification. The custodian identity and acknowledged transfer must be reconciled before qualification. No private payloads were accessed by implementation work. T2/T3/T4 held-out qualification, standalone/provider acceptance, long-task/fault-injection qualification, and successor-RC cross-runner reproducibility remain incomplete.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:29:**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. Publication authorization remains granted but gated on complete mandatory acceptance. PR #319 is integrated; main post-merge CI is running. PRs #320 and #322 are in exact-head Linux validation, PR #321 is rebased with fresh checks pending, and PR #318 needs the toolchain change integrated and its exact-base qualification rerun. Exact-RC construction and qualification remain gated on pre-RC source readiness and complete independent custody acceptance; terminal operator evidence is still required before independent RC acceptance at this checkpoint.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:35:**Source gates on main:** `origin/main` is `b10a85ad6305a4a3564a81d9bc66e88f55036c8d` (PR #312 merge). Exact-main CI run [40802654248](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40802654248) and CodeQL run [40802654255](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40802654255) passed on that SHA. The exact-source requirements gate passed with 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open); 12 requirements remain mapped to exact-RC qualification. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` reports `1.0.0-rc.10`. These are source-stage results, not installed-RC qualification.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:39:**Qualification and custody:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. The claims identify OpenCode as the prior/current custodian workflow, but do not verify the responsible human identity; SageBridge's 04:15 status says it is coordinating only. The successor T2 store remains 20/40 tasks; the remaining Go/Rust tasks need the reviewed, pinned-toolchain change integrated. Reported T3 digest/schema/isolation checks are 8/8, which is not full T3 task-quality qualification. At 04:23 UTC the OpenCode custodian holds SUITE for two-round setup/reference/oracle revalidation of the 20 converted tasks with isolated HOME; a live validator child process was observed. This is custody revalidation, not held-out qualification; no result or custody acceptance is recorded. Public Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned; the latest metadata-only correction was posted at 04:18 UTC. T2 custody acceptance and qualification, full T3/T4 qualification, current-candidate provider and standalone qualification, fault injection, successor-RC reproducibility and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. RC10 evidence does not qualify a successor candidate.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:43:**Suite evidence:** `make test` completed on immutable snapshot `03bfaa394c906d900574f35104e521844049403c` with isolated HOME and the required evaluator workspace/runtime fixtures: 1,993 tests across 224 suites, 1,991 passed, 0 failed, 2 skipped, 0 cancelled; Rust tests and post-test security lifecycle gates passed. The full run took 3,167,118 ms. This snapshot is not exact current main, PR #311 candidate `fe28ec9`, or an RC, so the result does not qualify those revisions. The SUITE claim transferred to the OpenCode custodian at 04:18 UTC for the 20-task custody revalidation above.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:45:**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. Stable publication remains gated on mandatory exact-RC qualification and acceptance. Publication authorization remains granted; no further authorization is requested.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:51:**Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0`, the merge commit for PR #305. Exact-main CI run [40751988282](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40751988282) and CodeQL run [40751988267](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40751988267) passed on that SHA. The source requirements check passed on this revision with 123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open, and 12 deferred to exact-RC qualification. These source-stage results do not qualify an installed release candidate.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:55:**Qualification and release:** Public [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) remains the latest release; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. Official cross-runner run [40564959805](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40564959805) passed for the published RC10 source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`, rebuilding on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04. Its machine-readable evidence reports `REQ-REL-114` / `ACC-SUP-08` `PASS` and matching hashes for six outputs, including the published archive and `sbom.cdx.json`; see the [RC10 reproducibility record](../reviews/evidence/v1/REQ-REL-114-rc10-20261027/README.md). The requirements ledger still marks `REQ-REL-114` `UNV`/open; its owner must reconcile that disposition. RC10 evidence does not establish successor-RC qualification. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned (last updated 2026-10-28 14:23 UTC); no custodian acceptance or held-out T2/T3/T4 qualification is established. The terminal matrix remains 0/15; the user waived screenshot artifacts, while terminal behavior checks remain unrun. Standalone/provider, fault-injection, successor-RC qualification, required human terminal behavior, and independent exact-RC acceptance gates remain outstanding. Stable publication remains gated.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:69:**Requirements and qualification:** Current-main CI's requirements checker passes; the most recent explicit `--enforce` result was on PR #302 head `c3901774` before the nested-workspace-only follow-up: 123 rows, 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open, with 12 requirements deferred to installed-RC qualification. RC10 has scope-limited exact-artifact evidence: OpenRouter pinned-model verification and one synthetic live task passed, and the cross-runner workflow passed for the six listed release artifacts across Ubuntu 22.04/24.04 and against published RC10 (run [40564959805](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40564959805)). A later checkpoint correction incorrectly claimed this workflow failed because of an npm-version mismatch. That correction is superseded: GitHub records run `40564959805` and its `compare` job as completed successfully; the current checkpoint above reports that final result. This historical correction is retained here to preserve the audit trail. These results apply only to immutable RC10 source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`; they do not qualify a successor candidate or establish full release acceptance. The newly pushed #302 head must complete exact checks before its requirements evidence is refreshed. Public [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) remains the latest release; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. GitHub installer is the selected distribution target; npm publication is inapplicable.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:71:Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned; its last update was 2026-10-28 14:23 UTC, with no custodian response observed. No held-out payload was accessed and no held-out qualification was run. The manual terminal matrix's last recorded result is 0/15; terminal setup exists on Ubuntu, but no operator screenshots or cell verdicts have been supplied. Held-out/T2/T3/T4, remaining provider and standalone coverage, successor-RC cross-runner reproducibility, the human terminal matrix, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:79:**Authoritative source and requirements gate:** `origin/main` is `b2ae2fe82640e44d58ef5418f49b46df03392212` (PR #304 merge). Current-main CI [40693030763](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40693030763) and CodeQL [40693030710](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40693030710) both completed SUCCESS on that exact revision. A clean detached worktree at that exact source ran `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` with isolated `HOME`: 123 rows; 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 remain explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification. This passes the source-stage enforcement gate only.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:85:**Qualification, custody, and publication:** GitHub still lists [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) as the latest release; there is no `v1.0.0` tag or stable release. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned, with the last metadata-only custodian request at 2026-10-28 14:23 UTC and no response observed. No protected payload was accessed