{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T06:33:41.029Z","ordinal":520678,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18b4e-a8d9-78f0-bd60-966a1e9e4357","session_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","root_turn_id":"01a18b4e-a8d9-78f0-bd60-966a1e9e4357","response_id":"resp_0db389702a7164cc016ae43a42c38c819f96a4754e84768cb5","usage":{"input_tokens":233809,"cached_input_tokens":231296,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":235,"reasoning_output_tokens":105,"total_tokens":234044},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":35423281,"cached_input_tokens":35194752,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":88530,"reasoning_output_tokens":53626,"total_tokens":35511811},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":9798012909,"cached_input_tokens":9694251264,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":28173022,"reasoning_output_tokens":16571353,"total_tokens":9826185931}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T06:33:41.332Z","ordinal":520679,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18b4e-a8d9-78f0-bd60-966a1e9e4357","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-658e411a-90b2-42ad-a547-8f4d8dfc0ffd","process_id":"20563","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | nl -ba | sed -n '30,65p'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md | nl -ba | sed -n '230,273p'; rg -n 'FILE_docs_v1_0_0|READINESS.md' .git/nexus-claims"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | nl -ba | sed -n '30,65p'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md | nl -ba | sed -n '230,273p'; rg -n 'FILE_docs_v1_0_0|READINESS.md' .git/nexus-claims"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"    30\tThe final G6 decision in §10 applies to promoting the accepted RC toward a stable release. It requires the applicable gates to pass for the accepted RC and authorizes the version-only stable commit and its source checks, followed by the stable tag and draft build; it does not waive source CI, artifact identity, installed-RC qualification, or any threshold. Public publication is a separate post-build gate in stage 5 above. The release workflow must keep stable assets in draft state until stable artifact checks pass. Source verification at integration 6a16cb6 confirms the tag-triggered release workflow now supports published RC prereleases and draft stable releases. The earlier immediate-stable-publication source blocker is resolved; an actual stable draft build, artifact verification, signed acceptance, and deliberate publication are still required and remain unproven until their run evidence is recorded.\n    31\t\n    32\tExact-RC requirements records identify at least one implementer and an independent reviewer. For a blocking requirement recorded as `tested` instead of `product-qualified`, the cited decision must be explicitly allowlisted for that requirement in the approved qualification-exceptions table below, and its `DECISIONS.md` section must contain a matching requirement-specific line of the form `Qualification applicability: REQ-... = NOT REQUIRED ...`. A record-supplied or unrelated decision cannot authorize an exception. The record must include digest-bound evidence for every `ACC-*` criterion in that requirement's ledger Acceptance column.\n    33\t\n    34\tThe post-RC closure requirements listed below may remain `open`, `partial`, or `implemented` in the source ledger at the RC commit because their remaining acceptance is completed during G6 or installed-RC qualification. The bare `--enforce` invocation is the pre-RC source gate: it checks every other B/RR row against the source threshold and reports mapped rows as deferred, not accepted. At G6, the exact-RC invocation must provide a record meeting the normal B/RR status threshold and digest-bound evidence for every criterion in this table. The table also supplies the criterion mapping for rows whose ledger points to an ACCEPTANCE section instead of naming ACC IDs. The source ledger is never rewritten by the record. Any below-tested required row omitted from this table still fails.\n    35\t\n    36\t<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:START -->\n    37\t### Qualification-only requirements for exact-RC enforcement\n    38\t\n    39\t| Requirement | Acceptance criteria required in the exact-RC record | Remaining stage |\n    40\t|---|---|---|\n    41\t| REQ-REL-003 | ACC-PLAT | Installed-RC platform and Node-version matrix |\n    42\t| REQ-AGT-002 | ACC-VER-03, ACC-VER-04, ACC-VER-09, ACC-QUAL-T2, ACC-QUAL-T3, ACC-QUAL-T4 | Installed-RC T2/T3/T4 outcome thresholds |\n    43\t| REQ-AGT-010 | ACC-TRUST-04 | Independent acceptance of the DEC-04 v1 subset |\n    44\t| REQ-PRV-003 | ACC-INF-10 | Installed-RC standalone and absent-gateway behavior |\n    45\t| REQ-REL-005 | ACC-SUP-04, ACC-SUP-05 | Exact-RC security and dependency artifact checks |\n    46\t| REQ-AGT-110 | ACC-CONT-10, ACC-GOV-06 | Installed-RC continuity and independent acceptance |\n    47\t| REQ-PRV-111 | ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC provider verification |\n    48\t| REQ-REL-114 | ACC-SUP-08 | Exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility |\n    49\t| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\n    50\t| REQ-QUAL-107 | ACC-PRV-STANDALONE, ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC standalone and provider matrix |\n    51\t| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y | Installed-RC automated and scripted PTY acceptance; the manual E3 matrix is waived by DEC-20 |\n    52\t| REQ-QUAL-109 | ACC-QUAL-T3 | Installed-RC T3 long-task qualification |\n    53\t<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:END -->\n    54\t\n    55\t<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:START -->\n    56\t### Approved exact-RC qualification exceptions\n    57\t\n    58\t| Requirement | Approved decision | Scope |\n    59\t|---|---|---|\n    60\t<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:END -->\n    61\t\n    62\t## 1. Rules\n    63\t\n    64\t1. The RC is built and published by the release workflow from a clean tag. Its version is identical across all components (REQ-REL-103).\n    65\t2. All qualification runs use the **installed RC package**, installed with the documented one-line command. They never use a checkout build. The only exception is CI unit and PTY suites, which run from source at the same commit.\n   230\t\n   231\tThe floor forces 400 and 200 tokens; the band caps at 1.5 × 200 = 300 and 1.5 × 120 = 180. No estimator can satisfy both. This is a genuine, arithmetic inconsistency, not a measurement defect: the reference counts were re-measured on the pinned worker and the estimator was reproduced exactly.\n   232\t\n   233\t**Decision (chosen).** REQ-AGT-118's `≥ 1 token/char` floor is an **admission-safety** requirement, not an accuracy requirement: it guarantees the estimator never *under-admits* tokens for a non-Latin context, because an under-estimate silently overflows the context window (the failure class REQ-AGT-118 exists to prevent). ACC-VER-07's `≤ 1.5×` band is an **accuracy** target. The two are distinct properties, and where a merging tokenizer makes them collide the admission-safety floor takes precedence. ACC-VER-07 is therefore scoped to the corpora the floor does not dominate; for a merging tokenizer the floor-driven over-estimate is admitted as a **bounded admission-safety bias**. The `≤ 1.5×` accuracy threshold itself is **unchanged**.\n   234\t\n   235\tThis amendment is **narrow by design**. It applies only to corpora where the measured estimator is floor-bound — currently exactly the two in the table above — and it **does not silently exempt any other corpus**: any corpus whose estimator lands between the floor and the band must be examined and recorded (`tokens.test.ts` pins the floor-bound set to these two names and the full 14-corpus set, so neither an added exemption nor a silent corpus deletion can pass the test). The original accuracy failures are **preserved** — in the table above, in the fixture's `floorBound` entries, and in the base ledger wording (git history at `e1759ca`; the live row now records the amendment and stays `partial` until the changed tests pass and the amendment is independently accepted) — as recorded, failed accuracy evidence. They are not deleted or rewritten into passes.\n   236\t\n   237\t**Rejected alternatives.** (A) Lower the floor to satisfy the band — rejected: reintroduces under-estimation and the context-overflow class REQ-AGT-118 exists to prevent. (B) Drop the CJK/Hangul corpora from the fixture — rejected: removes the evidence. (C) Change the pinned tokenizer — out of scope; the fixture pins the qualification worker.\n   238\t\n   239\t**Affected:** REQ-AGT-118; SPEC-11 §2.7 and ACC-VER-07; REQUIREMENTS ledger row REQ-AGT-118; `cli/test/fixtures/token_calibration.json` and `cli/test/tokens.test.ts`. No change to `cli/src/tokens.ts` behaviour.\n   240\t\n   241\t## DEC-18: v1.0.0 terminal screenshot-artifact waiver\n   242\t\n   243\t**Context.** The v1.0.0 manual terminal matrix requires real interaction in five terminal environments at three sizes. The release owner waived screenshot artifacts for this release.\n   244\t\n   245\t**Chosen (owner-confirmed 2026-10-28).** Approval-panel and post-exit screenshots are not required for v1.0.0. This waiver changes only the screenshot artifact requirement. It does not waive any interactive run, check, safety threshold, per-cell PASS/FAIL verdict, observed outcome, evidence record, exact installed-RC identity, or written disposition for non-safety failures. All 15 manual matrix cells remain mandatory; automated PTY runs cannot replace them.\n   246\t\n   247\t**Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §5.3 / ACC-TUI-MANUAL; SPEC-10 REQ-QUAL-108; `TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md`; PLAN-10 task 12.\n   248\t\n   249\t## DEC-19: v1.0.0 manual terminal-matrix waiver\n   250\t\n   251\t**Status: withdrawn.** The waiver described in this decision is not in effect.\n   252\t\n   253\t**History.** A prior revision of this decision recorded that the release owner waived the manual matrix. That record conflicted with the explicit release requirement for five terminal environments × three sizes. The waiver is withdrawn and must not be used to disposition any v1.0.0 gate.\n   254\t\n   255\t**Current decision (release owner direction, 2026-10-29).** All fifteen manual E3 cells remain mandatory on the exact installed RC. Record a PASS or FAIL and observed outcomes for every required check in every cell. Automated CI or PTY runs do not substitute for operator evidence. [DEC-18](#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver) remains in force and waives screenshot artifacts only; it does not waive interaction, checks, per-cell verdicts, evidence records, or safety gates. No cell is accepted as complete without actual manual execution.\n   256\t\n   257\t**Disclosure.** Do not describe the manual matrix as waived. Until all fifteen cells have verified operator evidence, ACC-TUI-MANUAL remains incomplete and v1.0.0 acceptance remains blocked.\n   258\t\n   259\t**Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §5.3 / ACC-TUI-MANUAL; ACCEPTANCE §10 G6; SPEC-10 REQ-QUAL-108; `TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md`; PLAN-10 task 12; READINESS; release notes.\n   260\t\n   261\t## DEC-20: v1.0.0 manual terminal-matrix waiver\n   262\t\n   263\t**Status: accepted by the release owner, 2026-10-29.** This decision supersedes DEC-19 for v1.0.0.\n   264\t\n   265\t**Direction.** The manual five-terminal by three-size matrix in ACCEPTANCE §5.3 is waived for v1.0.0. No manual operator run, cell verdict, or per-cell evidence is required, and the waiver does not claim that any cell passed. The automated CI gate in §5.1 and the scripted installed-RC PTY gate in §5.2 remain mandatory and must pass.\n   266\t\n   267\t**Scope.** This waiver applies only to ACC-TUI-MANUAL and only for v1.0.0. It does not waive ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, exact-RC identity, any §5.1 or §5.2 scenario, safety checks, or any other release gate. DEC-18's screenshot-artifact waiver remains recorded; no screenshots are required for a matrix that is not run.\n   268\t\n   269\t**Qualification applicability:** REQ-QUAL-108 = ACC-TUI-STEER and ACC-TUI-A11Y remain required; ACC-TUI-MANUAL is waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20.\n   270\t\n   271\t**Disclosure.** Report ACC-TUI-MANUAL as waived by this decision, not passed and not outstanding. Preserve historical operator observations as observations only; do not promote them to cell results.\n   272\t\n   273\t**Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §§1.1, 3.1, 5, and 10; REQ-QUAL-108 exact-RC evidence mapping; stable v1.0.0 release notes; READINESS; terminal-matrix worksheet disposition.\n.git/nexus-claims/archived/REDACTED/owner.json:1:{\"agent\":\"codex-root\",\"host\":\"mike-dev\",\"branch\":\"codex/release-readiness-timestamp\",\"worktree\":\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/release-readiness-timestamp\",\"base\":\"cbb3b653a6bb6060071d8927e08e30d63765865e\",\"since\":\"2026-10-28T22:40:00Z\",\"scope\":\"Carry the independently accepted one-line correction to main CI completed_at in READINESS.md from merged PR310 onto a follow-up branch; docs-only; no push or publication.\"}\n.git/nexus-claims/archived/recovery-20261022T0238Z/readiness-post127/PLAN-10_READINESS_POST127-owner.json:8:  \"scope\": \"Refresh docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md current checkpoint after PR127; record exact current-main CI failure and CodeQL result without changing requirement status or treating scanner failures as passes\",\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":33612}},"started_at_ms":1793342021331,"completed_at_ms":1793342021331}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T06:33:41.933Z","ordinal":520680,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18b83-a12d-7181-b043-c13fe151d23e","call_id":"call_d8879e558cbb4da3889d0bd32d08528c","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 2902)\nTotal output lines: 82\n\n    30\tThe final G6 decision in §10 applies to promoting the accepted RC toward a stable release. It requires the applicable gates to pass for the accepted RC and authorizes the version-only stable commit and its source checks, followed by the stable tag and draft build; it does not waive source CI, artifact identity, installed-RC qualification, or any threshold. Public publication is a separate post-build gate in stage 5 above. The release workflow must keep stable assets in draft state until stable artifact checks pass. Source verification at integration 6a16cb6 confirms the tag-triggered release workflow now supports published RC prereleases and draft stable releases. The earlier immediate-stable-publication source blocker is resolved; an actual stable draft build, artifact verification, signed acceptance, and deliberate publication are still required and remain unproven until their run evidence is recorded.\n    31\t\n    32\tExact-RC requirements records identify at least one implementer and an independent reviewer. For a blocking requirement recorded as `tested` instead of `product-qualified`, the cited decision must be explicitly allowlisted for that requirement in the approved qualification-exceptions table below, and its `DECISIONS.md` section must contain a matching requirement-specific line of the form `Qualification applicability: REQ-... = NOT REQUIRED ...`. A record-supplied or unrelated decision cannot authorize an exception. The record must include digest-bound evidence for every `ACC-*` criterion in that requirement's ledger Acceptance column.\n    33\t\n    34\tThe post-RC closure requirements listed below may remain `open`, `partial`, or `implemented` in the source ledger at the RC commit because their remaining acceptance is completed during G6 or installed-RC qualification. The bare `--enforce` invocation is the pre-RC source gate: it checks every other B/RR row against the source threshold and reports mapped rows as deferred, not accepted. At G6, the exact-RC invocation must provide a record meeting the normal B/RR status threshold and digest-bound evidence for every criterion in this table. The table also supplies the criterion mapping for rows whose ledger points to an ACCEPTANCE section instead of naming ACC IDs. The source ledger is never rewritten by the record. Any below-tested required row omitted from this table still fails.\n    35\t\n    36\t<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:START -->\n    37\t### Qualification-only requirements for exact-RC enforcement\n    38\t\n    39\t| Requirement | Acceptance criteria required in the exact-RC record | Remaining stage |\n    40\t|---|---|---|\n    41\t| REQ-REL-003 | ACC-PLAT | Installed-RC platform and Node-version matrix |\n    42\t| REQ-AGT-002 | ACC-VER-03, ACC-VER-04, ACC-VER-09, ACC-QUAL-T2, ACC-QUAL-T3, ACC-QUAL-T4 | Installed-RC T2/T3/T4 outcome thresholds |\n    43\t| REQ-AGT-010 | ACC-TRUST-04 | Independent acceptance of the DEC-04 v1 subset |\n    44\t| REQ-PRV-003 | ACC-INF-10 | Installed-RC standa…1402 tokens truncated…red check in every cell. Automated CI or PTY runs do not substitute for operator evidence. [DEC-18](#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver) remains in force and waives screenshot artifacts only; it does not waive interaction, checks, per-cell verdicts, evidence records, or safety gates. No cell is accepted as complete without actual manual execution.\n   256\t\n   257\t**Disclosure.** Do not describe the manual matrix as waived. Until all fifteen cells have verified operator evidence, ACC-TUI-MANUAL remains incomplete and v1.0.0 acceptance remains blocked.\n   258\t\n   259\t**Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §5.3 / ACC-TUI-MANUAL; ACCEPTANCE §10 G6; SPEC-10 REQ-QUAL-108; `TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md`; PLAN-10 task 12; READINESS; release notes.\n   260\t\n   261\t## DEC-20: v1.0.0 manual terminal-matrix waiver\n   262\t\n   263\t**Status: accepted by the release owner, 2026-10-29.** This decision supersedes DEC-19 for v1.0.0.\n   264\t\n   265\t**Direction.** The manual five-terminal by three-size matrix in ACCEPTANCE §5.3 is waived for v1.0.0. No manual operator run, cell verdict, or per-cell evidence is required, and the waiver does not claim that any cell passed. The automated CI gate in §5.1 and the scripted installed-RC PTY gate in §5.2 remain mandatory and must pass.\n   266\t\n   267\t**Scope.** This waiver applies only to ACC-TUI-MANUAL and only for v1.0.0. It does not waive ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, exact-RC identity, any §5.1 or §5.2 scenario, safety checks, or any other release gate. DEC-18's screenshot-artifact waiver remains recorded; no screenshots are required for a matrix that is not run.\n   268\t\n   269\t**Qualification applicability:** REQ-QUAL-108 = ACC-TUI-STEER and ACC-TUI-A11Y remain required; ACC-TUI-MANUAL is waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20.\n   270\t\n   271\t**Disclosure.** Report ACC-TUI-MANUAL as waived by this decision, not passed and not outstanding. Preserve historical operator observations as observations only; do not promote them to cell results.\n   272\t\n   273\t**Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §§1.1, 3.1, 5, and 10; REQ-QUAL-108 exact-RC evidence mapping; stable v1.0.0 release notes; READINESS; terminal-matrix worksheet disposition.\n.git/nexus-claims/archived/REDACTED/owner.json:1:{\"agent\":\"codex-root\",\"host\":\"mike-dev\",\"branch\":\"codex/release-readiness-timestamp\",\"worktree\":\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/release-readiness-timestamp\",\"base\":\"cbb3b653a6bb6060071d8927e08e30d63765865e\",\"since\":\"2026-10-28T22:40:00Z\",\"scope\":\"Carry the independently accepted one-line correction to main CI completed_at in READINESS.md from merged PR310 onto a follow-up branch; docs-only; no push or publication.\"}\n.git/nexus-claims/archived/recovery-20261022T0238Z/readiness-post127/PLAN-10_READINESS_POST127-owner.json:8:  \"scope\": \"Refresh docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md current checkpoint after PR127; record exact current-main CI failure and CodeQL result without changing requirement status or treating scanner failures as passes\",\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18b4e-a8d9-78f0-bd60-966a1e9e4357","create_time":1793342021.9330728}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
