{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T06:33:44.186Z","ordinal":520686,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18b4e-a8d9-78f0-bd60-966a1e9e4357","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-933a4d9c-0eb3-4a9f-9992-c6d845a1a93b","process_id":"22391","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | nl -ba | sed -n '37,66p'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | nl -ba | sed -n '100,132p'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | nl -ba | sed -n '1,28p'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | nl -ba | sed -n '37,66p'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | nl -ba | sed -n '100,132p'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | nl -ba | sed -n '1,28p'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"    37\t### Qualification-only requirements for exact-RC enforcement\n    38\t\n    39\t| Requirement | Acceptance criteria required in the exact-RC record | Remaining stage |\n    40\t|---|---|---|\n    41\t| REQ-REL-003 | ACC-PLAT | Installed-RC platform and Node-version matrix |\n    42\t| REQ-AGT-002 | ACC-VER-03, ACC-VER-04, ACC-VER-09, ACC-QUAL-T2, ACC-QUAL-T3, ACC-QUAL-T4 | Installed-RC T2/T3/T4 outcome thresholds |\n    43\t| REQ-AGT-010 | ACC-TRUST-04 | Independent acceptance of the DEC-04 v1 subset |\n    44\t| REQ-PRV-003 | ACC-INF-10 | Installed-RC standalone and absent-gateway behavior |\n    45\t| REQ-REL-005 | ACC-SUP-04, ACC-SUP-05 | Exact-RC security and dependency artifact checks |\n    46\t| REQ-AGT-110 | ACC-CONT-10, ACC-GOV-06 | Installed-RC continuity and independent acceptance |\n    47\t| REQ-PRV-111 | ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC provider verification |\n    48\t| REQ-REL-114 | ACC-SUP-08 | Exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility |\n    49\t| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\n    50\t| REQ-QUAL-107 | ACC-PRV-STANDALONE, ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC standalone and provider matrix |\n    51\t| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y | Installed-RC automated and scripted PTY acceptance; the manual E3 matrix is waived by DEC-20 |\n    52\t| REQ-QUAL-109 | ACC-QUAL-T3 | Installed-RC T3 long-task qualification |\n    53\t<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:END -->\n    54\t\n    55\t<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:START -->\n    56\t### Approved exact-RC qualification exceptions\n    57\t\n    58\t| Requirement | Approved decision | Scope |\n    59\t|---|---|---|\n    60\t<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:END -->\n    61\t\n    62\t## 1. Rules\n    63\t\n    64\t1. The RC is built and published by the release workflow from a clean tag. Its version is identical across all components (REQ-REL-103).\n    65\t2. All qualification runs use the **installed RC package**, installed with the documented one-line command. They never use a checkout build. The only exception is CI unit and PTY suites, which run from source at the same commit.\n    66\t3. Thresholds (DEC-05) are frozen before the first M5 run. A failing gate is fixed in code and the run is repeated as `rc.N+1`. A threshold is never relaxed after results are known.\n   100\t| Verification | ACC-VER-01 to ACC-VER-09 | SPEC-11 |\n   101\t| Upgrade | ACC-UPG-01 to ACC-UPG-14 | SPEC-12 |\n   102\t\n   103\t\n   104\t### 3.1 Acceptance IDs defined in this file\n   105\t\n   106\tThese are retained commitments from REQUIREMENTS §2 and cross-cutting checks.\n   107\t\n   108\t| ID | Check | Pass condition |\n   109\t|---|---|---|\n   110\t| ACC-TUI-STEER | PTY: submit a task; while a tool runs, type steering text and press Enter; also queue a steer before a cancel | Steering is applied at the next step boundary. Unapplied steering is returned to the composer. Nothing is dropped silently (existing `sidecar_steering_diff` plus PTY s6). |\n   111\t| ACC-TUI-A11Y | PTY with `NO_COLOR=1` and with `TERM=dumb` at 40×14 and 100×30 | Zero colour SGR codes. Every state is distinguishable by glyph and word. Hints are complete at 40 columns (TUI-10). |\n   112\t| ACC-SEC-JAIL | `core/tests` plus harness-core calls with `..`, absolute, symlinked-file, symlinked-dir and symlinked-parent payloads | Every one is refused (C §4 R1 set). |\n   113\t| ACC-SEC-B6 | Re-run `docs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/repro/zz_trust_repro.test.ts`. Seeded-secret scan of `~/.nexus` and `.nexus` after a scripted turn. | Zero plaintext seeded secrets in durable stores or outbound bodies. |\n   114\t| ACC-PRV-LIVE | `nexus providers verify --provider <p> -m <pinned model> -j` for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06) | `passed: true`. Receipts archived. |\n   115\t| ACC-PRV-STANDALONE | §4.2 on the installed RC through the approved stripped proxy, with gateway credentials absent from the child environment | Every required profile completes through the proxy and the absent-gateway boundary holds; receipts archived. |\n   116\t| ACC-PLAT | E2 matrix, §7 | All rows pass. |\n   117\t| ACC-QUAL-T2 | §6.1 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n   118\t| ACC-QUAL-T3 | §6.3 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n   119\t| ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n   120\t| ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\n   121\t| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five terminal environments and three sizes | Waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20. No manual-cell execution or evidence is required, and no result is inferred. Automated §5.1 and scripted PTY §5.2 remain mandatory. |\n   122\t\n   123\t## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\n   124\t\n   125\t### 4.1 Clean-HOME procedure\n   126\t\n   127\t1. `export HOME=$(mktemp -d)`.\n   128\t2. Install the RC with the documented command.\n   129\t3. Create `~/.config/nexus/config.env` containing only:\n   130\t   - `LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:<proxy>/v1`\n   131\t   - `LOCAL_LLM_MODEL=<id as listed by the proxy>`\n   132\t   - `LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY=REDACTED\n     1\t# v1.0.0 release readiness checkpoint\n     2\t\n     3\t## Terminal waiver disposition update (reconciled 2026-10-29 19:32 UTC)\n     4\t\n     5\tThe release owner accepted DEC-20: the manual five-terminal by three-size matrix in Acceptance §5.3 is waived for v1.0.0. No operator runs, cell verdicts, or per-cell results are required or inferred. Automated CI checks (§5.1) and scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios (§5.2) remain mandatory. The dated checkpoint below refreshes the release, PR, CI, and custody status; older checkpoint sections remain historical evidence.\n     6\t\n     7\t## Current convergence checkpoint (observed 2026-10-29 19:32 UTC)\n     8\t\n     9\t- **Authoritative source and CI:** Release convergence follows `origin/main` at `8d71e1a9207bf05baa54aa6bdfa121697469c9eb`, PR #328's merge. `origin/v1/integration` remains at `7d6673f108316dda015b858c85b2abe20f3a4f78` and is not the current release tip. Main CI run [40940653473](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40940653473) and CodeQL run [40940653572](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40940653572) are in progress on exact `8d71e1a`; Node 22/24 are building the release core. Earlier green results on `fe1c91d` are not evidence for this new main SHA.\n    10\t- **Source gates:** On a clean worktree at exact `8d71e1a`, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed: 123 rows, 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; the 12 exact-RC qualification deferrals remain unchanged. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` passed with all components at `1.0.0-rc.11`. These are source-stage results only.\n    11\t- **PR #318 evaluator remediation:** The pushed PR head is `eec83d6703ce5449ae868d67d1e3c906e7d3d00a`; focused `eval_integrity` and `eval_hardened` tests passed 48/48 after clean `npm ci`, CLI build, Rust release-core build, and isolated HOME/XDG/TMPDIR. No held-out tasks were used. Exact-head CI run [40940623810](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40940623810) is still running Node 22/24; CodeQL and JavaScript/TypeScript checks passed. The PR must be rebased onto `8d71e1a` and pass fresh exact-head review/checks before integration.\n    12\t- **Terminal gates:** DEC-20 waives only the manual §5.3 matrix; it is waived, not passed, and no manual cells are required. Automated CI PTY §5.1 and installed-RC scripted PTY §5.2 remain mandatory. The latest public release is RC10; its scripted PTY record is `PARTIAL_NOT_ACCEPTED`, including a 27.89-second cancellation-idle outlier. No accepted §5.2 result exists for an RC11 artifact because RC11 has not been published.\n    13\t- **Held-out custody:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned; its latest public update reports T2 at 20/40 tasks and no fresh custody acceptance. T3's reported 8/8 is digest/schema/isolation metadata, not qualification acceptance. Public records identify the prior custodian only as the `opencode` primary session; they do not identify a human custodian. SageBridge was named as a contact, but no new custody acceptance is recorded. No private payload was accessed or run.\n    14\t- **PR and release state:** PR #328 is merged. PR #318 remains open and pending refreshed exact-head CI. PR #327 remains open; Node 22/24, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL passed, while Entire Gates failed. Public releases still end at `v1.0.0-rc.10`; RC11 and stable `v1.0.0` are unpublished. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; provider and standalone matrices, held-out T2/T3/T4, cross-runner reproducibility, long-task/fault-injection, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete.\n    15\t- **Next executable steps:** Let the current-main and PR #318 CI runs finish; rebase PR #318 onto `8d71e1a`, obtain fresh exact-head review/checks, and integrate through the normal process. Continue the custodian handoff without exposing private material. Construct the next RC only after pre-RC gates pass, then execute all mandatory exact-RC gates, including §5.1 and §5.2, followed by independent acceptance.\n    16\t\n    17\t## Historical checkpoint (observed 2026-10-29 06:18 UTC; superseded for terminal disposition by DEC-20 above)\n    18\t\n    19\t**Authoritative source and CI:** `origin/main` is `a0356c4d8f0f0b9b943d4033aff59795fcab83b4`, merging PR #319 atop `6b786d54dd5bf60234c67fec6ef070c62af9b141`. `origin/v1/integration` remains at `7d6673f108316dda015b858c85b2abe20f3a4f78`, an ancestor of main. Pre-merge main CodeQL run [40822684525](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40822684525) and CI run [40822684551](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40822684551) passed on `6b786d54`. Post-merge CI [40828157972](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40828157972) and CodeQL [40828157982](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40828157982) are in progress on exact main `a0356c4d8f0f0b9b943d4033aff59795fcab83b4`.\n    20\t\n    21\t**Requirements and version:** On exact `origin/main` `a0356c4d8f0f0b9b943d4033aff59795fcab83b4`, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed: 123 rows, 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 remain deferred to exact-RC qualification: REQ-AGT-002, REQ-AGT-010, REQ-PRV-003, REQ-REL-003, REQ-REL-005, REQ-AGT-110, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-REL-114, REQ-QUAL-101, REQ-QUAL-107, REQ-QUAL-108 and REQ-QUAL-109. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` passes at `1.0.0-rc.10`. These are source-stage checks, not installed-RC acceptance.\n    22\t\n    23\t**Open source changes:** PR [#319](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/319), head `668721d8135d3a3332bca27b820caa5a4a76c7af`, merged as `a0356c4d8f0f0b9b943d4033aff59795fcab83b4` after its independent `ACCEPT` review and required Node 22/24/Linux, JS/TS, and CodeQL checks passed. Its post-merge CI and CodeQL checks are running. PR [#318](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/318), head `2c532d701c5b84b0d3308b02897520337addc36b`, has independent `ACCEPT` source review, but both Node matrix jobs failed because `eval_hardened.test.ts` could not find `go` while testing hidden-source isolation (exit 127); Linux was skipped. This is a CI toolchain-provisioning gap, not evaluator qualification evidence. PR [#322](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/322), head `d53caea7c480c5e88dff43c6e5d4cb8a16868400`, adds CI-only pinned Go/Rust toolchain provisioning and has independent `ACCEPT` review; its Node 22/24, JS/TS, and CodeQL checks pass, with Linux still running. PR [#320](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/320), head `2124538d21b84454319c5485140b266f11510a5a`, has independent `ACCEPT` review and passing Node 22/24, JS/TS, and CodeQL checks; Linux remains in progress. PR [#321](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/321) refreshes this checkpoint and has been rebased onto the new main; the previous head's checks do not qualify the rebased candidate, which requires fresh exact-head checks and independent review. None of PRs #318, #320, #321 or #322 is merged.\n    24\t\n    25\t**Held-out custody and qualification:** The latest public metadata update on issue #1 (06:02 UTC) records unresolved custody ownership: a historical handoff log names SageBridge as an accepted successor, while the active custody record still names OpenCode. The latest posted T2 count is 20/40 tasks; no new custody acceptance or qualification result is recorded. T3's reported 8/8 covers digest/schema/isolation metadata, not task-quality qualification. The custodian identity and acknowledged transfer must be reconciled before qualification. No private payloads were accessed by implementation work. T2/T3/T4 held-out qualification, standalone/provider acceptance, long-task/fault-injection qualification, and successor-RC cross-runner reproducibility remain incomplete.\n    26\t\n    27\t**Terminal and release gates:** Acceptance §5.3 requires actual operator execution for xterm, kitty with keyboard protocol, tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal, and GNOME Terminal, each at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60. There are **0/15 accepted cells**. The operator's partial RC10 report says the client rendered at tested sizes except tmux inside GNOME Terminal, which could not be resized below 43×13; other results “seemed okay.” The report lacks test time, exact installed artifact identity, terminal versions, and per-cell check outcomes, so it does not complete any cell. Automated PTY results do not count. `ubuntu-desktop` at `10.0.8.3` has the required terminal programs; the successor RC is not yet available for the matrix. Screenshots are waived by DEC-18 only; all interactive checks and per-cell verdicts remain mandatory under DEC-19. The latest public release at this checkpoint is `v1.0.0-rc.10`; the selected distribution target is the GitHub installer, not npm. No stable `v1.0.0` release exists.\n    28\t\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":27603}},"started_at_ms":1793342024185,"completed_at_ms":1793342024186}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T06:33:44.883Z","ordinal":520687,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18b83-acb3-7572-b68b-4dbd78503e8f","call_id":"call_4dfd1eb05c8144d3aab150a840d05b57","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 3498)\nTotal output lines: 91\n\n    37\t### Qualification-only requirements for exact-RC enforcement\n    38\t\n    39\t| Requirement | Acceptance criteria required in the exact-RC record | Remaining stage |\n    40\t|---|---|---|\n    41\t| REQ-REL-003 | ACC-PLAT | Installed-RC platform and Node-version matrix |\n    42\t| REQ-AGT-002 | ACC-VER-03, ACC-VER-04, ACC-VER-09, ACC-QUAL-T2, ACC-QUAL-T3, ACC-QUAL-T4 | Installed-RC T2/T3/T4 outcome thresholds |\n    43\t| REQ-AGT-010 | ACC-TRUST-04 | Independent acceptance of the DEC-04 v1 subset |\n    44\t| REQ-PRV-003 | ACC-INF-10 | Installed-RC standalone and absent-gateway behavior |\n    45\t| REQ-REL-005 | ACC-SUP-04, ACC-SUP-05 | Exact-RC security and dependency artifact checks |\n    46\t| REQ-AGT-110 | ACC-CONT-10, ACC-GOV-06 | Installed-RC continuity and independent acceptance |\n    47\t| REQ-PRV-111 | ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC provider verification |\n    48\t| REQ-REL-114 | ACC-SUP-08 | Exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility |\n    49\t| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\n    50\t| REQ-QUAL-107 | ACC-PRV-STANDALONE, ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC standalone and provider matrix |\n    51\t| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y | Installed-RC automated and scripted PTY acceptance; the manual E3 matrix is waived by DEC-20 |\n    52\t| REQ-QUAL-109 | ACC-QUAL-T3 | Installed-RC T3 long-task qualification |\n    53\t<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:END -->\n    54\t\n    55\t<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:START -->\n    56\t### Approved exact-RC qualification exceptions\n    57\t\n    58\t| Requirement | Approved decision | Scope |\n    59\t|---|---|---|\n    60\t<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:END -->\n    61\t\n    62\t## 1. Rules\n    63\t\n    64\t1. The RC is built and published by the release workflow from a clean tag. Its version is identical across all components (REQ-REL-103).\n    65\t2. All qualification runs use the **installed RC package**, installed with the documented one-line command. They never use a checkout build. The only exception is CI unit and PTY suites, which run from source at the same commit.\n    66\t3. Thresholds (DEC-05) are frozen before the first M5 run. A failing gate is fixed in code and the run is repeated as `rc.N+1`. A threshold is never relaxed after results are known.\n   100\t| Verification | ACC-VER-01 to ACC-VER-09 | SPEC-11 |\n   101\t| Upgrade | ACC-UPG-01 to ACC-UPG-14 | SPEC-12 |\n   102\t\n   103\t\n   104\t### 3.1 Acceptance IDs defined in this file\n   105\t\n   106\tThese are retained commitments from REQUIREMENTS §2 and cross-cutting checks.\n   107\t\n   108\t| ID | Check | Pass condition |\n   109\t|---|---|---|\n   110\t| A…2198 tokens truncated…ode/pull/322), head `d53caea7c480c5e88dff43c6e5d4cb8a16868400`, adds CI-only pinned Go/Rust toolchain provisioning and has independent `ACCEPT` review; its Node 22/24, JS/TS, and CodeQL checks pass, with Linux still running. PR [#320](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/320), head `2124538d21b84454319c5485140b266f11510a5a`, has independent `ACCEPT` review and passing Node 22/24, JS/TS, and CodeQL checks; Linux remains in progress. PR [#321](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/321) refreshes this checkpoint and has been rebased onto the new main; the previous head's checks do not qualify the rebased candidate, which requires fresh exact-head checks and independent review. None of PRs #318, #320, #321 or #322 is merged.\n    24\t\n    25\t**Held-out custody and qualification:** The latest public metadata update on issue #1 (06:02 UTC) records unresolved custody ownership: a historical handoff log names SageBridge as an accepted successor, while the active custody record still names OpenCode. The latest posted T2 count is 20/40 tasks; no new custody acceptance or qualification result is recorded. T3's reported 8/8 covers digest/schema/isolation metadata, not task-quality qualification. The custodian identity and acknowledged transfer must be reconciled before qualification. No private payloads were accessed by implementation work. T2/T3/T4 held-out qualification, standalone/provider acceptance, long-task/fault-injection qualification, and successor-RC cross-runner reproducibility remain incomplete.\n    26\t\n    27\t**Terminal and release gates:** Acceptance §5.3 requires actual operator execution for xterm, kitty with keyboard protocol, tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal, and GNOME Terminal, each at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60. There are **0/15 accepted cells**. The operator's partial RC10 report says the client rendered at tested sizes except tmux inside GNOME Terminal, which could not be resized below 43×13; other results “seemed okay.” The report lacks test time, exact installed artifact identity, terminal versions, and per-cell check outcomes, so it does not complete any cell. Automated PTY results do not count. `ubuntu-desktop` at `10.0.8.3` has the required terminal programs; the successor RC is not yet available for the matrix. Screenshots are waived by DEC-18 only; all interactive checks and per-cell verdicts remain mandatory under DEC-19. The latest public release at this checkpoint is `v1.0.0-rc.10`; the selected distribution target is the GitHub installer, not npm. No stable `v1.0.0` release exists.\n    28\t\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18b4e-a8d9-78f0-bd60-966a1e9e4357","create_time":1793342024.8833296}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
