{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T06:33:57.788Z","ordinal":520709,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18b4e-a8d9-78f0-bd60-966a1e9e4357","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-8b0cfe2e-1436-4ec2-9f1d-e06a238b9b23","process_id":"99778","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc11-cross-runner-evidence show HEAD:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | nl -ba | sed -n '1,35p'; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc11-cross-runner-evidence show --stat --oneline HEAD"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc11-cross-runner-evidence show HEAD:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | nl -ba | sed -n '1,35p'; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc11-cross-runner-evidence show --stat --oneline HEAD"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"     1\t# v1.0.0 release readiness checkpoint\n     2\t\n     3\t## Current convergence checkpoint (observed 2026-10-30 05:38 UTC)\n     4\t\n     5\t- **Authoritative source and RC:** `origin/main` is `1acff70018c00c2459c388f34dfb2997b8b4d7c6`; PR #341 merged at this exact commit and tag `v1.0.0-rc.13` points to it. In a clean detached worktree at the tag with isolated HOME/XDG, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed (123 rows; 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 exact-RC qualification deferrals) and `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check --tag v1.0.0-rc.13` passed. The RC13 release workflow [41009328850](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/41009328850) was still packaging; no RC13 asset or installed-RC evidence was available at this checkpoint. No stable `v1.0.0` release exists.\n     6\t- **Post-merge CI:** CI [41009312010](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/41009312010) on exact `1acff700` remained active in Node 22 and Node 24 test matrices. The release workflow and CI were running the runner setup and test stages; neither had a final conclusion.\n     7\t- **Evaluator source PR #335:** exact head `391f49bcddb75e63d73b232b3cdec88a17fd6f66`, based on `38a875cc`; Node 22 and Node 24 passed, CodeQL [41005410293](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/41005410293) passed, and the Linux packaging/reproducibility job in CI [41005410294](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/41005410294) remained active. This PR was open and not integrated; its checks are bound to its stale base and must not be combined with current-main evidence.\n     8\t- **RC11 historical evidence:** exact RC11 cross-runner evidence remains limited to RC11. Existing RC11 provider and scripted-PTY packets are historical and do not qualify RC13. They are not substitutes for installed-RC13 provider or §5.2 runs.\n     9\t- **Held-out custody:** public Issue #1 was last updated at 04:28:47 UTC with no fresh custodian acceptance. The protected corpus claim remains separate; no private payloads or validators were accessed, and T2/T3 qualification has not started.\n    10\t- **Terminal and acceptance gates:** DEC-20 waives manual §5.3 for v1.0.0. Automated §5.1 and scripted installed-RC §5.2 remain mandatory. T2/T3/T4, long-task and fault-injection, installed-RC provider/standalone qualification, exact-RC cross-runner qualification, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain open. Acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; no stable `v1.0.0` release is claimed.\n    11\t\n    12\t**Next execution:** verify and install the exact RC13 workflow artifact once the release run completes, then execute all unblocked artifact-bound checks. Continue PR #335 through its owner and exact-head checks. Keep held-out qualification stopped until custodian acceptance.\n    13\t## Terminal waiver disposition update (reconciled 2026-10-29 19:32 UTC)\n    14\t\n    15\tThe release owner accepted DEC-20: the manual five-terminal by three-size matrix in Acceptance §5.3 is waived for v1.0.0. No operator runs, cell verdicts, or per-cell results are required or inferred. Automated CI checks (§5.1) and scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios (§5.2) remain mandatory. The dated checkpoint below refreshes the release, PR, CI, and custody status; older checkpoint sections remain historical evidence.\n    16\t\n    17\t## Current convergence checkpoint (observed 2026-10-29 19:32 UTC)\n    18\t\n    19\t- **Authoritative source and CI:** Release convergence follows `origin/main` at `8d71e1a9207bf05baa54aa6bdfa121697469c9eb`, PR #328's merge. `origin/v1/integration` remains at `7d6673f108316dda015b858c85b2abe20f3a4f78` and is not the current release tip. Main CI run [40940653473](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40940653473) and CodeQL run [40940653572](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40940653572) are in progress on exact `8d71e1a`; Node 22/24 are building the release core. Earlier green results on `fe1c91d` are not evidence for this new main SHA.\n    20\t- **Source gates:** On a clean worktree at exact `8d71e1a`, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed: 123 rows, 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; the 12 exact-RC qualification deferrals remain unchanged. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` passed with all components at `1.0.0-rc.11`. These are source-stage results only.\n    21\t- **PR #318 evaluator remediation:** The pushed PR head is `eec83d6703ce5449ae868d67d1e3c906e7d3d00a`; focused `eval_integrity` and `eval_hardened` tests passed 48/48 after clean `npm ci`, CLI build, Rust release-core build, and isolated HOME/XDG/TMPDIR. No held-out tasks were used. Exact-head CI run [40940623810](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40940623810) is still running Node 22/24; CodeQL and JavaScript/TypeScript checks passed. The PR must be rebased onto `8d71e1a` and pass fresh exact-head review/checks before integration.\n    22\t- **Terminal gates:** DEC-20 waives only the manual §5.3 matrix; it is waived, not passed, and no manual cells are required. Automated CI PTY §5.1 and installed-RC scripted PTY §5.2 remain mandatory. The latest public release is RC10; its scripted PTY record is `PARTIAL_NOT_ACCEPTED`, including a 27.89-second cancellation-idle outlier. No accepted §5.2 result exists for an RC11 artifact because RC11 has not been published.\n    23\t- **Held-out custody:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned; its latest public update reports T2 at 20/40 tasks and no fresh custody acceptance. T3's reported 8/8 is digest/schema/isolation metadata, not qualification acceptance. Public records identify the prior custodian only as the `opencode` primary session; they do not identify a human custodian. SageBridge was named as a contact, but no new custody acceptance is recorded. No private payload was accessed or run.\n    24\t- **PR and release state:** PR #328 is merged. PR #318 remains open and pending refreshed exact-head CI. PR #327 remains open; Node 22/24, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL passed, while Entire Gates failed. Public releases still end at `v1.0.0-rc.10`; RC11 and stable `v1.0.0` are unpublished. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; provider and standalone matrices, held-out T2/T3/T4, cross-runner reproducibility, long-task/fault-injection, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete.\n    25\t- **Next executable steps:** Let the current-main and PR #318 CI runs finish; rebase PR #318 onto `8d71e1a`, obtain fresh exact-head review/checks, and integrate through the normal process. Continue the custodian handoff without exposing private material. Construct the next RC only after pre-RC gates pass, then execute all mandatory exact-RC gates, including §5.1 and §5.2, followed by independent acceptance.\n    26\t\n    27\t## Historical checkpoint (observed 2026-10-29 06:18 UTC; superseded for terminal disposition by DEC-20 above)\n    28\t\n    29\t**Authoritative source and CI:** `origin/main` is `a0356c4d8f0f0b9b943d4033aff59795fcab83b4`, merging PR #319 atop `6b786d54dd5bf60234c67fec6ef070c62af9b141`. `origin/v1/integration` remains at `7d6673f108316dda015b858c85b2abe20f3a4f78`, an ancestor of main. Pre-merge main CodeQL run [40822684525](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40822684525) and CI run [40822684551](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40822684551) passed on `6b786d54`. Post-merge CI [40828157972](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40828157972) and CodeQL [40828157982](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40828157982) are in progress on exact main `a0356c4d8f0f0b9b943d4033aff59795fcab83b4`.\n    30\t\n    31\t**Requirements and version:** On exact `origin/main` `a0356c4d8f0f0b9b943d4033aff59795fcab83b4`, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed: 123 rows, 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 remain deferred to exact-RC qualification: REQ-AGT-002, REQ-AGT-010, REQ-PRV-003, REQ-REL-003, REQ-REL-005, REQ-AGT-110, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-REL-114, REQ-QUAL-101, REQ-QUAL-107, REQ-QUAL-108 and REQ-QUAL-109. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` passes at `1.0.0-rc.10`. These are source-stage checks, not installed-RC acceptance.\n    32\t\n    33\t**Open source changes:** PR [#319](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/319), head `668721d8135d3a3332bca27b820caa5a4a76c7af`, merged as `a0356c4d8f0f0b9b943d4033aff59795fcab83b4` after its independent `ACCEPT` review and required Node 22/24/Linux, JS/TS, and CodeQL checks passed. Its post-merge CI and CodeQL checks are running. PR [#318](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/318), head `2c532d701c5b84b0d3308b02897520337addc36b`, has independent `ACCEPT` source review, but both Node matrix jobs failed because `eval_hardened.test.ts` could not find `go` while testing hidden-source isolation (exit 127); Linux was skipped. This is a CI toolchain-provisioning gap, not evaluator qualification evidence. PR [#322](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/322), head `d53caea7c480c5e88dff43c6e5d4cb8a16868400`, adds CI-only pinned Go/Rust toolchain provisioning and has independent `ACCEPT` review; its Node 22/24, JS/TS, and CodeQL checks pass, with Linux still running. PR [#320](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/320), head `2124538d21b84454319c5485140b266f11510a5a`, has independent `ACCEPT` review and passing Node 22/24, JS/TS, and CodeQL checks; Linux remains in progress. PR [#321](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/321) refreshes this checkpoint and has been rebased onto the new main; the previous head's checks do not qualify the rebased candidate, which requires fresh exact-head checks and independent review. None of PRs #318, #320, #321 or #322 is merged.\n    34\t\n    35\t**Held-out custody and qualification:** The latest public metadata update on issue #1 (06:02 UTC) records unresolved custody ownership: a historical handoff log names SageBridge as an accepted successor, while the active custody record still names OpenCode. The latest posted T2 count is 20/40 tasks; no new custody acceptance or qualification result is recorded. T3's reported 8/8 covers digest/schema/isolation metadata, not task-quality qualification. The custodian identity and acknowledged transfer must be reconciled before qualification. No private payloads were accessed by implementation work. T2/T3/T4 held-out qualification, standalone/provider acceptance, long-task/fault-injection qualification, and successor-RC cross-runner reproducibility remain incomplete.\nba2b2a91 docs(release): refresh RC13 qualification checkpoint\n docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | 24 +++++++++++-------------\n 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":43796}},"started_at_ms":1793342037788,"completed_at_ms":1793342037788}}
