{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T06:34:50.439Z","ordinal":520763,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18b4e-a8d9-78f0-bd60-966a1e9e4357","session_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","root_turn_id":"01a18b4e-a8d9-78f0-bd60-966a1e9e4357","response_id":"resp_0db389702a7164cc016ae43a88668c819f870d1afbe4efe40f","usage":{"input_tokens":63156,"cached_input_tokens":60160,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":139,"reasoning_output_tokens":30,"total_tokens":63295},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":37895169,"cached_input_tokens":37651968,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":95525,"reasoning_output_tokens":56378,"total_tokens":37990694},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":9800484797,"cached_input_tokens":9696708480,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":28180017,"reasoning_output_tokens":16574105,"total_tokens":9828664814}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T06:34:50.693Z","ordinal":520764,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18b4e-a8d9-78f0-bd60-966a1e9e4357","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-638b741f-ea3f-4a80-81ee-6e5705eb0bb8","process_id":"41770","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n \"Nexus|RC13|PR335|release convergence\" /home/mike/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'Nexus|RC13|PR335|release convergence' /home/mike/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md","query":"Nexus|RC13|PR335|release convergence","path":"MEMORY.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"1:# Task Group: Nexus Code client release and Cloudflare contest publication\n2:scope: Package the installed Nexus Code Linux client and prepare the distinct Nexus Workers/Artifacts contest submission in `/home/mike/nexus-code`; retain separate readiness dispositions and do not treat CI or offline fixtures as a clean-account proof.\n15:## Task 2: Package Nexus Code as a complete Linux client with installer and CI, partial\n27:- for Cloudflare contest work, the user required using the existing repository, preserving unrelated history/work, and distinguishing the Nexus Code client from the Cloudflare Workers/Artifacts submission -> do not replace repositories or wholesale-integrate unaccepted candidates. [Task 1]\n34:- Contest-specific CI passed at `ce7e58b9ce3f6e4a72f84d205c5319b241ca0aa9` in workflow `38471712649`; it covered demo tests and Worker build/typecheck, not a real Cloudflare account run. The service is the submission; Nexus Code is its client/demo harness. [Task 1]\n45:# Task Group: Nexus agent effectiveness: unbounded continuation and evidence-bounded diagnosis\n46:scope: Review failed Nexus agent exports and maintain prompt/regression safeguards for progressing continuation loops, direct diagnostic questions, and timeout claims in `/home/mike/nexus-code`.\n57:- Nexus, nexus-session-session_20261014_091558_9m78.json, CONTEXT_CAPACITY_EXCEEDED, 54582+8192+4096>65536, make test, timeout, truncated output, direct status question, evidence-bounded diagnosis\n108:- Flash-Next Q-TOOLS passed 7/7 synthetic categories and 20/20 Nexus replay points. Q-LONGCTX passed probes from 16K through 59,913 tokens; a 67,335-token input was rejected with HTTP 400 in 0.14s. Both selected models passed production qualification after reboot and rollback restoration. [Task 1]\n146:# Task Group: Nexus dogfood-blockers independent candidate review and compaction evidence integrity\n147:scope: Review-only, isolated validation of `fix/dogfood-blockers` candidates against Nexus baseline; use before selecting an I1/objective-supervisor base or relying on context admission, unseen-result, or modified-file evidence.\n158:- Nexus, fix/dogfood-blockers, 6b34f5f, 2860228, 6f71043, 6845415, unseen tool results, CONTEXT_CAPACITY_EXCEEDED, compaction, modified files, repeated tool-call IDs, editedPaths, editChangedFile, EALLOWSCRIPTS\n168:- Nexus, fix/dogfood-blockers, 1b71e27, 2860228, MAX_READ_LINES, StreamRedactor, tester.ts, verifier baseline, BASELINE_FAILURES_ONLY, EALLOWSCRIPTS, native Git metadata\n172:- for review-only candidate work, the user required: “Do not modify Nexus source”, “use a scratch copy”, “If something is wrong, REPORT IT”, and preserve the operator’s dirty tree -> isolate builds/tests, preserve negative results, and report rather than remediate. [Task 1]\n192:# Task Group: Nexus architecture reconnaissance and context-engineering baseline\n193:scope: Strictly read-only mapping of Nexus information/context flow, durable state, admission, and validation; use when the requested deliverable is an architecture investigation rather than remediation or design work.\n196:## Task 1: Capture baseline for the intended A-I Nexus architecture reconnaissance, incomplete\n204:- Nexus, read-only, architecture reconnaissance, context-engineering, CURRENT-NEXUS-CONTEXT-ARCHITECTURE.md, 2860228, linear transcript resend, context admission, deterministic compaction, durable session state, no context router\n208:- for Nexus reconnaissance, the user required “read-only” and “do not modify source, tests, configuration, documentation, dependencies, Git state” -> preserve scope, record exact snapshot SHA plus concurrent-change risk, and do not implement optimization or prove a preferred theory. [Task 1]\n220:# Task Group: Nexus live Ratatui TUI review and redaction/observer isolation\n240:- At reviewed HEAD `2860228`, Nexus had moved from a snapshot viewer to a live Ratatui client: multiline composer, approval overlays, slash commands, cancellation, tool-detail/evidence panels, receipt panels, and default TUI launch in a terminal. `--repl` remains the readline fallback. [Task 1]\n251:# Task Group: Nexus CRED-003 FlightRecorder and audit-log credential sanitization\n283:# Task Group: Nexus Cloudflare Artifacts capability, agent-native collaboration, and contest evidence\n327:## Task 5: Prepare the Nexus Workers/Artifacts contest submission, partial\n342:- for contest preparation, the user required the existing target repository and unrelated work/history to be preserved; distinguish Nexus Code (client/harness) from Nexus (the submitted service), and never present offline fixtures as real Cloudflare evidence. [Task 5]\n349:- Artifacts should own Git persistence, refs, objects, transport, isolation, forks, and repository token handling; Nexus/collaboration logic should own actor/task authority, intent, semantic contention, validation freshness, acceptance, and provenance. Textual overlap is not duplicate intent, clean merge is not semantic correctness, and ancestry is not authorization or acceptance. Prefer experiments with versioned work statements, exact candidate/evidence links, source/confidence/freshness relevance signals, state-change notifications, and explicit dispositions; avoid all-to-all broadcast reasoning. [Task 2]\n352:- Proposed minimum product: a Worker coordinates two isolated external Nexus runners, uses real Artifacts repositories/forks from one baseline, records exact-SHA validation/review, captures operator disposition, and integrates only the accepted candidate. Durable Objects fit serialized per-run coordination; external Nexus processes should perform shell/Git work rather than running the local agent in Workers. First implementation proof: create/import repository, issue a short-lived scoped token, clone/push a commit, then read that exact commit back. [Task 4]\n366:# Task Group: Nexus Phase 2 independent requirements and architecture review\n370:## Task 1: Independently review Nexus Phase 2 requirements, accepted with recorded concerns for Phase 2S\n378:- Nexus, issue-12, Phase-2, Phase-2S, ACCEPT_WITH_RECORDED_CONCERNS_FOR_PHASE_2S, CAP, AUTH, CTX, DATA, UI, EXEC-001, capability-identity, full-access, context-admission, sensitive-data, no-remote\n580:# Task Group: Nexus v1 CI prerequisite integration and release qualification handoff\n581:scope: Integrate reviewed CI prerequisites and accurately track Nexus v1 release gates, claims, and held-out boundaries; use for `v1/integration` readiness work, not as a substitute for exact-RC qualification.\n592:- Nexus v1, PR #10, bdc705e593def11ee5e44a6ebd0703b57e5953a0, CI 39085388798, v1/integration, 2c70d39ad4f9c29cff04c909eef9de6d2a29bdb2, check_requirements.mjs --enforce, REQ-QUAL-101, ACCEPTANCE.md, CONCURRENCY.md\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":37704}},"started_at_ms":1793342090692,"completed_at_ms":1793342090693}}
