{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T06:43:50.758Z","ordinal":521197,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18b4e-a8d9-78f0-bd60-966a1e9e4357","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae43ca362e0819f90aa013f76765d9f","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"## Convergence update\n\n**Campaign:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`  \n**Acceptance:** `IN_PROGRESS`\n\n- Requirements enforcement passed on exact `origin/main` `1acff700`. Twelve requirements remain explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification; source-gate success does not qualify an RC.\n- RC13 release run `41009328850` is still in the CLI test step, and no RC13 release asset is available. Main CI `41009312010` is also still in the CLI suite.\n- PR #335 head `d01b25c` has CodeQL and JS/TS passing. Its fresh Node 22/24 suites are running. The earlier candidate’s full CI passed, but PR #335 remains blocked by its required independent Entire approval; I did not approve it or bypass that gate.\n- Held-out custody remains protected and unaccepted. The latest public issue update still reports 20/40 T2 tasks; no held-out qualification has started.\n- The manual terminal matrix waiver remains in effect under DEC-20. Scripted installed-RC PTY checks remain required.\n- The local endpoint setup path exists in current main: the TUI connection list includes the appliance entry, and the model-picker E2E test checks that it appears before cloud providers ([models.rs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/pr335-release-parity-combination/core/src/bin/nexus_tui/models.rs:301), [tui_model_picker_e2e.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/pr335-release-parity-combination/cli/test/tui_model_picker_e2e.test.ts:121)). This does not establish behavior in an installed RC.\n\nI refreshed the suite claim and claims log with the active run IDs. The shared dirty checkout remains untouched. Next I’m waiting on these exact CI runs; after they conclude, I’ll proceed with the resulting remediation or RC artifact checks. No stable release or RC acceptance is claimed.\n\nThe remaining external blockers are the required reviewer approval for PR #335 and custodian acceptance of the held-out corpus. I’m not requesting either again in this update.\n\n"}],"phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":{"entries":[{"path":"MEMORY.md","lineStart":580,"lineEnd":605,"note":"used prior guidance to keep source CI distinct from exact-RC qualification and acceptance"}],"rolloutIds":["019a0000-0000-7000-8000-000000000000"]}},"started_at_ms":1793342627501,"completed_at_ms":1793342630757}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T06:43:50.762Z","ordinal":521198,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","status":"completed","id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae43ca362e0819f90aa013f76765d9f","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"## Convergence update\n\n**Campaign:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`  \n**Acceptance:** `IN_PROGRESS`\n\n- Requirements enforcement passed on exact `origin/main` `1acff700`. Twelve requirements remain explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification; source-gate success does not qualify an RC.\n- RC13 release run `41009328850` is still in the CLI test step, and no RC13 release asset is available. Main CI `41009312010` is also still in the CLI suite.\n- PR #335 head `d01b25c` has CodeQL and JS/TS passing. Its fresh Node 22/24 suites are running. The earlier candidate’s full CI passed, but PR #335 remains blocked by its required independent Entire approval; I did not approve it or bypass that gate.\n- Held-out custody remains protected and unaccepted. The latest public issue update still reports 20/40 T2 tasks; no held-out qualification has started.\n- The manual terminal matrix waiver remains in effect under DEC-20. Scripted installed-RC PTY checks remain required.\n- The local endpoint setup path exists in current main: the TUI connection list includes the appliance entry, and the model-picker E2E test checks that it appears before cloud providers ([models.rs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/pr335-release-parity-combination/core/src/bin/nexus_tui/models.rs:301), [tui_model_picker_e2e.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/pr335-release-parity-combination/cli/test/tui_model_picker_e2e.test.ts:121)). This does not establish behavior in an installed RC.\n\nI refreshed the suite claim and claims log with the active run IDs. The shared dirty checkout remains untouched. Next I’m waiting on these exact CI runs; after they conclude, I’ll proceed with the resulting remediation or RC artifact checks. No stable release or RC acceptance is claimed.\n\nThe 