{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T06:45:49.575Z","ordinal":521312,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18b8d-60e7-7130-962f-f0eb9e68c409","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae43d18ec60819fb6ebda385577f09d","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The cancelled CI logs clarify the hang: on the old source, evaluator preflight failed closed in tests 310/312/314/315 and test 351. Test 351 then failed before closing its local HTTP listener, leaving the test process alive. PR #335’s earlier head passed the full Linux suite after the compiler-scan fix; the current corrected head is running its own exact suites now. I’ve recorded the old failures as failures and the hang as a consequence, not as a pass or unrelated infrastructure issue."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1793342744944,"completed_at_ms":1793342749575}}
