{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T06:45:59.864Z","ordinal":521324,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18b8d-60e7-7130-962f-f0eb9e68c409","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae43d27c0b4819f88a555411d0c6709","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"Correction: I traced test 351’s control flow more carefully. Its first `runIsolated` call happens before the test creates the local HTTP listener, so that failure cannot leave that listener open. The exact log proves the compiler-exposure failure and subsequent process hang, but not the hang’s resource leak source. I’m correcting the coordination record; the independent hang cause remains unresolved pending the corrected candidate’s full-suite result."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1793342759779,"completed_at_ms":1793342759864}}
