{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T06:46:02.138Z","ordinal":521326,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0db389702a7164cc016ae43d27d624819f86c6b54a1a015756","status":"completed","call_id":"call_c5e1a2300b3847e598af1e405d3080ba","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"python3 - <<'PY'\\nimport json\\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nroot=Path('/home/mike/nexus-code/.git')\\nstamp=datetime.now(timezone.utc).strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ')\\nlog=root/'nexus-claims.log'\\nwith log.open('a') as f:\\n f.write(f'{stamp} CI_FAILURE_CORRECTION RC13_test351 first runIsolated occurs before test creates networkServer; earlier log attribution to this listener leak was incorrect and is superseded. Exact logs establish fail-closed compiler-exposure failure at test351 and later test-process non-exit, but do not prove which handle leaked. Preserve hang root cause as UNKNOWN pending CI-equivalent trace; PR335 scanner fix remains relevant for the primary qualification test failures. no code/test bypass.\\\\n')\\np=root/'nexus-claims/SUITE/owner.json'\\ndata=json.loads(p.read_text())\\ndata['status']='active; PR335 correction d01b25cc exact CI 41014835061 Node22/24 full CLI suites in progress; main CI 41009312010 and RC13 run 41009328850 cancelled/no artifact. Old-source CI logs show evaluator compiler-exposure failures in tests 310/312/314/315/351; test351 then process failed to exit, but cause is UNKNOWN (it fails before creating its own HTTP listener). PR334 exact CI 41009682069 Linux remains in progress on older source. No local suite or held-out run.'\\ndata['last_updated']=datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(timespec='seconds')\\np.write_text(json.dumps(data, indent=2)+'\\\\n')\\nPY\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:200});\ntext(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18b8d-60e7-7130-962f-f0eb9e68c409","create_time":1793342759.837749}}}
