PTY and provider tests are timing-sensitive. Take the claim `SUITE` before running a full suite (`make test`, or `npm test` over all files). While anyone holds `SUITE`, nobody runs other suites or targeted test files on the same machine. Concurrent load caused a false failure on 2026-10-15: `cloud_providers` saw an extra provider request after a load-induced timeout. Release the claim when the run ends. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:86:3. Merge order follows the precedence rules in §4 and the ROADMAP milestone order. Within a milestone, the slice with fewer hot-file claims merges first.\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:95:| Claims | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/` | Who owns which slice or file right now |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:96:| Claim log | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims.log` (append-only, one line per event) | Claim, release, broken claim, boundary request |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:102:The following groupings can run at the same time with no hot-file contention beyond §4 claims. They are listed by milestone.\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:110:| M4 (alongside M3) | PLAN-08 PR-8b..8e. Coordinate with PLAN-04 on `state.ts` through `FILE_` claims. |\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":67004}},"started_at_ms":1793344802807,"completed_at_ms":1793344802807}}
