{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T07:20:47.611Z","ordinal":521932,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18b8d-60e7-7130-962f-f0eb9e68c409","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-fc42a509-951a-4949-8e68-2e93c1a23125","process_id":"51619","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","cd /home/mike/nexus-wt/post-pr335-source-gates-20261030T0720Z && rg -n -i \"rc construction|release candidate|version-only|require a version|pre-rc|exact rc|rc tag|tag.*main|release workflow\" docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md docs/v1.0.0/README.md docs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md .github/workflows/release.yml scripts/sync-version.mjs | head -150"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n -i 'rc construction|release candidate|version-only|require a version|pre-rc|exact rc|rc tag|tag.*main|release workflow' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md docs/v1.0.0/README.md docs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md .github/workflows/release.yml scripts/sync-version.mjs","query":"rc construction|release candidate|version-only|require a version|pre-rc|exact rc|rc tag|tag.*main|release workflow","path":"ACCEPTANCE.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"scripts/sync-version.mjs:3:// disagrees (run in CI and the release workflow). `--tag vX.Y.Z` additionally requires the tag to match.\ndocs/v1.0.0/README.md:16:| Qualify a release candidate | [ACCEPTANCE.md](ACCEPTANCE.md) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:3:This is the procedure that decides whether a release candidate (RC) may become v1.0.0. It defines:\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:22:The release sequence has five distinct stages. Passing an earlier stage is a prerequisite for the next stage, not a substitute for it. Every G0–G4 acceptance ID remains mandatory; the stage determines which exact input and evidence it evaluates, not whether the check applies.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:24:1. **Pre-RC source gates.** Before creating an RC tag, run required source CI and every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method evaluates source, a source-built test binary, or an environment without requiring a published RC. Record the full commit ID and check results. Source checks do not establish behavior of the installed package.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:25:2. **RC artifact construction.** After the required owner authorization, create the version-matched RC tag on that exact source commit and use the repository release workflow to build and publish the RC artifacts. Record the workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and provenance. The workflow-produced artifacts are the candidates for qualification; a local build or a different commit is not interchangeable. RC artifact publication is not product qualification or final release acceptance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:26:3. **RC artifact gates.** Before installed-RC product qualification, run every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method requires the RC archive, RC attestation/release, or workflow-produced artifact. This includes ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08. ACC-PKG checks that explicitly require an installed package run against this RC as specified by their test method. Record the RC tag commit, workflow run, artifact digests, and each check result. A source-level analogue does not replace an artifact-bound check.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:28:5. **Stable promotion and publication.** After exact-RC acceptance and G6 pass, create a stable-version commit directly on the accepted RC commit, changing only the synchronized version metadata required for v1.0.0. Record both commits and the version-only diff. Run required source CI and all applicable source G0–G4 checks on this exact stable-version commit before tagging. If any other source changes, restart RC construction and qualification. Then create the `v1.0.0` tag on that checked commit and build a draft release. Keep its assets unpublished while verifying the stable artifact identity, provenance, package contents, installation, and publication metadata. Compare the stable package contents with the accepted RC; if packaged behavior or content differs beyond version-specific metadata, rerun affected installed-RC qualification gates and obtain independent acceptance for the stable artifact. Publish the draft only after these checks pass and the signed acceptance disposition is recorded. Record the published digests and provenance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:30:The final G6 decision in §10 applies to promoting the accepted RC toward a stable release. It requires the applicable gates to pass for the accepted RC and authorizes the version-only stable commit and its source checks, followed by the stable tag and draft build; it does not waive source CI, artifact identity, installed-RC qualification, or any threshold. Public publication is a separate post-build gate in stage 5 above. The release workflow must keep stable assets in draft state until stable artifact checks pass. Source verification at integration 6a16cb6 confirms the tag-triggered release workflow now supports published RC prereleases and draft stable releases. The earlier immediate-stable-publication source blocker is resolved; an actual stable draft build, artifact verification, signed acceptance, and deliberate publication are still required and remain unproven until their run evidence is recorded.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:34:The post-RC closure requirements listed below may remain `open`, `partial`, or `implemented` in the source ledger at the RC commit because their remaining acceptance is completed during G6 or installed-RC qualification. The bare `--enforce` invocation is the pre-RC source gate: it checks every other B/RR row against the source threshold and reports mapped rows as deferred, not accepted. At G6, the exact-RC invocation must provide a record meeting the normal B/RR status threshold and digest-bound evidence for every criterion in this table. The table also supplies the criterion mapping for rows whose ledger points to an ACCEPTANCE section instead of naming ACC IDs. The source ledger is never rewritten by the record. Any below-tested required row omitted from this table still fails.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:64:1. The RC is built and published by the release workflow from a clean tag. Its version is identical across all components (REQ-REL-103).\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:87:Every ACC ID below is defined in the linked spec. The plan for each spec names the test that implements it. Run each check at the lifecycle stage dictated by its acceptance method in §1.1: source-applicable checks before the RC tag; checks requiring the RC archive, attestation, release, or installed package after RC construction; environment-specific checks in their declared environment. Bind every result to the exact source commit and, when artifact-dependent, the RC package digest. A source test or local build does not replace an artifact-bound check, and no G0–G4 ID is complete until all of its applicable checks pass.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:97:| Supply chain | ACC-SUP-01 to ACC-SUP-08 (artifact-bound ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08 after RC construction) | SPEC-07 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:331:G6 passes only when every item below holds. It authorizes a version-only stable commit from the accepted RC source, followed by its source checks, stable tag, and unpublished draft candidate; it does not authorize making stable assets publicly available. RC tags are candidate construction inputs governed by §1.1; an RC tag or its successful build does not satisfy this release decision.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:340:- [ ] The pre-RC source gate passes from a clean source worktree: `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce`. Every B/RR source row outside the §1.1 qualification-only map must be ≥ `tested`. A mapped row below `tested` is reported as deferred; this result does not accept or qualify it.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:341:- [ ] The exact-RC evidence gate passes from the clean RC worktree and is bound to the exact RC source commit and installed RC artifact. Run the checker with the custodian-approved, immutable qualification record and evidence directory:\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:343:  The version 1 record contains `sourceCommit` (full commit ID), `rcTag` (for example `v1.0.0-rc.1`), `artifactSha256`, `artifactProvenance` (`sourceCommit`, `artifactSha256`, and a hashed provenance report), `independentAcceptance` (`disposition`, `reviewer`, `implementers`, zero `blockingDefects`, and a hashed report reference), and one `requirements` entry for every B/RR row. For `ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS`, include each non-blocking defect with its owner disposition; unresolved or blocking defects fail. Each requirement entry records its status and one or more hashed evidence files covering the exact criteria required by the ledger and the §1.1 qualification-only map. Every criterion evidence file must be a JSON object with top-level `sourceCommit`, `rcTag`, and `artifactSha256` values exactly matching the validated qualification record, current RC source commit, and installed RC artifact. A digest-valid report copied from another source revision, RC tag, or artifact is rejected. A B row recorded as `tested` also needs a non-empty `qualificationNotApplicable.reason` and a `qualificationNotApplicable.decision` matching the approved per-requirement exception table and a matching applicability declaration in DECISIONS.md; an unrelated or record-supplied decision is rejected. Evidence paths must be relative regular files under the evidence root, with no symlinks. Missing, unknown, stale, mismatched, or incomplete evidence fails the gate. The checker requires a clean worktree, rejects `--ledger` overrides, enforces source-ledger thresholds outside the explicit §1.1 lifecycle rows, and requires the exact-RC record itself to meet the normal status threshold for every row. It never mutates the source ledger or relaxes a requirement's B/RR record threshold. The checker validates source/tag/artifact identity bindings and evidence hashes; it does not authenticate the reviewer or prove that the artifact was built from the source commit. The approved release workflow must independently verify build provenance/attestation, and the designated custodian and independent reviewer must verify their respective approvals and custody evidence.\n.github/workflows/release.yml:84:      - name: Require a version-matched tag on main\n.github/workflows/release.yml:91:      - name: Require a stable tag to be a version-only commit on its RC\n.github/workflows/release.yml:94:        # commit cannot replace it; branch and tag protection remain the control over the workflow file itself.\n.github/workflows/release.yml:98:          git show \"$rc:scripts/check-version-only-diff.mjs\" > \"$RUNNER_TEMP/check-version-only-diff.mjs\"\n.github/workflows/release.yml:99:          node \"$RUNNER_TEMP/check-version-only-diff.mjs\" \"$rc\" \"$GITHUB_SHA\"\n.github/workflows/release.yml:122:      # RC tags (vX.Y.Z-rc.N) publish a prerelease: the workflow-produced RC is the qualification candidate\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:30:| **RC1** | After PLAN-09 task 7's pre-RC source-ledger reconciliation and enforce gate, tag `v1.0.0-rc.1` (owner approves publishing a prerelease; X7) | RC build installed through the documented command | G0–G4 green on the exact RC source; pre-RC requirements enforcement passed | <1 ed |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:33:| **M6 Release** | PLAN-09 task 7 (verify the pre-RC source-ledger reconciliation and enforcement evidence; record exact-RC dispositions in the acceptance record without mutating the accepted RC source); docs sign-off; release notes; tag `v1.0.0` (X7) | Published v1.0.0 with notices, SBOM and attestation | **G6**: ACCEPTANCE §10 checklist | 2–4 ed |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:136:- The local-only tags `v1.1.0`, `v1.2.0` and `v1.2.1` are to be **deleted locally**: `git tag -d v1.1.0 v1.2.0 v1.2.1`. The owner confirmed on 2026-10-14 that they never existed on the remote, and the audit's `git ls-remote --tags origin` agrees. They are not ancestors of main. Their impact is local only. They sort above v1.0.0 and would confuse `git describe` and the tooling. This is an owner action (see the last section) because it removes local references.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:176:**Status amendment (2026-10-21):** The contest has concluded. The release coordinator confirmed that no contest freeze applies. The historical freeze above is no longer a restriction; PLAN-C1 and other contest-related maintenance may proceed through normal claims, review, and validation. Preserve submitted tags, run records, and manifests as historical evidence, and do not represent changed current sources as the original submission. The retired `cloudflare-contest-contract` check remains retired and must not be reintroduced as a release gate.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:285:| X7 | **Authorized by the owner in the implementation/release handoff, reaffirmed by the 2026-10-18 takeover instruction.** Necessary commits, pushes, PRs, merges, RC tags and final v1.0.0 publication are authorized, conditional on the existing checks and acceptance gates. Release publisher: `codex-api-root`, succeeding rate-limited `claude-code`; no duplicate publisher. See [authorization and handoff](../reviews/evidence/v1/RELEASE-TAKEOVER/authorization-and-handoff.md). | Release | Authorization resolved; execution remains gated |\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":65857}},"started_at_ms":1793344847611,"completed_at_ms":1793344847611}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T07:20:47.850Z","ordinal":521933,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18bae-bfea-72a0-9289-708057b6a054","call_id":"call_84c019574fe74356b1174802ba898b3b","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.6 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"scripts/sync-version.mjs:3:// disagrees (run in CI and the release workflow). `--tag vX.Y.Z` additionally requires the tag to match.\ndocs/v1.0.0/README.md:16:| Qualify a release candidate | [ACCEPTANCE.md](ACCEPTANCE.md) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:3:This is the procedure that decides whether a release candidate (RC) may become v1.0.0. It defines:\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:22:The release sequence has five distinct stages. Passing an earlier stage is a prerequisite for the next stage, not a substitute for it. Every G0–G4 acceptance ID remains mandatory; the stage determines which exact input and evidence it evaluates, not whether the check applies.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:24:1. **Pre-RC source gates.** Before creating an RC tag, run required source CI and every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method evaluates source, a source-built test binary, or an environment without requiring a published RC. Record the full commit ID and check results. Source checks do not establish behavior of the installed package.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:25:2. **RC artifact construction.** After the required owner authorization, create the version-matched RC tag on that exact source commit and use the repository release workflow to build and publish the RC artifacts. Record the workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and provenance. The workflow-produced artifacts are the candidates for qualification; a local build or a different commit is not interchangeable. RC artifact publication is not product qualification or final release acceptance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:26:3. **RC artifact gates.** Before installed-RC product qualification, run every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method requires the RC archive, RC attestation/release, or workflow-produced artifact. This includes ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08. ACC-PKG checks that explicitly require an installed package run against this RC as specified by their test method. Record the RC tag commit, workflow run, artifact digests, and each check result. A source-level analogue does not replace an artifact-bound check.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:28:5. **Stable promotion and publication.** After exact-RC acceptance and G6 pass, create a stable-version commit directly on the accepted RC commit, changing only the synchronized version metadata required for v1.0.0. Record both commits and the version-only diff. Run required source CI and all applicable source G0–G4 checks on this exact stable-version commit before tagging. If any other source changes, restart RC construction and qualification. Then create the `v1.0.0` tag on that checked commit and build a draft release. Keep its assets unpublished while verifying the stable artifact identity, provenance, package contents, installation, and publication metadata. Compare the stable package contents with the accepted RC; if packaged behavior or content differs beyond version-specific metadata, rerun affected installed-RC qualification gates and obtain independent acceptance for the stable artifact. Publish the draft only after these checks pass and the signed acceptance disposition is recorded. Record the published digests and provenance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:30:The final G6 decision in §10 applies to promoting the accepted RC toward a stable release. It requires the applicable gates to pass for the accepted RC and authorizes the version-only stable commit and its source checks, followed by the stable tag and draft build; it does not waive source CI, artifact identity, installed-RC qualification, or any threshold. Public publication is a separate post-build gate in stage 5 above. The release workflow must keep stable assets in draft state until stable artifact checks pass. Source verification at integration 6a16cb6 confirms the tag-triggered release workflow now supports published RC prereleases and draft stable releases. The earlier immediate-stable-publication source blocker is resolved; an actual stable draft build, artifact verification, signed acceptance, and deliberate publication are still required and remain unproven until their run evidence is recorded.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:34:The post-RC closure requirements listed below may remain `open`, `partial`, or `implemented` in the source ledger at the RC commit because their remaining acceptance is completed during G6 or installed-RC qualification. The bare `--enforce` invocation is the pre-RC source gate: it checks every other B/RR row against the source threshold and reports mapped rows as deferred, not accepted. At G6, the exact-RC invocation must provide a record meeting the normal B/RR status threshold and digest-bound evidence for every criterion in this table. The table also supplies the criterion mapping for rows whose ledger points to an ACCEPTANCE section instead of naming ACC IDs. The source ledger is never rewritten by the record. Any below-tested required row omitted from this table still fails.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:64:1. The RC is built and published by the release workflow from a clean tag. Its version is identical across all components (REQ-REL-103).\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:87:Every ACC ID below is defined in the linked spec. The plan for each spec names the test that implements it. Run each check at the lifecycle stage dictated by its acceptance method in §1.1: source-applicable checks before the RC tag; checks requiring the RC archive, attestation, release, or installed package after RC construction; environment-specific checks in their declared environment. Bind every result to the exact source commit and, when artifact-dependent, the RC package digest. A source test or local build does not replace an artifact-bound check, and no G0–G4 ID is complete until all of its applicable checks pass.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:97:| Supply chain | ACC-SUP-01 to ACC-SUP-08 (artifact-bound ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08 after RC construction) | SPEC-07 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:331:G6 passes only when every item below holds. It authorizes a version-only stable commit from the accepted RC source, followed by its source checks, stable tag, and unpublished draft candidate; it does not authorize making stable assets publicly available. RC tags are candidate construction inputs governed by §1.1; an RC tag or its successful build does not satisfy this release decision.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:340:- [ ] The pre-RC source gate passes from a clean source worktree: `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce`. Every B/RR source row outside the §1.1 qualification-only map must be ≥ `tested`. A mapped row below `tested` is reported as deferred; this result does not accept or qualify it.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:341:- [ ] The exact-RC evidence gate passes from the clean RC worktree and is bound to the exact RC source commit and installed RC artifact. Run the checker with the custodian-approved, immutable qualification record and evidence directory:\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:343:  The version 1 record contains `sourceCommit` (full commit ID), `rcTag` (for example `v1.0.0-rc.1`), `artifactSha256`, `artifactProvenance` (`sourceCommit`, `artifactSha256`, and a hashed provenance report), `independentAcceptance` (`disposition`, `reviewer`, `implementers`, zero `blockingDefects`, and a hashed report reference), and one `requirements` entry for every B/RR row. For `ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS`, include each non-blocking defect with its owner disposition; unresolved or blocking defects fail. Each requirement entry records its status and one or more hashed evidence files covering the exact criteria required by the ledger and the §1.1 qualification-only map. Every criterion evidence file must be a JSON object with top-level `sourceCommit`, `rcTag`, and `artifactSha256` values exactly matching the validated qualification record, current RC source commit, and installed RC artifact. A digest-valid report copied from another source revision, RC tag, or artifact is rejected. A B row recorded as `tested` also needs a non-empty `qualificationNotApplicable.reason` and a `qualificationNotApplicable.decision` matching the approved per-requirement exception table and a matching applicability declaration in DECISIONS.md; an unrelated or record-supplied decision is rejected. Evidence paths must be relative regular files under the evidence root, with no symlinks. Missing, unknown, stale, mismatched, or incomplete evidence fails the gate. The checker requires a clean worktree, rejects `--ledger` overrides, enforces source-ledger thresholds outside the explicit §1.1 lifecycle rows, and requires the exact-RC record itself to meet the normal status threshold for every row. It never mutates the source ledger or relaxes a requirement's B/RR record threshold. The checker validates source/tag/artifact identity bindings and evidence hashes; it does not authenticate the reviewer or prove that the artifact was built from the source commit. The approved release workflow must independently verify build provenance/attestation, and the designated custodian and independent reviewer must verify their respective approvals and custody evidence.\n.github/workflows/release.yml:84:      - name: Require a version-matched tag on main\n.github/workflows/release.yml:91:      - name: Require a stable tag to be a version-only commit on its RC\n.github/workflows/release.yml:94:        # commit cannot replace it; branch and tag protection remain the control over the workflow file itself.\n.github/workflows/release.yml:98:          git show \"$rc:scripts/check-version-only-diff.mjs\" > \"$RUNNER_TEMP/check-version-only-diff.mjs\"\n.github/workflows/release.yml:99:          node \"$RUNNER_TEMP/check-version-only-diff.mjs\" \"$rc\" \"$GITHUB_SHA\"\n.github/workflows/release.yml:122:      # RC tags (vX.Y.Z-rc.N) publish a prerelease: the workflow-produced RC is the qualification candidate\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:30:| **RC1** | After PLAN-09 task 7's pre-RC source-ledger reconciliation and enforce gate, tag `v1.0.0-rc.1` (owner approves publishing a prerelease; X7) | RC build installed through the documented command | G0–G4 green on the exact RC source; pre-RC requirements enforcement passed | <1 ed |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:33:| **M6 Release** | PLAN-09 task 7 (verify the pre-RC source-ledger reconciliation and enforcement evidence; record exact-RC dispositions in the acceptance record without mutating the accepted RC source); docs sign-off; release notes; tag `v1.0.0` (X7) | Published v1.0.0 with notices, SBOM and attestation | **G6**: ACCEPTANCE §10 checklist | 2–4 ed |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:136:- The local-only tags `v1.1.0`, `v1.2.0` and `v1.2.1` are to be **deleted locally**: `git tag -d v1.1.0 v1.2.0 v1.2.1`. The owner confirmed on 2026-10-14 that they never existed on the remote, and the audit's `git ls-remote --tags origin` agrees. They are not ancestors of main. Their impact is local only. They sort above v1.0.0 and would confuse `git describe` and the tooling. This is an owner action (see the last section) because it removes local references.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:176:**Status amendment (2026-10-21):** The contest has concluded. The release coordinator confirmed that no contest freeze applies. The historical freeze above is no longer a restriction; PLAN-C1 and other contest-related maintenance may proceed through normal claims, review, and validation. Preserve submitted tags, run records, and manifests as historical evidence, and do not represent changed current sources as the original submission. The retired `cloudflare-contest-contract` check remains retired and must not be reintroduced as a release gate.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:285:| X7 | **Authorized by the owner in the implementation/release handoff, reaffirmed by the 2026-10-18 takeover instruction.** Necessary commits, pushes, PRs, merges, RC tags and final v1.0.0 publication are authorized, conditional on the existing checks and acceptance gates. Release publisher: `codex-api-root`, succeeding rate-limited `claude-code`; no duplicate publisher. See [authorization and handoff](../reviews/evidence/v1/RELEASE-TAKEOVER/authorization-and-handoff.md). | Release | Authorization resolved; execution remains gated |\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18b8d-60e7-7130-962f-f0eb9e68c409","create_time":1793344847.8501306}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
