{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T07:21:22.282Z","ordinal":521962,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18b8d-60e7-7130-962f-f0eb9e68c409","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-cd1ff9b1-618d-49eb-baa0-4d259d0fcdd6","process_id":"53357","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n \"RC|release|version-only|qualification|publish|tag\" docs/v1.0.0/README.md docs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md .github/workflows/release.yml scripts/sync-version.mjs"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/post-pr335-source-gates-20261030T0720Z","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'RC|release|version-only|qualification|publish|tag' docs/v1.0.0/README.md docs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md .github/workflows/release.yml scripts/sync-version.mjs","query":"RC|release|version-only|qualification|publish|tag","path":"README.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"scripts/sync-version.mjs:3:// disagrees (run in CI and the release workflow). `--tag vX.Y.Z` additionally requires the tag to match.\nscripts/sync-version.mjs:11:const tagIndex = args.indexOf(\"--tag\");\nscripts/sync-version.mjs:12:const tag = tagIndex >= 0 ? args[tagIndex + 1] : undefined;\nscripts/sync-version.mjs:42:if (tag !== undefined && tag !== `v${version}`) {\nscripts/sync-version.mjs:43:  console.error(`tag ${tag} does not match package.json version ${version}`);\n.github/workflows/release.yml:5:    tags: [\"v*.*.*\"]\n.github/workflows/release.yml:36:          root=/mnt/nexus-eval-release\n.github/workflows/release.yml:38:          sudo mount -t tmpfs -o size=128m,mode=0711,uid=\"$(id -u)\",gid=\"$(id -g)\" nexus-eval-release \"$root\"\n.github/workflows/release.yml:52:          curl -fsSL https://github.com/EmbarkStudios/cargo-deny/releases/download/0.20.2/cargo-deny-0.20.2-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.gz | tar -xz -C \"$RUNNER_TEMP\"\n.github/workflows/release.yml:54:          curl -fsSL https://github.com/EmbarkStudios/cargo-about/releases/download/0.9.2/cargo-about-0.9.2-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.gz | tar -xz -C \"$RUNNER_TEMP\"\n.github/workflows/release.yml:56:          curl -fsSL https://github.com/CycloneDX/cyclonedx-rust-cargo/releases/download/cargo-cyclonedx-0.5.9/cargo-cyclonedx-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.xz | tar -xJ -C \"$RUNNER_TEMP\"\n.github/workflows/release.yml:58:          curl -fsSL https://github.com/CycloneDX/cyclonedx-cli/releases/download/v0.33.1/cyclonedx-linux-x64 -o \"$CARGO_HOME/bin/cyclonedx\"\n.github/workflows/release.yml:65:      - name: Require the pinned release Node and npm versions\n.github/workflows/release.yml:84:      - name: Require a version-matched tag on main\n.github/workflows/release.yml:86:          git fetch origin main --no-tags\n.github/workflows/release.yml:89:          node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check --tag \"$GITHUB_REF_NAME\"\n.github/workflows/release.yml:90:          test -f \"docs/releases/${GITHUB_REF_NAME}.md\" || { echo \"Missing docs/releases/${GITHUB_REF_NAME}.md\" >&2; exit 1; }\n.github/workflows/release.yml:91:      - name: Require a stable tag to be a version-only commit on its RC\n.github/workflows/release.yml:93:        # The checkout has full history and tags (fetch-depth: 0). The checker runs from the RC's own copy so a stable\n.github/workflows/release.yml:94:        # commit cannot replace it; branch and tag protection remain the control over the workflow file itself.\n.github/workflows/release.yml:96:          rc=\"$(git tag --points-at \"$GITHUB_SHA^\" | grep -E \"^${GITHUB_REF_NAME//./\\\\.}-rc\\.[0-9]+$\" | sort -V | tail -n 1 || true)\"\n.github/workflows/release.yml:97:          test -n \"$rc\" || { echo \"the parent of $GITHUB_REF_NAME is not a ${GITHUB_REF_NAME}-rc.N tag\" >&2; exit 1; }\n.github/workflows/release.yml:98:          git show \"$rc:scripts/check-version-only-diff.mjs\" > \"$RUNNER_TEMP/check-version-only-diff.mjs\"\n.github/workflows/release.yml:99:          node \"$RUNNER_TEMP/check-version-only-diff.mjs\" \"$rc\" \"$GITHUB_SHA\"\n.github/workflows/release.yml:103:      - run: cargo build --locked --release --manifest-path core/Cargo.toml --bin harness-core --bin nexus-tui\n.github/workflows/release.yml:122:      # RC tags (vX.Y.Z-rc.N) publish a prerelease: the workflow-produced RC is the qualification candidate\n.github/workflows/release.yml:123:      # (ACCEPTANCE §1.1 stage 2). Stable tags only build an unpublished draft (stage 5); it is published by hand with\n.github/workflows/release.yml:124:      # `gh release edit <tag> --draft=false` after the stable artifact checks and the signed acceptance disposition.\n.github/workflows/release.yml:125:      - uses: softprops/action-gh-release@3bb12739c298aeb8a4eeaf626c5b8d85266b0e65 # v2\n.github/workflows/release.yml:128:          body_path: docs/releases/${{ github.ref_name }}.md\n.github/workflows/release.yml:129:          prerelease: ${{ contains(github.ref_name, '-') }}\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:9:- **Uncertainty.** The largest unknown is how many fix loops M5 qualification triggers. The pilot's history suggests at least one.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:15:M0 Foundation ──► M1 Safety floor ──────────────► M3 Continuity & inference ──► RC1 ──► M5 Qualification ──► M6 Release\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:25:| **M0 Foundation** | PLAN-08 task 1 (test HOME isolation); PLAN-06 task 3 (version sync). Owner action X1 (stale local tags deleted) is already done.; PLAN-09 tasks 1, 2, 5 (ledger checker in report mode, historical banners, cheap doc truth fixes) | Tests never touch the real HOME. One version identity. The ledger is enforced in CI. | **G0**: ACC-PER-03, ACC-PKG-03, ACC-GOV-01/03 | 2–4 ed |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:27:| **M2 Product parity and supply chain** (parallel with M1 after PLAN-01 PR-1b) | PLAN-06 (unified launcher with the TUI as the packaged default, doc commands, doctor, installer); PLAN-07 (notices, SBOM, provenance, CI matrix, `cli/dist` untracked, SECURITY.md, CHANGELOG); PLAN-12 (CLI and TUI upgrade engine) | The installed product equals the tested product. Compliant release assets. In-place upgrade safely verifies and swaps releases. | **G2**: ACC-PKG-01..09, ACC-SUP-01..07, ACC-UPG-01..06 | 8–14 ed |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:28:| **M3 Continuity and inference** | PLAN-04 (resume, durable work units, accounting, error path, stagnation, team semantics); PLAN-05 code tasks (server-kind discovery, compact-and-retry, error bounds, timeouts, parser robustness, receipts, startup probe, decoupling, CA); PLAN-11 PR-11c..e; PLAN-10 harness tasks 1–7, 9, 10, 13 | Resume and compaction never lose state. Standalone sizing works. Eval harness ready. | **G3**: ACC-CONT-01..09, ACC-INF-01..09, ACC-VER-05..09, eval self-tests | 15–25 ed |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:30:| **RC1** | After PLAN-09 task 7's pre-RC source-ledger reconciliation and enforce gate, tag `v1.0.0-rc.1` (owner approves publishing a prerelease; X7) | RC build installed through the documented command | G0–G4 green on the exact RC source; pre-RC requirements enforcement passed | <1 ed |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:31:| **M5 Qualification** | PLAN-10 task 11 (T2 held-out 5×, T3, T4, standalone stripped-proxy profiles, provider verify); task 12 (terminal matrix); ACC-SUP-08 cross-runner reproducibility; independent acceptance (X5) of continuity and of the RC | Qualification evidence archive, scorer verdict table, independent reports | **G5**: ACCEPTANCE §4–§8 all PASS | 10–20 calendar days. About 84 h of serial inference for T2, plus T3/T4/standalone. Excludes fix loops. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:33:| **M6 Release** | PLAN-09 task 7 (verify the pre-RC source-ledger reconciliation and enforcement evidence; record exact-RC dispositions in the acceptance record without mutating the accepted RC source); docs sign-off; release notes; tag `v1.0.0` (X7) | Published v1.0.0 with notices, SBOM and attestation | **G6**: ACCEPTANCE §10 checklist | 2–4 ed |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:41:**M0 → M1 → M3 → RC1 → M5 (T2 held-out runs) → M6**\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:49:Off the critical path, but must finish before RC1:\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:52:- the 40 held-out T2 tasks and 8 T3 tasks (agent-authored), with their manifest sealed **before** RC1;\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:64:| G5 | After the RC | ACCEPTANCE §4–§8 pass. The DEC-05 thresholds are met. Independent reports are filed. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:71:| **Release blockers** (31 B rows) | M0–M3 for implementation, M5 for qualification evidence |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:83:| Parser restriction (PLAN-11) lowers the tool-call rate on text-only models | Task quality falls | Recorded fixtures; one-RC escape hatch; the qualification measures it |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:88:Everything marked RT or MEAS in AUDIT §5 must be re-run on the RC:\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:95:The baseline suite (905 CLI + 266 Rust tests) must be re-run at every gate. The two live provider verifications and the live end-to-end run (EVIDENCE §3) must be repeated on the RC with pinned models.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:16:| [DEC-08](#dec-08-version-identity-and-stale-v1x-tags) | Version identity, stale v1.x tags | `package.json` is the source of truth; local v1.x tags deleted (owner action) | No |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:17:| [DEC-09](#dec-09-release-provenance-mechanism) | Release provenance | GitHub artifact attestations | No |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:24:| [DEC-16](#dec-16-standalone-qualification-under-a-gateway-only-environment) | Standalone qualification with no direct worker access | Stripping proxy over the gateway for live runs, plus server-kind conformance fixtures | No |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:62:**Options.** (A) Fully supported. **(B, chosen)** Shipped and labelled **experimental** in help and docs. Excluded from the qualification task-quality claims. But the following are still fixed for v1:\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:110:**Task authorship.** The owner authorized agent authorship for the T2 tasks on 2026-10-14. A separately-run agent session authors the held-out tasks. It is given only the task schema and the external repositories, with no access to Nexus source, the development set, or tuning history. Its sha256 manifest is committed before the RC freeze. The qualification report must state that the authors were agents, not humans.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:114:**Rationale.** These figures are the pilot's pre-registered thresholds (eval/README), tightened where the pilot showed weakness: false VERIFIED, crash accounting. The absolute floor prevents \"beat a weak peer\" from passing. Thresholds are fixed **before** the RC run.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:120:| **Supported** | OpenAI-compatible local servers (llama.cpp server, vLLM, LM Studio, Ollama) | The release notes name the server kinds that pass the standalone matrix (≥ 2 required). Others are listed as \"compatible, not qualified\". |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:122:| **Supported** | OpenRouter | Live-verified 2026-10-14 at db1ca55 (`evidence/live/verify_openrouter.json`); re-verify at RC with a **pinned** model (not `openrouter/free`). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:123:| **Experimental → Supported if live-verified at RC** | OpenAI API key (Responses), Anthropic (Messages), generic compatible cloud | Not connected on the owner's install. They stay experimental unless keys are added and `nexus providers verify` passes at RC. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:128:- **`nexus eval`.** Labelled experimental. Its scoring is not fixed in v1, but its unsafe `git checkout` in the operator's workspace **is** fixed: it must run in a worktree (VER-07a). It is excluded from all claims. The SPEC-10 harness (`eval/`) is the qualification tool.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:132:## DEC-08: Version identity and stale v1.x tags\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:134:- `package.json` is the single source of truth. `scripts/sync-version.mjs` updates `cli/package.json` and `core/Cargo.toml`. Release CI asserts that all three equal the tag.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:135:- Release line: `v1.0.0-rc.N` prereleases, then `v1.0.0`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:136:- The local-only tags `v1.1.0`, `v1.2.0` and `v1.2.1` are to be **deleted locally**: `git tag -d v1.1.0 v1.2.0 v1.2.1`. The owner confirmed on 2026-10-14 that they never existed on the remote, and the audit's `git ls-remote --tags origin` agrees. They are not ancestors of main. Their impact is local only. They sort above v1.0.0 and would confuse `git describe` and the tooling. This is an owner action (see the last section) because it removes local references.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:159:**Chosen:** Linux x86-64, glibc ≥ 2.35, Node ≥ 22 for v1.0.0. The owner selected Node 22 as the minimum on 2026-10-22 because Node 20 reached end of life on 2026-04-30; v1.0.0 must not require or build on an end-of-life Node runtime. Validate Node 22 and 24 in the source CI matrix, with release and reproducibility builds on Node 22. The docs keep the conservative glibc \"≥ 2.35\" claim; the binaries reference glibc symbols ≤ 2.34. macOS, arm64 and musl are post-v1 roadmap items.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:161:This supersedes the earlier Node ≥ 20 decision. The immutable `v1.0.0-rc.2` tag targets `19d6f0a80e21f9b640a46ee12200c4f5f6d967a4`, whose package engine and workflows still use Node 20; that tag is not a qualifying RC under this decision.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:176:**Status amendment (2026-10-21):** The contest has concluded. The release coordinator confirmed that no contest freeze applies. The historical freeze above is no longer a restriction; PLAN-C1 and other contest-related maintenance may proceed through normal claims, review, and validation. Preserve submitted tags, run records, and manifests as historical evidence, and do not represent changed current sources as the original submission. The retired `cloudflare-contest-contract` check remains retired and must not be reintroduced as a release gate.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:188:## DEC-16: Standalone qualification under a gateway-only environment\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:208:- Response-shape fixtures for llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio and Ollama are written from each project's published API documentation, with source references and versions recorded. They cover `/models`, `/props`, `/api/v0/models`, `/api/show`, SSE tool-call deltas, think tags and overflow bodies.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:237:**Rejected alternatives.** (A) Lower the floor to satisfy the band — rejected: reintroduces under-estimation and the context-overflow class REQ-AGT-118 exists to prevent. (B) Drop the CJK/Hangul corpora from the fixture — rejected: removes the evidence. (C) Change the pinned tokenizer — out of scope; the fixture pins the qualification worker.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:243:**Context.** The v1.0.0 manual terminal matrix requires real interaction in five terminal environments at three sizes. The release owner waived screenshot artifacts for this release.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:245:**Chosen (owner-confirmed 2026-10-28).** Approval-panel and post-exit screenshots are not required for v1.0.0. This waiver changes only the screenshot artifact requirement. It does not waive any interactive run, check, safety threshold, per-cell PASS/FAIL verdict, observed outcome, evidence record, exact installed-RC identity, or written disposition for non-safety failures. All 15 manual matrix cells remain mandatory; automated PTY runs cannot replace them.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:253:**History.** A prior revision of this decision recorded that the release owner waived the manual matrix. That record conflicted with the explicit release requirement for five terminal environments × three sizes. The waiver is withdrawn and must not be used to disposition any v1.0.0 gate.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:255:**Current decision (release owner direction, 2026-10-29).** All fifteen manual E3 cells remain mandatory on the exact installed RC. Record a PASS or FAIL and observed outcomes for every required check in every cell. Automated CI or PTY runs do not substitute for operator evidence. [DEC-18](#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver) remains in force and waives screenshot artifacts only; it does not waive interaction, checks, per-cell verdicts, evidence records, or safety gates. No cell is accepted as complete without actual manual execution.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:259:**Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §5.3 / ACC-TUI-MANUAL; ACCEPTANCE §10 G6; SPEC-10 REQ-QUAL-108; `TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md`; PLAN-10 task 12; READINESS; release notes.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:263:**Status: accepted by the release owner, 2026-10-29.** This decision supersedes DEC-19 for v1.0.0.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:265:**Direction.** The manual five-terminal by three-size matrix in ACCEPTANCE §5.3 is waived for v1.0.0. No manual operator run, cell verdict, or per-cell evidence is required, and the waiver does not claim that any cell passed. The automated CI gate in §5.1 and the scripted installed-RC PTY gate in §5.2 remain mandatory and must pass.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:267:**Scope.** This waiver applies only to ACC-TUI-MANUAL and only for v1.0.0. It does not waive ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, exact-RC identity, any §5.1 or §5.2 scenario, safety checks, or any other release gate. DEC-18's screenshot-artifact waiver remains recorded; no screenshots are required for a matrix that is not run.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:273:**Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §§1.1, 3.1, 5, and 10; REQ-QUAL-108 exact-RC evidence mapping; stable v1.0.0 release notes; READINESS; terminal-matrix worksheet disposition.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:279:| X1 | ~~`git tag -d v1.1.0 v1.2.0 v1.2.1`~~ **Done by the owner on 2026-10-14.** Verified: `git tag -l` now lists only `v0.1.0-alpha.1` and `v0.1.0-alpha.2`. | DEC-08 | Done |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:283:| X5 | Independent reviewer for continuity/compaction acceptance and RC acceptance | REQ-AGT-110, ACCEPTANCE §8 | M5/M6 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:285:| X7 | **Authorized by the owner in the implementation/release handoff, reaffirmed by the 2026-10-18 takeover instruction.** Necessary commits, pushes, PRs, merges, RC tags and final v1.0.0 publication are authorized, conditional on the existing checks and acceptance gates. Release publisher: `codex-api-root`, succeeding rate-limited `claude-code`; no duplicate publisher. See [authorization and handoff](../reviews/evidence/v1/RELEASE-TAKEOVER/authorization-and-handoff.md). | Release | Authorization resolved; execution remains gated |\ndocs/v1.0.0/README.md:5:**Historical verdict: v1.0.0 readiness was BLOCKED at the 2026-10-16 source-suite checkpoint.** Candidate source revision `6151a231e9179c109cfbe8cff87e0a4148587b6a` passed an isolated `make build` and full `make test` run on 2026-10-16 (Rust 281/281; CLI 1087/1087; zero skipped). This is source-suite evidence, not RC qualification. At that checkpoint, held-out task quality, T3/T4 qualification, standalone/provider qualification, the manual terminal matrix, package/install matrix on the RC, and independent RC acceptance remained incomplete. For v1.0.0, the manual matrix was later waived by DEC-20; see [the current readiness reconciliation](READINESS.md) for the current disposition and remaining gates. The contest entry remains a separate track; judging has concluded and no contest freeze applies.\ndocs/v1.0.0/README.md:12:| See current release readiness and remaining actions | [READINESS.md](READINESS.md) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/README.md:16:| Qualify a release candidate | [ACCEPTANCE.md](ACCEPTANCE.md) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/README.md:31:| 07 | Supply chain, compliance, release engineering | [SPEC-07](specs/SPEC-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md) | [PLAN-07](plans/PLAN-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md) | M2 | REL-107 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/README.md:34:| 10 | v1 qualification and evaluation | [SPEC-10](specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md) | [PLAN-10](plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md) | M3/M5 | QUAL-101 to 107 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/README.md:50:5. Cut `v1.0.0-rc.1` only when G0–G4 pass. Then run ACCEPTANCE §4–§8 against the **installed** RC.\ndocs/v1.0.0/README.md:57:- **Evidence labels.** SRC, TEST, RT, MEAS, DOC, HIST, INF, UNV (REQUIREMENTS §1).\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:1:# Nexus Code v1.0.0: release qualification procedure\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:3:This is the procedure that decides whether a release candidate (RC) may become v1.0.0. It defines:\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:15:| **Product qualification** | Did the RC meet these gates on real workflows? |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:18:A gate passes only on archived evidence bound to the source commit or installed RC artifact that the gate evaluates. Source-level evidence names the exact source commit; installed-RC evidence names both that commit and the installed package digest. A green test suite alone never qualifies the product.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:22:The release sequence has five distinct stages. Passing an earlier stage is a prerequisite for the next stage, not a substitute for it. Every G0–G4 acceptance ID remains mandatory; the stage determines which exact input and evidence it evaluates, not whether the check applies.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:24:1. **Pre-RC source gates.** Before creating an RC tag, run required source CI and every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method evaluates source, a source-built test binary, or an environment without requiring a published RC. Record the full commit ID and check results. Source checks do not establish behavior of the installed package.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:25:2. **RC artifact construction.** After the required owner authorization, create the version-matched RC tag on that exact source commit and use the repository release workflow to build and publish the RC artifacts. Record the workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and provenance. The workflow-produced artifacts are the candidates for qualification; a local build or a different commit is not interchangeable. RC artifact publication is not product qualification or final release acceptance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:26:3. **RC artifact gates.** Before installed-RC product qualification, run every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method requires the RC archive, RC attestation/release, or workflow-produced artifact. This includes ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08. ACC-PKG checks that explicitly require an installed package run against this RC as specified by their test method. Record the RC tag commit, workflow run, artifact digests, and each check result. A source-level analogue does not replace an artifact-bound check.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:27:4. **Installed-RC qualification.** Install the workflow-produced RC package using the documented procedure and run the applicable product, provider, task-quality, terminal, installation, and independent-acceptance gates in §§4–8. Bind each result to both the RC source commit and installed package digest. If a source change or rebuilt artifact changes either identity, rerun every affected gate against the new candidate and retain prior results as historical evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:28:5. **Stable promotion and publication.** After exact-RC acceptance and G6 pass, create a stable-version commit directly on the accepted RC commit, changing only the synchronized version metadata required for v1.0.0. Record both commits and the version-only diff. Run required source CI and all applicable source G0–G4 checks on this exact stable-version commit before tagging. If any other source changes, restart RC construction and qualification. Then create the `v1.0.0` tag on that checked commit and build a draft release. Keep its assets unpublished while verifying the stable artifact identity, provenance, package contents, installation, and publication metadata. Compare the stable package contents with the accepted RC; if packaged behavior or content differs beyond version-specific metadata, rerun affected installed-RC qualification gates and obtain independent acceptance for the stable artifact. Publish the draft only after these checks pass and the signed acceptance disposition is recorded. Record the published digests and provenance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:30:The final G6 decision in §10 applies to promoting the accepted RC toward a stable release. It requires the applicable gates to pass for the accepted RC and authorizes the version-only stable commit and its source checks, followed by the stable tag and draft build; it does not waive source CI, artifact identity, installed-RC qualification, or any threshold. Public publication is a separate post-build gate in stage 5 above. The release workflow must keep stable assets in draft state until stable artifact checks pass. Source verification at integration 6a16cb6 confirms the tag-triggered release workflow now supports published RC prereleases and draft stable releases. The earlier immediate-stable-publication source blocker is resolved; an actual stable draft build, artifact verification, signed acceptance, and deliberate publication are still required and remain unproven until their run evidence is recorded.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:32:Exact-RC requirements records identify at least one implementer and an independent reviewer. For a blocking requirement recorded as `tested` instead of `product-qualified`, the cited decision must be explicitly allowlisted for that requirement in the approved qualification-exceptions table below, and its `DECISIONS.md` section must contain a matching requirement-specific line of the form `Qualification applicability: REQ-... = NOT REQUIRED ...`. A record-supplied or unrelated decision cannot authorize an exception. The record must include digest-bound evidence for every `ACC-*` criterion in that requirement's ledger Acceptance column.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:34:The post-RC closure requirements listed below may remain `open`, `partial`, or `implemented` in the source ledger at the RC commit because their remaining acceptance is completed during G6 or installed-RC qualification. The bare `--enforce` invocation is the pre-RC source gate: it checks every other B/RR row against the source threshold and reports mapped rows as deferred, not accepted. At G6, the exact-RC invocation must provide a record meeting the normal B/RR status threshold and digest-bound evidence for every criterion in this table. The table also supplies the criterion mapping for rows whose ledger points to an ACCEPTANCE section instead of naming ACC IDs. The source ledger is never rewritten by the record. Any below-tested required row omitted from this table still fails.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:36:<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:START -->\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:37:### Qualification-only requirements for exact-RC enforcement\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:39:| Requirement | Acceptance criteria required in the exact-RC record | Remaining stage |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:41:| REQ-REL-003 | ACC-PLAT | Installed-RC platform and Node-version matrix |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:42:| REQ-AGT-002 | ACC-VER-03, ACC-VER-04, ACC-VER-09, ACC-QUAL-T2, ACC-QUAL-T3, ACC-QUAL-T4 | Installed-RC T2/T3/T4 outcome thresholds |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:44:| REQ-PRV-003 | ACC-INF-10 | Installed-RC standalone and absent-gateway behavior |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:45:| REQ-REL-005 | ACC-SUP-04, ACC-SUP-05 | Exact-RC security and dependency artifact checks |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:46:| REQ-AGT-110 | ACC-CONT-10, ACC-GOV-06 | Installed-RC continuity and independent acceptance |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:47:| REQ-PRV-111 | ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC provider verification |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:48:| REQ-REL-114 | ACC-SUP-08 | Exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:49:| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:50:| REQ-QUAL-107 | ACC-PRV-STANDALONE, ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC standalone and provider matrix |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:51:| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y | Installed-RC automated and scripted PTY acceptance; the manual E3 matrix is waived by DEC-20 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:52:| REQ-QUAL-109 | ACC-QUAL-T3 | Installed-RC T3 long-task qualification |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:53:<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:END -->\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:55:<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:START -->\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:56:### Approved exact-RC qualification exceptions\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:60:<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:END -->\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:64:1. The RC is built and published by the release workflow from a clean tag. Its version is identical across all components (REQ-REL-103).\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:65:2. All qualification runs use the **installed RC package**, installed with the documented one-line command. They never use a checkout build. The only exception is CI unit and PTY suites, which run from source at the same commit.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:67:4. Evidence goes to `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`. The directory contains:\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:82:| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:87:Every ACC ID below is defined in the linked spec. The plan for each spec names the test that implements it. Run each check at the lifecycle stage dictated by its acceptance method in §1.1: source-applicable checks before the RC tag; checks requiring the RC archive, attestation, release, or installed package after RC construction; environment-specific checks in their declared environment. Bind every result to the exact source commit and, when artifact-dependent, the RC package digest. A source test or local build does not replace an artifact-bound check, and no G0–G4 ID is complete until all of its applicable checks pass.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:97:| Supply chain | ACC-SUP-01 to ACC-SUP-08 (artifact-bound ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08 after RC construction) | SPEC-07 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:113:| ACC-SEC-B6 | Re-run `docs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/repro/zz_trust_repro.test.ts`. Seeded-secret scan of `~/.nexus` and `.nexus` after a scripted turn. | Zero plaintext seeded secrets in durable stores or outbound bodies. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:115:| ACC-PRV-STANDALONE | §4.2 on the installed RC through the approved stripped proxy, with gateway credentials absent from the child environment | Every required profile completes through the proxy and the absent-gateway boundary holds; receipts archived. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:121:| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five terminal environments and three sizes | Waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20. No manual-cell execution or evidence is required, and no result is inferred. Automated §5.1 and scripted PTY §5.2 remain mandatory. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:123:## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:128:2. Install the RC with the documented command.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:148:ACC-INF-10 passes only when every row passes. The release notes state the scope in the form required by DEC-16.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:155:| ChatGPT sign-in | Experimental | Verify PASS recorded (already PASS at db1ca55; repeat on the RC) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:176:### 5.2 Scripted PTY scenarios against the installed RC (E3, mock gateway)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:192:**Waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20.** The five-terminal by three-size manual matrix below is not a release gate; no operator runs, cell verdicts, or per-cell evidence are required, and none are claimed. Automated CI checks in §5.1 and scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios in §5.2 remain mandatory and must pass.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:206:Record PASS/FAIL per cell and the observed outcomes for each check, bound to the exact installed RC artifact, terminal environment, and size. Screenshot artifacts are waived for v1.0.0 per [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver); this does not waive any interactive check, safety gate, per-cell verdict, or evidence record.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:210:## 6. Task-quality qualification (REQ-QUAL-101 to REQ-QUAL-106, REQ-QUAL-109)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:216:- 40 sealed tasks. The manifest is committed before RC1, and authorship is recorded (agent-authored, DEC-05).\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:217:- 5 runs × {Nexus RC, Goose, OpenCode}.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:218:- Before execution, freeze three qualification configs at `eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json`, `eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json`, and `eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json`. Each must set `qualification: true`, identify the same model fingerprint and sampling settings, and record equal context/output and task budgets; the Nexus config must identify the installed RC and its package digest. Do not derive these files from the pilot configs by silently inheriting or changing settings.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:233:  Record the resolved `T2_TASKS`, unique `T2_OUT`, config digests, installed RC identity, model fingerprint, and exact commands in the frozen run record before starting. A failed or interrupted invocation remains evidence; any permitted infrastructure rerun uses the accepted rerun procedure and is retained separately. Do not score until all required runs and manifests exist. The scorer accepts exactly the Nexus, Goose and OpenCode result files.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:237:9 fault classes × 5 runs on the Nexus RC. The configured faults run through `eval/run.mjs` and `eval/model_proxy.mjs`; the hanging-command and full-disk cases use task fixtures, and SIGTERM-then-resume uses the runner case (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-17: the union of the distinct scenarios below):\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:275:| Fresh install, each image with Node ≥ 22 | Documented one-line command with `NEXUS_VERSION=<rc>`, then the no-version command after v1.0.0 is published | Installed. `nexus --version` equals the RC. `nexus doctor` shows no version warning and an empty stderr. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:277:| Upgrade alpha.2 → RC | Same, with the tag | Symlink swapped. Old version retained. User state intact. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:278:| Rollback RC → alpha.2 | Same, with the old tag | Works. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:283:| Upgrade self-test failure | `nexus upgrade` (broken candidate package) | Refused. Staging verified before switch; if post-switch verification fails, launcher atomically rolls back to previous target and journal records `rolled_back`. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:284:| Upgrade crash recovery | `nexus upgrade --recover` | Idempotent recovery. Cleans incomplete staging, restores unverified launcher symlink, verifies functional installation. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:294:- the RC package;\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:311:2. One live long task (≥ 60 steps, ≥ 2 compactions) on the RC through the gateway, including one kill and resume.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:327:| CON-A6 | The video source commits are tagged and published, or the docs state that they are unpublished. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:331:G6 passes only when every item below holds. It authorizes a version-only stable commit from the accepted RC source, followed by its source checks, stable tag, and unpublished draft candidate; it does not authorize making stable assets publicly available. RC tags are candidate construction inputs governed by §1.1; an RC tag or its successful build does not satisfy this release decision.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:333:- [ ] G0–G4 automated gates pass on the final RC commit (§3).\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:334:- [ ] RC artifact gates pass on the workflow-produced RC, including ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08; record the exact source commit, workflow run, and artifact digest.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:340:- [ ] The pre-RC source gate passes from a clean source worktree: `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce`. Every B/RR source row outside the §1.1 qualification-only map must be ≥ `tested`. A mapped row below `tested` is reported as deferred; this result does not accept or qualify it.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:341:- [ ] The exact-RC evidence gate passes from the clean RC worktree and is bound to the exact RC source commit and installed RC artifact. Run the checker with the custodian-approved, immutable qualification record and evidence directory:\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:342:  `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce --qualification-record <record.json> --rc-artifact <installed-rc-package> --evidence-root <evidence-directory>`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:343:  The version 1 record contains `sourceCommit` (full commit ID), `rcTag` (for example `v1.0.0-rc.1`), `artifactSha256`, `artifactProvenance` (`sourceCommit`, `artifactSha256`, and a hashed provenance report), `independentAcceptance` (`disposition`, `reviewer`, `implementers`, zero `blockingDefects`, and a hashed report reference), and one `requirements` entry for every B/RR row. For `ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS`, include each non-blocking defect with its owner disposition; unresolved or blocking defects fail. Each requirement entry records its status and one or more hashed evidence files covering the exact criteria required by the ledger and the §1.1 qualification-only map. Every criterion evidence file must be a JSON object with top-level `sourceCommit`, `rcTag`, and `artifactSha256` values exactly matching the validated qualification record, current RC source commit, and installed RC artifact. A digest-valid report copied from another source revision, RC tag, or artifact is rejected. A B row recorded as `tested` also needs a non-empty `qualificationNotApplicable.reason` and a `qualificationNotApplicable.decision` matching the approved per-requirement exception table and a matching applicability declaration in DECISIONS.md; an unrelated or record-supplied decision is rejected. Evidence paths must be relative regular files under the evidence root, with no symlinks. Missing, unknown, stale, mismatched, or incomplete evidence fails the gate. The checker requires a clean worktree, rejects `--ledger` overrides, enforces source-ledger thresholds outside the explicit §1.1 lifecycle rows, and requires the exact-RC record itself to meet the normal status threshold for every row. It never mutates the source ledger or relaxes a requirement's B/RR record threshold. The checker validates source/tag/artifact identity bindings and evidence hashes; it does not authenticate the reviewer or prove that the artifact was built from the source commit. The approved release workflow must independently verify build provenance/attestation, and the designated custodian and independent reviewer must verify their respective approvals and custody evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:346:- [ ] Owner approval to publish (X7).\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:348:After G6, complete source checks on the exact stable-version commit before tagging, then complete the stable artifact checks in §1.1 stage 5 before publishing the draft. A failure keeps publication blocked and requires remediation plus the applicable requalification; do not mark the campaign released until published artifacts are independently verified.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:350:**Outcome recording.** The release decision record goes in `docs/releases/v1.0.0.md`, with links to every evidence directory.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":973919843}},"started_at_ms":1793344880307,"completed_at_ms":1793344882282}}
