{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T07:21:31.145Z","ordinal":521972,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18b8d-60e7-7130-962f-f0eb9e68c409","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-09363e29-19d6-44d6-aef4-8efd877a4d96","process_id":"56477","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh pr view 342 --json number,title,state,isDraft,headRefName,headRefOid,baseRefOid,mergeable,reviewDecision,latestReviews,reviews,commits,statusCheckRollup,url && git -C /home/mike/nexus-code show-ref --verify refs/remotes/origin/main && git -C /home/mike/nexus-code tag -l v1.0.0-rc.14"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh pr view 342 --json number,title,state,isDraft,headRefName,headRefOid,baseRefOid,mergeable,reviewDecision,latestReviews,reviews,commits,statusCheckRollup,url && git -C /home/mike/nexus-code show-ref --verify refs/remotes/origin/main && git -C /home/mike/nexus-code tag -l v1.0.0-rc.14"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\"baseRefOid\":\"d68695f3cb299c51959169d2373f7b924496486e\",\"commits\":[{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-10-30T06:56:56Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"mike@holownych.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Opus 5.5\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-10-30T07:20:25Z\",\"messageBody\":\"The rc.13 release run and a main CI run stalled after the evaluator test\\nfile finished because its test process did not exit; with no limit the\\njob would hold for GitHub's six-hour default. Give the CLI test step 45\\nminutes (normal runs take 12-20) in both CI jobs and the release job, and\\nassert the bound in the workflow parity test.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"ci: bound the CLI suite so a hung test process fails the job\",\"oid\":\"38cd7dce00e309d10b045e64092ab3a840bb7a5a\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-10-30T06:56:57Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"mike@holownych.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Opus 5.5\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-10-30T07:20:26Z\",\"messageBody\":\"RC13 was tagged but its release workflow failed before publishing. RC14\\nadds the evaluator compiler-exposure fixes (#335) and the CLI test bound.\\nNo product code changed since the RC12 tag.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"release: cut the 1.0.0-rc.14 candidate\",\"oid\":\"9be75eabb0b16e780f7f6ccd4253e569000b5659\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-10-30T07:15:27Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"mike@holownych.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Opus 5.5\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-10-30T07:20:26Z\",\"messageBody\":\"Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"docs(release): scope rc.14 notes to what the evaluator and limit do\",\"oid\":\"26c1f541beb3d868e0c3e1604abf674e7aa05949\"}],\"headRefName\":\"claude/rc14-candidate\",\"headRefOid\":\"26c1f541beb3d868e0c3e1604abf674e7aa05949\",\"isDraft\":false,\"latestReviews\":[],\"mergeable\":\"MERGEABLE\",\"number\":342,\"reviewDecision\":\"\",\"reviews\":[],\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"statusCheckRollup\":[{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"conclusion\":\"\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/41019505916/job/123943361949\",\"name\":\"test-matrix (22)\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-10-30T07:20:41Z\",\"status\":\"IN_PROGRESS\",\"workflowName\":\"CI\"},{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"conclusion\":\"\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/41019505875/job/123943361937\",\"name\":\"javascript-typescript\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-10-30T07:20:42Z\",\"status\":\"IN_PROGRESS\",\"workflowName\":\"CodeQL\"},{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"conclusion\":\"\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/41019505916/job/123943362235\",\"name\":\"test-matrix (24)\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-10-30T07:20:42Z\",\"status\":\"IN_PROGRESS\",\"workflowName\":\"CI\"},{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"conclusion\":\"\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://entire.com/gh/mikeholownych/-/trails/58/changes/nexus-code/57\",\"name\":\"Entire Gates\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-10-30T07:20:38Z\",\"status\":\"IN_PROGRESS\",\"workflowName\":\"\"},{\"__typename\":\"StatusContext\",\"context\":\"CodeRabbit\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-10-30T07:21:00Z\",\"state\":\"SUCCESS\",\"targetUrl\":\"\"}],\"title\":\"release: bound the CLI suite; cut 1.0.0-rc.14\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/342\"}\nd68695f3cb299c51959169d2373f7b924496486e refs/remotes/origin/main\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":764926179}},"started_at_ms":1793344890380,"completed_at_ms":1793344891145}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T07:21:31.366Z","ordinal":521973,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18b8d-60e7-7130-962f-f0eb9e68c409","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-56253c8a-dbd4-454f-a94c-68c756626f19","process_id":"15138","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '74,135p' .github/workflows/release.yml; sed -n '1,75p' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md; sed -n '325,350p' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md; sed -n '1,60p' docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.14.md 2>&1"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/post-pr335-source-gates-20261030T0720Z","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"sed -n '74,135p' .github/workflows/release.yml; sed -n '1,75p' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md; sed -n '325,350p' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md; sed -n '1,60p' docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.14.md 2>&1"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"failed","aggregated_output":"          case \"$npm_root\" in */lib/node_modules/npm) ;; *) echo \"Unexpected setup-node npm package path\" >&2; exit 1 ;; esac\n          test -f \"$npm_root/package.json\"\n          sudo install -o root -g root -m 0755 \"$node_runtime\" /usr/bin/node\n          sudo install -d -o root -g root -m 0755 /usr/lib/nexus-ci/npm\n          sudo cp -a \"$npm_root/.\" /usr/lib/nexus-ci/npm/\n          sudo chown -hR root:root /usr/lib/nexus-ci/npm\n          sudo chmod 0755 /usr/lib/nexus-ci/npm/bin/npm-cli.js\n          sudo ln -sfn /usr/lib/nexus-ci/npm/bin/npm-cli.js /usr/bin/npm\n          test \"$(/usr/bin/node --version)\" = \"$(node --version)\"\n          test \"$(env PATH=/usr/bin:/bin /usr/bin/npm --version)\" = \"$(npm --version)\"\n      - name: Require a version-matched tag on main\n        run: |\n          git fetch origin main --no-tags\n          git merge-base --is-ancestor \"$GITHUB_SHA\" origin/main\n          test \"${GITHUB_REF_NAME#v}\" = \"$(node -p 'require(\"./package.json\").version')\"\n          node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check --tag \"$GITHUB_REF_NAME\"\n          test -f \"docs/releases/${GITHUB_REF_NAME}.md\" || { echo \"Missing docs/releases/${GITHUB_REF_NAME}.md\" >&2; exit 1; }\n      - name: Require a stable tag to be a version-only commit on its RC\n        if: ${{ !contains(github.ref_name, '-') }}\n        # The checkout has full history and tags (fetch-depth: 0). The checker runs from the RC's own copy so a stable\n        # commit cannot replace it; branch and tag protection remain the control over the workflow file itself.\n        run: |\n          rc=\"$(git tag --points-at \"$GITHUB_SHA^\" | grep -E \"^${GITHUB_REF_NAME//./\\\\.}-rc\\.[0-9]+$\" | sort -V | tail -n 1 || true)\"\n          test -n \"$rc\" || { echo \"the parent of $GITHUB_REF_NAME is not a ${GITHUB_REF_NAME}-rc.N tag\" >&2; exit 1; }\n          git show \"$rc:scripts/check-version-only-diff.mjs\" > \"$RUNNER_TEMP/check-version-only-diff.mjs\"\n          node \"$RUNNER_TEMP/check-version-only-diff.mjs\" \"$rc\" \"$GITHUB_SHA\"\n      - run: npm ci --prefix cli\n      - run: npm --prefix cli run build\n      - run: cargo test --locked --manifest-path core/Cargo.toml\n      - run: cargo build --locked --release --manifest-path core/Cargo.toml --bin harness-core --bin nexus-tui\n      - run: npm --prefix cli test\n      - run: bash scripts/security_gates.sh\n      - run: bash scripts/package-linux.sh \"$GITHUB_REF_NAME\" \"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist\"\n      - run: bash scripts/package-linux.sh \"$GITHUB_REF_NAME\" \"$RUNNER_TEMP/repro-check\"\n      - run: cmp \"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/nexus-linux-x86_64-$GITHUB_REF_NAME.tar.gz\" \"$RUNNER_TEMP/repro-check/nexus-linux-x86_64-$GITHUB_REF_NAME.tar.gz\"\n      - run: cmp \"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/SHA256SUMS\" \"$RUNNER_TEMP/repro-check/SHA256SUMS\"\n      - run: cmp \"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt\" \"$RUNNER_TEMP/repro-check/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt\"\n      - run: cyclonedx validate --input-file \"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/sbom.cdx.json\" --fail-on-errors\n      - run: cmp \"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/sbom.cdx.json\" \"$RUNNER_TEMP/repro-check/sbom.cdx.json\"\n      - run: cmp \"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/install.sh\" \"$RUNNER_TEMP/repro-check/install.sh\"\n      - run: bash scripts/smoke-package.sh \"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/nexus-linux-x86_64-$GITHUB_REF_NAME.tar.gz\"\n      - run: bash scripts/installer-smoke.sh \"$GITHUB_WORKSPACE/install.sh\" \"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/nexus-linux-x86_64-$GITHUB_REF_NAME.tar.gz\"\n      - name: Attest build provenance\n        uses: actions/attest-build-provenance@92c65d2898f1f53cfdc910b962cecff86e7f8fcc # v1\n        with:\n          subject-path: |\n            ${{ runner.temp }}/dist/nexus-linux-x86_64-${{ github.ref_name }}.tar.gz\n            ${{ runner.temp }}/dist/SHA256SUMS\n      # RC tags (vX.Y.Z-rc.N) publish a prerelease: the workflow-produced RC is the qualification candidate\n      # (ACCEPTANCE §1.1 stage 2). Stable tags only build an unpublished draft (stage 5); it is published by hand with\n      # `gh release edit <tag> --draft=false` after the stable artifact checks and the signed acceptance disposition.\n      - uses: softprops/action-gh-release@3bb12739c298aeb8a4eeaf626c5b8d85266b0e65 # v2\n        with:\n          files: ${{ runner.temp }}/dist/*\n          body_path: docs/releases/${{ github.ref_name }}.md\n          prerelease: ${{ contains(github.ref_name, '-') }}\n          draft: ${{ !contains(github.ref_name, '-') }}\n# Nexus Code v1.0.0: release qualification procedure\n\nThis is the procedure that decides whether a release candidate (RC) may become v1.0.0. It defines:\n\n- the environments;\n- the workflow matrix;\n- the evidence each step must produce;\n- explicit pass/fail gates.\n\nThree separate questions are judged and recorded separately:\n\n| Question | Who answers it |\n|---|---|\n| **Implementation self-assessment** | Did the implementer's tests pass? |\n| **Product qualification** | Did the RC meet these gates on real workflows? |\n| **Independent acceptance** | Did a reviewer other than the implementer agree? |\n\nA gate passes only on archived evidence bound to the source commit or installed RC artifact that the gate evaluates. Source-level evidence names the exact source commit; installed-RC evidence names both that commit and the installed package digest. A green test suite alone never qualifies the product.\n\n## 1.1 Release-candidate lifecycle and evidence identity\n\nThe release sequence has five distinct stages. Passing an earlier stage is a prerequisite for the next stage, not a substitute for it. Every G0–G4 acceptance ID remains mandatory; the stage determines which exact input and evidence it evaluates, not whether the check applies.\n\n1. **Pre-RC source gates.** Before creating an RC tag, run required source CI and every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method evaluates source, a source-built test binary, or an environment without requiring a published RC. Record the full commit ID and check results. Source checks do not establish behavior of the installed package.\n2. **RC artifact construction.** After the required owner authorization, create the version-matched RC tag on that exact source commit and use the repository release workflow to build and publish the RC artifacts. Record the workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and provenance. The workflow-produced artifacts are the candidates for qualification; a local build or a different commit is not interchangeable. RC artifact publication is not product qualification or final release acceptance.\n3. **RC artifact gates.** Before installed-RC product qualification, run every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method requires the RC archive, RC attestation/release, or workflow-produced artifact. This includes ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08. ACC-PKG checks that explicitly require an installed package run against this RC as specified by their test method. Record the RC tag commit, workflow run, artifact digests, and each check result. A source-level analogue does not replace an artifact-bound check.\n4. **Installed-RC qualification.** Install the workflow-produced RC package using the documented procedure and run the applicable product, provider, task-quality, terminal, installation, and independent-acceptance gates in §§4–8. Bind each result to both the RC source commit and installed package digest. If a source change or rebuilt artifact changes either identity, rerun every affected gate against the new candidate and retain prior results as historical evidence.\n5. **Stable promotion and publication.** After exact-RC acceptance and G6 pass, create a stable-version commit directly on the accepted RC commit, changing only the synchronized version metadata required for v1.0.0. Record both commits and the version-only diff. Run required source CI and all applicable source G0–G4 checks on this exact stable-version commit before tagging. If any other source changes, restart RC construction and qualification. Then create the `v1.0.0` tag on that checked commit and build a draft release. Keep its assets unpublished while verifying the stable artifact identity, provenance, package contents, installation, and publication metadata. Compare the stable package contents with the accepted RC; if packaged behavior or content differs beyond version-specific metadata, rerun affected installed-RC qualification gates and obtain independent acceptance for the stable artifact. Publish the draft only after these checks pass and the signed acceptance disposition is recorded. Record the published digests and provenance.\n\nThe final G6 decision in §10 applies to promoting the accepted RC toward a stable release. It requires the applicable gates to pass for the accepted RC and authorizes the version-only stable commit and its source checks, followed by the stable tag and draft build; it does not waive source CI, artifact identity, installed-RC qualification, or any threshold. Public publication is a separate post-build gate in stage 5 above. The release workflow must keep stable assets in draft state until stable artifact checks pass. Source verification at integration 6a16cb6 confirms the tag-triggered release workflow now supports published RC prereleases and draft stable releases. The earlier immediate-stable-publication source blocker is resolved; an actual stable draft build, artifact verification, signed acceptance, and deliberate publication are still required and remain unproven until their run evidence is recorded.\n\nExact-RC requirements records identify at least one implementer and an independent reviewer. For a blocking requirement recorded as `tested` instead of `product-qualified`, the cited decision must be explicitly allowlisted for that requirement in the approved qualification-exceptions table below, and its `DECISIONS.md` section must contain a matching requirement-specific line of the form `Qualification applicability: REQ-... = NOT REQUIRED ...`. A record-supplied or unrelated decision cannot authorize an exception. The record must include digest-bound evidence for every `ACC-*` criterion in that requirement's ledger Acceptance column.\n\nThe post-RC closure requirements listed below may remain `open`, `partial`, or `implemented` in the source ledger at the RC commit because their remaining acceptance is completed during G6 or installed-RC qualification. The bare `--enforce` invocation is the pre-RC source gate: it checks every other B/RR row against the source threshold and reports mapped rows as deferred, not accepted. At G6, the exact-RC invocation must provide a record meeting the normal B/RR status threshold and digest-bound evidence for every criterion in this table. The table also supplies the criterion mapping for rows whose ledger points to an ACCEPTANCE section instead of naming ACC IDs. The source ledger is never rewritten by the record. Any below-tested required row omitted from this table still fails.\n\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:START -->\n### Qualification-only requirements for exact-RC enforcement\n\n| Requirement | Acceptance criteria required in the exact-RC record | Remaining stage |\n|---|---|---|\n| REQ-REL-003 | ACC-PLAT | Installed-RC platform and Node-version matrix |\n| REQ-AGT-002 | ACC-VER-03, ACC-VER-04, ACC-VER-09, ACC-QUAL-T2, ACC-QUAL-T3, ACC-QUAL-T4 | Installed-RC T2/T3/T4 outcome thresholds |\n| REQ-AGT-010 | ACC-TRUST-04 | Independent acceptance of the DEC-04 v1 subset |\n| REQ-PRV-003 | ACC-INF-10 | Installed-RC standalone and absent-gateway behavior |\n| REQ-REL-005 | ACC-SUP-04, ACC-SUP-05 | Exact-RC security and dependency artifact checks |\n| REQ-AGT-110 | ACC-CONT-10, ACC-GOV-06 | Installed-RC continuity and independent acceptance |\n| REQ-PRV-111 | ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC provider verification |\n| REQ-REL-114 | ACC-SUP-08 | Exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility |\n| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\n| REQ-QUAL-107 | ACC-PRV-STANDALONE, ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC standalone and provider matrix |\n| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y | Installed-RC automated and scripted PTY acceptance; the manual E3 matrix is waived by DEC-20 |\n| REQ-QUAL-109 | ACC-QUAL-T3 | Installed-RC T3 long-task qualification |\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:END -->\n\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:START -->\n### Approved exact-RC qualification exceptions\n\n| Requirement | Approved decision | Scope |\n|---|---|---|\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:END -->\n\n## 1. Rules\n\n1. The RC is built and published by the release workflow from a clean tag. Its version is identical across all components (REQ-REL-103).\n2. All qualification runs use the **installed RC package**, installed with the documented one-line command. They never use a checkout build. The only exception is CI unit and PTY suites, which run from source at the same commit.\n3. Thresholds (DEC-05) are frozen before the first M5 run. A failing gate is fixed in code and the run is repeated as `rc.N+1`. A threshold is never relaxed after results are known.\n4. Evidence goes to `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`. The directory contains:\n   - `manifest.json`: commit, package sha256, environment, model fingerprint, dates;\n   - raw outputs;\n   - a `SHA256SUMS` file.\n\n   Secrets are redacted before commit.\n5. Any step that cannot run in the available environment is recorded as **NOT RUN** with its reason. A NOT RUN on a blocker gate fails the gate.\n\n## 2. Environments\n| CON-A4 | `sudo -l` for the demo user shows only fixed argv. `sudo setpriv --reuid=0 id` is denied. |\n| CON-A5 | One clean-account `--mode cloudflare --agents real` run, with a committed, redacted run record. |\n| CON-A6 | The video source commits are tagged and published, or the docs state that they are unpublished. |\n\n## 10. Release decision (G6)\n\nG6 passes only when every item below holds. It authorizes a version-only stable commit from the accepted RC source, followed by its source checks, stable tag, and unpublished draft candidate; it does not authorize making stable assets publicly available. RC tags are candidate construction inputs governed by §1.1; an RC tag or its successful build does not satisfy this release decision.\n\n- [ ] G0–G4 automated gates pass on the final RC commit (§3).\n- [ ] RC artifact gates pass on the workflow-produced RC, including ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08; record the exact source commit, workflow run, and artifact digest.\n- [ ] §4 standalone and provider matrix: all rows PASS.\n- [ ] §5 terminal acceptance: automated CI (§5.1) and scripted PTY (§5.2) gates PASS. The manual 5×3 matrix (§5.3) is waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20.\n- [ ] §6 thresholds: all hold.\n- [ ] §7 install matrix: all rows PASS.\n- [ ] §8 independent acceptance: ACCEPT, or ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS with owner dispositions and no blocker defects outstanding.\n- [ ] The pre-RC source gate passes from a clean source worktree: `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce`. Every B/RR source row outside the §1.1 qualification-only map must be ≥ `tested`. A mapped row below `tested` is reported as deferred; this result does not accept or qualify it.\n- [ ] The exact-RC evidence gate passes from the clean RC worktree and is bound to the exact RC source commit and installed RC artifact. Run the checker with the custodian-approved, immutable qualification record and evidence directory:\n  `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce --qualification-record <record.json> --rc-artifact <installed-rc-package> --evidence-root <evidence-directory>`.\n  The version 1 record contains `sourceCommit` (full commit ID), `rcTag` (for example `v1.0.0-rc.1`), `artifactSha256`, `artifactProvenance` (`sourceCommit`, `artifactSha256`, and a hashed provenance report), `independentAcceptance` (`disposition`, `reviewer`, `implementers`, zero `blockingDefects`, and a hashed report reference), and one `requirements` entry for every B/RR row. For `ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS`, include each non-blocking defect with its owner disposition; unresolved or blocking defects fail. Each requirement entry records its status and one or more hashed evidence files covering the exact criteria required by the ledger and the §1.1 qualification-only map. Every criterion evidence file must be a JSON object with top-level `sourceCommit`, `rcTag`, and `artifactSha256` values exactly matching the validated qualification record, current RC source commit, and installed RC artifact. A digest-valid report copied from another source revision, RC tag, or artifact is rejected. A B row recorded as `tested` also needs a non-empty `qualificationNotApplicable.reason` and a `qualificationNotApplicable.decision` matching the approved per-requirement exception table and a matching applicability declaration in DECISIONS.md; an unrelated or record-supplied decision is rejected. Evidence paths must be relative regular files under the evidence root, with no symlinks. Missing, unknown, stale, mismatched, or incomplete evidence fails the gate. The checker requires a clean worktree, rejects `--ledger` overrides, enforces source-ledger thresholds outside the explicit §1.1 lifecycle rows, and requires the exact-RC record itself to meet the normal status threshold for every row. It never mutates the source ledger or relaxes a requirement's B/RR record threshold. The checker validates source/tag/artifact identity bindings and evidence hashes; it does not authenticate the reviewer or prove that the artifact was built from the source commit. The approved release workflow must independently verify build provenance/attestation, and the designated custodian and independent reviewer must verify their respective approvals and custody evidence.\n- [ ] Docs checklist (SPEC-09 §3.2) is signed off.\n- [ ] Release notes state the standalone scope (DEC-16), the provider tiers (DEC-06), the experimental surfaces (DEC-03, DEC-07) and the known limitations.\n- [ ] Owner approval to publish (X7).\n\nAfter G6, complete source checks on the exact stable-version commit before tagging, then complete the stable artifact checks in §1.1 stage 5 before publishing the draft. A failure keeps publication blocked and requires remediation plus the applicable requalification; do not mark the campaign released until published artifacts are independently verified.\n\n**Outcome recording.** The release decision record goes in `docs/releases/v1.0.0.md`, with links to every evidence directory.\nsed: can't read docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.14.md: No such file or directory\n","exit_code":2,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":982118095}},"started_at_ms":1793344890384,"completed_at_ms":1793344891366}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T07:21:32.636Z","ordinal":521974,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18baf-6edb-7271-911e-6a41a491442a","call_id":"call_ff861ed537364873b12ffd6377b17864","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.6 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":0,\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"024695\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000061842,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":171,\"output\":\"ls: cannot access '/home/mike/nexus-wt/post-pr335-source-gates-20261030T0720Z/.entire': No such file or directory\\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.entire:\\ntotal 40\\ndrwxr-x---  5 mike mike 4096 Oct 28 07:40 .\\ndrwxrwxr-x 28 mike mike 4096 Oct 30 07:04 ..\\n-rw-r--r--  1 mike mike   58 Oct 28 01:10 .gitignore\\n-rw-r--r--  1 mike mike 5397 Oct 28 07:40 agent-guide.md\\ndrwxr-x---  2 mike mike 4096 Oct 28 01:10 logs\\ndrwxr-x---  8 mike mike 4096 Oct 28 15:18 metadata\\n-rw-r--r--  1 mike mike  115 Oct 28 01:10 settings.json\\n-rw-r--r--  1 mike mike   78 Oct 28 07:27 settings.local.json\\ndrwxr-x---  2 mike mike 4096 Oct 30 07:20 tmp\\nfatal: path '.entire/agent-guide.md' does not exist in 'origin/main'\\n\"}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":1,\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"7dce76\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.764995128,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":940,\"output\":\"{\\\"baseRefOid\\\":\\\"d68695f3cb299c51959169d2373f7b924496486e\\\",\\\"commits\\\":[{\\\"authoredDate\\\":\\\"2026-10-30T06:56:56Z\\\",\\\"authors\\\":[{\\\"email\\\":\\\"mike@holownych.com\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\\\",\\\"login\\\":\\\"mikeholownych\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Mike Holownych\\\"},{\\\"email\\\":\\\"noreply@anthropic.com\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\\\",\\\"login\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Claude Opus 5.5\\\"}],\\\"committedDate\\\":\\\"2026-10-30T07:20:25Z\\\",\\\"messageBody\\\":\\\"The rc.13 release run and a main CI run stalled after the evaluator test\\\\nfile finished because its test process did not exit; with no limit the\\\\njob would hold for GitHub's six-hour default. Give the CLI test step 45\\\\nminutes (normal runs take 12-20) in both CI jobs and the release job, and\\\\nassert the bound in the workflow parity test.\\\\n\\\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\\",\\\"messageHeadline\\\":\\\"ci: bound the CLI suite so a hung test process fails the job\\\",\\\"oid\\\":\\\"38cd7dce00e309d10b045e64092ab3a840bb7a5a\\\"},{\\\"authoredDate\\\":\\\"2026-10-30T06:56:57Z\\\",\\\"authors\\\":[{\\\"email\\\":\\\"mike@holownych.com\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\\\",\\\"login\\\":\\\"mikeholownych\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Mike Holownych\\\"},{\\\"email\\\":\\\"noreply@anthropic.com\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\\\",\\\"login\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Claude Opus 5.5\\\"}],\\\"committedDate\\\":\\\"2026-10-30T07:20:26Z\\\",\\\"messageBody\\\":\\\"RC13 was tagged but its release workflow failed before publishing. RC14\\\\nadds the evaluator compiler-exposure fixes (#335) and the CLI test bound.\\\\nNo product code changed since the RC12 tag.\\\\n\\\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\\",\\\"messageHeadline\\\":\\\"release: cut the 1.0.0-rc.14 candidate\\\",\\\"oid\\\":\\\"9be75eabb0b16e780f7f6ccd4253e569000b5659\\\"},{\\\"authoredDate\\\":\\\"2026-10-30T07:15:27Z\\\",\\\"authors\\\":[{\\\"email\\\":\\\"mike@holownych.com\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\\\",\\\"login\\\":\\\"mikeholownych\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Mike Holownych\\\"},{\\\"email\\\":\\\"noreply@anthropic.com\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\\\",\\\"login\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Claude Opus 5.5\\\"}],\\\"committedDate\\\":\\\"2026-10-30T07:20:26Z\\\",\\\"messageBody\\\":\\\"Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\\",\\\"messageHeadline\\\":\\\"docs(release): scope rc.14 notes to what the evaluator and limit do\\\",\\\"oid\\\":\\\"26c1f541beb3d868e0c3e1604abf674e7aa05949\\\"}],\\\"headRefName\\\":\\\"claude/rc14-candidate\\\",\\\"headRefOid\\\":\\\"26c1f541beb3d868e0c3e1604abf674e7aa05949\\\",\\\"isDraft\\\":false,\\\"latestReviews\\\":[],\\\"mergeable\\\":\\\"MERGEABLE\\\",\\\"number\\\":342,\\\"reviewDecision\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"reviews\\\":[],\\\"state\\\":\\\"OPEN\\\",\\\"statusCheckRollup\\\":[{\\\"__typename\\\":\\\"CheckRun\\\",\\\"completedAt\\\":\\\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\\\",\\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"detailsUrl\\\":\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/41019505916/job/123943361949\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"test-matrix (22)\\\",\\\"startedAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-30T07:20:41Z\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"IN_PROGRESS\\\",\\\"workflowName\\\":\\\"CI\\\"},{\\\"__typename\\\":\\\"CheckRun\\\",\\\"completedAt\\\":\\\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\\\",\\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"detailsUrl\\\":\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/41019505875/job/123943361937\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"javascript-typescript\\\",\\\"startedAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-30T07:20:42Z\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"IN_PROGRESS\\\",\\\"workflowName\\\":\\\"CodeQL\\\"},{\\\"__typename\\\":\\\"CheckRun\\\",\\\"completedAt\\\":\\\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\\\",\\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"detailsUrl\\\":\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/41019505916/job/123943362235\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"test-matrix (24)\\\",\\\"startedAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-30T07:20:42Z\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"IN_PROGRESS\\\",\\\"workflowName\\\":\\\"CI\\\"},{\\\"__typename\\\":\\\"CheckRun\\\",\\\"completedAt\\\":\\\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\\\",\\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"detailsUrl\\\":\\\"https://entire.com/gh/mikeholownych/-/trails/58/changes/nexus-code/57\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Entire Gates\\\",\\\"startedAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-30T07:20:38Z\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"IN_PROGRESS\\\",\\\"workflowName\\\":\\\"\\\"},{\\\"__typename\\\":\\\"StatusContext\\\",\\\"context\\\":\\\"CodeRabbit\\\",\\\"startedAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-30T07:21:00Z\\\",\\\"state\\\":\\\"SUCCESS\\\",\\\"targetUrl\\\":\\\"\\\"}],\\\"title\\\":\\\"release: bound the CLI suite; cut 1.0.0-rc.14\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/342\\\"}\\nd68695f3cb299c51959169d2373f7b924496486e refs/remotes/origin/main\\n\"}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":2,\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"dd4c27\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000031299,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":4660,\"output\":\"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 4660)\\nTotal output lines: 138\\n\\n--- .git/nexus-claims/RELEASE_PUBLISHER/owner.json\\n{\\n  \\\"acceptance\\\": \\\"IN_PROGRESS; RC10 exact cross-runner PASS only for published source 16ee8ca; held-out custody/T2/T3/T4, remaining provider/standalone, exact successor-RC acceptance and human terminal 0/15 remain open\\\",\\n  \\\"active_pr\\\": \\\"268 readiness refresh after current-main CI\\\",\\n  \\\"active_pr_CI\\\": \\\"40414348606 SUCCESS\\\",\\n  \\\"active_pr_CodeQL\\\": \\\"Run 40574356438 SUCCESS on exact PR head e4db23eb5d57a42691d6cd8b5a100a57d9862763.\\\",\\n  \\\"active_pr_base\\\": \\\"fc582c66bf70e00938eedc0ce3cafc635f582540 (stale)\\\",\\n  \\\"active_pr_ci\\\": \\\"Prior PR268 checks passed on exact old head; readiness contents stale and need refresh after a33ee main gates.\\\",\\n  \\\"active_pr_codeql\\\": \\\"40299056538 SUCCESS\\\",\\n  \\\"active_pr_head\\\": \\\"eac6cdb452726368d37a8ca373b56c688e0274da\\\",\\n  \\\"active_pr_review\\\": \\\"Prior exact PR268 review was ACCEPT, but local owner commit 9ee2eb5 is not the remote head and requires a fresh exact review after refresh.\\\",\\n  \\\"agent\\\": \\\"/root\\\",\\n  \\\"base\\\": \\\"d68695f3cb299c51959169d2373f7b924496486e\\\",\\n  \\\"branch\\\": \\\"v1/rc9-credential-origin-binding\\\",\\n  \\\"current_main\\\": \\\"a33ee450bcb9fdea1c2a7c7f7e167483d85aa8f4\\\",\\n  \\\"current_main_CI\\\": \\\"40566591904 IN_PROGRESS on exact fc582c66; CodeQL status requires refresh\\\",\\n  \\\"current_main_CodeQL\\\": \\\"40419408185 SUCCESS\\\",\\n  \\\"current_main_ci\\\": \\\"CI 40580432225 exact a33ee: Node22 and Node24 SUCCESS; Linux job is setting up Node before CLI/package checks.\\\",\\n  \\\"current_main_codeql\\\": \\\"CodeQL 40580432183 SUCCESS exact a33ee450bcb9fdea1c2a7c7f7e167483d85aa8f4.\\\",\\n  \\\"current_main_requirements\\\": \\\"PASS exact clean worktree; 123 rows, 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 explicit exact-RC deferrals\\\",\\n  \\\"current_main_version\\\": \\\"PASS exact clean worktree; all components 1.0.0-rc.9\\\",\\n  \\\"desktop_terminal_preflight\\\": \\\"ubuntu-desktop 10.0.8.3 reachable with strict host key; GitHub CLI authenticated; active local Wayland session 7; xterm, kitty, gnome-terminal, tmux, code present; human matrix remains 0/15, awaits installed exact RC\\\",\\n  \\\"head\\\": \\\"cfee7f561540b5e9e02f03f540614c5efcdb4b35\\\",\\n  \\\"heldout_custody_refresh\\\": \\\"Issue #1 remains OPEN with no custodian response to coordinator metadata-only request at 2026-10-27T18:47:09Z; no private corpus access or qualification.\\\",\\n  \\\"host\\\": \\\"mike-dev\\\",\\n  \\\"independent_review\\\": \\\"ACCEPT by rc5_candidate_review at exact base-to-head diff SHA-256 06ac7420c9901f4c9d77367900de7ce3e9b4eae3fa3535144501dd614a71f5a0\\\",\\n  \\\"last_observed_at\\\": \\\"2026-10-27T21:00:40Z\\\",\\n  \\\"latest_main\\\": \\\"cf05322cc0368af900b2fb425852daa2d0de403e\\\",\\n  \\\"latest_main_ci\\\": \\\"40561348972 IN_PROGRESS (Node 22/24 npm cli tests); CodeQL 40561348985 SUCCESS\\\",\\n  \\\"latest_requirements\\\": \\\"PASS exact cf05322: 123 rows; 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 exact-RC deferrals; RC10 version sync PASS\\\",\\n  \\\"main_ci_run\\\": \\\"40327501470 SUCCESS on b73b6ecaf753ff3eba8d5e1930ede7a471359421\\\",\\n  \\\"main_codeql_run\\\": \\\"40327501389 IN_PROGRESS on b73b6ecaf753ff3eba8d5e1930ede7a471359421\\\",\\n  \\\"main_codeql_runs\\\": \\\"40327501389 SUCCESS; 40331254134 SUCCESS on b73b6ecaf753ff3eba8d5e1930ede7a471359421\\\",\\n  \\\"merge_commit\\\": \\\"468646bb58f22db573b06db2c2fc889b444df6cc\\\",\\n  \\\"merged_pr\\\": 246,\\n  \\\"merged_pr254\\\": \\\"PR #254 exact head 24774a1136775a9069981a5d8d9b763d8fa09253, base 7f52ed1b76e2fa69dee1416d1b13f1e1263ff52d; merged 2026-10-26T13:04:33Z as b73b6ecaf753ff3eba8d5e1930ede7a471359421; exact CI40322090307 all required jobs SUCCESS, CodeQL40322090216 SUCCESS; independent ACCEPT.\\\",\\n  \\\"next\\\": \\\"Continue independent exact-RC acceptance. Held-out T2/T3 task custody is externally blocked; human real-terminal 15-cell matrix needs …2860 tokens truncated… \\\"updated_at\\\": \\\"2026-10-30T07:20:44+00:00\\\",\\n  \\\"version_sync\\\": \\\"PASS: components at 1.0.0-rc.8\\\",\\n  \\\"worktree\\\": \\\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc7-version-bump\\\",\\n  \\\"pr281_merge\\\": \\\"MERGED 2026-10-27T19:55:27Z as 45ca37b467b5e6a7b42be733be61e6964c73b4fd after exact head e17419414b3e01d835fd54ae7589e3aad50272d9; Node22, Node24, Linux packaging, JS/TS and CodeQL PASS; independent evidence review ACCEPT. Promotes evidence availability only; requirement ledger owner still must reconcile REQ-REL-114.\\\",\\n  \\\"current_main_source_gates\\\": \\\"PASS exact main 45ca37b467b5e6a7b42be733be61e6964c73b4fd in clean detached worktree with isolated HOME/XDG: check_requirements --enforce (123 rows:108 tested,6 partial,2 implemented,7 open; 12 explicit exact-RC deferrals) and sync-version --check --tag v1.0.0-rc.10.\\\",\\n  \\\"post_merge_ci\\\": \\\"Run 40580432225 exact a33ee in progress; Node22 Rust tests, Node24 release build; prior source/version/requirements checks passed in both lanes.\\\",\\n  \\\"post_merge_codeql\\\": \\\"Run 40580432183 exact a33ee in progress.\\\",\\n  \\\"pr282\\\": \\\"MERGED 2026-10-27T20:42:26Z as a33ee450bcb9fdea1c2a7c7f7e167483d85aa8f4; exact checks and independent review passed; corrects PR281 reproducibility claim to six checked artifacts.\\\",\\n  \\\"pr283\\\": \\\"Open RC10 E2 install/doctor evidence PR, head 71a4218a on old base 45ca37b; active Kimi claim QUAL_RC10_E2; independent review identified 21 ignored logs missing from SHA256SUMS. Do not accept or integrate pending owner correction and review.\\\",\\n  \\\"historical_rc9_status\\\": \\\"RC9 release workflow 40370485753 SUCCESS; tag signature locally good and GitHub verified; complete release assets SHA256SUMS pass; GitHub attestations pass for archive and checksum index; installed exact RC9 on ubuntu-desktop in isolated prefix with archive SHA-256 35795d2b7639b68a541c512976d8bc7f251115ebdccf48f6b9cf5f98ef1af9bb; acceptance IN_PROGRESS; held-out custody and manual terminal matrix still pending.\\\",\\n  \\\"historical_terminal_matrix\\\": \\\"0/15; user cannot run the xterm 80x24 cell now. No manual checks started. Idle SUITE/GATEWAY claims released and logged; worksheet/procedure remains ready.\\\",\\n  \\\"release_authorization\\\": \\\"Granted by operator for required pushes, PRs, merges, RC tags, and stable publication after acceptance; execution remains gated by mandatory acceptance. No further authorization request required.\\\"\\n}\\n--- .git/nexus-claims/FILE_.github_workflows_release.yml/owner.json\\n{\\n  \\\"agent\\\": \\\"codex-root\\\",\\n  \\\"host\\\": \\\"mike-dev\\\",\\n  \\\"branch\\\": \\\"codex/pr335-release-parity-combination\\\",\\n  \\\"worktree\\\": \\\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/pr335-release-parity-combination\\\",\\n  \\\"base\\\": \\\"391f49bcddb75e63d73b232b3cdec88a17fd6f66\\\",\\n  \\\"since\\\": \\\"2026-10-30T05:10:59Z\\\",\\n  \\\"scope\\\": \\\"PR341 stalled-slice takeover: remove release dependence on retired evaluator runner-trim script and strengthen parity test to require mandatory setup in both workflows before CLI suite. Preserve original claude worktree and branch; no tag or publication.\\\",\\n  \\\"head\\\": \\\"d01b25cc7dceee02e3e1f37e88bf9e82705dffef\\\",\\n  \\\"review\\\": {\\n    \\\"reviewer\\\": \\\"pr311_draft_review\\\",\\n    \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"ACCEPT\\\",\\n    \\\"base\\\": \\\"391f49bcddb75e63d73b232b3cdec88a17fd6f66\\\",\\n    \\\"head\\\": \\\"b2b9ac825c2e3d5a4961d91f020b2a0d1c1f7e45\\\",\\n    \\\"diff_sha256\\\": \\\"52ffa07bb59e9d1051fa293ee644a61cdfe08564d0ab973ccefd67d76bfa7000\\\",\\n    \\\"findings\\\": []\\n  },\\n  \\\"status\\\": \\\"PR335 exact head d01b25cc pushed; alias-mask correction independently ACCEPTed; focused evaluator 31/31 PASS; exact-head CI 41014835061 and CodeQL 41014833152 running. Existing main and RC13 suites remain separately tracked under SUITE claim.\\\",\\n  \\\"last_updated\\\": \\\"2026-10-30T06:35:44.124Z\\\"\\n}\\n\"}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":3,\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"069272\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.982147648,\"exit_code\":2,\"original_token_count\":4581,\"output\":\"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 4581)\\nTotal output lines: 159\\n\\n          case \\\"$npm_root\\\" in */lib/node_modules/npm) ;; *) echo \\\"Unexpected setup-node npm package path\\\" >&2; exit 1 ;; esac\\n          test -f \\\"$npm_root/package.json\\\"\\n          sudo install -o root -g root -m 0755 \\\"$node_runtime\\\" /usr/bin/node\\n          sudo install -d -o root -g root -m 0755 /usr/lib/nexus-ci/npm\\n          sudo cp -a \\\"$npm_root/.\\\" /usr/lib/nexus-ci/npm/\\n          sudo chown -hR root:root /usr/lib/nexus-ci/npm\\n          sudo chmod 0755 /usr/lib/nexus-ci/npm/bin/npm-cli.js\\n          sudo ln -sfn /usr/lib/nexus-ci/npm/bin/npm-cli.js /usr/bin/npm\\n          test \\\"$(/usr/bin/node --version)\\\" = \\\"$(node --version)\\\"\\n          test \\\"$(env PATH=/usr/bin:/bin /usr/bin/npm --version)\\\" = \\\"$(npm --version)\\\"\\n      - name: Require a version-matched tag on main\\n        run: |\\n          git fetch origin main --no-tags\\n          git merge-base --is-ancestor \\\"$GITHUB_SHA\\\" origin/main\\n          test \\\"${GITHUB_REF_NAME#v}\\\" = \\\"$(node -p 'require(\\\"./package.json\\\").version')\\\"\\n          node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check --tag \\\"$GITHUB_REF_NAME\\\"\\n          test -f \\\"docs/releases/${GITHUB_REF_NAME}.md\\\" || { echo \\\"Missing docs/releases/${GITHUB_REF_NAME}.md\\\" >&2; exit 1; }\\n      - name: Require a stable tag to be a version-only commit on its RC\\n        if: ${{ !contains(github.ref_name, '-') }}\\n        # The checkout has full history and tags (fetch-depth: 0). The checker runs from the RC's own copy so a stable\\n        # commit cannot replace it; branch and tag protection remain the control over the workflow file itself.\\n        run: |\\n          rc=\\\"$(git tag --points-at \\\"$GITHUB_SHA^\\\" | grep -E \\\"^${GITHUB_REF_NAME//./\\\\\\\\.}-rc\\\\.[0-9]+$\\\" | sort -V | tail -n 1 || true)\\\"\\n          test -n \\\"$rc\\\" || { echo \\\"the parent of $GITHUB_REF_NAME is not a ${GITHUB_REF_NAME}-rc.N tag\\\" >&2; exit 1; }\\n          git show \\\"$rc:scripts/check-version-only-diff.mjs\\\" > \\\"$RUNNER_TEMP/check-version-only-diff.mjs\\\"\\n          node \\\"$RUNNER_TEMP/check-version-only-diff.mjs\\\" \\\"$rc\\\" \\\"$GITHUB_SHA\\\"\\n      - run: npm ci --prefix cli\\n      - run: npm --prefix cli run build\\n      - run: cargo test --locked --manifest-path core/Cargo.toml\\n      - run: cargo build --locked --release --manifest-path core/Cargo.toml --bin harness-core --bin nexus-tui\\n      - run: npm --prefix cli test\\n      - run: bash scripts/security_gates.sh\\n      - run: bash scripts/package-linux.sh \\\"$GITHUB_REF_NAME\\\" \\\"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist\\\"\\n      - run: bash scripts/package-linux.sh \\\"$GITHUB_REF_NAME\\\" \\\"$RUNNER_TEMP/repro-check\\\"\\n      - run: cmp \\\"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/nexus-linux-x86_64-$GITHUB_REF_NAME.tar.gz\\\" \\\"$RUNNER_TEMP/repro-check/nexus-linux-x86_64-$GITHUB_REF_NAME.tar.gz\\\"\\n      - run: cmp \\\"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/SHA256SUMS\\\" \\\"$RUNNER_TEMP/repro-check/SHA256SUMS\\\"\\n      - run: cmp \\\"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt\\\" \\\"$RUNNER_TEMP/repro-check/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt\\\"\\n      - run: cyclonedx validate --input-file \\\"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/sbom.cdx.json\\\" --fail-on-errors\\n      - run: cmp \\\"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/sbom.cdx.json\\\" \\\"$RUNNER_TEMP/repro-check/sbom.cdx.json\\\"\\n      - run: cmp \\\"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/install.sh\\\" \\\"$RUNNER_TEMP/repro-check/install.sh\\\"\\n      - run: bash scripts/smoke-package.sh \\\"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/nexus-linux-x86_64-$GITHUB_REF_NAME.tar.gz\\\"\\n      - run: bash scripts/installer-smoke.sh \\\"$GITHUB_WORKSPACE/install.sh\\\" \\\"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/nexus-linux-x86_64-$GITHUB_REF_NAME.tar.gz\\\"\\n      - name: Attest build provenance\\n        uses: actions/attest-build-provenance@92c65d2898f1f53cfdc910b962cecff86e7f8fcc # v1\\n        with:\\n          subject-path: |\\n            ${{ runner.temp }}/dist/nexus-linux-x86_64-${{ github.ref_name }}.tar.gz\\n            ${{ runner.temp }}/dist/SHA256SUMS\\n      # RC tags (vX.Y.Z-rc.N) publish a prerelease: the workflow-produced RC is the qualification candidate\\n      # (ACCEPTANCE §1.1 stage 2). Stable tags only build an unpublished draft (stage 5); it is published by hand with\\n      # `gh release edit <tag> --draft=false` after the stable artifact checks and the signed acceptance disposition.\\n      - uses: softprops/action-gh-release@3bb12739c298aeb8a4eeaf626c5b8d85266b0e65 # v2\\n        with:\\n          files: ${{ runner.temp }}/dist/*\\n          body_path: docs/releases/${{ github.ref_name }}.md\\n          prerelease: ${{ contains(github.ref_name, '-') }}\\n          draft: ${{ !contains(github.ref_name, '-') }}\\n# Nexus Code v1.0.0: release qualification procedure\\n\\nThis is the procedure that decides whether a release candidate (RC) may become v1.0.0. It defines:\\n\\n- the environments;\\n- the workflow matrix;\\n- the evidence each step must produce;\\n- explicit pass/fail gates.\\n\\nThree separate questions are judged and recorded separately:\\n\\n| Question | Who answers it |\\n|---|---|\\n| **Implementation self-assessment** | Did the implementer's tests pass? |\\n| **Product qualification** | Did the RC meet these gates on real workflows? |\\n| **Independent acceptance** | Did a reviewer other than the implementer agree? |\\n\\nA gate passes only on archived evidence bound to the source commit o…2081 tokens truncated… user shows only fixed argv. `sudo setpriv --reuid=0 id` is denied. |\\n| CON-A5 | One clean-account `--mode cloudflare --agents real` run, with a committed, redacted run record. |\\n| CON-A6 | The video source commits are tagged and published, or the docs state that they are unpublished. |\\n\\n## 10. Release decision (G6)\\n\\nG6 passes only when every item below holds. It authorizes a version-only stable commit from the accepted RC source, followed by its source checks, stable tag, and unpublished draft candidate; it does not authorize making stable assets publicly available. RC tags are candidate construction inputs governed by §1.1; an RC tag or its successful build does not satisfy this release decision.\\n\\n- [ ] G0–G4 automated gates pass on the final RC commit (§3).\\n- [ ] RC artifact gates pass on the workflow-produced RC, including ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08; record the exact source commit, workflow run, and artifact digest.\\n- [ ] §4 standalone and provider matrix: all rows PASS.\\n- [ ] §5 terminal acceptance: automated CI (§5.1) and scripted PTY (§5.2) gates PASS. The manual 5×3 matrix (§5.3) is waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20.\\n- [ ] §6 thresholds: all hold.\\n- [ ] §7 install matrix: all rows PASS.\\n- [ ] §8 independent acceptance: ACCEPT, or ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS with owner dispositions and no blocker defects outstanding.\\n- [ ] The pre-RC source gate passes from a clean source worktree: `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce`. Every B/RR source row outside the §1.1 qualification-only map must be ≥ `tested`. A mapped row below `tested` is reported as deferred; this result does not accept or qualify it.\\n- [ ] The exact-RC evidence gate passes from the clean RC worktree and is bound to the exact RC source commit and installed RC artifact. Run the checker with the custodian-approved, immutable qualification record and evidence directory:\\n  `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce --qualification-record <record.json> --rc-artifact <installed-rc-package> --evidence-root <evidence-directory>`.\\n  The version 1 record contains `sourceCommit` (full commit ID), `rcTag` (for example `v1.0.0-rc.1`), `artifactSha256`, `artifactProvenance` (`sourceCommit`, `artifactSha256`, and a hashed provenance report), `independentAcceptance` (`disposition`, `reviewer`, `implementers`, zero `blockingDefects`, and a hashed report reference), and one `requirements` entry for every B/RR row. For `ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS`, include each non-blocking defect with its owner disposition; unresolved or blocking defects fail. Each requirement entry records its status and one or more hashed evidence files covering the exact criteria required by the ledger and the §1.1 qualification-only map. Every criterion evidence file must be a JSON object with top-level `sourceCommit`, `rcTag`, and `artifactSha256` values exactly matching the validated qualification record, current RC source commit, and installed RC artifact. A digest-valid report copied from another source revision, RC tag, or artifact is rejected. A B row recorded as `tested` also needs a non-empty `qualificationNotApplicable.reason` and a `qualificationNotApplicable.decision` matching the approved per-requirement exception table and a matching applicability declaration in DECISIONS.md; an unrelated or record-supplied decision is rejected. Evidence paths must be relative regular files under the evidence root, with no symlinks. Missing, unknown, stale, mismatched, or incomplete evidence fails the gate. The checker requires a clean worktree, rejects `--ledger` overrides, enforces source-ledger thresholds outside the explicit §1.1 lifecycle rows, and requires the exact-RC record itself to meet the normal status threshold for every row. It never mutates the source ledger or relaxes a requirement's B/RR record threshold. The checker validates source/tag/artifact identity bindings and evidence hashes; it does not authenticate the reviewer or prove that the artifact was built from the source commit. The approved release workflow must independently verify build provenance/attestation, and the designated custodian and independent reviewer must verify their respective approvals and custody evidence.\\n- [ ] Docs checklist (SPEC-09 §3.2) is signed off.\\n- [ ] Release notes state the standalone scope (DEC-16), the provider tiers (DEC-06), the experimental surfaces (DEC-03, DEC-07) and the known limitations.\\n- [ ] Owner approval to publish (X7).\\n\\nAfter G6, complete source checks on the exact stable-version commit before tagging, then complete the stable artifact checks in §1.1 stage 5 before publishing the draft. A failure keeps publication blocked and requires remediation plus the applicable requalification; do not mark the campaign released until published artifacts are independently verified.\\n\\n**Outcome recording.** The release decision record goes in `docs/releases/v1.0.0.md`, with links to every evidence directory.\\nsed: can't read docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.14.md: No such file or directory\\n\"}}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18b8d-60e7-7130-962f-f0eb9e68c409","create_time":1793344892.6357825}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
