{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T07:21:34.290Z","ordinal":521980,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a18baf-7552-7952-92e4-3dd9c23079da","call_id":"call_83edeaccc8d1456392864bf12c82cb01","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/pr311_draft_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** — staged index tree `779dac36c7f464f9cbec8fffcf58d4ce01faa1b4`; the scoped release/test diff against current main matches SHA-256 `6f204694cbbda61be88753e6bbfee353382852f3e27cc16995c44eb5565d5c2a`.\\n\\nAfter PR335 removes the runner-trim calls and script, release and both CI jobs use the required Go/Rust toolchain, sandbox, tmpfs, and isolated Node setup before their CLI suites. The parity test checks setup presence and order for all three jobs and rejects the retired trim invocation ([test](/home/mike/nexus-wt/pr335-release-parity-combination/cli/test/release_workflow_parity.test.ts:34)). No trim calls remain in either workflow.\\n\\nNo findings. Read-only review; no tests run.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/review_pr300_readiness\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** — reviewed the uncommitted delta over `ba72d2cbfb8f446254cf829ac5990148fed82500`. The new report binds the task to RC11’s source revision, archive digest, installed version, OpenRouter model, declared deliverable, and explicit verifier (`openrouter-live-task-20261030.md:5–11`). It preserves the incomplete and unverified attempts, records the final verified disposition and reported independent 2/2 rerun, and limits the claim to one synthetic task rather than E5 or RC acceptance (`:15–19, :29–39`; `README.md:32–40`).\\n\\n`sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS` passed for all 23 entries; `git diff --check` passed. The new report contains no credentials or raw prompt transcript. Its hashes for source, test, flight log, and receipts are documented, but those raw files are not included, so those hashes and run details remain operator-reported rather than independently reproducible (`:29–35`).\\n\\nDiff SHA-256: `db79879f51989668a8b6367b78329df9584114e34abe53d0fa564eeeffd8d09f`. I did not edit files or run qualification.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/review_pr302\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT.** The lockfile-only change resolves the cited RUSTSEC-2026-0418: it upgrades `libz-sys` to the stated fixed version, 1.1.31. The locked `cc` is 1.5.1, below the advisory’s affected `cc >= 1.6.0` condition. The new checksum matches the local crates.io index entry, and the diff changes no other dependencies.\\n\\nI could not retrieve RUSTSEC-2026-0418 through the available advisory lookup, so that applicability assessment relies on the exact advisory details you supplied from main CI. No tests or suites were run.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18b8d-60e7-7130-962f-f0eb9e68c409","create_time":1793344894.2907417}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
