{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Independent read-only review at exact head `26c1f541beb3d868e0c3e1604abf674e7aa05949` (base `d68695f3cb299c51959169d2373f7b924496486e`), diff SHA-256 `cf75b63f9d3b90491e5bb1f03f4486fcf2dbf1e9654be17079d21bf2b17781d0`:\\n\\n**CONCERNS (one non-blocking test gap).** The three workflow CLI suite steps use the intended 45-minute timeout, and the RC14 notes accurately describe the timeout and unresolved hang cause. The parity assertion currently accepts any numeric timeout, so it would also pass if one workflow drifted from the intended 45 minutes. Please assert `timeout-minutes: 45` for each workflow job. No source or tests were run by the reviewer; this review does not qualify the RC.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-30T07:23:05Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only audit found a factual correction needed in the RC14 release notes: tag run 41009328850 for RC13 is verified as CANCELLED while CLI tests were active, with downstream packaging skipped. The available logs do not show a test failure or the stated compiler-exposure refusal. Please describe the run as cancelled unless you have a separate exact failure record to cite. This preserves the verified outcome without attributing an unsupported cause.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-30T07:23:11Z\"}],\"reviewDecision\":\"\",\"reviews\":[]}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":567839686}},"started_at_ms":1793344997300,"completed_at_ms":1793344997869}}
