{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T07:23:48.474Z","ordinal":522131,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18b8d-60e7-7130-962f-f0eb9e68c409","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-8624e13f-7473-456b-9bc1-a61248508a8e","process_id":"8894","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh run view 40994457283 --json headSha,conclusion,jobs --jq '{headSha,conclusion,jobs:(.jobs|map({name,conclusion,steps:(.steps|map(select(.conclusion==\"failure\")|{name,number,conclusion}))}))}'; gh pr view 339 --comments --json comments --jq '.comments|map({author:.author.login,createdAt,body})|.[-8:]'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh run view 40994457283 --json headSha,conclusion,jobs --jq '{headSha,conclusion,jobs:(.jobs|map({name,conclusion,steps:(.steps|map(select(.conclusion==\"failure\")|{name,number,conclusion}))}))}'; gh pr view 339 --comments --json comments --jq '.comments|map({author:.author.login,createdAt,body})|.[-8:]'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"failed","aggregated_output":"{\"conclusion\":\"failure\",\"headSha\":\"165a2734548737de3ea426887dcb25980e6f0a8a\",\"jobs\":[{\"conclusion\":\"failure\",\"name\":\"test-matrix (22)\",\"steps\":[{\"conclusion\":\"failure\",\"name\":\"Run npm --prefix cli test\",\"number\":20}]},{\"conclusion\":\"success\",\"name\":\"test-matrix (24)\",\"steps\":[]},{\"conclusion\":\"skipped\",\"name\":\"linux-x86_64\",\"steps\":[]}]}\nspecify only one of --comments or --json\n\nDisplay the title, body, and other information about a pull request.\n\nWithout an argument, the pull request that belongs to the current branch\nis displayed.\n\nWhen `--comments` is used, terminal output includes the pull request details, comments,\nand reviews. When output is piped or redirected, only comments and reviews are printed.\n\nWith `--web` flag, open the pull request in a web browser instead.\n\nFor more information about output formatting flags, see `gh help formatting`.\n\nUSAGE\n  gh pr view [<number> | <url> | <branch>] [flags]\n\nFLAGS\n  -c, --comments          View pull request comments\n  -q, --jq expression     Filter JSON output using a jq expression\n      --json fields       Output JSON with the specified fields\n  -t, --template string   Format JSON output using a Go template; see \"gh help formatting\"\n  -w, --web               Open a pull request in the browser\n\nINHERITED FLAGS\n      --help                     Show help for command\n  -R, --repo [HOST/]OWNER/REPO   Select another repository using the [HOST/]OWNER/REPO format\n\nJSON FIELDS\n  additions, assignees, author, autoMergeRequest, baseRefName, baseRefOid, body,\n  changedFiles, closed, closedAt, closingIssuesReferences, comments, commits,\n  createdAt, deletions, files, fullDatabaseId, headRefName, headRefOid,\n  headRepository, headRepositoryOwner, id, isCrossRepository, isDraft, labels,\n  latestReviews, maintainerCanModify, mergeCommit, mergeStateStatus, mergeable,\n  mergedAt, mergedBy, milestone, number, potentialMergeCommit, projectCards,\n  projectItems, reactionGroups, reviewDecision, reviewRequests, reviews, state,\n  statusCheckRollup, title, updatedAt, url\n\nLEARN MORE\n  Use `gh <command> <subcommand> --help` for more information about a command.\n  Read the manual at https://cli.github.com/manual\n  Learn about exit codes using `gh help exit-codes`\n  Learn about accessibility experiences using `gh help accessibility`\n\n","exit_code":1,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":823265230}},"started_at_ms":1793345027648,"completed_at_ms":1793345028474}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T07:23:48.721Z","ordinal":522132,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18b8d-60e7-7130-962f-f0eb9e68c409","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-1385b399-28ff-46c1-a02e-159ce9f06d17","process_id":"29973","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh pr view 339 --json number,title,body,state,isDraft,headRefName,headRefOid,baseRefOid,mergeable,reviewDecision,reviews,statusCheckRollup,commits,files,url"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh pr view 339 --json number,title,body,state,isDraft,headRefName,headRefOid,baseRefOid,mergeable,reviewDecision,reviews,statusCheckRollup,commits,files,url"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\"baseRefOid\":\"5c516476e8dfcaf9cdd59eaa204134e25d2be673\",\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\nArchives installed `v1.0.0-rc.11` scripted PTY evidence against the exact candidate artifact:\\n\\n- Source: `8d4e5319f1a31ee67e31d3edb6b44c2e7d9ecb05`\\n- Linux archive SHA-256: `72d73f3565a48fb83d0c9a13a93fe38c2a3ae8af75184dab3af73c0b749c4053`\\n\\nThe packet preserves raw PTY captures and scripts, corrected s1 follow-up evidence, three s9 named-survivor runs, and a timestamped three-trial s5 cancellation rerun. The s5 rerun observed the first `cancelling…` output 2.266–3.366ms after Ctrl-C and idle within 188.367–521.106ms. That is within the recorded 16.667ms one-frame budget and 5s idle bound for the synthetic PTY scenario.\\n\\n## Independent review and limits\\n\\n`plan05_readonly_review` independently ACCEPTed the earlier corrected packet’s accuracy and integrity, including s9, while §5.2 was pending due to missing s5 timing. The new s5 timestamped evidence was added afterward and is awaiting fresh independent review. This PR does not claim exact-RC or whole-release acceptance. No held-out material or user workspace was accessed.\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\n- Outer and nested SHA-256 inventories verified.\\n- `gitleaks dir` found no leaks.\\n- No embedded `.git` stores or Python bytecode are included.\\n- The exact installed RC11 binary reported `1.0.0-rc.11 (8d4e5319f1a3)` and its archive digest matched the recorded release digest.\\n- The initial runner setup lacked `pyte` and stopped before any trial. The pinned dependency was installed in a disposable virtual environment; all three recorded trials then completed.\\n\",\"commits\":[{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-10-30T02:45:09Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"mike@holownych.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-10-30T02:45:09Z\",\"messageBody\":\"\",\"messageHeadline\":\"docs(qualification): archive RC11 scripted PTY evidence\",\"oid\":\"87a332f4036bb7af81ccf1e751189c19dd523149\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-10-30T02:50:35Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"mike@holownych.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-10-30T02:50:35Z\",\"messageBody\":\"\",\"messageHeadline\":\"docs(qualification): measure RC11 PTY cancel acknowledgment\",\"oid\":\"8ae6ec4d6e1efd2e1f1625d8488aed25b8c012fd\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-10-30T02:55:15Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"mike@holownych.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-10-30T02:55:15Z\",\"messageBody\":\"\",\"messageHeadline\":\"docs(qualification): correct RC11 PTY evidence file list\",\"oid\":\"165a2734548737de3ea426887dcb25980e6f0a8a\"}],\"files\":[{\"path\":\"docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.11/scripted-pty/RC11-SCRIPTED-RESULTS.md\",\"additions\":31,\"deletions\":0,\"changeType\":\"ADDED\"},{\"path\":\"docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.11/scripted-pty/README.md\",\"additions\":21,\"deletions\":0,\"changeType\":\"ADDED\"},{\"path\":\"docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.11/scripted-pty/RECOVERY-STA