{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T07:24:42.985Z","ordinal":522196,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18b8d-60e7-7130-962f-f0eb9e68c409","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-2f2d4085-0da4-4c67-b248-e8c0be93801a","process_id":"67915","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh pr view 342 --json updatedAt,comments,statusCheckRollup --jq '{updatedAt,comments:(.comments|map({author:.author.login,createdAt,body})|.[-5:]),checks:(.statusCheckRollup|map({name,status,conclusion}))}'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh pr view 342 --json updatedAt,comments,statusCheckRollup --jq '{updatedAt,comments:(.comments|map({author:.author.login,createdAt,body})|.[-5:]),checks:(.statusCheckRollup|map({name,status,conclusion}))}'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\"checks\":[{\"conclusion\":\"\",\"name\":\"test-matrix (22)\",\"status\":\"IN_PROGRESS\"},{\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"name\":\"javascript-typescript\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\"},{\"conclusion\":\"\",\"name\":\"test-matrix (24)\",\"status\":\"IN_PROGRESS\"},{\"conclusion\":\"\",\"name\":\"Entire Gates\",\"status\":\"IN_PROGRESS\"},{\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"name\":\"CodeQL\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\"},{\"conclusion\":null,\"name\":null,\"status\":null}],\"comments\":[{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Independent review (fresh-context read-only reviewer subagent, not the author) of delta d01b25cc..f05b3d40ed17602b1f8cd3387c67161b83c69c86: **ACCEPT**, 0 blocking.\\n- Step-level timeout-minutes is valid YAML and is on all three CLI test steps; 45 min is about 2.5× the slowest past run.\\n- The parity assertion passes on head and fails with the limit removed.\\n- sync-version --check and requirements --enforce both pass.\\n- `git diff v1.0.0-rc.12 f05b3d40` touches nothing under cli/src, core/src or cli/dist.\\n\\nThe author applied the two notes-accuracy non-blocking findings in 5e400d5c: the cause-reporting claim is scoped to inventory-helper failures, and the notes now say the hang's root cause hasn't been identified. Delta confirmation is pending.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-30T07:15:32Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Independent delta review (same fresh-context read-only reviewer) of f05b3d40..5e400d5c5af8e8c0e1a07bac59e54d921babe168: **ACCEPT**, 0 blocking. The delta is two lines in docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.14.md, and both wordings match eval/isolate.mjs. The reviewer's caveat that a main CI run stalled is verified by run 40999028554: test-matrix (22) ran 03:44:14Z to 04:57:05Z and was cancelled; its last completed test was the final test in eval_integrity.test.ts.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-30T07:15:55Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Rebased onto main d68695f3 (the #335 merge, whose tree is identical to d01b25cc). The new head is 26c1f541beb3d868e0c3e1604abf674e7aa05949. `git diff origin/main 26c1f541beb3d868e0c3e1604abf674e7aa05949` is byte-identical to the reviewed `git diff d01b25cc 5e400d5c`, so the independent ACCEPTs carry over unchanged. requirements --enforce: exit 0; sync-version: rc.14. Marked ready; merge waits for exact-head green CI.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-30T07:20:38Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Independent read-only review at exact head `26c1f541beb3d868e0c3e1604abf674e7aa05949` (base `d68695f3cb299c51959169d2373f7b924496486e`), diff SHA-256 `cf75b63f9d3b90491e5bb1f03f4486fcf2dbf1e9654be17079d21bf2b17781d0`:\\n\\n**CONCERNS (one non-blocking test gap).** The three workflow CLI suite steps use the intended 45-minute timeout, and the RC14 notes accurately describe the timeout and unresolved hang cause. The parity assertion currently accepts any numeric timeout, so it would also pass if one workflow drifted from the intended 45 minutes. Please assert `timeout-minutes: 45` for each workflow job. No source or tests were run by the reviewer; this review does not qualify the RC.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-30T07:23:05Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only audit found a factual correction needed in the RC14 release notes: tag run 41009328850 for RC13 is verified as CANCELLED while CLI tests were active, with downstream packaging skipped. The available logs do not show a test failure or the stated compiler-exposure refusal. Please describe the run as cancelled unless you have a separate exact failure record to cite. This preserves the verified outcome without attributing an unsupported cause.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-30T07:23:11Z\"}],\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-30T07:23:11Z\"}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":612017901}},"started_at_ms":1793345082367,"completed_at_ms":1793345082985}}
