{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T07:24:48.785Z","ordinal":522206,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18b8d-60e7-7130-962f-f0eb9e68c409","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-e6353804-4907-446e-912a-b0726668e63d","process_id":"74282","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh run view --help | sed -n '1,100p'; gh api repos/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/41009328850 --jq '{run_attempt,created_at,updated_at,status,conclusion,html_url}'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh run view --help | sed -n '1,100p'; gh api repos/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/41009328850 --jq '{run_attempt,created_at,updated_at,status,conclusion,html_url}'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"View a summary of a workflow run.\n\nDue to platform limitations, `gh` may not always be able to associate jobs with their\ncorresponding logs when using the primary method of fetching logs in zip format.\n\nIn such cases, `gh` will attempt to fetch logs for each job individually via the API.\nThis fallback is slower and more resource-intensive. If more than 25 job logs are missing,\nthe operation will fail with an error.\n\nAdditionally, due to similar platform constraints, some log lines may not be\nassociated with a specific step within a job. In these cases, the step name will\nappear as `UNKNOWN STEP` in the log output.\n\nFor more information about output formatting flags, see `gh help formatting`.\n\nUSAGE\n  gh run view [<run-id>] [flags]\n\nFLAGS\n  -a, --attempt uint      The attempt number of the workflow run\n      --exit-status       Exit with non-zero status if run failed\n  -j, --job string        View a specific job ID from a run\n  -q, --jq expression     Filter JSON output using a jq expression\n      --json fields       Output JSON with the specified fields\n      --log               View full log for either a run or specific job\n      --log-failed        View the log for any failed steps in a run or specific job\n  -t, --template string   Format JSON output using a Go template; see \"gh help formatting\"\n  -v, --verbose           Show job steps\n  -w, --web               Open run in the browser\n\nINHERITED FLAGS\n      --help                     Show help for command\n  -R, --repo [HOST/]OWNER/REPO   Select another repository using the [HOST/]OWNER/REPO format\n\nJSON FIELDS\n  attempt, conclusion, createdAt, databaseId, displayTitle, event, headBranch,\n  headSha, jobs, name, number, startedAt, status, updatedAt, url,\n  workflowDatabaseId, workflowName\n\nEXAMPLES\n  # Interactively select a run to view, optionally selecting a single job\n  $ gh run view\n  \n  # View a specific run\n  $ gh run view 12345\n  \n  # View a specific run with specific attempt number\n  $ gh run view 12345 --attempt 3\n  \n  # View a specific job within a run\n  $ gh run view --job 456789\n  \n  # View the full log for a specific job\n  $ gh run view --log --job 456789\n  \n  # Exit non-zero if a run failed\n  $ gh run view 0451 --exit-status && echo \"run pending or passed\"\n\nLEARN MORE\n  Use `gh <command> <subcommand> --help` for more information about a command.\n  Read the manual at https://cli.github.com/manual\n  Learn about exit codes using `gh help exit-codes`\n  Learn about accessibility experiences using `gh help accessibility`\n\n{\"conclusion\":\"cancelled\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-30T05:36:00Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/41009328850\",\"run_attempt\":2,\"status\":\"completed\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-10-30T06:44:19Z\"}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":404825863}},"started_at_ms":1793345088380,"completed_at_ms":1793345088785}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T07:24:48.991Z","ordinal":522207,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18bb2-6dde-7eb1-87df-2c7a7d7b8ddf","call_id":"call_6109c705ee2645f7b81172c486f513f4","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"b4828f\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.404907054,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":686,\"output\":\"View a summary of a workflow run.\\n\\nDue to platform limitations, `gh` may not always be able to associate jobs with their\\ncorresponding logs when using the primary method of fetching logs in zip format.\\n\\nIn such cases, `gh` will attempt to fetch logs for each job individually via the API.\\nThis fallback is slower and more resource-intensive. If more than 25 job logs are missing,\\nthe operation will fail with an error.\\n\\nAdditionally, due to similar platform constraints, some log lines may not be\\nassociated with a specific step within a job. In these cases, the step name will\\nappear as `UNKNOWN STEP` in the log output.\\n\\nFor more information about output formatting flags, see `gh help formatting`.\\n\\nUSAGE\\n  gh run view [<run-id>] [flags]\\n\\nFLAGS\\n  -a, --attempt uint      The attempt number of the workflow run\\n      --exit-status       Exit with non-zero status if run failed\\n  -j, --job string        View a specific job ID from a run\\n  -q, --jq expression     Filter JSON output using a jq expression\\n      --json fields       Output JSON with the specified fields\\n      --log               View full log for either a run or specific job\\n      --log-failed        View the log for any failed steps in a run or specific job\\n  -t, --template string   Format JSON output using a Go template; see \\\"gh help formatting\\\"\\n  -v, --verbose           Show job steps\\n  -w, --web               Open run in the browser\\n\\nINHERITED FLAGS\\n      --help                     Show help for command\\n  -R, --repo [HOST/]OWNER/REPO   Select another repository using the [HOST/]OWNER/REPO format\\n\\nJSON FIELDS\\n  attempt, conclusion, createdAt, databaseId, displayTitle, event, headBranch,\\n  headSha, jobs, name, number, startedAt, status, updatedAt, url,\\n  workflowDatabaseId, workflowName\\n\\nEXAMPLES\\n  # Interactively select a run to view, optionally selecting a single job\\n  $ gh run view\\n  \\n  # View a specific run\\n  $ gh run view 12345\\n  \\n  # View a specific run with specific attempt number\\n  $ gh run view 12345 --attempt 3\\n  \\n  # View a specific job within a run\\n  $ gh run view --job 456789\\n  \\n  # View the full log for a specific job\\n  $ gh run view --log --job 456789\\n  \\n  # Exit non-zero if a run failed\\n  $ gh run view 0451 --exit-status && echo \\\"run pending or passed\\\"\\n\\nLEARN MORE\\n  Use `gh <command> <subcommand> --help` for more information about a command.\\n  Read the manual at https://cli.github.com/manual\\n  Learn about exit codes using `gh help exit-codes`\\n  Learn about accessibility experiences using `gh help accessibility`\\n\\n{\\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"cancelled\\\",\\\"created_at\\\":\\\"2026-10-30T05:36:00Z\\\",\\\"html_url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/41009328850\\\",\\\"run_attempt\\\":2,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\",\\\"updated_at\\\":\\\"2026-10-30T06:44:19Z\\\"}\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18b8d-60e7-7130-962f-f0eb9e68c409","create_time":1793345088.9909482}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
