{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T08:03:53.513Z","ordinal":523195,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18b8d-60e7-7130-962f-f0eb9e68c409","session_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","root_turn_id":"01a18b8d-60e7-7130-962f-f0eb9e68c409","response_id":"resp_0db389702a7164cc016ae44f67b220819fb33229ee296af67e","usage":{"input_tokens":217945,"cached_input_tokens":217344,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":168,"reasoning_output_tokens":98,"total_tokens":218113},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":54350800,"cached_input_tokens":54023680,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":79093,"reasoning_output_tokens":40595,"total_tokens":54429893},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":9862594166,"cached_input_tokens":9758374784,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":28284109,"reasoning_output_tokens":16630996,"total_tokens":9890878275}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T08:03:53.888Z","ordinal":523196,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18b8d-60e7-7130-962f-f0eb9e68c409","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-2d7b8785-e21e-4405-ae14-46c47ddb2492","process_id":"12158","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","export ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE=file; entire trail show --help; entire trail approvals --help; entire trail finding --help"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"export ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE=file; entire trail show --help; entire trail approvals --help; entire trail finding --help"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"Show a project trail by its project-local number or ULID, or the trail of <repo>/<number> branch work. Without a selector, follow the current branch's parent. Use --branch to follow another branch's parent.\n\nUsage:\n  entire trail show [<trail>] [flags]\n\nFlags:\n      --branch string   Discover the project trail through this repository branch (defaults to current branch when no trail is given)\n  -h, --help            help for show\n      --json            Output raw JSON instead of a table\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name     Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n      --project string   Project as gh/<owner> or et/<project>; required for list, otherwise defaults to the repository's namespace\n      --repo string      Target repository as forge/owner/repo (e.g. gh/acme/app) or a clone URL; for list, only filters the required --project\nList approval decisions on a trail\n\nUsage:\n  entire trail approvals [<trail>] [flags]\n\nFlags:\n      --branch string   Select a repository branch within the trail\n  -h, --help            help for approvals\n      --json            Output as JSON\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name     Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n      --project string   Project as gh/<owner> or et/<project>; required for list, otherwise defaults to the repository's namespace\n      --repo string      Target repository as forge/owner/repo (e.g. gh/acme/app) or a clone URL; for list, only filters the required --project\nManage a trail's agent-native findings.\n\nRunning 'entire trail finding' shows the finding dashboard for the current\nbranch's trail. Pass a project trail number, ID, or <repo>/<number> to inspect another trail.\n--repo and --branch select the working context; findings apply only to that\nbranch, not the whole trail. Use 'entire trail list' to discover trails.\n\nUsage:\n  entire trail finding [<trail>] [flags]\n  entire trail finding [command]\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  add         Create a finding on a trail\n  apply       Apply a finding's unified-diff suggestion\n  dismiss     Dismiss a finding\n  list        List findings for a trail\n  reopen      Reopen a finding\n  resolve     Resolve a finding\n  show        Show a finding\n  update      Update a finding's metadata\n\nFlags:\n      --branch string       Select a repository branch within the trail\n      --cursor string       Continue from the next cursor returned by a previous page\n      --freshness string    Filter code-version freshness: current,stale,any (default \"current\")\n  -h, --help                help for finding\n      --include-dismissed   Include dismissed findings\n      --json                Output as JSON\n  -n, --limit int           Maximum number of findings to show (default 100)\n      --severity string     Filter by comma-separated severity value(s): high,medium,low\n      --status string       Filter by lifecycle status(es): open,resolved,dismissed; use 'any' for all (default \"open\")\n      --trail string        Project trail number, ID, or <repo>/<number> (defaults to the current branch's parent)\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name     Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n      --project string   Project as gh/<owner> or et/<project>; required for list, otherwise defaults to the repository's namespace\n      --repo string      Target repository as forge/owner/repo (e.g. gh/acme/app) or a clone URL; for list, only filters the required --project\n\nUse \"entire trail finding [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":135803424}},"started_at_ms":1793347433752,"completed_at_ms":1793347433888}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T08:03:54.081Z","ordinal":523197,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18bd6-3661-77a0-9944-5abe6849cb84","call_id":"call_67ec4f351a454b6da99e5d96ebc5d93a","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.7 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"106eb4\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.135874651,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":964,\"output\":\"Show a project trail by its project-local number or ULID, or the trail of <repo>/<number> branch work. Without a selector, follow the current branch's parent. Use --branch to follow another branch's parent.\\n\\nUsage:\\n  entire trail show [<trail>] [flags]\\n\\nFlags:\\n      --branch string   Discover the project trail through this repository branch (defaults to current branch when no trail is given)\\n  -h, --help            help for show\\n      --json            Output raw JSON instead of a table\\n\\nGlobal Flags:\\n      --context name     Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\\n      --project string   Project as gh/<owner> or et/<project>; required for list, otherwise defaults to the repository's namespace\\n      --repo string      Target repository as forge/owner/repo (e.g. gh/acme/app) or a clone URL; for list, only filters the required --project\\nList approval decisions on a trail\\n\\nUsage:\\n  entire trail approvals [<trail>] [flags]\\n\\nFlags:\\n      --branch string   Select a repository branch within the trail\\n  -h, --help            help for approvals\\n      --json            Output as JSON\\n\\nGlobal Flags:\\n      --context name     Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\\n      --project string   Project as gh/<owner> or et/<project>; required for list, otherwise defaults to the repository's namespace\\n      --repo string      Target repository as forge/owner/repo (e.g. gh/acme/app) or a clone URL; for list, only filters the required --project\\nManage a trail's agent-native findings.\\n\\nRunning 'entire trail finding' shows the finding dashboard for the current\\nbranch's trail. Pass a project trail number, ID, or <repo>/<number> to inspect another trail.\\n--repo and --branch select the working context; findings apply only to that\\nbranch, not the whole trail. Use 'entire trail list' to discover trails.\\n\\nUsage:\\n  entire trail finding [<trail>] [flags]\\n  entire trail finding [command]\\n\\nAvailable Commands:\\n  add         Create a finding on a trail\\n  apply       Apply a finding's unified-diff suggestion\\n  dismiss     Dismiss a finding\\n  list        List findings for a trail\\n  reopen      Reopen a finding\\n  resolve     Resolve a finding\\n  show        Show a finding\\n  update      Update a finding's metadata\\n\\nFlags:\\n      --branch string       Select a repository branch within the trail\\n      --cursor string       Continue from the next cursor returned by a previous page\\n      --freshness string    Filter code-version freshness: current,stale,any (default \\\"current\\\")\\n  -h, --help                help for finding\\n      --include-dismissed   Include dismissed findings\\n      --json                Output as JSON\\n  -n, --limit int           Maximum number of findings to show (default 100)\\n      --severity string     Filter by comma-separated severity value(s): high,medium,low\\n      --status string       Filter by lifecycle status(es): open,resolved,dismissed; use 'any' for all (default \\\"open\\\")\\n      --trail string        Project trail number, ID, or <repo>/<number> (defaults to the current branch's parent)\\n\\nGlobal Flags:\\n      --context name     Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\\n      --project string   Project as gh/<owner> or et/<project>; required for list, otherwise defaults to the repository's namespace\\n      --repo string      Target repository as forge/owner/repo (e.g. gh/acme/app) or a clone URL; for list, only filters the required --project\\n\\nUse \\\"entire trail finding [command] --help\\\" for more information about a command.\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18b8d-60e7-7130-962f-f0eb9e68c409","create_time":1793347434.081381}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
