{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T08:07:34.747Z","ordinal":523359,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18b8d-60e7-7130-962f-f0eb9e68c409","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae450430048819fa5e0f1570c7f37a2","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"**Disposition: `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_BLOCKED`**  \n**Acceptance: `IN_PROGRESS`**\n\n- **Integration:** `origin/main` is `d68695f3cb299c51959169d2373f7b924496486e`. Post-merge CI run `41019427932` and CodeQL run `41019427930` passed.\n- **RC14 candidate:** PR #342 at `26c1f541beb3d868e0c3e1604abf674e7aa05949` passed CI `41019505916`—Node 22, Node 24, and Linux package/repro checks—and CodeQL `41019505875`. Exact-head requirements enforcement and RC14 version sync also passed. This is PR validation; **no RC14 tag or release artifact exists**.\n- **Review gate:** Independent review found one non-blocking gap: the timeout parity test accepts any numeric timeout instead of requiring 45 minutes. Entire trail 58 still has no approvals. The reviewer confirmed only the author’s Mike account is active there, so merging requires a distinct external reviewer’s approval. I did not bypass that gate.\n- **Nexus identity:** The runtime prompt identifies Nexus Code and rejects identity changes based on provider, model, or skill ([agent.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/post-pr335-source-gates-20261030T0720Z/cli/src/agent.ts:231)). A regression test checks that identity instruction alongside a Claude-specific skill ([agent_runtime_identity.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/post-pr335-source-gates-20261030T0720Z/cli/test/agent_runtime_identity.test.ts:38)); exact-main CI passed. This is source and test evidence, not a live RC behavior result.\n- **Qualification:** No exact-RC qualification has started. The last public held-out status I checked reported 20/40 T2 tasks and no fresh custody acceptance. No protected corpus material was accessed.\n- **Coordination:** Released the completed PR #335 file claims and the SUITE claim after both CI runs completed; recorded the new results and blockers in the claims log. The dirty shared checkout remains untouched.\n\nThe next integration step needs the independent Entire reviewer approval; exact-RC qualification also depends on custodian acceptance of the held-out corpus. No further release authorization is needed.\n\n"}],"phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":{"entries":[{"path":"MEMORY.md","lineStart":580,"lineEnd":606,"note":"source CI and independent review do not establish exact RC acceptance"}],"rolloutIds":["01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0"]}},"started_at_ms":1793347652630,"completed_at_ms":1793347654746}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T08:07:34.753Z","ordinal":523360,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","status":"completed","id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae450430048819fa5e0f1570c7f37a2","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"**Disposition: `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_BLOCKED`**  \n**Acceptance: `IN_PROGRESS`**\n\n- **Integration:** `origin/main` is `d68695f3cb299c51959169d2373f7b924496486e`. Post-merge CI run `41019427932` and CodeQL run `41019427930` passed.\n- **RC14 candidate:** PR #342 at `26c1f541beb3d868e0c3e1604abf674e7aa05949` passed CI `41019505916`—Node 22, Node 24, and Linux package/repro checks—and CodeQL `41019505875`. Exact-head requirements enforcement and RC14 version sync also passed. This is PR validation; **no RC14 tag or release artifact exists**.\n- **Review gate:** Independent review found one non-blocking gap: the timeout parity test accepts any numeric timeout instead of requiring 45 minutes. Entire trail 58 still has no approvals. The reviewer confirmed only the author’s Mike account is active there, so merging requires a distinct external reviewer’s approval. I did not bypass that gate.\n- **Nexus identity:** The runtime prompt identifies Nexus Code and rejects identity changes based on provider, model, or skill ([agent.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/post-pr335-source-gates-20261030T0720Z/cli/src/agent.ts:231)). A regression test checks that identity instruction alongside a Claude-specific skill ([agent_runtime_identity.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/post-pr335-source-gates-20261030T0720Z/cli/test/agent_runtime_identity.test.ts:38)); exact-main CI passed. This is source and test evidence, not a live RC behavior result.\n- **Qualification:** No exact-RC qualification has started. The last public held-out status I checked reported 20/40 T2 tasks and no fresh custody acceptance. No protected corpus material was accessed.\n- **Coordination:** Released the completed PR #335 file claims and the SUITE claim after both CI runs completed; recorded the new results and blockers in the claims log. The dirty shared checkout remains untouched.\n\nThe next integration step needs the independent Entire reviewer approval; exact-RC qualification also depends on custodian acceptance of the held-out corpus. No further release authorization is needed.\n\n<oai-mem-citation>\n<citation_entries>\nMEMORY.md:580-606|note=[source CI and independent review do not establish exact RC acceptance]\n</citation_entries>\n<rollout_ids>\n01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0\n</rollout_ids>\n</oai-mem-citation>","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"final_answer","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18b8d-60e7-7130-962f-f0eb9e68c409","create_time":1793347651.0033214,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae450430048819fa5e0f1570c7f37a2","turn_id":"01a18b8d-60e7-7130-962f-f0eb9e68c409","role":"assistant"},"revision":"retained_01a18bd9-9461-7362-b023-657b334b7311","complete":true},"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":24107}}
