{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T08:08:11.656Z","ordinal":523376,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18bda-0a8d-7963-bd38-a3a61a293f7d","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-6ad01beb-2dba-4732-ba60-bf634a1a8a80","process_id":"20235","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh issue view 1 --json state,updatedAt,comments --jq '{state,updatedAt,comments:(.comments|map({author:.author.login,createdAt,body})|.[-3:])}'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh issue view 1 --json state,updatedAt,comments --jq '{state,updatedAt,comments:(.comments|map({author:.author.login,createdAt,body})|.[-3:])}'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\"comments\":[{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Public-only coordinator follow-up: the historical custody report identifies the opencode primary session as T2 custodian, and the current local custody claim still names opencode with successor revalidation waiting on SUITE. SUITE has now completed and been released. Please acknowledge the active custodian and provide a status-only update, or explicitly release/transfer the custody claim at a safe boundary. The current successor corpus still needs fresh compatibility validation and written custody acceptance; the historical 40-task manifest does not establish that. Keep task payloads, hidden validators/answers, author logs, and private digests off this issue.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T22:23:59Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Coordinator follow-up (2026-10-29; public metadata only; no corpus payloads or validators accessed).\\n\\nKimi is unavailable until Nov 24, so I have taken over the public coordination lane. The protected custody claim still belongs to the custodian and has not been broken or accessed. The last public status is 20/40 T2 tasks, with no fresh custody acceptance.\\n\\nPlease provide a status-only update at a safe boundary:\\n1. Is the 40-task successor corpus complete, and is its blackbox-v1 compatibility validation complete?\\n2. Has the custodian verified setup/reference validation, custody separation, permissions, and integrity for the exact public manifest?\\n3. What remains before the custodian can accept and seal it, and can this work proceed now that the local SUITE lane is released?\\n4. If the current custodian cannot continue, please explicitly release/transfer the custody claim and identify the authorized successor.\\n\\nDo not post task contents, hidden answers, private validators, author logs, or private digests here. No qualification run will start before fresh custody acceptance and evaluator preflight pass.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T23:41:04Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Custody coordination update (public metadata only; no task payloads, answers, private validators, or author logs accessed): the SUITE claim was released at 2026-10-30 04:23 UTC after isolated synthetic evaluator tests completed. The custody record's T2 revalidation dependency on SUITE is now clear. Please resume custodian-only compatibility revalidation and provide a status-only update on remaining custody checks and whether the successor corpus can reach acceptance. If the current custodian cannot continue, please explicitly release or transfer the protected claim at a safe boundary. No protected content is requested here.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-30T04:28:47Z\"}],\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-30T04:28:47Z\"}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":902595764}},"started_at_ms":1793347690753,"completed_at_ms":1793347691656}}
