{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T08:09:38.168Z","ordinal":523441,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a18bdb-7678-7971-a2a1-e479015d021b","call_id":"call_f02dc8b7ece3497b8e637f9b9b708b67","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/pr311_draft_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"PR #342 is on trail 58, current change 57, branch `claude/rc14-candidate`. The trail is open, has no approvals, no findings, and no discussions. Its author and assignee are `mikeholownych`; the only active Entire context is Mike Holownych’s account.\\n\\nThe CLI supports adding a trail finding, so the prior parity-test concern could be recorded as an agent finding. That would be attributed to the same owner account and would **not** satisfy independent approval. I did not submit it or approve the trail. A distinct external reviewer must provide the required approval.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/review_pr300_readiness\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** — reviewed the uncommitted delta over `ba72d2cbfb8f446254cf829ac5990148fed82500`. The new report binds the task to RC11’s source revision, archive digest, installed version, OpenRouter model, declared deliverable, and explicit verifier (`openrouter-live-task-20261030.md:5–11`). It preserves the incomplete and unverified attempts, records the final verified disposition and reported independent 2/2 rerun, and limits the claim to one synthetic task rather than E5 or RC acceptance (`:15–19, :29–39`; `README.md:32–40`).\\n\\n`sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS` passed for all 23 entries; `git diff --check` passed. The new report contains no credentials or raw prompt transcript. Its hashes for source, test, flight log, and receipts are documented, but those raw files are not included, so those hashes and run details remain operator-reported rather than independently reproducible (`:29–35`).\\n\\nDiff SHA-256: `db79879f51989668a8b6367b78329df9584114e34abe53d0fa564eeeffd8d09f`. I did not edit files or run qualification.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/review_pr302\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT.** The lockfile-only change resolves the cited RUSTSEC-2026-0418: it upgrades `libz-sys` to the stated fixed version, 1.1.31. The locked `cc` is 1.5.1, below the advisory’s affected `cc >= 1.6.0` condition. The new checksum matches the local crates.io index entry, and the diff changes no other dependencies.\\n\\nI could not retrieve RUSTSEC-2026-0418 through the available advisory lookup, so that applicability assessment relies on the exact advisory details you supplied from main CI. No tests or suites were run.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18bda-0a8d-7963-bd38-a3a61a293f7d","create_time":1793347778.1681607}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
