{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T08:13:10.893Z","ordinal":523592,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18bda-0a8d-7963-bd38-a3a61a293f7d","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-9eccd53a-bfe5-4d40-84fd-5bb5650a2ade","process_id":"61700","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,120p' cli/test/release_workflow_parity.test.ts; sed -n '1,35p' docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.13.md; sed -n '1,35p' docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.14.md; cat cli/package.json | sed -n '1,100p'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/rc14-release-parity-docs","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,120p' cli/test/release_workflow_parity.test.ts","name":"release_workflow_parity.test.ts","path":"cli/test/release_workflow_parity.test.ts"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,35p' docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.13.md","name":"v1.0.0-rc.13.md","path":"docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.13.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,35p' docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.14.md","name":"v1.0.0-rc.14.md","path":"docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.14.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"cat cli/package.json","name":"package.json","path":"cli/package.json"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"import { test } from \"node:test\";\nimport assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport path from \"node:path\";\nimport { fileURLToPath } from \"node:url\";\n\n// The release job runs the same CLI suite as CI, including evaluator tests that need the\n// pinned toolchains and sandbox. rc.12's release failed with \"go: command not found\"\n// because release.yml lacked steps that ci.yml had; keep the two environments aligned.\nconst root = path.resolve(path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), \"../..\");\nconst read = (name: string) => fs.readFileSync(path.join(root, \".github/workflows\", name), \"utf8\");\n\nconst REQUIRED_EVALUATOR_SETUP = [\n  \"go-version: '1.22.12'\",\n  \"run: bash scripts/install-evaluator-toolchains.sh\",\n  \"run: bash scripts/ensure-ci-bubblewrap.sh\",\n  \"run: bash scripts/ensure-ci-user-cgroups.sh\",\n  'echo \"NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT=$root\" >> \"$GITHUB_ENV\"',\n  'echo \"NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_RUNTIME_ROOT=$runtime_root\" >> \"$GITHUB_ENV\"',\n  \"sudo install -o root -g root -m 0755 \\\"$node_runtime\\\" /usr/bin/node\",\n];\nconst RETIRED_RUNNER_TRIM_STEP = \"bash scripts/ci-trim-runner-image.sh\";\n\nfunction jobSection(workflow: string, name: string): string {\n  const marker = `\\n  ${name}:`;\n  const start = workflow.indexOf(marker);\n  assert.notEqual(start, -1, `workflow defines the ${name} job`);\n  const bodyStart = start + marker.length;\n  const remaining = workflow.slice(bodyStart);\n  const nextJob = remaining.search(/\\n  [a-zA-Z0-9_-]+:/);\n  return nextJob === -1 ? remaining : remaining.slice(0, nextJob);\n}\n\ntest(\"release job prepares the same evaluator environment as CI before running the CLI suite\", () => {\n  const ci = read(\"ci.yml\");\n  const release = read(\"release.yml\");\n  const jobs = [\n    [\"CI Node matrix\", jobSection(ci, \"test-matrix\")],\n    [\"CI Linux packaging\", jobSection(ci, \"linux-x86_64\")],\n    [\"release package\", jobSection(release, \"package\")],\n  ] as const;\n\n  for (const [jobName, job] of jobs) {\n    assert.ok(\n      !job.includes(RETIRED_RUNNER_TRIM_STEP),\n      `${jobName} does not invoke the retired runner trim script`,\n    );\n    const suite = job.indexOf(\"run: npm --prefix cli test\");\n    assert.ok(suite >= 0, `${jobName} runs the CLI suite`);\n    assert.match(job, /timeout-minutes: \\d+\\n\\s+run: npm --prefix cli test/, `${jobName} bounds the CLI suite so a hung test process fails the job`);\n    const positions = REQUIRED_EVALUATOR_SETUP.map((step) => {\n      const position = job.indexOf(step);\n      assert.ok(position >= 0, `${jobName} includes required evaluator setup: ${step}`);\n      assert.ok(position < suite, `${jobName} runs evaluator setup before the CLI suite: ${step}`);\n      return position;\n    });\n    for (let index = 1; index < positions.length; index += 1) {\n      assert.ok(positions[index - 1] < positions[index], `${jobName} preserves evaluator setup order`);\n    }\n  }\n});\n# Nexus Code v1.0.0-rc.13 release candidate\n\n**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\n\n**Not published:** the `v1.0.0-rc.13` release workflow failed in its test step (two evaluator tests refused with `compiler exposure could not be checked; refusing qualification`, then the evaluator test process did not exit), so no RC13 package exists. [RC14](v1.0.0-rc.14.md) replaces it.\n\n**Status:** this candidate is for exact-artifact qualification. It does not establish independent acceptance or authorize stable v1.0.0 promotion. Qualification results must identify the workflow-produced package and its digest.\n\nThis release packages the Nexus Code Linux x86-64 client: the TypeScript CLI and sidecar, production Node dependencies, Rust `harness-core`, and Ratatui `nexus-tui`. It replaces RC12, which was tagged but never published: its release workflow failed in the test step, so no RC12 package exists. RC13 ships the same product changes as RC12; everything in the [RC12 notes](v1.0.0-rc.12.md) and the [RC11 notes](v1.0.0-rc.11.md) is included.\n\n## Changes since RC12\n\n### Release workflow (not in the package)\n\n- The release job now prepares the same evaluator environment as CI before it runs the test suite: the pinned Go toolchain, the pinned evaluator toolchains, and removal of the hosted runner's preinstalled SDK trees. RC12's release run failed without them (`go: command not found`, and `compiler exposure could not be checked; refusing qualification`). A test now fails if the release and CI workflows disagree on this setup.\n\nNo product code changed between RC12's tag and RC13.\n\n## Runtime requirements\n\n- Linux x86-64 with glibc 2.35 or newer.\n- Node.js 22 or newer.\n- An OpenAI-compatible inference endpoint, local or explicitly selected provider.\n\nThe archive does not include Node.js. Rust and Cargo are not required at runtime. No other OS or architecture is claimed.\n\n## Candidate assets\n\nThe release workflow for `v1.0.0-rc.13` is expected to produce the version-matched Linux archive, `SHA256SUMS`, SBOM, notices, installer, and provenance. The workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and qualification evidence must be recorded before this candidate can be accepted. Local builds are not interchangeable with the workflow-produced artifacts.\n\n## Qualification status\n\nThis is a candidate, not an accepted release. The installed-RC gates — platform and lifecycle evidence including the power-loss cell, mandatory automated CI PTY (§5.1) and scripted installed-RC PTY (§5.2), provider and standalone qualification, held-out task quality, cross-runner reproducibility, independent exact-RC acceptance and the requirements ledger — remain outstanding for this artifact. RC11 evidence does not carry over to RC13 without an explicit, reviewed carry-forward. The manual matrix (§5.3) is waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20; this does not waive steering, accessibility, or any other release gate. Passing source CI does not satisfy installed-RC qualification.\n# Nexus Code v1.0.0-rc.14 release candidate\n\n**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\n\n**Status:** this candidate is for exact-artifact qualification. It does not establish independent acceptance or authorize stable v1.0.0 promotion. Qualification results must identify the workflow-produced package and its digest.\n\nThis release packages the Nexus Code Linux x86-64 client: the TypeScript CLI and sidecar, production Node dependencies, Rust `harness-core`, and Ratatui `nexus-tui`. It replaces RC12 and RC13, which were tagged but never published: both release workflows failed in the test step, so neither package exists. RC14 ships the same product changes as RC12; everything in the [RC13](v1.0.0-rc.13.md), [RC12](v1.0.0-rc.12.md) and [RC11](v1.0.0-rc.11.md) notes is included.\n\n## Changes since RC13\n\n### Qualification tooling and release workflow (not in the package)\n\n- The evaluator's compiler-exposure check no longer depends on deleting the hosted runner's preinstalled SDK trees. It masks host-only SDK directories inside the candidate sandbox under every mounted spelling, ignores an inventoried path only when it has been removed before inspection, and names the cause when its inventory helper fails (timeout, kill, nonzero exit or unexpected output). Every other inspection error still refuses qualification. RC13's release run failed when this check refused in two evaluator tests.\n- The CLI test step in the release and CI workflows now has a 45-minute limit. RC13's release run and a main CI run stalled after the evaluator test file finished, because its test process did not exit; a hung step now fails the job instead of running for six hours. The limit bounds the damage; the cause of the non-exiting test process has not been identified.\n\nNo product code changed between RC12's tag and RC14.\n\n## Runtime requirements\n\n- Linux x86-64 with glibc 2.35 or newer.\n- Node.js 22 or newer.\n- An OpenAI-compatible inference endpoint, local or explicitly selected provider.\n\nThe archive does not include Node.js. Rust and Cargo are not required at runtime. No other OS or architecture is claimed.\n\n## Candidate assets\n\nThe release workflow for `v1.0.0-rc.14` is expected to produce the version-matched Linux archive, `SHA256SUMS`, SBOM, notices, installer, and provenance. The workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and qualification evidence must be recorded before this candidate can be accepted. Local builds are not interchangeable with the workflow-produced artifacts.\n\n## Qualification status\n\nThis is a candidate, not an accepted release. The installed-RC gates — platform and lifecycle evidence including the power-loss cell, mandatory automated CI PTY (§5.1) and scripted installed-RC PTY (§5.2), provider and standalone qualification, held-out task quality, cross-runner reproducibility, independent exact-RC acceptance and the requirements ledger — remain outstanding for this artifact. RC11 evidence does not carry over to RC14 without an explicit, reviewed carry-forward. The manual matrix (§5.3) is waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20; this does not waive steering, accessibility, or any other release gate. Passing source CI does not satisfy installed-RC qualification.\n{\n  \"name\": \"local-code-harness\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0-rc.14\",\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"description\": \"Autonomous local AI coding harness (Codex / Claude-Code style) for LM Studio and vLLM\",\n  \"main\": \"dist/index.js\",\n  \"bin\": {\n    \"harness\": \"./dist/index.js\"\n  },\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"build\": \"tsc && node scripts/write_build_info.mjs\",\n    \"test\": \"node scripts/run_tests.mjs && bash ../scripts/terminal-acceptance/test-scope-procs.sh\",\n    \"start\": \"node dist/index.js\",\n    \"dev\": \"tsx watch src/index.ts\"\n  },\n  \"keywords\": [\n    \"ai\",\n    \"coding-agent\",\n    \"codex\",\n    \"claude-code\",\n    \"vllm\",\n    \"lm-studio\",\n    \"rust\"\n  ],\n  \"author\": \"\",\n  \"license\": \"MIT\",\n  \"engines\": {\n    \"node\": \">=22\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"commander\": \"^12.1.0\",\n    \"dotenv\": \"^16.4.5\",\n    \"ora\": \"^8.1.0\",\n    \"picocolors\": \"^1.1.1\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@types/node\": \"^22.5.0\",\n    \"tsx\": \"^4.19.0\",\n    \"typescript\": \"^5.5.4\"\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":38399224}},"started_at_ms":1793347989853,"completed_at_ms":1793347990892}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T08:13:11.113Z","ordinal":523593,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18bde-b649-7301-b3c9-cf3a310ad617","call_id":"call_296803b3ae9d4d65aed621929fbe570f","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.6 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"import { test } from \"node:test\";\nimport assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport path from \"node:path\";\nimport { fileURLToPath } from \"node:url\";\n\n// The release job runs the same CLI suite as CI, including evaluator tests that need the\n// pinned toolchains and sandbox. rc.12's release failed with \"go: command not found\"\n// because release.yml lacked steps that ci.yml had; keep the two environments aligned.\nconst root = path.resolve(path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), \"../..\");\nconst read = (name: string) => fs.readFileSync(path.join(root, \".github/workflows\", name), \"utf8\");\n\nconst REQUIRED_EVALUATOR_SETUP = [\n  \"go-version: '1.22.12'\",\n  \"run: bash scripts/install-evaluator-toolchains.sh\",\n  \"run: bash scripts/ensure-ci-bubblewrap.sh\",\n  \"run: bash scripts/ensure-ci-user-cgroups.sh\",\n  'echo \"NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT=$root\" >> \"$GITHUB_ENV\"',\n  'echo \"NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_RUNTIME_ROOT=$runtime_root\" >> \"$GITHUB_ENV\"',\n  \"sudo install -o root -g root -m 0755 \\\"$node_runtime\\\" /usr/bin/node\",\n];\nconst RETIRED_RUNNER_TRIM_STEP = \"bash scripts/ci-trim-runner-image.sh\";\n\nfunction jobSection(workflow: string, name: string): string {\n  const marker = `\\n  ${name}:`;\n  const start = workflow.indexOf(marker);\n  assert.notEqual(start, -1, `workflow defines the ${name} job`);\n  const bodyStart = start + marker.length;\n  const remaining = workflow.slice(bodyStart);\n  const nextJob = remaining.search(/\\n  [a-zA-Z0-9_-]+:/);\n  return nextJob === -1 ? remaining : remaining.slice(0, nextJob);\n}\n\ntest(\"release job prepares the same evaluator environment as CI before running the CLI suite\", () => {\n  const ci = read(\"ci.yml\");\n  const release = read(\"release.yml\");\n  const jobs = [\n    [\"CI Node matrix\", jobSection(ci, \"test-matrix\")],\n    [\"CI Linux packaging\", jobSection(ci, \"linux-x86_64\")],\n    [\"release package\", jobSection(release, \"package\")],\n  ] as const;\n\n  for (const [jobName, job] of jobs) {\n    assert.ok(\n      !job.includes(RETIRED_RUNNER_TRIM_STEP),\n      `${jobName} does not invoke the retired runner trim script`,\n    );\n    const suite = job.indexOf(\"run: npm --prefix cli test\");\n    assert.ok(suite >= 0, `${jobName} runs the CLI suite`);\n    assert.match(job, /timeout-minutes: \\d+\\n\\s+run: npm --prefix cli test/, `${jobName} bounds the CLI suite so a hung test process fails the job`);\n    const positions = REQUIRED_EVALUATOR_SETUP.map((step) => {\n      const position = job.indexOf(step);\n      assert.ok(position >= 0, `${jobName} includes required evaluator setup: ${step}`);\n      assert.ok(position < suite, `${jobName} runs evaluator setup before the CLI suite: ${step}`);\n      return position;\n    });\n    for (let index = 1; index < positions.length; index += 1) {\n      assert.ok(positions[index - 1] < positions[index], `${jobName} preserves evaluator setup order`);\n    }\n  }\n});\n# Nexus Code v1.0.0-rc.13 release candidate\n\n**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\n\n**Not published:** the `v1.0.0-rc.13` release workflow failed in its test step (two evaluator tests refused with `compiler exposure could not be checked; refusing qualification`, then the evaluator test process did not exit), so no RC13 package exists. [RC14](v1.0.0-rc.14.md) replaces it.\n\n**Status:** this candidate is for exact-artifact qualification. It does not establish independent acceptance or authorize stable v1.0.0 promotion. Qualification results must identify the workflow-produced package and its digest.\n\nThis release packages the Nexus Code Linux x86-64 client: the TypeScript CLI and sidecar, production Node dependencies, Rust `harness-core`, and Ratatui `nexus-tui`. It replaces RC12, which was tagged but never published: its release workflow failed in the test step, so no RC12 package exists. RC13 ships the same product changes as RC12; everything in the [RC12 notes](v1.0.0-rc.12.md) and the [RC11 notes](v1.0.0-rc.11.md) is included.\n\n## Changes since RC12\n\n### Release workflow (not in the package)\n\n- The release job now prepares the same evaluator environment as CI before it runs the test suite: the pinned Go toolchain, the pinned evaluator toolchains, and removal of the hosted runner's preinstalled SDK trees. RC12's release run failed without them (`go: command not found`, and `compiler exposure could not be checked; refusing qualification`). A test now fails if the release and CI workflows disagree on this setup.\n\nNo product code changed between RC12's tag and RC13.\n\n## Runtime requirements\n\n- Linux x86-64 with glibc 2.35 or newer.\n- Node.js 22 or newer.\n- An OpenAI-compatible inference endpoint, local or explicitly selected provider.\n\nThe archive does not include Node.js. Rust and Cargo are not required at runtime. No other OS or architecture is claimed.\n\n## Candidate assets\n\nThe release workflow for `v1.0.0-rc.13` is expected to produce the version-matched Linux archive, `SHA256SUMS`, SBOM, notices, installer, and provenance. The workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and qualification evidence must be recorded before this candidate can be accepted. Local builds are not interchangeable with the workflow-produced artifacts.\n\n## Qualification status\n\nThis is a candidate, not an accepted release. The installed-RC gates — platform and lifecycle evidence including the power-loss cell, mandatory automated CI PTY (§5.1) and scripted installed-RC PTY (§5.2), provider and standalone qualification, held-out task quality, cross-runner reproducibility, independent exact-RC acceptance and the requirements ledger — remain outstanding for this artifact. RC11 evidence does not carry over to RC13 without an explicit, reviewed carry-forward. The manual matrix (§5.3) is waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20; this does not waive steering, accessibility, or any other release gate. Passing source CI does not satisfy installed-RC qualification.\n# Nexus Code v1.0.0-rc.14 release candidate\n\n**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\n\n**Status:** this candidate is for exact-artifact qualification. It does not establish independent acceptance or authorize stable v1.0.0 promotion. Qualification results must identify the workflow-produced package and its digest.\n\nThis release packages the Nexus Code Linux x86-64 client: the TypeScript CLI and sidecar, production Node dependencies, Rust `harness-core`, and Ratatui `nexus-tui`. It replaces RC12 and RC13, which were tagged but never published: both release workflows failed in the test step, so neither package exists. RC14 ships the same product changes as RC12; everything in the [RC13](v1.0.0-rc.13.md), [RC12](v1.0.0-rc.12.md) and [RC11](v1.0.0-rc.11.md) notes is included.\n\n## Changes since RC13\n\n### Qualification tooling and release workflow (not in the package)\n\n- The evaluator's compiler-exposure check no longer depends on deleting the hosted runner's preinstalled SDK trees. It masks host-only SDK directories inside the candidate sandbox under every mounted spelling, ignores an inventoried path only when it has been removed before inspection, and names the cause when its inventory helper fails (timeout, kill, nonzero exit or unexpected output). Every other inspection error still refuses qualification. RC13's release run failed when this check refused in two evaluator tests.\n- The CLI test step in the release and CI workflows now has a 45-minute limit. RC13's release run and a main CI run stalled after the evaluator test file finished, because its test process did not exit; a hung step now fails the job instead of running for six hours. The limit bounds the damage; the cause of the non-exiting test process has not been identified.\n\nNo product code changed between RC12's tag and RC14.\n\n## Runtime requirements\n\n- Linux x86-64 with glibc 2.35 or newer.\n- Node.js 22 or newer.\n- An OpenAI-compatible inference endpoint, local or explicitly selected provider.\n\nThe archive does not include Node.js. Rust and Cargo are not required at runtime. No other OS or architecture is claimed.\n\n## Candidate assets\n\nThe release workflow for `v1.0.0-rc.14` is expected to produce the version-matched Linux archive, `SHA256SUMS`, SBOM, notices, installer, and provenance. The workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and qualification evidence must be recorded before this candidate can be accepted. Local builds are not interchangeable with the workflow-produced artifacts.\n\n## Qualification status\n\nThis is a candidate, not an accepted release. The installed-RC gates — platform and lifecycle evidence including the power-loss cell, mandatory automated CI PTY (§5.1) and scripted installed-RC PTY (§5.2), provider and standalone qualification, held-out task quality, cross-runner reproducibility, independent exact-RC acceptance and the requirements ledger — remain outstanding for this artifact. RC11 evidence does not carry over to RC14 without an explicit, reviewed carry-forward. The manual matrix (§5.3) is waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20; this does not waive steering, accessibility, or any other release gate. Passing source CI does not satisfy installed-RC qualification.\n{\n  \"name\": \"local-code-harness\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0-rc.14\",\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"description\": \"Autonomous local AI coding harness (Codex / Claude-Code style) for LM Studio and vLLM\",\n  \"main\": \"dist/index.js\",\n  \"bin\": {\n    \"harness\": \"./dist/index.js\"\n  },\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"build\": \"tsc && node scripts/write_build_info.mjs\",\n    \"test\": \"node scripts/run_tests.mjs && bash ../scripts/terminal-acceptance/test-scope-procs.sh\",\n    \"start\": \"node dist/index.js\",\n    \"dev\": \"tsx watch src/index.ts\"\n  },\n  \"keywords\": [\n    \"ai\",\n    \"coding-agent\",\n    \"codex\",\n    \"claude-code\",\n    \"vllm\",\n    \"lm-studio\",\n    \"rust\"\n  ],\n  \"author\": \"\",\n  \"license\": \"MIT\",\n  \"engines\": {\n    \"node\": \">=22\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"commander\": \"^12.1.0\",\n    \"dotenv\": \"^16.4.5\",\n    \"ora\": \"^8.1.0\",\n    \"picocolors\": \"^1.1.1\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@types/node\": \"^22.5.0\",\n    \"tsx\": \"^4.19.0\",\n    \"typescript\": \"^5.5.4\"\n  }\n}\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18bda-0a8d-7963-bd38-a3a61a293f7d","create_time":1793347991.1136067}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
