{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T08:14:57.653Z","ordinal":523703,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18bda-0a8d-7963-bd38-a3a61a293f7d","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae451ff27b8819fbb42847071d20b7c","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"## Checkpoint\n\n**Campaign:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`  \n**Acceptance:** `IN_PROGRESS`\n\n- Integration is `890c553d6f283176d9d95edaea489811584c8930` (PR #342). Requirements enforcement and RC14 version checks pass on this exact revision.\n- Post-merge CI run `41024603827` is still running Node 22 and Node 24. CodeQL/JavaScript-TypeScript run `41024603876` passed.\n- Independent review found two issues in PR #342: its timeout test accepted any numeric limit, and it changed RC13’s tagged notes. I prepared [PR #343](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/343) to require exactly 45 minutes and restore the tagged RC13 notes. A fresh review accepted that diff; its focused test passed. Exact-head CI is running.\n- No RC14 tag or GitHub release exists. I’ll keep RC construction gated on PR #343 and post-merge checks.\n- Held-out issue #1 remains open without a custodian update since 04:28 UTC. The protected corpus remains untouched; no held-out qualification has started.\n\nI recorded the refreshed state in the release claim and corrected a checkpoint timestamp that was ahead of the host clock. The shared dirty checkout remains unchanged.\n\n**Next:** wait for the current CI runs, integrate PR #343 if its exact checks remain green, then recheck source gates before constructing the RC. Held-out custody and exact-RC qualification remain downstream acceptance gates.\n\n"}],"phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":{"entries":[{"path":"MEMORY.md","lineStart":580,"lineEnd":606,"note":"source CI and code review do not replace exact RC acceptance"}],"rolloutIds":["01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0"]}},"started_at_ms":1793348095173,"completed_at_ms":1793348097653}}
