{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T08:25:51.209Z","ordinal":524205,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18be5-e339-7910-80af-f4c3f5102373","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae4548d4564819f88528ab4f531398e","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"**Campaign:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`  \n**Acceptance:** `IN_PROGRESS`\n\nThe live Node 22/24 suites on `890c553d` and PR #343 are still running. I did not start a competing suite.\n\nI reviewed the failures in stale evidence PRs #336, #338, #339, and #334. The compiler-exposure failures occurred on older source that predates the scanner changes present in `890c553d`. PR #334 also exposed an unresolved failure in the synthetic T4 overload smoke test: the failed record lacks `model.faultsInjected`, and the runner’s exception path omits the underlying error. I recorded this without classifying it as a product defect or dismissing it as a flake.\n\nAfter the active suite finishes and releases the SUITE claim, the next diagnostic step is to reproduce that single synthetic T4 case against current main with enough failure detail to identify the cause. No held-out material was accessed; no RC14 tag or release exists.\n\n"}],"phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":{"entries":[{"path":"MEMORY.md","lineStart":580,"lineEnd":606,"note":"green source CI is not exact RC acceptance evidence"}],"rolloutIds":["01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0"]}},"started_at_ms":1793348749284,"completed_at_ms":1793348751209}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T08:25:51.224Z","ordinal":524206,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","status":"completed","id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae4548d4564819f88528ab4f531398e","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"**Campaign:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`  \n**Acceptance:** `IN_PROGRESS`\n\nThe live Node 22/24 suites on `890c553d` and PR #343 are still running. I did not start a competing suite.\n\nI reviewed the failures in stale evidence PRs #336, #338, #339, and #334. The compiler-exposure failures occurred on older source that predates the scanner changes present in `890c553d`. PR #334 also exposed an unresolved failure in the synthetic T4 overload smoke test: the failed record lacks `model.faultsInjected`, and the runner’s exception path omits the underlying error. I recorded this without classifying it as a product defect or dismissing it as a flake.\n\nAfter the active suite finishes and releases the SUITE claim, the next diagnostic step is to reproduce that single synthetic T4 case against current main with enough failure detail to identify the cause. No held-out material was accessed; no RC14 tag or release exists.\n\n<oai-mem-citation>\n<citation_entries>\nMEMORY.md:580-606|note=[green source CI is not exact RC acceptance evidence]\n</citation_entries>\n<rollout_ids>\n01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0\n</rollout_ids>\n</oai-mem-citation>","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"final_answer","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18be5-e339-7910-80af-f4c3f5102373","create_time":1793348749.2728312,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae4548d4564819f88528ab4f531398e","turn_id":"01a18be5-e339-7910-80af-f4c3f5102373","role":"assistant"},"revision":"retained_01a18bea-4f78-7b92-bf11-3d9e53ef9420","complete":true},"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":24143}}
