{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T08:33:27.350Z","ordinal":524551,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18bed-1e39-7a80-8dda-b29fbcdc44b3","session_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","root_turn_id":"01a18bed-1e39-7a80-8dda-b29fbcdc44b3","response_id":"resp_0db389702a7164cc016ae45655e564819f962057320aa70621","usage":{"input_tokens":68789,"cached_input_tokens":63360,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":111,"reasoning_output_tokens":94,"total_tokens":68900},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":6819463,"cached_input_tokens":6787584,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":13895,"reasoning_output_tokens":6546,"total_tokens":6833358},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":9891915340,"cached_input_tokens":9787458304,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":28372690,"reasoning_output_tokens":16684350,"total_tokens":9920288030}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T08:33:27.522Z","ordinal":524552,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a18bf1-45e1-70f0-a8ae-cb27504aea29","call_id":"call_53f1a7361e8c4cbd81462b839918e26f","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/pr311_draft_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**Finding: T4 overloaded smoke — unresolved, likely failure-path observability rather than a demonstrated fault-injection defect.**\\n\\nRun [41009682069](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/41009682069), job `123929299347`, ran head `f28263e0fa143f4b7ca3d7563ad38773076b8dd2`. Its log records test 313 failing at `cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts:115`: `r.model.faultsInjected` was `undefined`; the expected value was the injected overloaded fault. The assertion is unchanged at current main `890c553d` ([test lines 112–120](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/blob/890c553d/cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts#L112-L120)).\\n\\nThe runner normally takes `model` from proxy stats and includes it in the returned record ([`eval/run.mjs:218–245, 278–298`](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/blob/890c553d/eval/run.mjs#L218-L245)). But its exception path returns a reduced record without `model` or the underlying error details ([`eval/run.mjs:299–300`](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/blob/890c553d/eval/run.mjs#L299-L300)). Thus the assertion does not establish whether the fault was missed or the run failed earlier. I can’t classify this as a product defect or a flake from the available log; it remains a real regression-test failure with inadequate diagnostic information.\\n\\n**Compiler-exposure failures — stale-source issue.**\\n\\nThe failing PR bases were `8f742f1` for #336 and `b97297c` / `165a273` for #338 / #339, each based on `5c516476`. Their CI logs show hardened checks and the Go/Rust source-isolation test aborting with `compiler exposure could not be checked; refusing qualification` (for example, [run 40992017829](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40992017829), job `123863637143`, tests 304, 308, and 310). That is the scanner’s intended fail-closed outcome, but it prevented those tests from completing.\\n\\nCurrent main `890c553d` includes follow-up scanner changes absent from the failing base: bounded batching of inventory roots and more specific failure reasons ([`eval/scan-compiler-exposure.mjs:15–26, 62–85, 167–185, 192–222, 280–282`](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/blob/890c553d/eval/scan-compiler-exposure.mjs#L15-L26)). This makes the old failures stale-source evidence, not evidence of a current-main compiler-isolation defect. The logs don’t reveal which scanner failure reason occurred on those old heads.\\n\\n**Next discriminating check:** run only the T4 overloaded smoke on current main with the exception-path error retained in its diagnostic output. If it fails again, that will distinguish a repeatable runner defect from a transient CI failure. I did not run tests or inspect held-out material.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/review_pr300_readiness\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** — reviewed the uncommitted delta over `ba72d2cbfb8f446254cf829ac5990148fed82500`. The new report binds the task to RC11’s source revision, archive digest, installed version, OpenRouter model, declared deliverable, and explicit verifier (`openrouter-live-task-20261030.md:5–11`). It preserves the incomplete and unverified attempts, records the final verified disposition and reported independent 2/2 rerun, and limits the claim to one synthetic task rather than E5 or RC acceptance (`:15–19, :29–39`; `README.md:32–40`).\\n\\n`sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS` passed for all 23 entries; `git diff --check` passed. The new report contains no credentials or raw prompt transcript. Its hashes for source, test, flight log, and receipts are documented, but those raw files are not included, so those hashes and run details remain operator-reported rather than independently reproducible (`:29–35`).\\n\\nDiff SHA-256: `db79879f51989668a8b6367b78329df9584114e34abe53d0fa564eeeffd8d09f`. I did not edit files or run qualification.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/review_pr302\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**CHANGES_REQUIRED** — reviewed base `d68695f3cb299c51959169d2373f7b924496486e` to head `26c1f541beb3d868e0c3e1604abf674e7aa05949`. Cumulative diff SHA-256: `cf75b63f9d3b90491e5bb1f03f4486fcf2dbf1e9654be17079d21bf2b17781d0`.\\n\\n- **P2 — Timeout parity regression is too weak.** [`release_workflow_parity.test.ts:50`](/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc14-source-gates-20261030T0723Z/cli/test/release_workflow_parity.test.ts:50) checks that each CLI test step has *some numeric timeout*. It would pass if CI used 2 minutes while release used 45, so it does not protect the workflow parity this test covers. Assert the expected `45` for each job, or assert all three parsed values match.\\n- **P2 — RC13 notes are changed after its tag.** The candidate adds a “Not published” status to [`v1.0.0-rc.13.md:5`](/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc14-source-gates-20261030T0723Z/docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.13.md:5), but the RC13 tag’s copy does not contain it. The RC14 notes already record RC13’s failed workflow and unpublished status at [`v1.0.0-rc.14.md:7`](/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc14-source-gates-20261030T0723Z/docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.14.md:7). Keep the correction in RC14/current status documentation and leave the tagged RC13 notes unchanged to preserve the release-note freeze.\\n\\nThe 45-minute bound is applied consistently to the three workflow steps, and the RC14 notes state the non-exit cause is unknown and qualification remains outstanding. No tests were run. The candidate worktree lacks `.entire/agent-guide.md`; I used the available release-process guidance that tagged RC notes are frozen.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18bed-1e39-7a80-8dda-b29fbcdc44b3","create_time":1793349207.5219235}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
