e handshake failed: ${result.error || \"Unknown error\"}`);\n        }\n        let data: any;\n        try {\n          data = JSON.parse(result.output);\n        } catch {\n          throw new Error(`Invalid JSON in core engine hello handshake response: ${result.output}`);\n        }\n        const coreProtocol = data.protocol;\n        const coreVersion = data.version;\n        const expectedVersion = getBuildIdentity().version;\n\n        if (coreProtocol !== CORE_PROTOCOL_VERSION) {\n          throw new Error(\n            `Engine protocol mismatch: core engine reports protocol ${coreProtocol}, but CLI expects ${CORE_PROTOCOL_VERSION}. Run 'make build' to update.`\n          );\n        }\n        if (expectedVersion !== \"unknown\" && coreVersion !== expectedVersion) {\n          throw new Error(\n            `Engine version mismatch: core engine reports version ${coreVersion}, but CLI is ${expectedVersion}. Run 'make build' to update.`\n          );\n        }\n        return { version: coreVersion, protocol: coreProtocol };\n      } catch (err: any) {\n        this.handshakeError = err;\n        this.cleanupRpc();\n        throw err;\n      }\n    })();\n\n    return this.handshakePromise;\n  }\n\n  public static shutdownAllGlobal(): void {\n    for (const b of RustCoreBridge.activeBridges) {\n      b.shutdown();\n    }\n    RustCoreBridge.activeBridges.clear();\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * The abort signal of the turn now running. Every RPC sent while it is set is tied to it: when the turn is cancelled,\n   * the runner is told to end that request's command (its whole process group) instead of leaving it running.\n    }\n}\n\n/**\n * Asynchronous Non-Blocking JSON-RPC Stdio Server using Tokio (Candidate #05)\n */\nasync fn run_rpc_async(workspace: &Path) {\n    use std::sync::Arc;\n    use tokio::io::{AsyncBufReadExt, AsyncWriteExt, BufReader};\n\n    let stdin = tokio::io::stdin();\n    let reader = BufReader::new(stdin);\n    let mut lines = reader.lines();\n\n    let stdout = Arc::new(tokio::sync::Mutex::new(tokio::io::stdout()));\n    let ws = Arc::new(workspace.to_path_buf());\n\n    // The engine owns the commands it started: when its client goes away (stdin closes), or it is told to stop, every\n    // command group still running (and every background process they left) is ended before it exits (REQ-SEC-106).\n    #[cfg(unix)]\n    {\n        use tokio::signal::unix::{signal, SignalKind};\n        for kind in [SignalKind::terminate(), SignalKind::hangup(), SignalKind::interrupt()] {\n            if let Ok(mut stream) = signal(kind) {\n                tokio::spawn(async move {\n                    if stream.recv().await.is_some() {\n                        shutdown_and_exit(143).await;\n                    }\n                });\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    while let Ok(Some(line)) = lines.next_line().await {\n        let trimmed = line.trim().to_string();\n        if trimmed.is_empty() {\n            continue;\n        }\n\n        let stdout_clone = Arc::clone(&stdout);\n        let ws_clone = Arc::clone(&ws);\n\n        tokio::spawn(async move {\n            let response = match serde_json::from_str::<RpcRequest>(&trimmed) {\n                Ok(req) => {\n                    let method = req.method;\n                    let params = req.params;\n                    let id = req.id;\n                    let key = id.as_ref().map(|v| v.to_string());\n                    let exec_res = tokio::task::spawn_blocking(move || {\n                        execute_request(&method, params, &ws_clone, key)\n                    })\n                    .await;\n\n                    match exec_res {\n                        Ok(Ok(result)) => RpcResponse {\n                            id,\n                            result: Some(result),\n                            error: None,\n                        },\n                        Ok(Err(err)) => RpcResponse {\n                            id,\n                            result: None,\n                            error: Some(err),\n                        },\n                        Err(join_err) => RpcResponse {\n                            id,\n                            result: None,\n                            error: Some(format!(\"Task execution failed: {join_err}\")),\n                        },\n                    }\n                }\n                Err(e) => RpcResponse {\n                    id: None,\n                    result: None,\n                    error: Some(format!(\"Invalid JSON-RPC request: {e}\")),\n                },\n            };\n\n            if let Ok(json) = serde_json::to_string(&response) {\n                let mut out = stdout_clone.lock().await;\n                let _ = out.write_all(format!(\"{json}\\n\").as_bytes()).await;\n                let _ = out.flush().await;\n            }\n        });\n    }\n    shutdown_and_exit(0).await;\n}\n\n/// Ends every command group the engine started, then exits.\nasync fn shutdown_and_exit(code: i32) {\n    #[cfg(unix)]\n    {\n        let _ = tokio::task::spawn_blocking(|| runner::end_all_commands(CANCEL_GRACE)).await;\n    }\n    std::process::exit(code);\n                }\n            };\n            match execute_tool(&tool, params, &workspace) {\n                Ok(res) => {\n                    println!(\"{}\", serde_json::to_string_pretty(&res).unwrap());\n                }\n                Err(e) => {\n                    eprintln!(\"Error executing {tool}: {e}\");\n                    std::process::exit(1);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        Commands::Rpc => {\n            // If the client dies without closing stdin, the kernel delivers SIGTERM, which runs the same shutdown.\n            #[cfg(target_os = \"linux\")]\n            unsafe {\n                libc::prctl(libc::PR_SET_PDEATHSIG, libc::SIGTERM);\n            }\n            run_rpc_async(&workspace).await;\n        }\n    }\n}\ncore/src/main.rs-60-/// `key` identifies