{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T09:02:09.571Z","ordinal":525674,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18bff-7011-7da3-8833-52d22c944baa","session_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","root_turn_id":"01a18bff-7011-7da3-8833-52d22c944baa","response_id":"resp_0db389702a7164cc016ae45d0d31dc819f929ded90cef3ee08","usage":{"input_tokens":237401,"cached_input_tokens":236160,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":300,"reasoning_output_tokens":283,"total_tokens":237701},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":16653326,"cached_input_tokens":16527488,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":34912,"reasoning_output_tokens":21072,"total_tokens":16688238},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":9914335871,"cached_input_tokens":9809696640,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":28423494,"reasoning_output_tokens":16713158,"total_tokens":9942759365}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T09:02:09.576Z","ordinal":525675,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a18c0b-8ca7-76a2-917e-86b2c5ff0d59","call_id":"call_eb4ebf8dc0414396ba6ad7cc06c012c3","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/pr311_draft_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** — reviewed the one-file diff against base `890c553d6f283176d9d95edaea489811584c8930`. Diff SHA-256: `d4b51c5450d98343c3cd7e6cd7fe216363541b11f3df97c5bfaa847d88b7d2a3`.\\n\\nThe added checks preserve the existing acceptance conditions: missing telemetry still fails the expected-value assertion, and `hiddenPass` must still be true. They add failure context for an error record, missing proxy telemetry, or a failed hidden check. The expanded messages concern the synthetic `selftest-add` fixture and fake peer in [eval_harness.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-t4-overload-diagnostic/cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts:50); its hidden test only exercises `add` and prints `hidden: add ok`. I found no held-out content exposure in these diagnostics.\\n\\nSource review only; I did not run tests.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/review_pr300_readiness\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** — reviewed the uncommitted delta over `ba72d2cbfb8f446254cf829ac5990148fed82500`. The new report binds the task to RC11’s source revision, archive digest, installed version, OpenRouter model, declared deliverable, and explicit verifier (`openrouter-live-task-20261030.md:5–11`). It preserves the incomplete and unverified attempts, records the final verified disposition and reported independent 2/2 rerun, and limits the claim to one synthetic task rather than E5 or RC acceptance (`:15–19, :29–39`; `README.md:32–40`).\\n\\n`sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS` passed for all 23 entries; `git diff --check` passed. The new report contains no credentials or raw prompt transcript. Its hashes for source, test, flight log, and receipts are documented, but those raw files are not included, so those hashes and run details remain operator-reported rather than independently reproducible (`:29–35`).\\n\\nDiff SHA-256: `db79879f51989668a8b6367b78329df9584114e34abe53d0fa564eeeffd8d09f`. I did not edit files or run qualification.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/review_pr302\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**CHANGES_REQUIRED** — reviewed base `d68695f3cb299c51959169d2373f7b924496486e` to head `26c1f541beb3d868e0c3e1604abf674e7aa05949`. Cumulative diff SHA-256: `cf75b63f9d3b90491e5bb1f03f4486fcf2dbf1e9654be17079d21bf2b17781d0`.\\n\\n- **P2 — Timeout parity regression is too weak.** [`release_workflow_parity.test.ts:50`](/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc14-source-gates-20261030T0723Z/cli/test/release_workflow_parity.test.ts:50) checks that each CLI test step has *some numeric timeout*. It would pass if CI used 2 minutes while release used 45, so it does not protect the workflow parity this test covers. Assert the expected `45` for each job, or assert all three parsed values match.\\n- **P2 — RC13 notes are changed after its tag.** The candidate adds a “Not published” status to [`v1.0.0-rc.13.md:5`](/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc14-source-gates-20261030T0723Z/docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.13.md:5), but the RC13 tag’s copy does not contain it. The RC14 notes already record RC13’s failed workflow and unpublished status at [`v1.0.0-rc.14.md:7`](/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc14-source-gates-20261030T0723Z/docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.14.md:7). Keep the correction in RC14/current status documentation and leave the tagged RC13 notes unchanged to preserve the release-note freeze.\\n\\nThe 45-minute bound is applied consistently to the three workflow steps, and the RC14 notes state the non-exit cause is unknown and qualification remains outstanding. No tests were run. The candidate worktree lacks `.entire/agent-guide.md`; I used the available release-process guidance that tagged RC notes are frozen.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18bff-7011-7da3-8833-52d22c944baa","create_time":1793350929.575862}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
