ive inference remains unverified)\n23:- NEXUS_HOME, install.sh, scripts/package-linux.sh, scripts/smoke-package.sh, cli/src/tools.ts, cli/src/tui.ts, harness-core, nexus-tui, Node.js 20+, Linux x86-64/glibc, v0.1.0-alpha.1, 38459471967, 39548ab8b6ba4043e930f8a30d99ce6f9f787f68c8c46b1b10a9a2f1ea7e5ec8\n27:- for Cloudflare contest work, the user required using the existing repository, preserving unrelated history/work, and distinguishing the Nexus Code client from the Cloudflare Workers/Artifacts submission -> do not replace repositories or wholesale-integrate unaccepted candidates. [Task 1]\n29:- when preparing a client deliverable, the user required proving the actual architecture rather than assuming one Rust executable -> include the TypeScript sidecar/CLI, production Node dependencies, `harness-core`, `nexus-tui`, and assets in both packaging and clean-environment verification. [Task 2]\n34:- Contest-specific CI passed at `ce7e58b9ce3f6e4a72f84d205c5319b241ca0aa9` in workflow `38471712649`; it covered demo tests and Worker build/typecheck, not a real Cloudflare account run. The service is the submission; Nexus Code is its client/demo harness. [Task 1]\n41:- Symptom: parameterized source, synthetic broker tests, Worker build/typecheck, or public video is called contest-ready. Cause: the installed protected broker launcher clears inherited configuration and depends on a prior root-owned `/opt/nexus-cloudflare-broker`, external credential files, and fixed runtime identity. Fix: keep disposition blocked until a fresh account/resource run verifies candidate refs, work-state, Worker response, and integration output; a safe clean-host broker/credential bootstrap is still needed. [Task 1]\n45:# Task Group: Nexus agent effectiveness: unbounded continuation and evidence-bounded diagnosis\n46:scope: Review failed Nexus agent exports and maintain prompt/regression safeguards for progressing continuation loops, direct diagnostic questions, and timeout claims in `/home/mike/nexus-code`.\n47:applies_to: cwd=/home/mike/nexus-code; reuse_rule=recheck the current agent prompt, test suite, and exact export before attributing a specific failure; the no-cumulative-step-ceiling preference is durable, while the observed run metrics are export-specific.\n53:- rollout_summaries/2026-10-14T22-57-40-v8Tm-nexus_agent_effectiveness_unbounded_loops_evidence_bounded_d.md (cwd=/home/mike/nexus-code, rollout_path=/home/mike/.codex/sessions/2026/10/14/rollout-2026-10-14T22-57-40-01a13ca2-bc00-7060-ba3c-76dfba4736c0.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-14T23:14:22+00:00, thread_id=01a13ca2-bc00-7060-ba3c-76dfba4736c0, completed diagnosis with failure evidence)\n57:- Nexus, nexus-session-session_20261014_091558_9m78.json, CONTEXT_CAPACITY_EXCEEDED, 54582+8192+4096>65536, make test, timeout, truncated output, direct status question, evidence-bounded diagnosis\n63:- rollout_summaries/2026-10-14T22-57-40-v8Tm-nexus_agent_effectiveness_unbounded_loops_evidence_bounded_d.md (cwd=/home/mike/nexus-code, rollout_path=/home/mike/.codex/sessions/2026/10/14/rollout-2026-10-14T22-57-40-01a13ca2-bc00-7060-ba3c-76dfba4736c0.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-14T23:14:22+00:00, thread_id=01a13ca2-bc00-7060-ba3c-76dfba4736c0, focused regressions passed; full `make test` not rerun)\n108:- Flash-Next Q-TOOLS passed 7/7 synthetic categories and 20/20 Nexus replay points. Q-LONGCTX passed probes from 16K through 59,913 tokens; a 67,335-token input was rejected with HTTP 400 in 0.14s. Both selected models passed production qualification after reboot and rollback restoration. [Task 1]\n146:# Task Group: Nexus dogfood-blockers independent candidate review and compaction evidence integrity\n147:scope: Review-only, isolated validation of `fix/dogfood-blockers` candidates against Nexus baseline; use before selecting an I1/objective-supervisor base or relying on context admission, unseen-result, or modified-file evidence.\n148:applies_to: cwd=/home/mike/nexus-code and /home/mike/nexus-blockers (one rollou