thetic broker tests, and public video must not be presented as Cloudflare-backed acceptance; do not automate application entry. [Task 1]\n    29\t- when preparing a client deliverable, the user required proving the actual architecture rather than assuming one Rust executable -> include the TypeScript sidecar/CLI, production Node dependencies, `harness-core`, `nexus-tui`, and assets in both packaging and clean-environment verification. [Task 2]\n    30\t- the user required exact downloadable-artifact and clean-environment verification before declaring readiness -> packaging structure, a release workflow, or a fresh-home install alone is insufficient. [Task 2]\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":27350}},"started_at_ms":1793351303611,"completed_at_ms":1793351303612}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T09:08:24.587Z","ordinal":525921,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18c11-458b-7292-a5e1-3749360c13aa","call_id":"call_344974ea0a8b4bc7b6f14cb00ac5e145","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"    15\t## Task 2: Package Nexus Code as a complete Linux client with installer and CI, partial\n    16\t\n    17\t### rollout_summary_files\n    18\t\n    19\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/mike/nexus-code, rollout_path=/home/mike/.codex/sessions/2026/10/13/rollout-2026-10-13T16-47-30-01a13629-7b99-7b61-a6e3-88bb4ac1dd15.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-23T04:47:40+00:00, thread_id=01a13629-7b99-7b61-a6e3-88bb4ac1dd15, prerelease/installer evidence exists; representative inference remains unverified)\n    20\t\n    21\t### keywords\n    22\t\n    23\t- NEXUS_HOME, install.sh, scripts/package-linux.sh, scripts/smoke-package.sh, cli/src/tools.ts, cli/src/tui.ts, harness-core, nexus-tui, Node.js 20+, Linux x86-64/glibc, v0.1.0-alpha.1, 38459471967, 39548ab8b6ba4043e930f8a30d99ce6f9f787f68c8c46b1b10a9a2f1ea7e5ec8\n    24\t\n    25\t## User preferences\n    26\t\n    27\t- for Cloudflare contest work, the user required using the existing repository, preserving unrelated history/work, and distinguishing the Nexus Code client from the Cloudflare Workers/Artifacts submission -> do not replace repositories or wholesale-integrate unaccepted candidates. [Task 1]\n    28\t- the user required evidence-supported claims and separate ready/blocked dispositions -> local fixtures, structural checks, synthetic broker tests, and public video must not be presented as Cloudflare-backed acceptance; do not automate application entry. [Task 1]\n    29\t- when preparing a client deliverable, the user required proving the actual architecture rather than assuming one Rust executable -> include the TypeScript sidecar/CLI, production Node dependencies, `harness-core`, `nexus-tui`, and assets in both packaging and clean-environment verification. [Task 2]\n    30\t- the user required exact downloadable-artifact and clean-environment verification before declaring readiness -> packaging structure, a release workflow, or a fresh-home install alone is insufficient. [Task 2]\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18bff-7011-7da3-8833-52d22c944baa","create_time":1793351304.5877733}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
