{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T09:08:59.774Z","ordinal":525927,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"task_complete","root_turn_id":"01a18bff-7011-7da3-8833-52d22c944baa","turn_id":"01a18bff-7011-7da3-8833-52d22c944baa","last_agent_message":"## Progress checkpoint\n\n**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`  \n**Acceptance:** `IN_PROGRESS` — no accepted RC or completed release.\n\n- **Integration:** `origin/main` is `16eeb6eeffe7fc0bae234aa34dcb671a6ba5ff99`. PR #343 is merged.\n- **CI:** Post-merge run [41029564419](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/41029564419) is still running the Node 22 and Node 24 suites. CodeQL run 41029564602 passed. I did not start overlapping local tests.\n- **Evaluator diagnostics:** Commit `c6f00e8f` rebases the diagnostic-only test change onto current main. Its exact diff matches the independently accepted review. Two focused synthetic tests passed on the prior base, after building the evaluator’s required CLI and Rust release artifacts. The rerun on current main and PR checks remain queued until SUITE is released. No held-out tasks were accessed.\n- **Claims:** Updated the two claims for this diagnostic slice and appended its evidence to the claims log. Other held-out and evidence-consolidation lanes remain owned; I did not take them over.\n- **Release:** GitHub’s latest release remains RC11; no RC14 tag or release is present. Held-out custody and exact-RC qualification remain unresolved. Manual terminal evidence remains waived for v1.0.0 per the recorded decision.\n- **Tooling:** The required Entire Brain query timed out; I continued from the repository’s checked-in release and concurrency documentation.\n\n**Next:** Once the hosted suites finish, rerun the focused tests on `16eeb6ee`, then open the diagnostic PR and let exact-head checks run. Reconcile that result with the post-merge CI before proceeding toward RC14. The public release is not verified.\n\n","started_at":1793350135,"completed_at":1793351339,"duration_ms":1203931,"time_to_first_token_ms":1566}}
