nce is recorded. Public Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned; the latest metadata-only correction was posted at 04:18 UTC. T2 custody acceptance and qualification, full T3/T4 qualification, current-candidate provider and standalone qualification, fault injection, successor-RC reproducibility and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. RC10 evidence does not qualify a successor candidate.\n\n**Terminal gate:** The release owner requires all 15 manual terminal cells (five environments × three sizes) on the exact installed RC. The latest verified worksheet status is 0/15 accepted cells; blank cells remain incomplete. Actual operator execution and per-cell outcomes are mandatory; automated CI or PTY results do not substitute. [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver) waives screenshots only. [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver) withdraws the prior matrix-waiver record. `ubuntu-desktop` at `10.0.8.3` has the required terminal applications, but the manual matrix remains outstanding. This 04:23 snapshot predates DEC-20 and is superseded by the current checkpoint above.\n\n**Suite evidence:** `make test` completed on immutable snapshot `03bfaa394c906d900574f35104e521844049403c` with isolated HOME and the required evaluator workspace/runtime fixtures: 1,993 tests across 224 suites, 1,991 passed, 0 failed, 2 skipped, 0 cancelled; Rust tests and post-test security lifecycle gates passed. The full run took 3,167,118 ms. This snapshot is not exact current main, PR #311 candidate `fe28ec9`, or an RC, so the result does not qualify those revisions. The SUITE claim transferred to the OpenCode custodian at 04:18 UTC for the 20-task custody revalidation above.\n\n**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. Stable publication remains gated on mandatory exact-RC qualification and acceptance. Publication authorization remains granted; no further authorization is requested.\n\n## Historical checkpoint (observed 2026-10-28 20:18 UTC; superseded)\n\nThis historical checkpoint includes a matrix-waiver conclusion that was later withdrawn by the current DEC-19 decision. It records the prior checkpoint only and is not the current acceptance disposition.\n\n**Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0`, the merge commit for PR #305. Exact-main CI run [40751988282](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40751988282) and CodeQL run [40751988267](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40751988267) passed on that SHA. The source requirements check passed on this revision with 123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open, and 12 deferred to exact-RC qualification. These source-stage results do not qualify an installed release candidate.\n\n**Integrated changes and open PRs:** PR #299 merged as `004234de6d8599d71083b4f686c1bdbffe21dd2f` (merge commit `145d464dd819a20bf918dfbb4f0176f2c4840a08`). PR #307 merged as `90837aa5193d7c071066d27ccefd2b2ea2db0aff`. PR #305 merged at `13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0`; its GitHub Entire Gates check concluded **NEUTRAL** (“No trail tracks this branch”). PR #302 was closed unmerged. PR #308 supersedes it and is open at `2c1b2dfa6b10f736367020a86228ab64a4173500` on current base `13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0`. Exact-head CI run [40757432379](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40757432379) has Node 22 and Node 24 passing; Linux packaging/tests remain in progress. CodeQL and JavaScript/TypeScript passed. The PR head fixes the `globName` test by staging it with the literal `:(literal)` pathspec. A separate local follow-up commit `9829c61d9b2556bba25a5ec6aee8fa9f1acf9bc8` applies literal staging to the `magicName` fixture and asserts that it entered the index; this follow-up is not on the PR head. Its focused 77/77 result is owner-reported without a retained log, so that additional fixture change still needs exact-head checks before integration. PR #309 is open at `aace981bc3f46e10f1e57c5498825a76e9994ee5` on the current base. Run [40758300812](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40758300812) has Node 22 and Node 24 passing; CodeQL and JavaScript/TypeScript passed, and Linux packaging/tests are in progress. PR #300 is open at `f3957a67ac8f9b5ea1e60be2494b9402d943230f` on the current base. Run [40757603196](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40757603196) has Node 22 and Node 24 passing; Linux packaging/tests remain in progress. A fresh checkpoint accuracy correction was posted on PR #300 (comment [6479279112](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/300#issuecomment-6479279112)); this local update addresses the stale PR heads and main-CI status identified there. Source PR checks are distinct from release qualification.\n\n**Qualification and release:** Public [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) remains the latest release; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. Official cross-runner run [40564959805](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40564959805) passed for the published RC10 source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`, rebuilding on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04. Its machine-readable evidence reports `REQ-REL-114` / `ACC-SUP-08` `PASS` and matching hashes for six outputs, including the published archive and `sbom.cdx.json`; see the [RC10 reproducibility record](../reviews/evidence/v1/REQ-REL-114-rc10-20261027/README.md). The requirements ledger still marks `REQ-REL-114` `UNV`/open; its owner must reconcile that disposition. RC10 evidence does not establish successor-RC qualification. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned (last updated 2026-10-28 14:23 UTC); no custodian acceptance or held-out T2/T3/T4 qualification is established. The terminal matrix remains 0/15; the user waived screenshot artifacts, while terminal behavior checks remain unrun. Standalone/provider, fault-injection, successor-RC qualification, required human terminal behavior, and independent exact-RC acceptance gates remain outstanding. Stable publication remains gated.\n\n**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. Passing source CI and RC10-only provider/reproducibility evidence do not establish release acceptance. Existing publication authorization remains gated by acceptance.\n\nThe checkpoints below are retained as historical evidence; their source revision, PR, CI, and qualification statements are superseded by this observation.\n\n## Historical checkpoint (observed 2026-10-28 16:25 UTC; superseded)\n\n**Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `145d464dd819a20bf918dfbb4f0176f2c4840a08`. Exact-head CI run [40720824591](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40720824591) passed the Node 22 and Node 24 test matrices; the Linux packaging/reproducibility job was still running at observation time. CodeQL run [40720824319](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40720824319) passed. The CI jobs completed `sync-version --check` and the requirements checker successfully on this source. These results qualify the source revision only; they do not qualify an installed release candidate.\n\n**Release PRs:** PR [#299](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/299) is merged at `004234de6d8599d71083b4f686c1bdbffe21dd2f`, included in current main. PR [#302](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302) is based on `145d464` at exact head `49a2af0c1d556912d12b834aa7f2022ef63b528c`; its latest follow-up scopes checkout to the nested workspace and extends the regression to preserve both staged and unstaged sibling state. The prior nested-index delta at `662d084` was independently ACCEPTed (SHA-256 `61f4e40bc135152ffa003c82bdc31fc15703542b5bd9ba3b67f7b6b1edae1cb2`), and the checkout-scope delta was independently ACCEPTed by `review_pr302` (SHA-256 `26ce020bdc1f6865e194f02e45c6889eaa32415cc786a457fbcfae1ddaa78605`, tests not run). PR #302 CodeQL and JS/TS checks pass; Node 22/24 CI and Entire are running. TypeScript `--noEmit` and `git diff --check` passed on the prior delta; no local suite was run under the active SUITE claim.\n\nPR [#307](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/307) is based on `145d464` at `88bf19c817f8de7461faf9826e405e52630bb08f`. Its clean-checkout build-identity correction has an independent ACCEPT review for the exact diff (SHA-256 `c0c7b8be14de2cf1aab3246b2f34596ba4aae30c2d527c1afbe93e1ce0105295`); JS/TS, CodeQL and Node 22/24 pass, Linux packaging and Entire remain pending. PR [#300](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/300) contains this readiness record at exact head `dded46ba54001bd511aefce4719839f4b77c85ef`; its corrected checkpoint has just been pushed and all exact-head checks are pending. PRs [#305](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/305) and [#306](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/306) are explicitly v1.1 scope and are not part of the v1.0.0 merge path.\n\n**Requirements and qualification:** Current-main CI's requirements checker passes; the most recent explicit `--enforce` result was on PR #302 head `c3901774` before the nested-workspace-only follow-up: 123 rows, 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open, with 12 requirements deferred to installed-RC qualification. RC10 has scope-limited exact-artifact evidence: OpenRouter pinned-model verification and one synthetic live task passed, and the cross-runner workflow passed for the six listed release artifacts across Ubuntu 22.04/24.04 and against published RC10 (run [40564959805](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40564959805)). A later checkpoint correction incorrectly claimed this workflow failed because of an npm-version mismatch. That correction is superseded: GitHub records run `40564959805` and its `compare` job as completed successfully; the current checkpoint above reports that final result. This historical correction is retained here to preserve the audit trail. These results apply only to immutable RC10 source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`; they do not qualify a successor candidate or establish full release acceptance. The newly pushed #302 head must complete exact checks before its requirements evidence is refreshed. Public [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) remains the latest release; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. GitHub installer is the selected distribution target; npm publication is inapplicable.\n\nIssue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned; its last update was 2026-10-28 14:23 UTC, with no custodian response observed. No held-out payload was accessed and no held-out qualification was run. The manual terminal matrix's last recorded result is 0/15; terminal setup exists on Ubuntu, but no operator screenshots or cell verdicts have been supplied. Held-out/T2/T3/T4, remaining provider and standalone coverage, successor-RC cross-runner reproducibility, the human terminal matrix, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding.\n\n**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. Source CI is mostly complete on `145d464`; PR #302's latest delta awaits independent review and exact Node 22/24 completion, while #307 has independent source review but exact PR checks remain pending. RC10 has passing, bounded provider and cross-runner evidence, but no accepted RC exists and mandatory qualification remains open. Publication authorization remains granted and gated by acceptance.\n\nThe checkpoint below (observed 2026-10-28 15:28 UTC) is retained as historical evidence and is superseded for source revision, CI, PR heads, and release-gate state.\n\n## Historical checkpoint (observed 2026-10-28 15:28 UTC; superseded)\n\n**Authoritative source and requirements gate:** `origin/main` is `b2ae2fe82640e44d58ef5418f49b46df03392212` (PR #304 merge). Current-main CI [40693030763](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40693030763) and CodeQL [40693030710](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40693030710) both completed SUCCESS on that exact revision. A clean detached worktree at that exact source ran `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` with isolated `HOME`: 123 rows; 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 remain explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification. This passes the source-stage enforcement gate only.\n\n**Release PRs and exact-head checks:** PRs [#299](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/299) (`004234de6d8599d71083b4f686c1bdbffe21dd2f`), [#300](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/300) (`11dc196fcdd733f8de71dfc95ff70e109d8f4492`), [#302](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302) (`3c52580ae1da6b7f1282018f4d3702dcb75f8bd7`), and [#305](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/305) (`97f1c6ead710bc059126ba65b37ad1e5fde17666`) are all based on `b2ae2fe`. Exact-head Node 22/24, Linux x86_64, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL checks passed for these candidates. Their Entire Gates checks are failures, so none is mergeable through the required workflow. PR #302's trail reports five high-severity findings and missing reviewer approval. The independent source reviewer ACCEPTed the cumulative diff after a partial source read and did not run tests as part of that review. A separate owner-authored PR update records `tsc --noEmit` and 53/53 targeted restore tests, and advises a second review of `checkpoint.ts` because of its size. PR #299, #300, and #305 also lack successful Entire approval. No findings were bypassed and no self-approval was recorded.\n\n**Local suite attempt:** On a disposable PR #302 snapshot at `3c52580ae1da6b7f1282018f4d3702dcb75f8bd7` plus a 30-line checkpoint-config patch (patch SHA-256 `c80330bc5eeab0ee0bfe73f32a1fcd40e5850c8bc4270e1e08b98758a6aee213`), `make build` completed, but `make test` exited nonzero at `cli/test/eval_version_probe_storage.test.ts:15` because the required `NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT` variable was not set in that run. CI provisions a 128 MiB tmpfs at `/mnt/nexus-eval-ci` and a public runtime root at `/opt/nexus-eval-ci-runtime`. At the latest host check, the tmpfs is mounted with the expected 0711 mode and the runtime root exists; that does not mean the failed run used those fixtures. The result is neither a full-suite pass nor evidence of a product defect. The `SUITE` claim remains held by `kimi-main` for focused `operation_git` regressions; its owner record remains in place, so no overlapping test was started.\n\n**Qualification, custody, and publication:** GitHub still lists [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) as the latest release; there is no `v1.0.0` tag or stable release. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned, with the last metadata-only custodian request at 2026-10-28 14:23 UTC and no response observed. No protected payload was accessed or qualification run. The manual terminal matrix remains 0/15; the final installed RC does not exist. Exact-RC held-out/T2/T3/T4, provider and standalone coverage, cross-runner reproducibility, human terminal evidence, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding. The chosen distribution target remains the GitHub installer; npm publication is inapplicable.\n\n**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. PR integration is blocked by required Entire review findings/approvals; exact-RC qualification is additionally blocked by independent held-out custody and the required human terminal matrix. Existing publication authorization remains granted but gated. The checkpoint below is retained as the 13:34 UTC snapshot and is superseded for current CI, requirements, PR checks, local suite result, and release status.\n\n## Superseded checkpoint (observed 2026-10-28 13:34:51 UTC)\n\n**Authoritative source:** `origin/main` is `b2ae2fe82640e44d58ef5418f49b46df03392212`, the PR #304 merge. Main CI [40693030763](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40693030763) has Node 22 and Node 24 matrix jobs passed (13:23:35 and 13:23:05 UTC); Linux x86_64 remains in progress. CodeQL [40693030710](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40693030710) passed at 13:07:03 UTC. On a clean detached worktree at this exact head, `HOME=/tmp/nexus-req-home XDG_CONFIG_HOME=/tmp/nexus-req-xdg node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed: 123 requirements; 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open, with 12 requirements deferred to exact-RC qualification. PR #304 adds opt-in v1.1 Git-aware operations to current main; its exact-head CI and CodeQL passed and Entire Gates concluded neutral. The independent review recorded an unresolved correctness defect: an explicit restart recreates a clean worktree while resuming the old agent conversation. That behavior must be fixed and requalified before an RC built from this main can be accepted.\n\n**Source PRs:** PR [#303](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/303) is integrated at `4cac22d`; its exact-head required CI and independent review passed. PR [#304](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/304) is integrated at `b2ae2fe`; its exact-head Node 22/24, Linux, CodeQL and JS/TS checks passed and Entire Gates concluded neutral. Its independent review nevertheless found the restart/conversation defect above. PR [#305](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/305) addresses that defect at `f7e573ec8de98fb3ec24a96e148a84b4ccab151f`, with independent review ACCEPT at diff SHA-256 `cf1abd6ce5e7083aebe526efaaee85380dee295fced7814a7ddedcd609a11615`. Build and focused test TypeScript check passed; the runtime test was not run locally because `SUITE` is claimed by `kimi-main`. Exact-head Node 22 and Node 24 jobs in run `40694815985` both failed with 1,882 passed, 2 failed and 2 skipped: `durable_continuity.test.ts` expected the explicit-restart recovery warning, and `tdd_work_units.test.ts` uses a fake agent without `restartConversation`. JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed; Linux was skipped after the matrix failures, and Entire Gates remain pending. PR [#299](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/299) is at `004234de6d8599d71083b4f686c1bdbffe21dd2f` on base `b2ae2fe`; independent review ACCEPTed this exact head at diff SHA-256 `55afcdc8ed8044bb0aa0a54932c5ba6513763b564bc8fb76014b3334db33ae38`. Its Node 22/24 jobs are in progress, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed, and Entire Gates are pending. Issue [#298](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/298) remains open until its fix is integrated and current-main checks pass. At the 13:34:51 UTC snapshot cutoff, before the readiness-only correction was pushed, PR [#300](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/300) was at `e1974fd82dba1aba8e5e2e5b1bc9cf964fe6db20` on base `b2ae2fe`; Node 22/24 and Entire were in progress, while JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed. The subsequent documentation-only update restarted exact-head checks; the claim record tracks its latest head and current statuses. The independent factual review found stale status/head references in the prior checkpoint; corrected evidence is pending re-review. PR [#302](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302) is at `659d6a63a8708ebe98240ec1937b0f2acdcdfac4` on base `b2ae2fe`; Node 22/24, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL pas\n... command output truncated for persistence ...\nikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/297). Its exact-head Node 22/24, Linux, JS/TS, and CodeQL checks passed; Entire Gates was neutral. Post-merge CI [40652572596](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40652572596) is running and CodeQL [40652572591](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40652572591) passed. Exact-main CI [40647479745](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40647479745) completed successfully on its parent source commit `ceaf60072b7c364edac523d2517fb12df8f5f6cd`, including Node 22/24 tests, Linux tests, packaging, reproducibility, SBOM, and installer checks. The requirements gate also passed on exact current main `7970958749fc17be3b0ef4bb725b8e2f0d825ed4` in an isolated worktree (123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 applicable release-qualification rows remain deferred to their documented exact-RC stages). PR [#300](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/300) is being updated to this exact main revision. Source checks do not establish installed-RC acceptance.\n\n**Requested codebase-review findings are part of the v1.0.0 scope:** The large capability registry is split into category modules (`cli/src/core/capabilities.ts`, 10,046 bytes, plus `capability_definitions/`); scheduler logic is in `cli/src/core/scheduler.ts` (23,696 bytes), with `operation.ts` reduced to 12,818 bytes; runner revalidation, execution, and persistence are separated from `operation_runner.ts` (14,931 bytes). Runner decomposition and bounded revalidation/runner diagnostics were integrated through PR [#287](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/287); TDD evidence diagnostics landed through PR [#295](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/295), and scheduler observer diagnostics through PR [#296](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/296). PR [#297](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/297), now merged, adds regression coverage for the TDD diagnostic paths. The capability split and scheduler extraction were integrated through PRs [#286](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/286) and [#285](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/285), respectively. PR [#293](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/293) added operator guidance for `DecisionRejected` and is merged with its Node 22/24, Linux, and CodeQL checks successful. These source changes are implemented on current `main`.\n\n**Lifecycle, scheduler, and evaluation evidence:** `cli/test/convergence_integration.test.ts` covers end-to-end scheduling and execution scenarios. `cli/test/convergence_scheduler_properties.test.ts` runs generated DAG invariants over 100 fixed seeds; this is reproducible generated coverage, not a claim that every scheduler property or arbitrary graph has been proven. PR #297’s regression tests for the TDD diagnostic paths are merged and its required CI passed. The `eval/` pilot suite does not satisfy held-out acceptance: the independent 40-task corpus, custody acceptance, and exact-RC qualification remain required and open.\n\n**Operator configuration scope:** `~/.config/nexus/config.json` is the operator-owned structured configuration entry point for `operationPolicy`, with schema validation, bounded file size, symlink rejection, and environment/config/default precedence documented in `docs/USER_MANUAL.md`. The schema is intentionally limited to that policy today; this record does not claim every runtime default is configurable or that a repository-level config can override operator policy.\n\n**Qualification and publication:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. Held-out T2/T3/T4, remaining live-provider and standalone gates, successor-RC artifact qualification, cross-runner evidence, the 15-cell human terminal matrix, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; stable publication remains gated on these mandatory checks.\n\nThe 03:50 checkpoint below is retained as historical evidence; its source, PR, CI, and qualification statements are superseded by this checkpoint.\n\n## Historical checkpoint (observed 2026-10-28 03:50 UTC)\n\n**Authoritative source and source checks:** `main` is now `d3b7af3ca3d216841f8ff8a0e7b4cefbd637ef9f`, the merge commit for PR [#285](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/285) (merged 2026-10-28 03:38:26 UTC). The exact PR-head Linux retry and required CI passed before merge. Post-merge CI [40627840511](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40627840511) is running the Node 22/24 matrix; CodeQL [40627840517](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40627840517) passed. This is source validation, not installed-RC acceptance. The prior main CI [40621815585](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40621815585) passed on `59f07c4` and does not establish post-merge `d3b7af3` status.\n\n**Integration queue:** PR #285 merged to `d3b7af3`; its exact diff hash and independent ACCEPT were preserved, and the initial state-store lock timeout did not reproduce in its full Linux retry. PR [#289](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/289) is refreshed onto `d3b7af3` at `3f66ee138b1d8aeded2902851f659873d887f307`; its seven-file patch SHA-256 remains `3e13bdaa…`. Fresh Node 22/24/JavaScript checks and Entire Gates are in progress. The first fresh reviewer response described only the docs file, but the GitHub and local diff both contain six implementation/test files plus docs; a complete read-only source review has been requested, so the rebase is not independently accepted yet. PR [#293](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/293), DecisionRejected operator documentation, is refreshed onto `d3b7af3` at `d0e1fbfb10463948b640361bb123177e9490ee1b`; its exact docs diff SHA-256 remains `83de84d7…`. Independent review ACCEPT was reconfirmed at this exact head. Fresh CI is running. Entire's refreshed trail currently reports Approvals failed (no reviewers approved), Findings passed, Up to date passed, and CI pending. The reviewer confirmed no Entire approval integration or distinct identity is available in their session, so the required trail approval remains outstanding. PR [#292](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/292) remains on base `8b24d8e1`, is reported conflicting against current main, and its Entire Gates check failed for missing reviewer approval and staleness. Its remote checks do not establish current-base readiness. No merge is inferred from stale checks.\n\n**RC10 E2 archive repair:** PR #288 restored the 21 retained log files whose entries were already present in the archive manifest, corrected the evidence README's attestation and lifecycle disclosures, and updated `SHA256SUMS`. On the merged candidate, all 45 manifest entries passed `sha256sum -c`; Gitleaks found no leaks; the exact diff received independent ACCEPT. This review accepted the archive repair and factual README corrections only. It did not accept the RC10 E2 product qualification or turn the historical logs into new test results.\n\n**RC10 E2 limits:** The archive still does not demonstrate a successful ordinary `nexus upgrade` from alpha.2 to RC10, successful provenance-attestation verification, power-loss recovery, or an explicit staging-directory-cleanup assertion. The recorded updater process-death recovery is not a power-loss test. E2 acceptance remains open.\n\n**Qualification and publication:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest prerelease, built from immutable source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and was last updated 2026-10-27 18:47 UTC; no custodian acceptance or compatible sealed held-out corpus is recorded, and no held-out payload has been accessed. T2/T3/T4, evaluator custody/host acceptance, remaining live provider and standalone gates, qualification of a candidate built from current source, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. The five-terminal by three-size matrix remains **0/15 formally recorded cell verdicts**, with no screenshots. The operator reports successful rendering at tested sizes but a 43×13 lower limit for tmux inside GNOME Terminal; this is partial observation, not completion of the prescribed matrix. The available `mike-dev` shell is headless, and its configured `ubuntu-desktop` host name does not resolve, so I could not produce real-terminal screenshots or verdicts from this session. Stable publication remains gated on every required acceptance gate.\n\nThe 2026-10-28 00:35 checkpoint below is retained as a historical snapshot; its source and PR-base statements are superseded by this update.\n\n## Historical checkpoint (observed 2026-10-28 00:35 UTC)\n\n**Authoritative source and source checks:** `main` is `1bc63ef471e0fedb3ad4e980cc12e9c303382c69`, the merge commit for PR [#288](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/288). PR #288's exact-head CI [40604512023](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40604512023) passed Node 22, Node 24, and Linux packaging/reproducibility/smoke; CodeQL [40604512234](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40604512234) and JavaScript/TypeScript also passed. The exact PR jobs passed `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` and `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs`. Post-merge CI [40608989828](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40608989828) is still running Node 22 and Node 24 on `1bc63ef`; post-merge CodeQL [40608989717](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40608989717) passed. The earlier run on base `171fca4` had one Node 22 failure in `tui_diff_e2e` (review navigation expected edit 1, observed edit 3); Node 24 passed there, and the exact PR #288 candidate passed all three test matrices. The exact post-merge CI run is the next source-level confirmation. These source checks are not installed-RC acceptance.\n\n**RC10 E2 archive repair:** PR #288 restored the 21 retained log files whose entries were already present in the archive manifest, corrected the evidence README's attestation and lifecycle disclosures, and updated `SHA256SUMS`. On the merged candidate, all 45 manifest entries passed `sha256sum -c`; Gitleaks found no leaks; the exact diff received independent ACCEPT. This review accepted the archive repair and factual README corrections only. It did not accept the RC10 E2 product qualification or turn the historical logs into new test results.\n\n**RC10 E2 limits:** The archive still does not demonstrate a successful ordinary `nexus upgrade` from alpha.2 to RC10, successful provenance-attestation verification, power-loss recovery, or an explicit staging-directory-cleanup assertion. The recorded updater process-death recovery is not a power-loss test. E2 acceptance remains open.\n\n**Other integration PRs:** PRs [#285](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/285), [#286](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/286), [#287](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/287), and [#289](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/289) remain open on base `171fca4cfa61e695441e4be83e6ae30f19a8005c`, which predates this merge. Their owners must rebase and rerun exact-head checks before integration.\n\n**Qualification and publication:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest release and is still a prerelease; its immutable source is `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`. No stable `v1.0.0` exists. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open without an independent custodian acceptance or a compatible sealed held-out corpus; no held-out payload has been accessed. T2/T3/T4, evaluator custody/host acceptance, remaining live provider and standalone gates, qualification of a candidate built from current source, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. The required five-terminal by three-size matrix has **0/15 formally recorded cell verdicts** and no screenshots. The operator reports that the client rendered at the sizes tried, but tmux inside GNOME Terminal could not be reduced below 43×13; this does not establish every prescribed interaction or matrix cell. Stable publication remains gated on all required acceptance gates.\n\nThe 2026-10-27 22:55 checkpoint below is retained as a historical snapshot; its archive-incomplete and pre-PR #288 statements are superseded by this update.\n\n## Historical checkpoint (observed 2026-10-27 22:55 UTC)\n\n**Authoritative source and checks:** `origin/main` is `7ddce16a900d2da9def27d53722243bf4df2de07`, merging PR #284 atop PR #283 and earlier RC10 fixes. Post-merge CI [40593091251](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40593091251) completed successfully on this exact SHA: Node 22, Node 24, and Linux packaging/reproducibility/smoke jobs passed. CodeQL [40593091302](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40593091302) also passed. On the refreshed readiness worktree, requirements enforcement passed (123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification), and version synchronization confirms every component remains `1.0.0-rc.10`. These are source checks, not installed-RC acceptance.\n\n**RC10 reproducibility scope:** PR [#281](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/281) recorded the successful exact-tag run [40564959805](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40564959805); PR [#282](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/282) clarified that the comparison established byte identity for the six listed release artifacts across Ubuntu 22.04/24.04 and against the published RC10. It does not claim byte identity for every build output. This evidence is bound to immutable RC10 source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`; any successor source needs its own exact-tag reproducibility run.\n\n**RC10 E2 evidence:** PR [#283](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/283) reports 20/20 fresh-install, doctor and Node-preflight cells: eight positive cells across Ubuntu 22.04/24.04, Debian 12 and Fedora 40 with Node 22/24, plus twelve negative preflight cells for absent Node or Node 12/20. However, independent review of merged head `71a4218` returned CHANGES_REQUIRED, and I confirmed the evidence archive is incomplete: 21 of 34 `SHA256SUMS` entries are missing, including all listed per-cell logs; `prepared-images.json` contains cell/image/id but not the distro and Node metadata claimed by the README; and the positive-cell script sets `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=0` without documenting that limitation. Treat the matrix as a recorded result, not independently accepted E2 evidence, until the archive and claims are corrected and reviewed. The single Ubuntu 22.04/Node 22 lifecycle script re-runs the installer for alpha.2→RC10, rollback, reinstall and repair; it does not exercise `nexus upgrade` or the separate self-test-failure, crash-recovery and backup-restore acceptance rows. Other lifecycle cases and platforms remain open. All evidence applies only to installed RC10.\n\n**PR #284 lifecycle follow-up:** PR [#284](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/284) added RC10 checksum-tamper, failed-self-test, backup-restore and updater-process-crash scripts and logs, then merged at `7ddce16a` despite an independent CHANGES_REQUIRED review. Its exact-head CI run [40586513330](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40586513330) passed Node 22, Node 24, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL. The independent review found the updated checksum index still has 21 missing files out of 45; the earlier lifecycle path still does not test successful `nexus upgrade`; the `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=0` bypass is not clearly disclosed; and the process-crash script does not verify the claimed staging cleanup. The merged code therefore does not close the E2 archive or lifecycle evidence gaps. Its process-death recovery result explicitly does not test power loss. The post-merge main CI and CodeQL runs subsequently passed on `7ddce16a`.\n\n**Readiness PR #268:** Its remote head remains `eac6cdb452726368d37a8ca373b56c688e0274da` on the older base `fc582c66`; its exact-head Node 22, Node 24, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL checks all passed on that older candidate. The refreshed local readiness candidate `a3bb9e59e56e08de66ea5b7eaf682ce408b2e57f` includes current main `7ddce16a` and received independent ACCEPT from `rc5_candidate_review` against that exact base. Exact-main CI and CodeQL are green, but the refreshed candidate has not been pushed and therefore has no exact-head hosted checks. No merge is claimed.\n\n**Qualification and publication:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the newest prerelease on source `16ee8ca`; stable `v1.0.0` is unpublished. Held-out custody acceptance and compatible frozen T2 data remain unresolved (issue #1 is open with no custodian response); T2/T3/T4, evaluator-host acceptance, the remaining live provider and standalone gates, and independent exact-RC acceptance are incomplete. The human five-environment by three-size terminal matrix remains **0/15**, pending the operator; no per-cell verdict or evidence is recorded. Keep stable publication gated on every required acceptance gate.\n\nThe 19:22 and earlier checkpoints below remain historical snapshots and are superseded for current source, evidence, PR, CI and acceptance status by this checkpoint.\n\n## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-27 19:22 UTC)\n\n**Authoritative source and checks:** `origin/main` is `fc582c66bf70e00938eedc0ce3cafc635f582540`, merging PR #279 after #278 and #277. Post-merge CI [40566591904](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40566591904) is running Node 22 and Node 24 on that exact SHA; CodeQL [40566591883](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40566591883) passed. Exact-main CI and CodeQL also passed on parent `cf05322` (runs [40561348972](https://github.com/mikeholow