quirements.mjs --enforce` (123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 exact-RC deferrals) and `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check --tag v1.0.0-rc.10`. The first requirements invocation on the documentation-dirty readiness worktree was correctly refused by its clean-worktree preflight and is not treated as a gate result. The existing [RC10 OpenRouter evidence bundle](../reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/openrouter-live-task/README.md) establishes a pinned provider verification and one passing synthetic small task; this does not establish the broader provider/standalone matrix. Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains an unaccepted prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` is listed. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open without independent custodian acceptance. T2/T3/T4, evaluator custody/host acceptance, remaining provider/standalone profiles, cross-runner exact-RC reproducibility, independent exact-RC acceptance, and scripted terminal gates remain incomplete.\n\n**Human terminal acceptance:** The five-terminal by three-size matrix remains **0/15**. The operator cannot run the requested xterm 80×24 cell now; no cell result or screenshots are inferred. The prepared Ubuntu/GNOME host and worksheet remain available for a later genuine operator run. Scripted PTY evidence does not replace the human matrix. Publication remains gated on all mandatory acceptance gates.\n\nThe 15:12 and earlier checkpoints below are retained as historical evidence and superseded for current source, PR, and CI status by this checkpoint.\n\n\n## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-27 15:12 UTC)\n\n**Authoritative source and CI:** `origin/main` is `3b7af5d3cd46ab1b83e9c8df9862e09cee22b1a7`, integrating PRs [#269](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/269) and [#270](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/270) after #271 and #272. Exact-main CI [40521505143](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/405215051