nvergence follows `origin/main` at `8d71e1a9207bf05baa54aa6bdfa121697469c9eb`, PR #328's merge. `origin/v1/integration` remains at `7d6673f108316dda015b858c85b2abe20f3a4f78` and is not the current release tip. Main CI run [40940653473](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40940653473) and CodeQL run [40940653572](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40940653572) are in progress on exact `8d71e1a`; Node 22/24 are building the release core. Earlier green results on `fe1c91d` are not evidence for this new main SHA.\n- **Source gates:** On a clean worktree at exact `8d71e1a`, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed: 123 rows, 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; the 12 exact-RC qualification deferrals remain unchanged. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` passed with all components at `1.0.0-rc.11`. These are source-stage results only.\n- **PR #318 evaluator remediation:** The pushed PR head is `eec83d6703ce5449ae868d67d1e3c906e7d3d00a`; focused `eval_integrity` and `eval_hardened` tests passed 48/48 after clean `npm ci`, CLI build, Rust release-core build, and isolated HOME/XDG/TMPDIR. No held-out tasks were used. Exact-head CI run [40940623810](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40940623810) is still running Node 22/24; CodeQL and JavaScript/TypeScript checks passed. The PR must be rebased onto `8d71e1a` and pass fresh exact-head review/checks before integration.\n- **Terminal gates:** DEC-20 waives only the manual §5.3 matrix; it is waived, not passed, and no manual cells are required. Automated CI PTY §5.1 and installed-RC scripted PTY §5.2 remain mandatory. The latest public release is RC10; its scripted PTY record is `PARTIAL_NOT_ACCEPTED`, including a 27.89-second cancellation-idle outlier. No accepted §5.2 result exists for an RC11 artifact because RC11 has not been published.\n- **Held-out custody:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned; its latest public update reports T2 at 20/40 tasks and no fresh custody acceptance. T3's reported 8/8 is digest/schema/isolation metadata, not qualification acceptance. Public records identify the prior custodian only as the `opencode` primary session; they do not identify a human custodian. SageBridge was named as a contact, but no new custody acceptance is recorded. No private payload was accessed or run.\n- **PR and release state:** PR #328 is merged. PR #318 remains open and pending refreshed exact-head CI. PR #327 remains open; Node 22/24, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL passed, while Entire Gates failed. Public releases still end at `v1.0.0-rc.10`; RC11 and stable `v1.0.0` are unpublished. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; provider and standalone matrices, held-out T2/T3/T4, cross-runner reproducibility, long-task/fault-injection, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete.\n- **Next executable steps:** Let the current-main and PR #318 CI runs finish; rebase PR #318 onto `8d71e1a`, obtain fresh exact-head review/checks, and integrate through the normal process. Continue the custodian handoff without exposing private material. Construct the next RC only after pre-RC gates pass, then execute all mandatory exact-RC gates, including §5.1 and §5.2, followed by independent acceptance.\n\n## Historical checkpoint (observed 2026-10-29 06:18 UTC; superseded for terminal disposition by DEC-20 above)\n\n**Authoritative source and CI:** `origin/main` is `a0356c4d8f0f0b9b943d4033aff59795fcab83b4`, merging PR #319 atop `6b786d54dd5bf60234c67fec6ef070c62af9b141`. `origin/v1/integration` remains at `7d6673f108316dda015b858c85b2abe20f3a4f78`, an ancestor of main. Pre-merge main CodeQL run [40822684525](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40822684525) and CI run [40822684551](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40822684551) passed on `6b786d54`. Post-merge CI [40828157972](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40828157972) and CodeQL [40828157982](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40828157982) are in progress on exact main `a0356c4d8f0f0b9b943d4033aff59795fcab83b4`.\n\n**Requirements and version:** On exact `origin/main` `a0356c4d8f0f0b9b943d4033aff59795fcab83b4`, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed: 123 rows, 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 remain deferred to exact-RC qualification: REQ-AGT-002, REQ-AGT-010, REQ-PRV-003, REQ-REL-003, REQ-REL-005, REQ-AGT-110, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-REL-114, REQ-QUAL-101, REQ-QUAL-107, REQ-QUAL-108 and REQ-QUAL-109. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` passes at `1.0.0-rc.10`. These are source-stage checks, not installed-RC acceptance.\n\n**Open source changes:** PR [#319](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/319), head `668721d8135d3a3332bca27b820caa5a4a76c7af`, merged as `a0356c4d8f0f0b9b943d4033aff59795fcab83b4` after its independent `ACCEPT` review and required Node 22/24/Linux, JS/TS, and CodeQL checks passed. Its post-merge CI and CodeQL checks are running. PR [#318](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/318), head `2c532d701c5b84b0d3308b02897520337addc36b`, has independent `ACCEPT` source review, but both Node matrix jobs failed because `eval_hardened.test.ts` could not find `go` while testing hidden-source isolation (exit 127); Linux was skipped. This is a CI toolchain-provisioning gap, not evaluator qualification evidence. PR [#322](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/322), head `d53caea7c480c5e88dff43c6e5d4cb8a16868400`, adds CI-only pinned Go/Rust toolchain provisioning and has independent `ACCEPT` review; its Node 22/24, JS/TS, and CodeQL checks pass, with Linux still running. PR [#320](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/320), head `2124538d21b84454319c5485140b266f11510a5a`, has independent `ACCEPT` review and passing Node 22/24, JS/TS, and CodeQL checks; Linux remains in progress. PR [#321](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/321) refreshes this checkpoint and has been rebased onto the new main; the previous head's checks do not qualify the rebased candidate, which requires fresh exact-head checks and independent review. None of PRs #318, #320, #321 or #322 is merged.\n\n**Held-out custody and qualification:** The latest public metadata update on issue #1 (06:02 UTC) records unresolved custody ownership: a historical ha…13240 tokens truncated…s an unaccepted prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` is listed. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open without independent custodian acceptance. T2/T3/T4, evaluator custody/host acceptance, remaining provider/standalone profiles, cross-runner exact-RC reproducibility, independent exact-RC acceptance, and scripted terminal gates remain incomplete.\n\n**Human terminal acceptance:** The five-terminal by three-size matrix remains **0/15**. The operator cannot run the requested xterm 80×24 cell now; no cell result or screenshots are inferred. The prepared Ubuntu/GNOME host and worksheet remain available for a later genuine operator run. Scripted PTY evidence does not replace the human matrix. Publication remains gated on all mandatory acceptance gates.\n\nThe 15:12 and earlier checkpoints below are retained as historical evidence and superseded for current source, PR, and CI status by this checkpoint.\n\n\n## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-27 15:12 UTC)\n\n**Authoritative source and CI:** `origin/main` is `3b7af5d3cd46ab1b83e9c8df9862e09cee22b1a7`, integrating PRs [#269](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/269) and [#270](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/270) after #271 and #272. Exact-main CI [40521505143](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40521505143) and CodeQL [40521505001](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40521505001) both passed on `3b7af5d`; CI passed Node 22, Node 24, Linux tests, security gates, packaging, reproducibility, package smoke, and installer smoke. PR #269 merge-commit CI [40519862728](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40519862728) passed on `f059770`. These runs establish CI for their exact commits, not the RC10 release gates.\n\n**Readiness PR #268:** The owner refreshed PR [#268](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/268) onto `main`; GitHub shows it open and mergeable at head `98f87bee6ca112e6d50f6fb2bc480fc47723c648`, based on `3b7af5d3cd46ab1b83e9c8df9862e09cee22b1a7`. Its Node 22, Node 24, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL checks pass; Linux packaging/reproducibility run [40524245685](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40524245685) is still pending. The 14:38 checkpoint update was independently accepted (diff SHA-256 `c8cf46163cd8be8666ea86e8a95a7483588e10aa3e8775fbfa213ce55895d41e`). The current local follow-up records terminal main and #269 CI plus the latest PR state; it has not been pushed, and no PR merge is claimed.\n\n**Merged hook remediations and residual:** PRs #269 (retention shell/hook execution) and #270 (checkpoint Git hooks) are merged at `f059770` and `3b7af5d`; both now have passing exact-merge CI. The merged implementation passes `core.hooksPath=/dev/null` to relevant Git commands. Configured `reference-transaction` hooks may remain callable despite that setting; this was independently reproduced and accepted on a local follow-up to #269 (`d349068`), whose focused tests passed 17/17 on Git 2.54.0 and Git 2.43.0 plus `tsc --noEmit`. That follow-up is not on current main or the merged #269 head and needs a separately refreshed fix and exact-head validation; its source and test files are currently claimed by another agent.\n\n**Qualification and publication:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains a prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` is listed. The human five-terminal by three-size matrix remains **0/15** and pending. The user's informal observation is that rendering works at tested sizes except tmux in GNOME Terminal, where the smallest usable size is 43×13; there are no per-cell records or screenshots, so human acceptance is not established. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open, last updated 2026-10-26 17:37:53 UTC, with no custodian acceptance. T2/T3/T4, evaluator custody and host acceptance, live provider/standalone, independent exact-RC, scripted terminal, and human acceptance gates remain incomplete. Publication authorization remains gated on every required acceptance gate.\n\nThe 14:38, 13:56 and earlier checkpoints below are retained as historical evidence and superseded for current source, PR, and CI status by this checkpoint.\n\n## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-27 12:46 UTC)\n\n**Authoritative source and post-merge CI:** `origin/main` is `1d9357ee63b1066a891584a898842814de614fbf`, integrating PR [#264](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/264). Its exact-head CI [40499840211](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40499840211) and CodeQL [40499839711](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40499839711) passed before merge. Post-merge CodeQL [40505388849](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40505388849) passed on `1d9357e`; post-merge CI [40505388775](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40505388775) is still running both Node 22 and Node 24 CLI suites. No result is inferred before they finish.\n\n**Readiness PR and local full-suite result:** PR [#268](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/268) remains remotely at `bda6714ff885f2fd4fef736b84ca7005a9cddbdf`, based on `303ea322a7148b4a9d1a8231d7ce1c8f824bbae4`; it is conflicting with current `main` and its old successful checks are stale. The claimed local branch had been refreshed through `bff9f13085368e6cc269b1bb294db5b3b810bd7a`; the updated branch now incorporates `1d9357e` and is awaiting final independent review. No push or merge is claimed.\n\nAn isolated immutable snapshot at `9344df578f8a39a55d82ead0f15c4811864d21f8` built successfully, but `make test` exited 2: 1,769 passed, 2 failed, and 1 was skipped. `eval_integrity.test.ts` observed three OOM kills during this host run, which did not have the dedicated capped workspace mount; the log does not establish that the missing mount caused those kills. `eval_version_probe_storage.test.ts` failed its precondition because `NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT` and `NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_RUNTIME_ROOT` were not configured. `/tmp`, `/var/tmp`, and `/home` were all on the same ext4 device. These are incomplete host-fixture checks, not a passing suite or a demonstrated source regression. The complete output is retained at `/var/tmp/nexus-pr268-make-test-9344df5.log`. Current exact-main hosted CI is still running the full CLI suite with its configured cgroups and capped tmpfs.\n\n**Release and acceptance gates:** Public [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) remains a prerelease; stable `v1.0.0` is unpublished. The human real-terminal matrix remains 0/15; the user's report of rendering at 43×13 in tmux on GNOME Terminal is not the full matrix and had no captured screenshots. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains OPEN, last updated 2026-10-26 17:37:53 UTC, with no recorded custodian acceptance. T2/T3/T4, live provider/standalone, independent exact-RC, and human acceptance gates remain incomplete. Publication authorization remains gated on all required acceptance.\n\nThe 12:42 checkpoint immediately below is retained as historical evidence and superseded for current branch, CI, and test status by this checkpoint.\n\n## Historical terminal cancellation checkpoint (observed 2026-10-27 02:11 UTC)\n\nFive targeted synthetic installed-RC10 cancellation rechecks at `TERM=dumb`, 100×30 completed with Esc delays from 0 to 1 second; idle return measured 0.405–0.507 s