{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T09:28:18.940Z","ordinal":526500,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0db389702a7164cc016ae4633225a4819f869eced80ff21d1d","status":"completed","call_id":"call_ac2c1ed18a354f9dbf702bad782bbaf4","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"nl -ba docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | sed -n '55,160p'; nl -ba docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | sed -n '285,365p'; nl -ba docs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md | sed -n '1,180p'\",workdir:\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/prerc14-enforce-16eeb6ee\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:7000}); text(r.output)\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18c20-aec5-7552-93bd-755d714c245e","create_time":1793352498.1489694}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T09:28:19.009Z","ordinal":526501,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18c20-aec5-7552-93bd-755d714c245e","session_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","root_turn_id":"01a18c20-aec5-7552-93bd-755d714c245e","response_id":"resp_0db389702a7164cc016ae463311c98819fbed2ffb141dc3c4a","usage":{"input_tokens":210023,"cached_input_tokens":209536,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":186,"reasoning_output_tokens":50,"total_tokens":210209},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":2878942,"cached_input_tokens":2867712,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":4199,"reasoning_output_tokens":2486,"total_tokens":2883141},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":9931690950,"cached_input_tokens":9826884352,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":28467818,"reasoning_output_tokens":16738726,"total_tokens":9960158768}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T09:28:20.135Z","ordinal":526502,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18c20-aec5-7552-93bd-755d714c245e","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-9e4e3153-1b71-4923-9455-e721cc980088","process_id":"45748","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","nl -ba docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | sed -n '55,160p'; nl -ba docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | sed -n '285,365p'; nl -ba docs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md | sed -n '1,180p'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/prerc14-enforce-16eeb6ee","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"nl -ba docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md","name":"ACCEPTANCE.md","path":"docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"nl -ba docs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md","name":"ROADMAP.md","path":"docs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"    55\t<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:START -->\n    56\t### Approved exact-RC qualification exceptions\n    57\t\n    58\t| Requirement | Approved decision | Scope |\n    59\t|---|---|---|\n    60\t<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:END -->\n    61\t\n    62\t## 1. Rules\n    63\t\n    64\t1. The RC is built and published by the release workflow from a clean tag. Its version is identical across all components (REQ-REL-103).\n    65\t2. All qualification runs use the **installed RC package**, installed with the documented one-line command. They never use a checkout build. The only exception is CI unit and PTY suites, which run from source at the same commit.\n    66\t3. Thresholds (DEC-05) are frozen before the first M5 run. A failing gate is fixed in code and the run is repeated as `rc.N+1`. A threshold is never relaxed after results are known.\n    67\t4. Evidence goes to `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`. The directory contains:\n    68\t   - `manifest.json`: commit, package sha256, environment, model fingerprint, dates;\n    69\t   - raw outputs;\n    70\t   - a `SHA256SUMS` file.\n    71\t\n    72\t   Secrets are redacted before commit.\n    73\t5. Any step that cannot run in the available environment is recorded as **NOT RUN** with its reason. A NOT RUN on a blocker gate fails the gate.\n    74\t\n    75\t## 2. Environments\n    76\t\n    77\t| ID | Environment | Used for |\n    78\t|---|---|---|\n    79\t| E1 | GitHub Actions: ubuntu-22.04 and ubuntu-24.04; Node 22 and 24; pinned Rust | Unit, integration and PTY suites; packaging; reproducibility |\n    80\t| E2 | Docker clean images: ubuntu:22.04, ubuntu:24.04, debian:12, fedora:40. Each with no Node, then with Node 20, Node 22 and Node 24. Non-root user. | Installer, upgrade, rollback, uninstall, platform failure messages |\n    81\t| E3 | Operator dev box: Linux x86-64, real terminals (xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal) | Terminal matrix, live sessions |\n    82\t| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\n    83\t| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\n    84\t\n    85\t## 3. Gate checklist (G0–G4: automated acceptance IDs)\n    86\t\n    87\tEvery ACC ID below is defined in the linked spec. The plan for each spec names the test that implements it. Run each check at the lifecycle stage dictated by its acceptance method in §1.1: source-applicable checks before the RC tag; checks requiring the RC archive, attestation, release, or installed package after RC construction; environment-specific checks in their declared environment. Bind every result to the exact source commit and, when artifact-dependent, the RC package digest. A source test or local build does not replace an artifact-bound check, and no G0–G4 ID is complete until all of its applicable checks pass.\n    88\t\n    89\t| Gate | Acceptance IDs | Spec |\n    90\t|---|---|---|\n    91\t| Safety | ACC-SAFE-01 to ACC-SAFE-10 | SPEC-01 |\n    92\t| Process ownership | ACC-PROC-01 to ACC-PROC-08 (ACC-PROC-07 is the load test, run in E3) | SPEC-02 |\n    93\t| Untrusted inputs | ACC-TRUST-01 to ACC-TRUST-09 | SPEC-03 |\n    94\t| Continuity | ACC-CONT-01 to ACC-CONT-09 (ACC-CONT-10 is in §8) | SPEC-04 |\n    95\t| Inference | ACC-INF-01 to ACC-INF-09 (ACC-INF-10 is in §4) | SPEC-05 |\n    96\t| Packaging | ACC-PKG-01 to ACC-PKG-09 | SPEC-06 |\n    97\t| Supply chain | ACC-SUP-01 to ACC-SUP-08 (artifact-bound ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08 after RC construction) | SPEC-07 |\n    98\t| Persistence | ACC-PER-01 to ACC-PER-07 | SPEC-08 |\n    99\t| Governance | ACC-GOV-01 to ACC-GOV-06 | SPEC-09 |\n   100\t| Verification | ACC-VER-01 to ACC-VER-09 | SPEC-11 |\n   101\t| Upgrade | ACC-UPG-01 to ACC-UPG-14 | SPEC-12 |\n   102\t\n   103\t\n   104\t### 3.1 Acceptance IDs defined in this file\n   105\t\n   106\tThese are retained commitments from REQUIREMENTS §2 and cross-cutting checks.\n   107\t\n   108\t| ID | Check | Pass condition |\n   109\t|---|---|---|\n   110\t| ACC-TUI-STEER | PTY: submit a task; while a tool runs, type steering text and press Enter; also queue a steer before a cancel | Steering is applied at the next step boundary. Unapplied steering is returned to the composer. Nothing is dropped silently (existing `sidecar_steering_diff` plus PTY s6). |\n   111\t| ACC-TUI-A11Y | PTY with `NO_COLOR=1` and with `TERM=dumb` at 40×14 and 100×30 | Zero colour SGR codes. Every state is distinguishable by glyph and word. Hints are complete at 40 columns (TUI-10). |\n   112\t| ACC-SEC-JAIL | `core/tests` plus harness-core calls with `..`, absolute, symlinked-file, symlinked-dir and symlinked-parent payloads | Every one is refused (C §4 R1 set). |\n   113\t| ACC-SEC-B6 | Re-run `docs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/repro/zz_trust_repro.test.ts`. Seeded-secret scan of `~/.nexus` and `.nexus` after a scripted turn. | Zero plaintext seeded secrets in durable stores or outbound bodies. |\n   114\t| ACC-PRV-LIVE | `nexus providers verify --provider <p> -m <pinned model> -j` for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06) | `passed: true`. Receipts archived. |\n   115\t| ACC-PRV-STANDALONE | §4.2 on the installed RC through the approved stripped proxy, with gateway credentials absent from the child environment | Every required profile completes through the proxy and the absent-gateway boundary holds; receipts archived. |\n   116\t| ACC-PLAT | E2 matrix, §7 | All rows pass. |\n   117\t| ACC-QUAL-T2 | §6.1 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n   118\t| ACC-QUAL-T3 | §6.3 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n   119\t| ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n   120\t| ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\n   121\t| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five terminal environments and three sizes | Waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20. No manual-cell execution or evidence is required, and no result is inferred. Automated §5.1 and scripted PTY §5.2 remain mandatory. |\n   122\t\n   123\t## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\n   124\t\n   125\t### 4.1 Clean-HOME procedure\n   126\t\n   127\t1. `export HOME=$(mktemp -d)`.\n   128\t2. Install the RC with the documented command.\n   129\t3. Create `~/.config/nexus/config.env` containing only:\n   130\t   - `LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:<proxy>/v1`\n   131\t   - `LOCAL_LLM_MODEL=<id as listed by the proxy>`\n   132\t   - `LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY=REDACTED\n   133\t\n   134\t   No gateway token file, no homelab paths, no `NODE_*` overrides.\n   135\t4. Start `node eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs --upstream <gateway> --token-file <operator token> [--emulate <kind>]`. The gateway token stays with the proxy and never reaches the Nexus HOME.\n   136\t5. Run `nexus doctor --json` and archive it. It must report the server kind and context source with no `gateway` capability.\n   137\t\n   138\t### 4.2 Standalone matrix\n   139\t\n   140\t| Profile | What Nexus sees | Runs | Pass condition |\n   141\t|---|---|---|---|\n   142\t| P-plain | Bare OpenAI-compatible `/models` and chat. No tokenize, no capacity headers. | Standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 held-out tasks) × 3 runs; T4 classes 1, 3, 4, 7 × 3 | T2 correctness ≥ (gateway-direct T2 correctness on the same tasks − 10 pts). False VERIFIED = 0. T4 truthful = 100%. Context source reported as `client_default` or an operator override, with no error. |\n   143\t| P-llamacpp | Emulated llama.cpp `/props` and overflow body | Same tasks × 1 run; plus the forced-overflow case (context limit set to 8k) | Context discovered from `/props`. Overflow gives one compact-and-retry, then success or an actionable error. |\n   144\t| P-vllm | Emulated `max_model_len` and vLLM overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `max_model_len` |\n   145\t| P-ollama | Emulated `/api/show` and Ollama overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `ollama_show` |\n   146\t| Conformance | CI fixtures for llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio and Ollama shapes | CI | All pass (ACC-INF-01, -02, -05) |\n   147\t\n   148\tACC-INF-10 passes only when every row passes. The release notes state the scope in the form required by DEC-16.\n   149\t\n   150\t### 4.3 Provider matrix (E5)\n   151\t\n   152\t| Provider | Tier (DEC-06) | Required for v1.0.0 |\n   153\t|---|---|---|\n   154\t| OpenRouter, pinned model | Supported | `providers verify` PASS, plus one live small task (a §6-style bug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\n   155\t| ChatGPT sign-in | Experimental | Verify PASS recorded (already PASS at db1ca55; repeat on the RC) |\n   156\t| OpenAI API key, Anthropic | Experimental unless keys are added | If promoted: verify PASS plus one live task. Otherwise NOT RUN, and they are labelled experimental. |\n   157\t| Copilot | Experimental | Not required |\n   158\t\n   159\t## 5. Terminal acceptance (REQ-QUAL-108)\n   160\t\n   285\t| Backup restore | `nexus upgrade --restore-backup <state-backup-directory>` | Snapshot of configuration and complete durable state restored from a recognized private backup directory (`backup.json`, `state/`, optional `config/`), with strict 0600 file / 0700 directory modes. A canonical `config.env.bak.*` path restores configuration only. Arbitrary files and tar archives are rejected. Run it through the stable `nexus` launcher; close existing legacy clients, then keep version-pinned legacy binaries and direct old entry points offline until the durable restore journal is cleared. |\n   286\t| Incompatible downgrade | `nexus upgrade --version <v> --allow-downgrade` (incompatible state schema) | Refused fail-closed with actionable state schema explanation. Existing installation unchanged. |\n   287\t\n   288\t## 8. Independent acceptance (REQ-AGT-110, ACC-CONT-10)\n   289\t\n   290\tThe reviewer is supplied by the owner (X5) and did not implement the work under review.\n   291\t\n   292\tThe reviewer receives:\n   293\t\n   294\t- the RC package;\n   295\t- this file;\n   296\t- the REQUIREMENTS ledger;\n   297\t- SPEC-04;\n   298\t- read access to the evidence directory.\n   299\t\n   300\tThe reviewer performs:\n   301\t\n   302\t1. An independent re-run of a sample. At minimum:\n   303\t   - ACC-SAFE-01, 03, 09;\n   304\t   - ACC-PROC-02;\n   305\t   - ACC-TRUST-01, 02;\n   306\t   - ACC-CONT-01, 03;\n   307\t   - ACC-VER-01, 03;\n   308\t   - ACC-PKG-01;\n   309\t   - 5 random T2 tasks;\n   310\t   - 2 T4 classes.\n   311\t2. One live long task (≥ 60 steps, ≥ 2 compactions) on the RC through the gateway, including one kill and resume.\n   312\t3. A review of the scorer verdict and of contamination handling.\n   313\t\n   314\t**Output:** `docs/reviews/<date>-v1-rc-independent-acceptance.md` with an ACCEPT, ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS, or REJECT verdict per area. \"Accept with defects\" needs an owner disposition for every defect, and for a blocker area the only acceptable disposition is a fix.\n   315\t\n   316\t## 9. Contest (separate product; not a client gate)\n   317\t\n   318\tThe contest submission is complete and judging has concluded. No contest freeze applies (DEC-13 status amendment); post-contest hardening is tracked separately from client v1.0.0 acceptance and is accepted by:\n   319\t\n   320\t| ID | Check |\n   321\t|---|---|\n   322\t| CON-A1 | Ordinary maintained package/experiment checks build `agent-collab-worker`. `worker.config.json` has the configured name, and the bundle contains the `/work-state` handler. Do not restore the retired `cloudflare-contest-contract` status check. |\n   323\t| CON-A2 | Broker negative tests: caller-supplied env paths and URLs are ignored. A host outside `*.artifacts.cloudflare.net` is refused. |\n   324\t| CON-A3 | On a clean VM, `install.sh --fresh` followed by `post-install-qualify.py` passes. |\n   325\t| CON-A4 | `sudo -l` for the demo user shows only fixed argv. `sudo setpriv --reuid=0 id` is denied. |\n   326\t| CON-A5 | One clean-account `--mode cloudflare --agents real` run, with a committed, redacted run record. |\n   327\t| CON-A6 | The video source commits are tagged and published, or the docs state that they are unpublished. |\n   328\t\n   329\t## 10. Release decision (G6)\n   330\t\n   331\tG6 passes only when every item below holds. It authorizes a version-only stable commit from the accepted RC source, followed by its source checks, stable tag, and unpublished draft candidate; it does not authorize making stable assets publicly available. RC tags are candidate construction inputs governed by §1.1; an RC tag or its successful build does not satisfy this release decision.\n   332\t\n   333\t- [ ] G0–G4 automated gates pass on the final RC commit (§3).\n   334\t- [ ] RC artifact gates pass on the workflow-produced RC, including ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08; record the exact source commit, workflow run, and artifact digest.\n   335\t- [ ] §4 standalone and provider matrix: all rows PASS.\n   336\t- [ ] §5 terminal acceptance: automated CI (§5.1) and scripted PTY (§5.2) gates PASS. The manual 5×3 matrix (§5.3) is waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20.\n   337\t- [ ] §6 thresholds: all hold.\n   338\t- [ ] §7 install matrix: all rows PASS.\n   339\t- [ ] §8 independent acceptance: ACCEPT, or ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS with owner dispositions and no blocker defects outstanding.\n   340\t- [ ] The pre-RC source gate passes from a clean source worktree: `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce`. Every B/RR source row outside the §1.1 qualification-only map must be ≥ `tested`. A mapped row below `tested` is reported as deferred; this result does not accept or qualify it.\n   341\t- [ ] The exact-RC evidence gate passes from the clean RC worktree and is bound to the exact RC source commit and installed RC artifact. Run the checker with the custodian-approved, immutable qualification record and evidence directory:\n   342\t  `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce --qualification-record <record.json> --rc-artifact <installed-rc-package> --evidence-root <evidence-directory>`.\n   343\t  The version 1 record contains `sourceCommit` (full commit ID), `rcTag` (for example `v1.0.0-rc.1`), `artifactSha256`, `artifactProvenance` (`sourceCommit`, `artifactSha256`, and a hashed provenance report), `independentAcceptance` (`disposition`, `reviewer`, `implementers`, zero `blockingDefects`, and a hashed report reference), and one `requirements` entry for every B/RR row. For `ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS`, include each non-blocking defect with its owner disposition; unresolved or blocking defects fail. Each requirement entry records its status and one or more hashed evidence files covering the exact criteria required by the ledger and the §1.1 qualification-only map. Every criterion evidence file must be a JSON object with top-level `sourceCommit`, `rcTag`, and `artifactSha256` values exactly matching the validated qualification record, current RC source commit, and installed RC artifact. A digest-valid report copied from another source revision, RC tag, or artifact is rejected. A B row recorded as `tested` also needs a non-empty `qualificationNotApplicable.reason` and a `qualificationNotApplicable.decision` matching the approved per-requirement exception table and a matching applicability declaration in DECISIONS.md; an unrelated or record-supplied decision is rejected. Evidence paths must be relative regular files under the evidence root, with no symlinks. Missing, unknown, stale, mismatched, or incomplete evidence fails the gate. The checker requires a clean worktree, rejects `--ledger` overrides, enforces source-ledger thresholds outside the explicit §1.1 lifecycle rows, and requires the exact-RC record itself to meet the normal status threshold for every row. It never mutates the source ledger or relaxes a requirement's B/RR record threshold. The checker validates source/tag/artifact identity bindings and evidence hashes; it does not authenticate the reviewer or prove that the artifact was built from the source commit. The approved release workflow must independently verify build provenance/attestation, and the designated custodian and independent reviewer must verify their respective approvals and custody evidence.\n   344\t- [ ] Docs checklist (SPEC-09 §3.2) is signed off.\n   345\t- [ ] Release notes state the standalone scope (DEC-16), the provider tiers (DEC-06), the experimental surfaces (DEC-03, DEC-07) and the known limitations.\n   346\t- [ ] Owner approval to publish (X7).\n   347\t\n   348\tAfter G6, complete source checks on the exact stable-version commit before tagging, then complete the stable artifact checks in §1.1 stage 5 before publishing the draft. A failure keeps publication blocked and requires remediation plus the applicable requalification; do not mark the campaign released until published artifacts are independently verified.\n   349\t\n   350\t**Outcome recording.** The release decision record goes in `docs/releases/v1.0.0.md`, with links to every evidence directory.\n     1\t# Roadmap: Nexus Code to v1.0.0\n     2\t\n     3\tThe starting point is `db1ca55` (`v0.1.0-alpha.2` + docs), which has 31 blocker requirements open (REQUIREMENTS §3). The roadmap is ordered by dependency, and every milestone ends at a gate defined in [ACCEPTANCE.md](ACCEPTANCE.md). There are no delivery dates; effort is given as ranges, with the assumptions stated.\n     4\t\n     5\t## Assumptions behind the estimates\n     6\t\n     7\t- **People.** One implementer working with agent assistance, as in this repository's history. An engineer-day (ed) means one focused day of implementation, review and test for that person.\n     8\t- **Inference.** Inference comes only from the homelab gateway (DEC-16): one model host, with runs serialised.\n     9\t- **Uncertainty.** The largest unknown is how many fix loops M5 qualification triggers. The pilot's history suggests at least one.\n    10\t- **Supporting labour.** Held-out tasks are written by an agent author (authorised, DEC-05). Independent acceptance is done by a reviewer the owner provides (X5).\n    11\t\n    12\t## Milestones\n    13\t\n    14\t```\n    15\tM0 Foundation ──► M1 Safety floor ──────────────► M3 Continuity & inference ──► RC1 ──► M5 Qualification ──► M6 Release\n    16\t        │               │                                ▲                                  ▲\n    17\t        │               └──► M2 Product parity & supply chain (parallel) ──────────────────┤\n    18\t        │                                                                                   │\n    19\t        └──► M4 Persistence hygiene (parallel with M2/M3) ──────────────────────────────────┤\n    20\t  (from M1) held-out task authoring, standalone proxy, fixtures (parallel) ─────────────────┘\n    21\t```\n    22\t\n    23\t| Milestone | Scope (plans) | Deliverables | Exit gate | Effort |\n    24\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n    25\t| **M0 Foundation** | PLAN-08 task 1 (test HOME isolation); PLAN-06 task 3 (version sync). Owner action X1 (stale local tags deleted) is already done.; PLAN-09 tasks 1, 2, 5 (ledger checker in report mode, historical banners, cheap doc truth fixes) | Tests never touch the real HOME. One version identity. The ledger is enforced in CI. | **G0**: ACC-PER-03, ACC-PKG-03, ACC-GOV-01/03 | 2–4 ed |\n    26\t| **M1 Safety floor** (critical path) | PLAN-01 (effect classes, DEC-01 posture, verifier gating, REPL approvals, read-only masking, argv sandbox, tripwire); PLAN-02 (process registry, cancel and shutdown sweep, bounds); PLAN-03 (project `.env` allowlist, CIDR locality, SSRF-safe fetch, skills/knowledge trust, plugin directories, EXT-004); PLAN-11 PR-11a/11b (parser, binding) | Untrusted input cannot cause unapproved exec, egress or configuration changes. Stop means stopped. No false VERIFIED from a filename coincidence. | **G1**: all ACC-SAFE, ACC-PROC, ACC-TRUST, ACC-VER-01..04 | 15–25 ed |\n    27\t| **M2 Product parity and supply chain** (parallel with M1 after PLAN-01 PR-1b) | PLAN-06 (unified launcher with the TUI as the packaged default, doc commands, doctor, installer); PLAN-07 (notices, SBOM, provenance, CI matrix, `cli/dist` untracked, SECURITY.md, CHANGELOG); PLAN-12 (CLI and TUI upgrade engine) | The installed product equals the tested product. Compliant release assets. In-place upgrade safely verifies and swaps releases. | **G2**: ACC-PKG-01..09, ACC-SUP-01..07, ACC-UPG-01..06 | 8–14 ed |\n    28\t| **M3 Continuity and inference** | PLAN-04 (resume, durable work units, accounting, error path, stagnation, team semantics); PLAN-05 code tasks (server-kind discovery, compact-and-retry, error bounds, timeouts, parser robustness, receipts, startup probe, decoupling, CA); PLAN-11 PR-11c..e; PLAN-10 harness tasks 1–7, 9, 10, 13 | Resume and compaction never lose state. Standalone sizing works. Eval harness ready. | **G3**: ACC-CONT-01..09, ACC-INF-01..09, ACC-VER-05..09, eval self-tests | 15–25 ed |\n    29\t| **M4 Persistence hygiene** (parallel with M2/M3) | PLAN-08 tasks 2–10 | Private state permissions, retention/GC, corruption reporting, schema policy | **G4**: ACC-PER-01..07 | 5–8 ed |\n    30\t| **RC1** | After PLAN-09 task 7's pre-RC source-ledger reconciliation and enforce gate, tag `v1.0.0-rc.1` (owner approves publishing a prerelease; X7) | RC build installed through the documented command | G0–G4 green on the exact RC source; pre-RC requirements enforcement passed | <1 ed |\n    31\t| **M5 Qualification** | PLAN-10 task 11 (T2 held-out 5×, T3, T4, standalone stripped-proxy profiles, provider verify); task 12 (terminal matrix); ACC-SUP-08 cross-runner reproducibility; independent acceptance (X5) of continuity and of the RC | Qualification evidence archive, scorer verdict table, independent reports | **G5**: ACCEPTANCE §4–§8 all PASS | 10–20 calendar days. About 84 h of serial inference for T2, plus T3/T4/standalone. Excludes fix loops. |\n    32\t| **Fix loop(s)** | Defects found in M5, landed as `rc.N` | Re-run the failed gate subsets, plus regression subsets | G5 | 0–15 ed per loop (unknown) |\n    33\t| **M6 Release** | PLAN-09 task 7 (verify the pre-RC source-ledger reconciliation and enforcement evidence; record exact-RC dispositions in the acceptance record without mutating the accepted RC source); docs sign-off; release notes; tag `v1.0.0` (X7) | Published v1.0.0 with notices, SBOM and attestation | **G6**: ACCEPTANCE §10 checklist | 2–4 ed |\n    34\t\n    35\t**Total implementation:** about 46–78 ed (the sum of M0–M4 and M6). **Qualification:** 2–4 calendar weeks. **Fix loops:** unknown. A plausible range is 0–2 loops.\n    36\t\n    37\t## Critical path\n    38\t\n    39\tThe longest dependency chain is:\n    40\t\n    41\t**M0 → M1 → M3 → RC1 → M5 (T2 held-out runs) → M6**\n    42\t\n    43\t- M1 comes first because the posture change (DEC-01) alters behaviour that every later test, eval and acceptance run depends on. Qualifying before it would have to be redone.\n    44\t- M3 is on the path because resume (AGT-01), work-unit durability (AGT-02a) and standalone sizing (PRV-06) are blockers, and the T4 class 9 test (SIGTERM, then resume) needs them.\n    45\t- M5 is bounded by serial inference on the single gateway host.\n    46\t\n    47\tWhen several agents work at once, the parallel lanes, hot-file serialisation and the single-`GATEWAY` lock in [CONCURRENCY.md](CONCURRENCY.md) govern the order in which work merges.\n    48\t\n    49\tOff the critical path, but must finish before RC1:\n    50\t\n    51\t- M2, M4;\n    52\t- the 40 held-out T2 tasks and 8 T3 tasks (agent-authored), with their manifest sealed **before** RC1;\n    53\t- the stripping proxy and the conformance fixtures.\n    54\t\n    55\t## Release gates\n    56\t\n    57\t| Gate | When | Pass condition |\n    58\t|---|---|---|\n    59\t| G0 | End of M0 | Foundation acceptance IDs pass. `make test` passes on a clean clone and leaves the real HOME untouched. |\n    60\t| G1 | End of M1 | All safety acceptance IDs pass in CI. Existing PTY suites stay green. No new skipped tests. |\n    61\t| G2 | End of M2 | A package smoke run in a PTY shows the TUI. The doc-command test passes. Release dry-run assets are complete. |\n    62\t| G3 | End of M3 | Continuity, inference and verification acceptance IDs pass. The eval harness self-tests pass, including the T4 smoke. |\n    63\t| G4 | End of M4 | Persistence acceptance IDs pass. |\n    64\t| G5 | After the RC | ACCEPTANCE §4–§8 pass. The DEC-05 thresholds are met. Independent reports are filed. |\n    65\t| G6 | Release | The ledger checker passes in enforce mode, so every B/RR row is ≥ tested and B rows are product-qualified where ACCEPTANCE requires it. Docs are signed off. Owner approval X7 is given. |\n    66\t\n    67\t## Classification of the work\n    68\t\n    69\t| Category | Contents |\n    70\t|---|---|\n    71\t| **Release blockers** (31 B rows) | M0–M3 for implementation, M5 for qualification evidence |\n    72\t| **Release-required improvements** (58 RR rows) | Spread across M1–M4; listed in each plan |\n    73\t| **Post-v1** | REQUIREMENTS §5: single step loop, full context provenance, knowledge freshness, `/tdd` and `nexus eval` fixes, cgroups, macOS/arm64, self-uninstall, and others |\n    74\t| **Contest track** | PLAN-C1, after judging. Independent of all gates (DEC-13). |\n    75\t\n    76\t## Risks to the roadmap\n    77\t\n    78\t| Risk | Effect | Mitigation |\n    79\t|---|---|---|\n    80\t| The DEC-01 default change breaks many test fixtures | M1 takes longer | PR-1a lands the classes behind a constant; PR-1b flips the default with mechanical fixture updates |\n    81\t| The gateway host is unavailable or thermally limited during M5 | M5 is delayed | Serial runs with resumable runner; schedule against the thermal-soak findings; T2 runs are resumable per task |\n    82\t| Held-out results miss the thresholds | Fix loops | Thresholds are pre-registered, so they are not moved after the fact. The fix is a code change, and the affected run classes are re-run. |\n    83\t| Parser restriction (PLAN-11) lowers the tool-call rate on text-only models | Task quality falls | Recorded fixtures; one-RC escape hatch; the qualification measures it |\n    84\t| Independent reviewer is unavailable (X5) | G5 cannot be met honestly | The owner must supply a reviewer. The audit does not substitute self-assessment for it. |\n    85\t\n    86\t## What must be re-run after implementation\n    87\t\n    88\tEverything marked RT or MEAS in AUDIT §5 must be re-run on the RC:\n    89\t\n    90\t- the PTY scripts in `evidence/D_pty`;\n    91\t- the probes in `evidence/prv`, `evidence/a2probe`, `evidence/probes` and `evidence/repro`;\n    92\t- the installer and doctor runs;\n    93\t- the memory measurements.\n    94\t\n    95\tThe baseline suite (905 CLI + 266 Rust tests) must be re-run at every gate. The two live provider verifications and the live end-to-end run (EVIDENCE §3) must be repeated on the RC with pinned models.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":780916353}},"started_at_ms":1793352499354,"completed_at_ms":1793352500135}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T09:28:20.351Z","ordinal":526503,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18c23-847f-7771-8c60-6fb974fcfac6","call_id":"call_ac2c1ed18a354f9dbf702bad782bbaf4","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.4 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"    55\t<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:START -->\n    56\t### Approved exact-RC qualification exceptions\n    57\t\n    58\t| Requirement | Approved decision | Scope |\n    59\t|---|---|---|\n    60\t<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:END -->\n    61\t\n    62\t## 1. Rules\n    63\t\n    64\t1. The RC is built and published by the release workflow from a clean tag. Its version is identical across all components (REQ-REL-103).\n    65\t2. All qualification runs use the **installed RC package**, installed with the documented one-line command. They never use a checkout build. The only exception is CI unit and PTY suites, which run from source at the same commit.\n    66\t3. Thresholds (DEC-05) are frozen before the first M5 run. A failing gate is fixed in code and the run is repeated as `rc.N+1`. A threshold is never relaxed after results are known.\n    67\t4. Evidence goes to `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`. The directory contains:\n    68\t   - `manifest.json`: commit, package sha256, environment, model fingerprint, dates;\n    69\t   - raw outputs;\n    70\t   - a `SHA256SUMS` file.\n    71\t\n    72\t   Secrets are redacted before commit.\n    73\t5. Any step that cannot run in the available environment is recorded as **NOT RUN** with its reason. A NOT RUN on a blocker gate fails the gate.\n    74\t\n    75\t## 2. Environments\n    76\t\n    77\t| ID | Environment | Used for |\n    78\t|---|---|---|\n    79\t| E1 | GitHub Actions: ubuntu-22.04 and ubuntu-24.04; Node 22 and 24; pinned Rust | Unit, integration and PTY suites; packaging; reproducibility |\n    80\t| E2 | Docker clean images: ubuntu:22.04, ubuntu:24.04, debian:12, fedora:40. Each with no Node, then with Node 20, Node 22 and Node 24. Non-root user. | Installer, upgrade, rollback, uninstall, platform failure messages |\n    81\t| E3 | Operator dev box: Linux x86-64, real terminals (xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal) | Terminal matrix, live sessions |\n    82\t| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\n    83\t| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\n    84\t\n    85\t## 3. Gate checklist (G0–G4: automated acceptance IDs)\n    86\t\n    87\tEvery ACC ID below is defined in the linked spec. The plan for each spec names the test that implements it. Run each check at the lifecycle stage dictated by its acceptance method in §1.1: source-applicable checks before the RC tag; checks requiring the RC archive, attestation, release, or installed package after RC construction; environment-specific checks in their declared environment. Bind every result to the exact source commit and, when artifact-dependent, the RC package digest. A source test or local build does not replace an artifact-bound check, and no G0–G4 ID is complete until all of its applicable checks pass.\n    88\t\n    89\t| Gate | Acceptance IDs | Spec |\n    90\t|---|---|---|\n    91\t| Safety | ACC-SAFE-01 to ACC-SAFE-10 | SPEC-01 |\n    92\t| Process ownership | ACC-PROC-01 to ACC-PROC-08 (ACC-PROC-07 is the load test, run in E3) | SPEC-02 |\n    93\t| Untrusted inputs | ACC-TRUST-01 to ACC-TRUST-09 | SPEC-03 |\n    94\t| Continuity | ACC-CONT-01 to ACC-CONT-09 (ACC-CONT-10 is in §8) | SPEC-04 |\n    95\t| Inference | ACC-INF-01 to ACC-INF-09 (ACC-INF-10 is in §4) | SPEC-05 |\n    96\t| Packaging | ACC-PKG-01 to ACC-PKG-09 | SPEC-06 |\n    97\t| Supply chain | ACC-SUP-01 to ACC-SUP-08 (artifact-bound ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08 after RC construction) | SPEC-07 |\n    98\t| Persistence | ACC-PER-01 to ACC-PER-07 | SPEC-08 |\n    99\t| Governance | ACC-GOV-01 to ACC-GOV-06 | SPEC-09 |\n   100\t| Verification | ACC-VER-01 to ACC-VER-09 | SPEC-11 |\n   101\t| Upgrade | ACC-UPG-01 to ACC-UPG-14 | SPEC-12 |\n   102\t\n   103\t\n   104\t### 3.1 Acceptance IDs defined in this file\n   105\t\n   106\tThese are retained commitments from REQUIREMENTS §2 and cross-cutting checks.\n   107\t\n   108\t| ID | Check | Pass condition |\n   109\t|---|---|---|\n   110\t| ACC-TUI-STEER | PTY: submit a task; while a tool runs, type steering text and press Enter; also queue a steer before a cancel | Steering is applied at the next step boundary. Unapplied steering is returned to the composer. Nothing is dropped silently (existing `sidecar_steering_diff` plus PTY s6). |\n   111\t| ACC-TUI-A11Y | PTY with `NO_COLOR=1` and with `TERM=dumb` at 40×14 and 100×30 | Zero colour SGR codes. Every state is distinguishable by glyph and word. Hints are complete at 40 columns (TUI-10). |\n   112\t| ACC-SEC-JAIL | `core/tests` plus harness-core calls with `..`, absolute, symlinked-file, symlinked-dir and symlinked-parent payloads | Every one is refused (C §4 R1 set). |\n   113\t| ACC-SEC-B6 | Re-run `docs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/repro/zz_trust_repro.test.ts`. Seeded-secret scan of `~/.nexus` and `.nexus` after a scripted turn. | Zero plaintext seeded secrets in durable stores or outbound bodies. |\n   114\t| ACC-PRV-LIVE | `nexus providers verify --provider <p> -m <pinned model> -j` for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06) | `passed: true`. Receipts archived. |\n   115\t| ACC-PRV-STANDALONE | §4.2 on the installed RC through the approved stripped proxy, with gateway credentials absent from the child environment | Every required profile completes through the proxy and the absent-gateway boundary holds; receipts archived. |\n   116\t| ACC-PLAT | E2 matrix, §7 | All rows pass. |\n   117\t| ACC-QUAL-T2 | §6.1 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n   118\t| ACC-QUAL-T3 | §6.3 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n   119\t| ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n   120\t| ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\n   121\t| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five terminal environments and three sizes | Waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20. No manual-cell execution or evidence is required, and no result is inferred. Automated §5.1 and scripted PTY §5.2 remain mandatory. |\n   122\t\n   123\t## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\n   124\t\n   125\t### 4.1 Clean-HOME procedure\n   126\t\n   127\t1. `export HOME=$(mktemp -d)`.\n   128\t2. Install the RC with the documented command.\n   129\t3. Create `~/.config/nexus/config.env` containing only:\n   130\t   - `LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:<proxy>/v1`\n   131\t   - `LOCAL_LLM_MODEL=<id as listed by the proxy>`\n   132\t   - `LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY=REDACTED\n   133\t\n   134\t   No gateway token file, no homelab paths, no `NODE_*` overrides.\n   135\t4. Start `node eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs --upstream <gateway> --token-file <operator token> [--emulate <kind>]`. The gateway token stays with the proxy and never reaches the Nexus HOME.\n   136\t5. Run `nexus doctor --json` and archive it. It must report the server kind and context source with no `gateway` capability.\n   137\t\n   138\t### 4.2 Standalone matrix\n   139\t\n   140\t| Profile | What Nexus sees | Runs | Pass condition |\n   141\t|---|---|---|---|\n   142\t| P-plain | Bare OpenAI-compatible `/models` and chat. No tokenize, no capacity headers. | Standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 held-out tasks) × 3 runs; T4 classes 1, 3, 4, 7 × 3 | T2 correctness ≥ (gateway-direct T2 correctness on the same tasks − 10 pts). False VERIFIED = 0. T4 truthful = 100%. Context source reported as `client_default` or an operator override, with no error. |\n   143\t| P-llamacpp | Emulated llama.cpp `/props` and overflow body | Same tasks × 1 run; plus the forced-overflow case (context limit set to 8k) | Context discovered from `/props`. Overflow gives one compact-and-retry, then success or an actionable error. |\n   144\t| P-vllm | Emulated `max_model_len` and vLLM overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `max_model_len` |\n   145\t| P-ollama | Emulated `/api/show` and Ollama overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `ollama_show` |\n   146\t| Conformance | CI fixtures for llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio and Ollama shapes | CI | All pass (ACC-INF-01, -02, -05) |\n   147\t\n   148\tACC-INF-10 passes only when every row passes. The release notes state the scope in the form required by DEC-16.\n   149\t\n   150\t### 4.3 Provider matrix (E5)\n   151\t\n   152\t| Provider | Tier (DEC-06) | Required for v1.0.0 |\n   153\t|---|---|---|\n   154\t| OpenRouter, pinned model | Supported | `providers verify` PASS, plus one live small task (a §6-style bug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\n   155\t| ChatGPT sign-in | Experimental | Verify PASS recorded (already PASS at db1ca55; repeat on the RC) |\n   156\t| OpenAI API key, Anthropic | Experimental unless keys are added | If promoted: verify PASS plus one live task. Otherwise NOT RUN, and they are labelled experimental. |\n   157\t| Copilot | Experimental | Not required |\n   158\t\n   159\t## 5. Terminal acceptance (REQ-QUAL-108)\n   160\t\n   285\t| Backup restore | `nexus upgrade --restore-backup <state-backup-directory>` | Snapshot of configuration and complete durable state restored from a recognized private backup directory (`backup.json`, `state/`, optional `config/`), with strict 0600 file / 0700 directory modes. A canonical `config.env.bak.*` path restores configuration only. Arbitrary files and tar archives are rejected. Run it through the stable `nexus` launcher; close existing legacy clients, then keep version-pinned legacy binaries and direct old entry points offline until the durable restore journal is cleared. |\n   286\t| Incompatible downgrade | `nexus upgrade --version <v> --allow-downgrade` (incompatible state schema) | Refused fail-closed with actionable state schema explanation. Existing installation unchanged. |\n   287\t\n   288\t## 8. Independent acceptance (REQ-AGT-110, ACC-CONT-10)\n   289\t\n   290\tThe reviewer is supplied by the owner (X5) and did not implement the work under review.\n   291\t\n   292\tThe reviewer receives:\n   293\t\n   294\t- the RC package;\n   295\t- this file;\n   296\t- the REQUIREMENTS ledger;\n   297\t- SPEC-04;\n   298\t- read access to the evidence directory.\n   299\t\n   300\tThe reviewer performs:\n   301\t\n   302\t1. An independent re-run of a sample. At minimum:\n   303\t   - ACC-SAFE-01, 03, 09;\n   304\t   - ACC-PROC-02;\n   305\t   - ACC-TRUST-01, 02;\n   306\t   - ACC-CONT-01, 03;\n   307\t   - ACC-VER-01, 03;\n   308\t   - ACC-PKG-01;\n   309\t   - 5 random T2 tasks;\n   310\t   - 2 T4 classes.\n   311\t2. One live long task (≥ 60 steps, ≥ 2 compactions) on the RC through the gateway, including one kill and resume.\n   312\t3. A review of the scorer verdict and of contamination handling.\n   313\t\n   314\t**Output:** `docs/reviews/<date>-v1-rc-independent-acceptance.md` with an ACCEPT, ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS, or REJECT verdict per area. \"Accept with defects\" needs an owner disposition for every defect, and for a blocker area the only acceptable disposition is a fix.\n   315\t\n   316\t## 9. Contest (separate product; not a client gate)\n   317\t\n   318\tThe contest submission is complete and judging has concluded. No contest freeze applies (DEC-13 status amendment); post-contest hardening is tracked separately from client v1.0.0 acceptance and is accepted by:\n   319\t\n   320\t| ID | Check |\n   321\t|---|---|\n   322\t| CON-A1 | Ordinary maintained package/experiment checks build `agent-collab-worker`. `worker.config.json` has the configured name, and the bundle contains the `/work-state` handler. Do not restore the retired `cloudflare-contest-contract` status check. |\n   323\t| CON-A2 | Broker negative tests: caller-supplied env paths and URLs are ignored. A host outside `*.artifacts.cloudflare.net` is refused. |\n   324\t| CON-A3 | On a clean VM, `install.sh --fresh` followed by `post-install-qualify.py` passes. |\n   325\t| CON-A4 | `sudo -l` for the demo user shows only fixed argv. `sudo setpriv --reuid=0 id` is denied. |\n   326\t| CON-A5 | One clean-account `--mode cloudflare --agents real` run, with a committed, redacted run record. |\n   327\t| CON-A6 | The video source commits are tagged and published, or the docs state that they are unpublished. |\n   328\t\n   329\t## 10. Release decision (G6)\n   330\t\n   331\tG6 passes only when every item below holds. It authorizes a version-only stable commit from the accepted RC source, followed by its source checks, stable tag, and unpublished draft candidate; it does not authorize making stable assets publicly available. RC tags are candidate construction inputs governed by §1.1; an RC tag or its successful build does not satisfy this release decision.\n   332\t\n   333\t- [ ] G0–G4 automated gates pass on the final RC commit (§3).\n   334\t- [ ] RC artifact gates pass on the workflow-produced RC, including ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08; record the exact source commit, workflow run, and artifact digest.\n   335\t- [ ] §4 standalone and provider matrix: all rows PASS.\n   336\t- [ ] §5 terminal acceptance: automated CI (§5.1) and scripted PTY (§5.2) gates PASS. The manual 5×3 matrix (§5.3) is waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20.\n   337\t- [ ] §6 thresholds: all hold.\n   338\t- [ ] §7 install matrix: all rows PASS.\n   339\t- [ ] §8 independent acceptance: ACCEPT, or ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS with owner dispositions and no blocker defects outstanding.\n   340\t- [ ] The pre-RC source gate passes from a clean source worktree: `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce`. Every B/RR source row outside the §1.1 qualification-only map must be ≥ `tested`. A mapped row below `tested` is reported as deferred; this result does not accept or qualify it.\n   341\t- [ ] The exact-RC evidence gate passes from the clean RC worktree and is bound to the exact RC source commit and installed RC artifact. Run the checker with the custodian-approved, immutable qualification record and evidence directory:\n   342\t  `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce --qualification-record <record.json> --rc-artifact <installed-rc-package> --evidence-root <evidence-directory>`.\n   343\t  The version 1 record contains `sourceCommit` (full commit ID), `rcTag` (for example `v1.0.0-rc.1`), `artifactSha256`, `artifactProvenance` (`sourceCommit`, `artifactSha256`, and a hashed provenance report), `independentAcceptance` (`disposition`, `reviewer`, `implementers`, zero `blockingDefects`, and a hashed report reference), and one `requirements` entry for every B/RR row. For `ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS`, include each non-blocking defect with its owner disposition; unresolved or blocking defects fail. Each requirement entry records its status and one or more hashed evidence files covering the exact criteria required by the ledger and the §1.1 qualification-only map. Every criterion evidence file must be a JSON object with top-level `sourceCommit`, `rcTag`, and `artifactSha256` values exactly matching the validated qualification record, current RC source commit, and installed RC artifact. A digest-valid report copied from another source revision, RC tag, or artifact is rejected. A B row recorded as `tested` also needs a non-empty `qualificationNotApplicable.reason` and a `qualificationNotApplicable.decision` matching the approved per-requirement exception table and a matching applicability declaration in DECISIONS.md; an unrelated or record-supplied decision is rejected. Evidence paths must be relative regular files under the evidence root, with no symlinks. Missing, unknown, stale, mismatched, or incomplete evidence fails the gate. The checker requires a clean worktree, rejects `--ledger` overrides, enforces source-ledger thresholds outside the explicit §1.1 lifecycle rows, and requires the exact-RC record itself to meet the normal status threshold for every row. It never mutates the source ledger or relaxes a requirement's B/RR record threshold. The checker validates source/tag/artifact identity bindings and evidence hashes; it does not authenticate the reviewer or prove that the artifact was built from the source commit. The approved release workflow must independently verify build provenance/attestation, and the designated custodian and independent reviewer must verify their respective approvals and custody evidence.\n   344\t- [ ] Docs checklist (SPEC-09 §3.2) is signed off.\n   345\t- [ ] Release notes state the standalone scope (DEC-16), the provider tiers (DEC-06), the experimental surfaces (DEC-03, DEC-07) and the known limitations.\n   346\t- [ ] Owner approval to publish (X7).\n   347\t\n   348\tAfter G6, complete source checks on the exact stable-version commit before tagging, then complete the stable artifact checks in §1.1 stage 5 before publishing the draft. A failure keeps publication blocked and requires remediation plus the applicable requalification; do not mark the campaign released until published artifacts are independently verified.\n   349\t\n   350\t**Outcome recording.** The release decision record goes in `docs/releases/v1.0.0.md`, with links to every evidence directory.\n     1\t# Roadmap: Nexus Code to v1.0.0\n     2\t\n     3\tThe starting point is `db1ca55` (`v0.1.0-alpha.2` + docs), which has 31 blocker requirements open (REQUIREMENTS §3). The roadmap is ordered by dependency, and every milestone ends at a gate defined in [ACCEPTANCE.md](ACCEPTANCE.md). There are no delivery dates; effort is given as ranges, with the assumptions stated.\n     4\t\n     5\t## Assumptions behind the estimates\n     6\t\n     7\t- **People.** One implementer working with agent assistance, as in this repository's history. An engineer-day (ed) means one focused day of implementation, review and test for that person.\n     8\t- **Inference.** Inference comes only from the homelab gateway (DEC-16): one model host, with runs serialised.\n     9\t- **Uncertainty.** The largest unknown is how many fix loops M5 qualification triggers. The pilot's history suggests at least one.\n    10\t- **Supporting labour.** Held-out tasks are written by an agent author (authorised, DEC-05). Independent acceptance is done by a reviewer the owner provides (X5).\n    11\t\n    12\t## Milestones\n    13\t\n    14\t```\n    15\tM0 Foundation ──► M1 Safety floor ──────────────► M3 Continuity & inference ──► RC1 ──► M5 Qualification ──► M6 Release\n    16\t        │               │                                ▲                                  ▲\n    17\t        │               └──► M2 Product parity & supply chain (parallel) ──────────────────┤\n    18\t        │                                                                                   │\n    19\t        └──► M4 Persistence hygiene (parallel with M2/M3) ──────────────────────────────────┤\n    20\t  (from M1) held-out task authoring, standalone proxy, fixtures (parallel) ─────────────────┘\n    21\t```\n    22\t\n    23\t| Milestone | Scope (plans) | Deliverables | Exit gate | Effort |\n    24\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n    25\t| **M0 Foundation** | PLAN-08 task 1 (test HOME isolation); PLAN-06 task 3 (version sync). Owner action X1 (stale local tags deleted) is already done.; PLAN-09 tasks 1, 2, 5 (ledger checker in report mode, historical banners, cheap doc truth fixes) | Tests never touch the real HOME. One version identity. The ledger is enforced in CI. | **G0**: ACC-PER-03, ACC-PKG-03, ACC-GOV-01/03 | 2–4 ed |\n    26\t| **M1 Safety floor** (critical path) | PLAN-01 (effect classes, DEC-01 posture, verifier gating, REPL approvals, read-only masking, argv sandbox, tripwire); PLAN-02 (process registry, cancel and shutdown sweep, bounds); PLAN-03 (project `.env` allowlist, CIDR locality, SSRF-safe fetch, skills/knowledge trust, plugin directories, EXT-004); PLAN-11 PR-11a/11b (parser, binding) | Untrusted input cannot cause unapproved exec, egress or configuration changes. Stop means stopped. No false VERIFIED from a filename coincidence. | **G1**: all ACC-SAFE, ACC-PROC, ACC-TRUST, ACC-VER-01..04 | 15–25 ed |\n    27\t| **M2 Product parity and supply chain** (parallel with M1 after PLAN-01 PR-1b) | PLAN-06 (unified launcher with the TUI as the packaged default, doc commands, doctor, installer); PLAN-07 (notices, SBOM, provenance, CI matrix, `cli/dist` untracked, SECURITY.md, CHANGELOG); PLAN-12 (CLI and TUI upgrade engine) | The installed product equals the tested product. Compliant release assets. In-place upgrade safely verifies and swaps releases. | **G2**: ACC-PKG-01..09, ACC-SUP-01..07, ACC-UPG-01..06 | 8–14 ed |\n    28\t| **M3 Continuity and inference** | PLAN-04 (resume, durable work units, accounting, error path, stagnation, team semantics); PLAN-05 code tasks (server-kind discovery, compact-and-retry, error bounds, timeouts, parser robustness, receipts, startup probe, decoupling, CA); PLAN-11 PR-11c..e; PLAN-10 harness tasks 1–7, 9, 10, 13 | Resume and compaction never lose state. Standalone sizing works. Eval harness ready. | **G3**: ACC-CONT-01..09, ACC-INF-01..09, ACC-VER-05..09, eval self-tests | 15–25 ed |\n    29\t| **M4 Persistence hygiene** (parallel with M2/M3) | PLAN-08 tasks 2–10 | Private state permissions, retention/GC, corruption reporting, schema policy | **G4**: ACC-PER-01..07 | 5–8 ed |\n    30\t| **RC1** | After PLAN-09 task 7's pre-RC source-ledger reconciliation and enforce gate, tag `v1.0.0-rc.1` (owner approves publishing a prerelease; X7) | RC build installed through the documented command | G0–G4 green on the exact RC source; pre-RC requirements enforcement passed | <1 ed |\n    31\t| **M5 Qualification** | PLAN-10 task 11 (T2 held-out 5×, T3, T4, standalone stripped-proxy profiles, provider verify); task 12 (terminal matrix); ACC-SUP-08 cross-runner reproducibility; independent acceptance (X5) of continuity and of the RC | Qualification evidence archive, scorer verdict table, independent reports | **G5**: ACCEPTANCE §4–§8 all PASS | 10–20 calendar days. About 84 h of serial inference for T2, plus T3/T4/standalone. Excludes fix loops. |\n    32\t| **Fix loop(s)** | Defects found in M5, landed as `rc.N` | Re-run the failed gate subsets, plus regression subsets | G5 | 0–15 ed per loop (unknown) |\n    33\t| **M6 Release** | PLAN-09 task 7 (verify the pre-RC source-ledger reconciliation and enforcement evidence; record exact-RC dispositions in the acceptance record without mutating the accepted RC source); docs sign-off; release notes; tag `v1.0.0` (X7) | Published v1.0.0 with notices, SBOM and attestation | **G6**: ACCEPTANCE §10 checklist | 2–4 ed |\n    34\t\n    35\t**Total implementation:** about 46–78 ed (the sum of M0–M4 and M6). **Qualification:** 2–4 calendar weeks. **Fix loops:** unknown. A plausible range is 0–2 loops.\n    36\t\n    37\t## Critical path\n    38\t\n    39\tThe longest dependency chain is:\n    40\t\n    41\t**M0 → M1 → M3 → RC1 → M5 (T2 held-out runs) → M6**\n    42\t\n    43\t- M1 comes first because the posture change (DEC-01) alters behaviour that every later test, eval and acceptance run depends on. Qualifying before it would have to be redone.\n    44\t- M3 is on the path because resume (AGT-01), work-unit durability (AGT-02a) and standalone sizing (PRV-06) are blockers, and the T4 class 9 test (SIGTERM, then resume) needs them.\n    45\t- M5 is bounded by serial inference on the single gateway host.\n    46\t\n    47\tWhen several agents work at once, the parallel lanes, hot-file serialisation and the single-`GATEWAY` lock in [CONCURRENCY.md](CONCURRENCY.md) govern the order in which work merges.\n    48\t\n    49\tOff the critical path, but must finish before RC1:\n    50\t\n    51\t- M2, M4;\n    52\t- the 40 held-out T2 tasks and 8 T3 tasks (agent-authored), with their manifest sealed **before** RC1;\n    53\t- the stripping proxy and the conformance fixtures.\n    54\t\n    55\t## Release gates\n    56\t\n    57\t| Gate | When | Pass condition |\n    58\t|---|---|---|\n    59\t| G0 | End of M0 | Foundation acceptance IDs pass. `make test` passes on a clean clone and leaves the real HOME untouched. |\n    60\t| G1 | End of M1 | All safety acceptance IDs pass in CI. Existing PTY suites stay green. No new skipped tests. |\n    61\t| G2 | End of M2 | A package smoke run in a PTY shows the TUI. The doc-command test passes. Release dry-run assets are complete. |\n    62\t| G3 | End of M3 | Continuity, inference and verification acceptance IDs pass. The eval harness self-tests pass, including the T4 smoke. |\n    63\t| G4 | End of M4 | Persistence acceptance IDs pass. |\n    64\t| G5 | After the RC | ACCEPTANCE §4–§8 pass. The DEC-05 thresholds are met. Independent reports are filed. |\n    65\t| G6 | Release | The ledger checker passes in enforce mode, so every B/RR row is ≥ tested and B rows are product-qualified where ACCEPTANCE requires it. Docs are signed off. Owner approval X7 is given. |\n    66\t\n    67\t## Classification of the work\n    68\t\n    69\t| Category | Contents |\n    70\t|---|---|\n    71\t| **Release blockers** (31 B rows) | M0–M3 for implementation, M5 for qualification evidence |\n    72\t| **Release-required improvements** (58 RR rows) | Spread across M1–M4; listed in each plan |\n    73\t| **Post-v1** | REQUIREMENTS §5: single step loop, full context provenance, knowledge freshness, `/tdd` and `nexus eval` fixes, cgroups, macOS/arm64, self-uninstall, and others |\n    74\t| **Contest track** | PLAN-C1, after judging. Independent of all gates (DEC-13). |\n    75\t\n    76\t## Risks to the roadmap\n    77\t\n    78\t| Risk | Effect | Mitigation |\n    79\t|---|---|---|\n    80\t| The DEC-01 default change breaks many test fixtures | M1 takes longer | PR-1a lands the classes behind a constant; PR-1b flips the default with mechanical fixture updates |\n    81\t| The gateway host is unavailable or thermally limited during M5 | M5 is delayed | Serial runs with resumable runner; schedule against the thermal-soak findings; T2 runs are resumable per task |\n    82\t| Held-out results miss the thresholds | Fix loops | Thresholds are pre-registered, so they are not moved after the fact. The fix is a code change, and the affected run classes are re-run. |\n    83\t| Parser restriction (PLAN-11) lowers the tool-call rate on text-only models | Task quality falls | Recorded fixtures; one-RC escape hatch; the qualification measures it |\n    84\t| Independent reviewer is unavailable (X5) | G5 cannot be met honestly | The owner must supply a reviewer. The audit does not substitute self-assessment for it. |\n    85\t\n    86\t## What must be re-run after implementation\n    87\t\n    88\tEverything marked RT or MEAS in AUDIT §5 must be re-run on the RC:\n    89\t\n    90\t- the PTY scripts in `evidence/D_pty`;\n    91\t- the probes in `evidence/prv`, `evidence/a2probe`, `evidence/probes` and `evidence/repro`;\n    92\t- the installer and doctor runs;\n    93\t- the memory measurements.\n    94\t\n    95\tThe baseline suite (905 CLI + 266 Rust tests) must be re-run at every gate. The two live provider verifications and the live end-to-end run (EVIDENCE §3) must be repeated on the RC with pinned models.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18c20-aec5-7552-93bd-755d714c245e","create_time":1793352500.3510487}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
