{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T09:45:37.091Z","ordinal":526963,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18c33-5643-7e22-9f7b-cf1996319642","call_id":"call_e7c61c4b5fe5408598c2ea07ddec865c","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.4 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 15799)\nTotal output lines: 155\n\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/CUSTODY_T2_BLACKBOX_CONVERSION/owner.json\topencode\t\t\t2026-10-29T02:24:10Z\t\t\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/DEFECT_CST_UNBOUNDED_REBASE_20261024/owner.json\tcodex-root\tmike-dev\tv1/defect-cst-memory-followup\t2026-10-24T18:19:09Z\treview finding follow-up for merged PR199: bound parser line-memory amplification; targeted regression; requalify against exact current main\tPR199 merged at 4adc61a; exact follow-up candidate under independent review\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/DEFECT_HTML_CONTROL_INJECTION_20261023/owner.json\tcodex-root\tmike-dev\tv1/defect-html-control-injection\t2026-10-23T23:31:00Z\tfix terminal carriage-return spoofing in HTML decoded text and search URL fields; refresh PR #175 to current main; add regressions and obtain independent review; no held-out access\t\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/DEFECT_MCP_PROTO_NAME_20261024/owner.json\tcodex-root\t\tv1/defect-mcp-proto-name\t2026-10-24T13:35:33Z\t\t\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/DOCS_POST_V1_ROADMAP/owner.json\tAntigravity\t\tv1/docs-post-v1-roadmap\t2026-10-21T16:33:56Z\tadd Dependabot PRs triage and work packages to v1.1.0 roadmap and documentation\t\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/DOCS_V11_LAYERED_MEMORY/owner.json\tCodex memory roadmap review\t\tv1/docs-v11-layered-memory\t2026-10-22T21:14:20.166350+00:00\tUser-authorized additive WP-1109 memory roadmap and README links in isolated worktree; preserve existing dependency planning on docs-post-v1 branch; no product code or v1.0 acceptance changes\tDocumentation checks passed; local commit prepared for owner integration into existing docs-post-v1 roadmap branch; no push or merge; file claims released\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/EVAL_T4_OVERLOAD_DIAGNOSTIC_20261030/owner.json\t/root\tmike-dev\tv1/eval-t4-overload-diagnostic\t2026-10-30T08:26:48Z\tImprove diagnostics for two historical synthetic evaluator failures in eval_harness.test.ts: T4 overloaded smoke missing model telemetry (PR334) and peer fake-OpenCode hiddenPass false (PR338); diagnostic-only assertions, no product behavior change, no held-out access; run focused cases only after hosted SUITE clears.\tFocused synthetic tests PASS on source base 890c553d after CI-equivalent CLI build and Rust release build: T4 overloaded endpoint smoke and fake OpenCode peer version/budget case (2 passed, 0 failed). Independent read-only review ACCEPT on exact unchanged diff SHA-256 d4b51c5450d98343c3cd7e6cd7fe216363541b11f3df97c5bfaa847d88b7d2a3. Rebased commit c6f00e8f onto origin/main 16eeb6ee; targeted rerun pending because hosted SUITE 41029564419 Node22/24 full suites remain active. Synthetic only, no held-out tasks. On rebased exact candidate c6f00e8f27c0af1a80e7131f8a6f52efa4aa0321 (differs from origin/main only by diagnostics test file), requirements enforcement PASS (123 rows; 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 mapped exact-RC deferrals), sync-version --check --tag v1.0.0-rc.14 PASS, diff-check PASS. These are source gates, not RC acceptance. Latest post-merge CI41029564419: Node22=SUCCESS, Node24=SUCCESS; Linux package/reproducibility job still in progress, so SUITE held. Independent reviewer re-reviewed rebased exact head c6f00e8f27c0af1a80e7131f8a6f52efa4aa0321 against base 16eeb6ee and reaffirmed ACCEPT; diff SHA-256 d4b51c5450d98343c3cd7e6cd7fe216363541b11f3df97c5bfaa847d88b7d2a3 unchanged; review only, no tests. Branch pushed to origin as v1/eval-t4-overload-diagnostic at c6f00e8f27c0af1a80e7131f8a6f52efa4aa0321. No PR opened yet: main CI41029564419 Linux CLI suite remains active; will rerun focused tests and open PR after SUITE release. Focused exact-current-base rerun completed after main SUITE: 2/2 synthetic cases passed on c6f00e8f27c0af1a80e7131f8a6f52efa4aa0321 with isolated HOME/XDG, CI-built release harness-core, and npm ci. Independent review ACCEPT remains valid. Remote branch is preserved; PR opening waits until RC14 release workflow full suite terminates to prevent overlap.\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/FEATURE_RC10_E2_POWERLOSS_20261030/owner.json\tcodex-root\tmike-dev\tcodex/pr334-evidence-correction\t2026-10-30T03:10:20.793Z\tTake over Kimi PR334 evidence-only E2 power-loss record; preserve original detached worktree; reconcile historical RC10 failure and RC11/RC12 fix evidence without claiming qualification; verify manifests, exact-base review, and checks.\tPR334 evidence correction locally integrated into full candidate 9f59384b7ad9390fac3cabc0cbede15a8c26bdb2 on PR335 exact base; independent full-candidate review ACCEPT; RC11 NOT VERIFIED due absent logs, RC10 failure and fixed-CLI demo retained; manifest 65/65 and diff check pass. Exact PR CI not run to avoid overlap with active PR335/PR341 suite jobs; branch local only.\n/home/mike/nexus-c…13399 tokens truncated…C10_CHATGPT_PROVIDER_EVIDENCE_20261028/owner.json\tcodex-root\tmike-dev\tv1/rc10-chatgpt-provider-evidence-20261028\t2026-10-28T19:03:37Z\tarchive sanitized exact-RC10 ChatGPT-plan provider verification and receipts; document artifact identity and unknown cost confidence; no production code or acceptance promotion\tPR #309 current head aace981b; independent review ACCEPT, diff 9dbb076c, five checksums verified. Exact-head CodeQL and JS/TS passed; Node22/24 in progress; Entire in progress; Linux not yet present. Protected GitHub auto-merge enabled at 19:56:34 UTC, gated by required checks. RC10 historical evidence only; no acceptance promotion.\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims