{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T09:51:18.278Z","ordinal":527201,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a18c38-8b06-7be3-acbb-d03ba7bdc1fa","call_id":"call_1424ae8425af4ec191e8339747944ba2","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/pr311_draft_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT.** Prior acceptance still applies after rebase.\\n\\nCandidate HEAD is `c6f00e8f27c0af1a80e7131f8a6f52efa4aa0321`; base is `16eeb6eeffe7fc0bae234aa34dcb671a6ba5ff99`. Diff SHA-256: `d4b51c5450d98343c3cd7e6cd7fe216363541b11f3df97c5bfaa847d88b7d2a3`. The diff changes only `cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts`. Assertions retain the same acceptance semantics, and the added diagnostics remain limited to synthetic fixture data. No changed concern; review only, no tests run.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/review_pr300_readiness\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"## Current state\\n\\nAt **2026-10-30 09:26 UTC**, `origin/main` is `16eeb6eeffe7fc0bae234aa34dcb671a6ba5ff99`, and all three version files identify `1.0.0-rc.14`.\\n\\n- [CI run 41029564419](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/41029564419) is **in progress** on that exact commit. Node 22 and 24 jobs passed. Linux is still running the CLI suite; security, requirements, packaging, reproducibility, SBOM, and installer-smoke steps remain pending. Do not treat this run as green yet.\\n- [CodeQL run 41029564602](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/41029564602) **passed** on the same commit.\\n- No RC14 tag or release exists. GitHub’s [release list](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases) currently ends at RC11; lookup of the RC14 tag and release returns 404.\\n- `docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md` is stale: its latest checkpoint is dated Oct 29 and still reports RC11 as unpublished. Use the current RC14 notes and live checks, and refresh readiness before relying on that document as a status record.\\n\\n## RC14 artifact prerequisites\\n\\nAcceptance §1.1 requires all applicable pre-RC source gates to pass on the exact source commit before tagging. Specifically:\\n\\n1. Let [CI 41029564419](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/41029564419) finish successfully. The Node 22/24 jobs have passed, but the Linux job has not.\\n2. Confirm exact-source version sync. `sync-version --check` has passed in the Node jobs on `16eeb6e`.\\n3. Run `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` on a clean checkout of `16eeb6e`. The CI jobs ran the checker **without** `--enforce`, so the required pre-RC enforcement result is not yet evidenced for this commit.\\n4. Complete any applicable source-stage G0–G4 checks. Acceptance says each required gate must run at the lifecycle stage appropriate to its acceptance method; source checks do not replace installed-artifact checks.\\n5. Once those pass, create the version-matched `v1.0.0-rc.14` tag on that exact main commit and let the release workflow build and publish the prerelease. The workflow builds twice and compares the archive, checksums, notices, SBOM, and installer; validates the SBOM; runs package and installer smoke checks; and attests provenance. Its RC output is the qualification candidate, not an accepted release. See [ACCEPTANCE §1.1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/blob/16eeb6eeffe7fc0bae234aa34dcb671a6ba5ff99/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md#L20-L34) and the [release workflow](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/blob/16eeb6eeffe7fc0bae234aa34dcb671a6ba5ff99/.github/workflows/release.yml#L84-L132).\\n\\nRelease and publication authorization was already granted, gated on acceptance. No new authorization request is needed.\\n\\n## Mandatory gates after the artifact exists\\n\\nThe workflow-produced archive, tag commit, run ID, digests, and attestation must be recorded first. Then:\\n\\n- **Artifact gates:** ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08, including notices, SBOM, attestation, release-note metadata, and cross-runner reproducibility. Package checks that require an installed RC must use this exact package. See [ACCEPTANCE §§1.1 and 3](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/blob/16eeb6eeffe7fc0bae234aa34dcb671a6ba5ff99/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md#L24-L27).\\n- **Installed-RC qualification:** platform/install/upgrade lifecycle checks, including the power-loss cell; provider verification and the required pinned-model live task; standalone profiles; sealed held-out T2, T3 long tasks, and nine-class T4 fault injection against frozen rules and thresholds; scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios; and independent exact-RC review. Evidence must bind to the RC commit and artifact digest. The [RC14 notes](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/blob/16eeb6eeffe7fc0bae234aa34dcb671a6ba5ff99/docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.14.md#L26-L32) explicitly say these gates remain outstanding and RC11 evidence does not automatically carry forward.\\n- **Requirements acceptance:** exact-RC enforcement requires a custodian-approved immutable qualification record with criteria evidence bound to the exact tag and artifact, plus independent acceptance. Source-only `--enforce` does not satisfy this. See [ACCEPTANCE §10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/blob/16eeb6eeffe7fc0bae234aa34dcb671a6ba5ff99/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md#L329-L348).\\n- **Terminal disposition:** DEC-20 waives the manual five-terminal × three-size matrix for v1.0.0; it is waived, not passed. Automated CI PTY and scripted installed-RC PTY gates remain mandatory. See [DECISIONS.md](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/blob/16eeb6eeffe7fc0bae234aa34dcb671a6ba5ff99/docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md#L261-L269) and [ACCEPTANCE §5](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/blob/16eeb6eeffe7fc0bae234aa34dcb671a6ba5ff99/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md#L159-L192).\\n\\nAfter exact-RC acceptance and G6, stable promotion still requires a version-only stable commit, its source gates, a stable tag and draft build, stable-artifact verification, and only then publication. Stable v1.0.0 is not currently released.\\n\\n## Current external dependencies and blockers\\n\\n- **Custody acceptance is unresolved.** [Issue #1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) is open and unassigned; its latest public update asks the custodian to resume status-only reporting after the SUITE claim was released. No fresh custody acceptance is recorded. I did not access held-out material. Acceptance requires a custodian-approved sealed 40-task corpus before T2 execution ([§6.1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/blob/16eeb6eeffe7fc0bae234aa34dcb671a6ba5ff99/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md#L214-L233)).\\n- **RC14 has no artifact yet**, so every artifact-bound and installed-RC gate is necessarily pending. [PR #334](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/334) records a power-loss failure on RC10; that is historical evidence, not an RC14 result. The current RC14 notes also list the power-loss cell as outstanding.\\n- **The independent RC acceptance reviewer must be supplied by the owner**; no RC14 acceptance report exists yet ([ACCEPTANCE §8](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/blob/16eeb6eeffe7fc0bae234aa34dcb671a6ba5ff99/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md#L288-L314), [DECISIONS X5](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/blob/16eeb6eeffe7fc0bae234aa34dcb671a6ba5ff99/docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md#L283-L285)).\\n- The E4 homelab gateway is specified as the qualification inference path, but I did not find current public evidence that it is unavailable; treat availability as an execution prerequisite, not a confirmed blocker.\\n\\n**Disposition:** RC14 artifact creation is gated on the remaining Linux CI job and a clean exact-revision `--enforce` result, plus any applicable source-stage checks. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; no RC14 qualification or stable release is established.\\n\\n\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/review_pr302\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18c35-b249-7353-ae41-f481d8a53b29","create_time":1793353878.2785954}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
