{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T09:51:34.369Z","ordinal":527227,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a18c38-c9e1-7e42-82a6-22e5ccfa914d","author":"/root/review_pr302","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/review_pr302\nPayload:\n**Exact source reviewed:** commit `16eeb6eeffe7fc0bae234aa34dcb671a6ba5ff99`, read with `git show`; the shared checkout has unrelated dirty files, which I did not inspect as candidate source. No tests or suite commands were run.\n\n**Confirmed from source**\n\n- `npm --prefix cli test` runs `node scripts/run_tests.mjs` and then `test-scope-procs.sh` ([`cli/package.json:12`]).\n- The runner selects every `*.test.ts` file when no file is supplied, launches `tsx --test --test-concurrency=1` via synchronous `spawnSync`, then removes its temporary HOME and exits only after that child exits ([`cli/scripts/run_tests.mjs:15-17, 33-40`]). A Node test child that retains a referenced handle would therefore keep the wrapper and CI step alive.\n- The second script has a 45-second limit for each of its two PTY fixture runs ([`test-scope-procs.sh:222-250, 257-268`]). It is a less likely explanation for a hang lasting tens of minutes.\n- There are unawaited HTTP server shutdowns in evaluator tests, including `networkServer.close()` and `upstream.close()` ([`cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts:1593-1608, 1725-1760`]), and in a shared test helper ([`cli/test/client_robustness.test.ts:9-21`]). These are plausible handles to inspect, but the source alone does not show that their connections remain open; Node’s server close behavior and the surrounding proxy cleanup can resolve them normally.\n- The client lease interval is explicitly `unref()`’d ([`cli/src/core/client_lease.ts:80-87`]), so it should not keep the test process alive.\n- Evaluator tests deliberately spawn contained descendants and timers, with explicit timeouts and cleanup paths ([`cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts:1209-1241, 1312-1378`]). They are worth correlating with the stalled run’s final test, but I found no source proof that they leak.\n\n**Assessment**\n\nI cannot confirm a specific root cause from static source inspection. The strongest leads are unawaited server closes and a contained subprocess/pipe that fails to complete teardown. The RC14 note also says the cause was not identified ([`docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.14.md:14`]); source inspection does not narrow that to one defect.\n\n**Smallest next diagnostic after SUITE clears:** run only `eval_integrity.test.ts` through the existing runner (`npm --prefix cli test -- test/eval_integrity.test.ts`) and capture whether the test summary appears while the process remains alive. If it reproduces, inspect the remaining PID’s active resources and child tree before changing teardown. If it exits, try the file containing the last test reported by the stalled full run. I would not apply a cleanup fix until a live handle or child is identified."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18c35-b249-7353-ae41-f481d8a53b29","create_time":1793353894.3692343,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":24265}}
