{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T09:54:06.070Z","ordinal":527304,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18c35-b249-7353-ae41-f481d8a53b29","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae4693bbbf8819f8fd3ae8e087a0bc1","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"**Campaign status:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`  \n**Acceptance:** `IN_PROGRESS`\n\nRC14 release workflow [41035120551](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/41035120551) is still running the CLI suite on exact commit `16eeb6eeffe7fc0bae234aa34dcb671a6ba5ff99`. The SUITE claim remains held for that run. The workflow-produced release and artifact are not available yet.\n\nA read-only review found no proven cause for the suite hang. The runner waits synchronously for the serial Node test process to exit; unawaited HTTP server closes are possible leads, but the source does not prove they leak. I made no speculative fix and ran no tests. Once the job terminates, its logs will let us target the actual final test or surviving process before changing teardown.\n\nThe held-out custody issue remains unresolved, and qualification has not started. The dirty shared checkout remains untouched. I recorded the updated CI and hang investigation in the existing claims log.\n\nNext: capture the hosted job’s final result and logs, then either verify the published RC14 artifact or diagnose the specific failure. Exact-RC acceptance and public v1.0.0 release remain outstanding."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1793354043753,"completed_at_ms":1793354046070}}
