{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T10:02:40.235Z","ordinal":527570,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18c3d-7cdd-71d3-966d-f30f05df4fb0","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-27ae5a52-08ba-4649-a2f7-fb73d564f195","process_id":"14589","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n \"install.sh|installation|Install Nexus|one-line|release artifact|GitHub release|nexus-linux\" docs README.md install.sh scripts/installer-smoke.sh"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/rc14-artifact-verification","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'install.sh|installation|Install Nexus|one-line|release artifact|GitHub release|nexus-linux' docs README.md install.sh scripts/installer-smoke.sh","query":"install.sh|installation|Install Nexus|one-line|release artifact|GitHub release|nexus-linux","path":"docs"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"install.sh:71:    fail \"could not query GitHub releases API (HTTP $LATEST_CODE); network failure or host unreachable.\"\ninstall.sh:77:ARCHIVE=\"nexus-linux-x86_64-$VERSION.tar.gz\"\ninstall.sh:86:(cd \"$TMP\" && sha256sum --check --status expected.sha256) || fail \"SHA-256 verification failed; no installation was changed.\"\ninstall.sh:111:  case \"$OLD\" in \"$PREFIX/lib/nexus/\"*) ;; *) fail \"$LINK points outside the Nexus installation; left it unchanged.\" ;; esac\nscripts/installer-smoke.sh:10:VERSION=${NAME#nexus-linux-x86_64-}\nscripts/installer-smoke.sh:148:# ACC-UPG-07: unsupported compatibility metadata schemas fail before installation.\nscripts/installer-smoke.sh:166:metadata.platforms[\"linux-x86_64\"].archive = `nexus-linux-x86_64-${tag}.tar.gz`;\nscripts/installer-smoke.sh:171:SCHEMA_ARCHIVE=\"nexus-linux-x86_64-$SCHEMA_VERSION.tar.gz\"\nscripts/installer-smoke.sh:221:metadata.platforms[\"linux-x86_64\"].archive = `nexus-linux-x86_64-${tag}.tar.gz`;\nscripts/installer-smoke.sh:225:UPGRADE_ARCHIVE=\"nexus-linux-x86_64-$UPGRADE_VERSION.tar.gz\"\nscripts/installer-smoke.sh:233:printf 'bad  %s\\n' \"nexus-linux-x86_64-$VERSION.tar.gz\" > \"$TMP/release/download/$VERSION/SHA256SUMS\"\nREADME.md:7:- **[Install and use Nexus Code](quickstart.md)** — supported platform, one-line installer, configuration, and first task.\nREADME.md:12:## Install Nexus Code\nREADME.md:17:curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/main/install.sh | sh\ndocs/DOCTOR_TROUBLESHOOTING.md:65:command-line flag → working-directory `.env` → `~/.config/nexus/config.env` → shell environment → installation\ndocs/DOCTOR_TROUBLESHOOTING.md:163:- `nexus doctor` diagnoses this installation; a different `nexus` on PATH is reported, not followed.\ndocs/PHASE2_RECONCILED_REQUIREMENTS.md:574:| **SCAN-004** | No known applicable HIGH or CRITICAL security vulnerability may survive in a supported release or deployment artifact. Documentation of a known High/Critical vulnerability does NOT constitute remediation; remediation, upgrade, or component removal is required. | Any release artifact containing an unresolved High or Critical CVE MUST be rejected at the release gate. |\ndocs/CLIENT_GUIDE.md:3:For binary installation and first run, start with the [quickstart](../quickstart.md). It documents the currently supported package target: Linux x86-64, glibc 2.35+, and Node.js 22+.\ndocs/PHASE2S_SECURITY_AND_DATA_REVIEW.md:285:- **Residual Exposure:** Network access during authorized package installations could still transmit data if an attacker controls build dependencies (mitigated by environment scrubbing and host-blind filesystem isolation).\ndocs/PHASE2S_SECURITY_AND_DATA_REVIEW.md:655:- **High/Critical Zero Tolerance:** No supported release artifact may contain an unresolved applicable High or Critical vulnerability. Documentation is not remediation; remediation, upgrade, or component elimination is required.\ndocs/PHASE3_IMPLEMENTATION_DECOMPOSITION.md:556:- **Release Gate:** High/Critical vulnerabilities block release artifacts; Medium/Low require documented dispositions.\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:376:The file is read only from the operator's home directory; a repository-level `nexus.config.json` cannot set operator policy. Unsupported fields, invalid values, symlinks and files larger than 64 KiB are rejected. Values resolve from the shell environment first, then `config.json`, then `config.env`, then built-in defaults. Existing `config.env` installations remain supported.\ndocs/PHASE2_REQUIREMENTS_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW.md:205:- **What Remains Implementation Choice:** Specific build tool flags, compiler cache configuration, and release artifact packaging scripts.\ndocs/ISSUE12_FINAL_ACCEPTANCE_MATRIX.md:110:| SCAN-004 | 18: Security Scanning | No known applicable HIGH or CRITICAL security vulnerability may survive in a supported release or deployment artifact. Documentation of a known High/Critical vulnerability does NOT constitute remediation; remediation, upgrade, or component removal is required. | Any release artifact containing an unresolved High or Critical CVE MUST be rejected at the release gate. | Phase 2 §22 | `scripts/security_gates.sh, scripts/audit_rust_deps.py`; cli/test/security_gates.test.ts, make test | DEMONSTRATED | None | Satisfied |\ndocs/DEVELOPMENT.md:27:bash scripts/smoke-package.sh \"./release/nexus-linux-x86_64-$NEXUS_VERSION.tar.gz\"\ndocs/DEVELOPMENT.md:30:Packaging builds the Rust binaries inside the approved, digest-pinned builder image (`APPROVED_RUST_BUILD_IMAGE` in the `Makefile`) and requires Docker. Unless `NEXUS_ALLOW_HOST_RUST_BUILD=1` is set, `scripts/package-linux.sh` exits with status 2 if `NEXUS_BUILD_CONTAINER_IMAGE` is unset; it always exits with status 2 if the variable names any other image. `make verify-reproducibility` builds the package twice with that image and compares the archive, `SHA256SUMS`, notices, SBOM and `install.sh` byte for byte. For a local, non-release build only, setting `NEXUS_ALLOW_HOST_RUST_BUILD=1` with `NEXUS_BUILD_CONTAINER_IMAGE` unset builds with the host Rust toolchain instead; if the image variable is set, packaging still uses the container and still rejects any non-approved image. A host-built package is not a release candidate.\ndocs/DEVELOPMENT.md:38:- `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/main/install.sh`\ndocs/UPGRADE_SECURITY.md:9:The self-upgrade mechanism enables operators to update their active Nexus installation to newer (or pinned) published releases directly from the CLI or TUI. Because executable updates run with the user's execution privileges and can replace core harness and TUI binaries, rigorous boundary enforcement is mandatory:\ndocs/UPGRADE_SECURITY.md:16:   - Malicious release archives attempting to write outside the isolated installation directory via `../` path traversal, absolute paths, escaping symlinks, devices, or hardlinks.\ndocs/UPGRADE_SECURITY.md:24:   - Accidental overwriting of installations managed by OS package managers (e.g. `apt`, `brew`, `npm`).\ndocs/UPGRADE_SECURITY.md:33:  - GitHub release asset CDN: `https://objects.githubusercontent.com/`\ndocs/UPGRADE_SECURITY.md:61:- Managed installations are distinguished from development checkouts (`git pull && make build`) and package-manager distributions (`apt`, `brew`).\ndocs/UPGRADE_SECURITY.md:62:- Self-upgrade refuses to overwrite package-manager installations, directing the user to their package manager.\ndocs/UPGRADE_SECURITY.md:98:         subject-path: 'nexus-linux-x86_64-*.tar.gz'\ndocs/UPGRADE_SECURITY.md:111:Replacement package backups are recorded before renaming as `$PREFIX/lib/nexus/.rollback-<transaction-id>`, outside disposable staging. Same-version repairs retain the real previous package for explicit binary rollback. Journal writes and rename boundaries are flushed before reporting completion. Recovery validates the complete source runtime and only records `rolled_back` after restoring and verifying the installation/link. Failure retains staging and package artifacts under `recovery_required` and returns a nonzero operational error; it never reports successful rollback after a failed restore. A previously verified target may be finalized only after another complete runtime check.\ndocs/CLOUDFLARE_CONTEST.md:65:**Reproducibility status: blocked pending clean-account acceptance.** Resource identity is now configurable in the demo adapter and Worker rather than pinned to the recorded account. However, the included protected broker installer is still an operator-specific upgrade bundle: it requires a prior root-owned `/opt/nexus-cloudflare-broker` installation, a host-specific runtime/manifest, and credential files provisioned outside the repository. Its launcher clears inherited configuration, so the new per-run configuration has not yet been proven through that installed broker. The restricted validator also requires Linux `sudo`, `setpriv`, `node`, and `tsc` with the specific no-capability UID 65534 boundary. The repo does not yet provide a clean judge bootstrap for those components. The commands above can typecheck and deploy the Worker, but they do not establish a complete fresh-account run. Do not treat local synthetic broker tests or offline fixtures as Cloudflare-backed evidence.\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-04-nexus-tui-live-spectator.md:5:**Goal:** `nexus-tui --live` (and `harness --live`) starts the phase-1 Node sidecar, renders its protocol events as a live full-screen session (status strip, streaming transcript, one-line tool calls, truthful turn banner), and accepts prompts through a minimal composer.\ndocs/WP11_INDEPENDENT_QUALIFICATION.md:142:- **Assessment:** Pre-commit and release boundaries are fully protected: untracked files cannot enter a committed candidate or release artifact without being tracked/staged, at which point `git grep -EI` evaluates them.\ndocs/security/2026-10-18-sharp-remediation.md:27:The vulnerable dependencies are outside the Nexus client packaging input; that source observation does not replace exact-release artifact/SBOM scanning. Alerts remain open until the default branch contains the fixed locks and GitHub rescans it. Do not dismiss the alerts to manufacture closure or bypass required checks.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0.md:153:- Reinstallation validates the installed tree against `MANIFEST.sha256` and automatically repairs damaged installations, or forces re-extraction with `NEXUS_FORCE=1`.\ndocs/releases/v0.1.0-alpha.1.md:21:- `nexus-linux-x86_64-v0.1.0-alpha.1.tar.gz`\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.8.md:14:- **Upgrade reliability:** GitHub release downloads now follow its signed release-asset redirect without forwarding GitHub credentials to the asset host. Large pre-migration backups report aggregate progress and avoid redundant directory syncs while retaining file and directory durability.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.12.md:9:This release packages the Nexus Code Linux x86-64 client: the TypeScript CLI and sidecar, production Node dependencies, Rust `harness-core`, and Ratatui `nexus-tui`. It supersedes RC11 because a power-loss test found that an interrupted upgrade could leave the installation unable to start. Everything in the [RC11 notes](v1.0.0-rc.11.md) is included.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.12.md:16:- **Installer durability:** `install.sh` now syncs after the verified extraction, before repointing the launcher, and after the switch. Re-running the installer over a working installation had the same 0-byte launcher exposure.\ndocs/releases/v0.1.0-alpha.2.md:47:- `nexus-linux-x86_64-v0.1.0-alpha.2.tar.gz`\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_ACCEPTANCE_BLOCKERS_2026-10-08.md:310:  `HOME`. A one-line project `.env` therefore re-opens both vectors that I6 claims are closed.\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_ACCEPTANCE_BLOCKERS_2026-10-08.md:362:reachable with a one-line project `.env`. It does not block running the unchanged dogfood path, which has no such\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_APPLICATION_MATURITY_REVIEW_2026-10-12.md:13:**Overall verdict: strong feature and internal-control maturity; operational/product maturity remains unproven.** Highest priorities are (1) define and enforce a deliberate trust/egress policy, (2) validate packaging and release artifacts from clean builds, (3) strengthen migration/compatibility and recovery testing, and (4) establish measurable reliability/telemetry and support practices. These are gaps or evidence gaps, not assertions that every mechanism is absent.\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_APPLICATION_MATURITY_REVIEW_2026-10-12.md:29:**Maturity gap:** Reproducible release builds, artifact provenance/signing, SBOM completeness/schema validation, installation/upgrade/uninstall tests, and a supported platform matrix are not established by the inspected evidence. Avoid overstating package contents or security properties.\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_APPLICATION_MATURITY_REVIEW_2026-10-12.md:51:The maturity fixes report extensive targeted tests and pseudo-terminal evidence, and the doctor work provides bounded diagnostics and repairs. These are strong feature-specific signals. They do not provide product-level reliability measures (crash-free sessions, recovery success, provider error rates, latency, cost, or safe cancellation) across representative installations.\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_APPLICATION_MATURITY_REVIEW_2026-10-12.md:57:### P2 — Product lifecycle: installation, upgrades, configuration, and recovery UX\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_APPLICATION_MATURITY_REVIEW_2026-10-12.md:61:**Maturity gap:** Prove the canonical installation path end to end, including fresh install, PATH resolution, native Rust binary selection, configuration precedence, upgrade with existing sessions/state, downgrade/rollback, and uninstall. Document supported environments and configuration precedence in one authoritative place.\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_APPLICATION_MATURITY_REVIEW_2026-10-12.md:84:This review is based on inspected repository files and dated assessment artifacts, not a fresh full test/build run, independent penetration test, or package installation exercise. The checkout status was previously observed clean during this session. Several observations are explicitly evidence gaps: absence of proof in the inspected materials is not proof that no implementation exists. The cloud/provider assessment is dated 2026-10-11 and must be revalidated against current source before treating its particulars as current facts. No defects were reproduced during this read-only review.\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_DOGFOODING_READINESS_REVIEW_2026-10-03.md:99:| Agent/profile selection | none per-task; one agent. Planner/coder tiers only via `--planner-*/--coder-*`, first-turn routing | partial | one-line \"Dual-Model Routing\" banner |\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_DOGFOODING_READINESS_REVIEW_2026-10-03.md:409:config-precedence change (B-10, a one-line decision for the operator); changing the security gate scripts (C-1 fix belongs in the test's environment).\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-04-nexus-tui-phase3b-slash-commands.md:40:- **Default entry.** `harness` with no arguments execs the live TUI when `core/target/release/nexus-tui` exists and both stdin and stdout are terminals; otherwise it runs the REPL (with a one-line note on stderr when the TUI is not built). `harness --repl [options]` runs the REPL. `harness --live [sidecar options]` stays.\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:27:| Published package used for installer checks | `v0.1.0-alpha.2` (`a2e94f3`). Assets: `nexus-linux-x86_64-v0.1.0-alpha.2.tar.gz` and `SHA256SUMS`. Installed in scratch HOMEs, plus the operator's existing `~/.local/lib/nexus/v0.1.0-alpha.2` (read only). |\ndocs/cloudflare/BROKERAGE_TRUST_ROOT_INSTALL_PLAN_2026-10-02.md:7:No credential operation, privileged installation, or experiment was run. This\ndocs/cloudflare/BROKERAGE_TRUST_ROOT_INSTALL_PLAN_2026-10-02.md:41:for that helper. Extracting auth through the current mutable `cf` installation\ndocs/cloudflare/BROKERAGE_TRUST_ROOT_INSTALL_PLAN_2026-10-02.md:60:installation. It must include a static native launcher, dedicated trusted\ndocs/cloudflare/BROKERAGE_TRUST_ROOT_INSTALL_PLAN_2026-10-02.md:64:installation must establish provenance from verified upstream artifacts and\ndocs/cloudflare/BROKERAGE_TRUST_ROOT_INSTALL_PLAN_2026-10-02.md:72:## Operator installation gate\ndocs/cloudflare/BROKERAGE_TRUST_ROOT_INSTALL_PLAN_2026-10-02.md:117:credential-free source cannot be staged. The exact privileged installation\ndocs/cloudflare/BROKERAGE_TRUST_ROOT_INSTALL_PLAN_2026-10-02.md:127:After operator installation, and before real token creation:\ndocs/cloudflare/BROKERAGE_TRUST_ROOT_INSTALL_PLAN_2026-10-02.md:169:the bundle before installation, disables npm lifecycle scripts, verifies npm\ndocs/cloudflare/BROKERAGE_TRUST_ROOT_INSTALL_PLAN_2026-10-02.md:194:source/test evidence. No actual protected installation, auth check, mutation\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_POST_REMEDIATION_DOGFOOD_QUALIFICATION.md:230:- It needs a planted symlink resolving to the real token, so it is narrower than the original one-line vector, but\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:76:| REQ-REL-001 | quickstart | Installer: non-root; SHA-256 verified; no shell-rc edits; refuses a foreign `nexus`; atomic symlink swap; failure leaves HOME untouched. | `install.sh` | RT (E §4); TEST installer-smoke | tested | N | — | ACC-PKG-05 | K | SPEC-06 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:78:| REQ-REL-003 | DEVELOPMENT.md; DEC-12 | Supported platform: Linux x86-64, glibc ≥ 2.35, Node ≥ 22. Clear failure messages elsewhere. | `install.sh`, doctor, upgrade preflight | Runtime/workflow source candidate `7c46a6d52095588f48579d9a96c5b2d526bdb3d9` passed PR #150 exact CI run `39866110578` (Node 22, Node 24, and `linux-x86_64`) and CodeQL `39866110533`; focused `node_floor.test.ts` passed 6/6 on Node 24. Installed-RC platform qualification E2 remains pending. | partial | N | Installed-RC platform qualification E2 remains pending. | ACC-PLAT | RR | SPEC-07 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:79:| REQ-REL-004 | quickstart | Upgrade and rollback by re-running the installer with a tag. Manual uninstall keeps user data. | `install.sh` | RT (alpha.1→2→1) | tested | N | Reinstall does not repair (REL-10) | ACC-PKG-05 | K | SPEC-06 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:190:| REQ-REL-105 | Audit | Installer: strict tag check, clear no-stable message, repair on reinstall, quiet output. | onboarding | `install.sh` | TEST (ACC-PKG-05; test:scripts/installer-smoke.sh) | tested | ACC-PKG-05 | RR | REL-08, REL-10, REL-11, REL-12 | SPEC-06 / PLAN-06 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:198:| REQ-REL-109 | TOP_TIER D4 | Provenance attestation; tag-pinned installer asset. | supply chain | `release.yml` | TEST (ACC-SUP-03; test:release.yml, install.sh) | tested | ACC-SUP-03 | RR | REL-09 | SPEC-07 / PLAN-07 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:205:| REQ-REL-116 | Scope addition | Machine-readable compatibility metadata, download origin & archive extraction safety, pre-migration backups, downgrade state protection, durable provenance, crash recovery, and runtime verification. | installation integrity & lifecycle | `cli/src/upgrade.ts`, `cli/src/compatibility.ts`, `cli/src/tar_safety.ts`, `cli/src/upgrade_journal.ts`, `docs/UPGRADE_SECURITY.md` | TEST (ACC-UPG-07 to ACC-UPG-14; test:cli/test/upgrade_safety.test.ts::\"rejects malicious tar archive with path traversal\", test:cli/test/upgrade_safety.test.ts::\"creates protected config and state backups with 0600 file and 0700 dir permissions\", test:cli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts::\"upgrades from previous release v0.1.0-alpha.2 to v1.0.0 preserving state, configuration and permissions\", test:cli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts::\"refuses downgrade when target release has incompatible state schema version\") | tested | ACC-UPG-07 to ACC-UPG-14 | **B** | REL-15 | SPEC-12 / PLAN-12 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:74:| `harness.sh`, `install.sh`, `scripts/package-linux.sh`, `.github/workflows/*` | 05, 06, 07, 09, C1 | Claim required. Workflow edits are separate commits. |\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:106:| Q7 product | **FAILS** | doctor with safe repairs; security gates (npm/cargo audit, secret scan); SBOM script | no build identity (D1); no CI (D2); dev checkout = installation (D3); no LICENSE/SECURITY/CHANGELOG, partial reproducibility (D4); Linux-only (D6); tracked transcript (D5) |\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:211:well; defects include ~25 empty rows in a one-line approval, the change card drawn before its \"approved\" line, wrapped\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:231:REPRODUCED · D2 no CI and no remote, P1 · D3 installation is the dev checkout (no versioned install/upgrade/rollback),\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-06-packaged-product-parity.md:65:- **Commander default action** (`cli/src/index.ts:745-757`). With no args, if `process.stdin.isTTY && process.stdout.isTTY` and `nexus-tui` resolves (`NEXUS_HOME/lib/core/nexus-tui`, or `<repo>/core/target/release/nexus-tui`), `execFileSync`/`spawn` it with `--live --sidecar <resolved> --node process.execPath -- <args>` and `stdio: inherit`, and exit with its code. Otherwise fall back to the REPL with a one-line notice.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:27:4. **Installed-RC qualification.** Install the workflow-produced RC package using the documented procedure and run the applicable product, provider, task-quality, terminal, installation, and independent-acceptance gates in §§4–8. Bind each result to both the RC source commit and installed package digest. If a source change or rebuilt artifact changes either identity, rerun every affected gate against the new candidate and retain prior results as historical evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:28:5. **Stable promotion and publication.** After exact-RC acceptance and G6 pass, create a stable-version commit directly on the accepted RC commit, changing only the synchronized version metadata required for v1.0.0. Record both commits and the version-only diff. Run required source CI and all applicable source G0–G4 checks on this exact stable-version commit before tagging. If any other source changes, restart RC construction and qualification. Then create the `v1.0.0` tag on that checked commit and build a draft release. Keep its assets unpublished while verifying the stable artifact identity, provenance, package contents, installation, and publication metadata. Compare the stable package contents with the accepted RC; if packaged behavior or content differs beyond version-specific metadata, rerun affected installed-RC qualification gates and obtain independent acceptance for the stable artifact. Publish the draft only after these checks pass and the signed acceptance disposition is recorded. Record the published digests and provenance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:65:2. All qualification runs use the **installed RC package**, installed with the documented one-line command. They never use a checkout build. The only exception is CI unit and PTY suites, which run from source at the same commit.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:275:| Fresh install, each image with Node ≥ 22 | Documented one-line command with `NEXUS_VERSION=<rc>`, then the no-version command after v1.0.0 is published | Installed. `nexus --version` equals the RC. `nexus doctor` shows no version warning and an empty stderr. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:284:| Upgrade crash recovery | `nexus upgrade --recover` | Idempotent recovery. Cleans incomplete staging, restores unverified launcher symlink, verifies functional installation. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:286:| Incompatible downgrade | `nexus upgrade --version <v> --allow-downgrade` (incompatible state schema) | Refused fail-closed with actionable state schema explanation. Existing installation unchanged. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:324:| CON-A3 | On a clean VM, `install.sh --fresh` followed by `post-install-qualify.py` passes. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:69:**Requirements and qualification:** Current-main CI's requirements checker passes; the most recent explicit `--enforce` result was on PR #302 head `c3901774` before the nested-workspace-only follow-up: 123 rows, 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open, with 12 requirements deferred to installed-RC qualification. RC10 has scope-limited exact-artifact evidence: OpenRouter pinned-model verification and one synthetic live task passed, and the cross-runner workflow passed for the six listed release artifacts across Ubuntu 22.04/24.04 and against published RC10 (run [40564959805](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40564959805)). A later checkpoint correction incorrectly claimed this workflow failed because of an npm-version mismatch. That correction is superseded: GitHub records run `40564959805` and its `compare` job as completed successfully; the current checkpoint above reports that final result. This historical correction is retained here to preserve the audit trail. These results apply only to immutable RC10 source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`; they do not qualify a successor candidate or establish full release acceptance. The newly pushed #302 head must complete exact checks before its requirements evidence is refreshed. Public [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) remains the latest release; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. GitHub installer is the selected distribution target; npm publication is inapplicable.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:151:**RC10 reproducibility scope:** PR [#281](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/281) recorded the successful exact-tag run [40564959805](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40564959805); PR [#282](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/282) clarified that the comparison established byte identity for the six listed release artifacts across Ubuntu 22.04/24.04 and against the published RC10. It does not claim byte identity for every build output. This evidence is bound to immutable RC10 source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`; any successor source needs its own exact-tag reproducibility run.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:250:**RC10 installation and terminal preparation:** Public [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) remains an unaccepted prerelease from `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`; Linux x86_64 archive SHA-256 is `444d0812ad583b7f688890ac8536cb872e92364c977d9fbf298fa0408d98b3e7`. The linked [RC10 desktop preflight record](../reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-manual-preflight/README.md) documents successful provenance-verified installation to an isolated qualification prefix on `ubuntu-desktop` (`10.0.8.3`), with CLI identity `1.0.0-rc.10 (16ee8ca36438)`. xterm, kitty, GNOME Terminal, tmux, and VS Code are present. This prepares the host only: the human matrix remains **0/15**. The operator must perform each of the five terminal environments at all three sizes and provide two genuine screenshots and a verdict per cell; scripted PTY evidence does not substitute.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:276:**RC10 artifact boundary:** The latest published prerelease is [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10), built from `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`, not current main. Its Linux archive SHA-256 is `444d0812ad583b7f688890ac8536cb872e92364c977d9fbf298fa0408d98b3e7`. Previously completed RC10 artifact, installation, provenance and cross-runner checks apply only to that immutable artifact. Scripted terminal coverage remains partial; the required manual real-terminal matrix is 0/15. No exact-RC acceptance is established. Further source changes require constructing and qualifying a new candidate.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:295:**RC9 artifact and installation record:** Tag object `d211d1c7545d2dd629531e4f712e98a240a782c6` targets the source above. Local `git verify-tag` reports a good signature; GitHub reports source-commit verification `verified: true, reason: valid` and tag-object verification `verified: false, reason: bad_email`. Release workflow [40370485753](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40370485753) succeeded and published RC9 as a prerelease. All nine downloaded assets matched GitHub Release API digests. `SHA256SUMS` covers the archive and `compatibility.json` (both entries verified), and `gh attestation verify` passed for the archive and checksum index. The archive was installed in an isolated prefix and reports `1.0.0-rc.9 (4cae11cbc3b0)`. Full artifact details remain in [RC9 artifact verification](evidence/rc9_artifact_install.md). This is artifact/install evidence, not product acceptance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:334:**RC8 upgrade diagnosis and installed artifact:** The attempted RC6-to-RC7 upgrade failed because RC7's updater rejects GitHub's signed release-asset redirect; its error also included the full signed URL. The published RC8 source and packaged upgrade.js accept HTTPS only for the restricted GitHub release-asset path and report only the origin on errors. On the local mike-dev installation, nexus --version reports 1.0.0-rc.8 (bbafae868939) under isolated HOME; the installed package manifest passes, and its recorded archive digest matches the published RC8 Linux archive digest sha256:bbded963a9bcaa9c0764b86d900f752c46ed364bfe30cc67e5bbf23b5fb5f48e. The downloaded archive and SHA256SUMS both passed gh attestation verify; the archive checksum matched the release index. A synthetic runtime probe of the installed RC8 validator accepted the release-asset path and rejected a generic path and HTTP. These checks establish the RC8 fix and this install's integrity; they are not a qualification run. RC8 remains based on bbafae868939084ccd49f21621695dff6b05f752, before current main, so it is not the exact candidate for current-source acceptance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:356:**RC8 construction and reproducibility:** Public prerelease [v1.0.0-rc.8](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.8) was published at 07:26 UTC and resolves to the exact source commit above. Its Linux archive has GitHub asset digest `sha256:bbded963a9bcaa9c0764b86d900f752c46ed364bfe30cc67e5bbf23b5fb5f48e`. Cross-runner RC reproducibility workflow [40286712425](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40286712425) completed successfully against that exact tag, including Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 builds and artifact comparison. An installed RC8 copy was also provenance-verified on the Ubuntu desktop in an isolated qualification prefix ([setup record](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/3#issuecomment-6411066559)); this was not the user's normal Nexus installation and is not full installed-RC acceptance. The tag's local GPG signature verifies, but GitHub reports it as unverified (`bad_email`); the stable tag must use a signer identity that GitHub verifies against the signing key. The earlier RC6-to-RC7 upgrade attempt failed because RC6 rejected GitHub's signed release-asset redirect. The redirect allowlist and URL-secret redaction are present in RC8; the RC6 installation was not changed by the isolated RC8 check.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:366:**RC and publication state:** The latest public prerelease remains `v1.0.0-rc.7`; `v1.0.0-rc.8` is not yet tagged or published. No stable `v1.0.0` release exists. The `rc.8` source version is not itself evidence of an accepted or installed RC. No release artifact should be published until every required acceptance gate passes.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:439:**RC7 artifact evidence:** The tag's release workflow produced the public assets and attestations. `gh attestation verify` passed for both the archive and `SHA256SUMS` under the exact repository, workflow, tag, and source constraints; the checksum-index attestation is [59728626](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/attestations/59728626). Cross-runner workflow [40248074777](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40248074777) passed on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04. Both manifests validated, and the archive, checksum manifest, notices, compatibility file, installer, and CycloneDX SBOM matched byte-for-byte across the two runner outputs and the public release. An isolated install reports `1.0.0-rc.7 (431cb194931f)`. These are artifact and installation checks, not product qualification.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:477:**RC3 artifact publication and provenance:** The annotated tag object is `dd68c222c57d0be0a4245a5b88092ff9df69201f`; its PGP signature verified good and it points to the source commit above. Release workflow [39927176480](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39927176480) completed successfully and published the [v1.0.0-rc.3 prerelease](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.3). The workflow-produced Linux x86-64 archive is `nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.0.0-rc.3.tar.gz`, SHA-256 `efb446d2760f2e1aa7890e9d786b8a2ba8e4ebb784fbcac1e66afe827428864d`; `SHA256SUMS` is `9288edb4655a19caa40e1598c0a642ab7f7e93aafbb187c2bfc8cfa9e19f116f`; the CycloneDX SBOM is `3a3176b4b3890c1bc07fb7b3acd80f7372f043819e6a8b296346d014b07f9d3a`. Downloaded checksums and SBOM sidecars passed. GitHub attestations for the archive and `SHA256SUMS` verified against the Release workflow, run `39927176480`, tag `v1.0.0-rc.3`, and source `1b9791f`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:597:- **Version, RC, and publication:** Root and CLI package versions remain `0.1.0-alpha.2`. GitHub currently lists only alpha pre-releases `v0.1.0-alpha.1` and `v0.1.0-alpha.2`; no `v1.0.0-rc.N` artifact/tag or stable v1.0.0 tag, npm package, or GitHub release exists. Follow the staged lifecycle in `ACCEPTANCE.md`: pre-RC source gates, RC construction, artifact-bound R\n... command output truncated for persistence ...\nd leaves the previous installation untouched\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SCHEMA2_INTEGRATION/targeted-tests.tap:891:    ok 2 - fails closed on checks