berate approval is declined in TUI\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SCHEMA2_INTEGRATION/failed-long-tmp-tests.tap:859:    # Subtest: detects packaged installation from NEXUS_HOME layout\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SCHEMA2_INTEGRATION/failed-long-tmp-tests.tap:860:    ok 1 - detects packaged installation from NEXUS_HOME layout\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SCHEMA2_INTEGRATION/failed-long-tmp-tests.tap:876:    # Subtest: starts mock HTTP server for GitHub release endpoints\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SCHEMA2_INTEGRATION/failed-long-tmp-tests.tap:877:    ok 1 - starts mock HTTP server for GitHub release endpoints\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SCHEMA2_INTEGRATION/failed-long-tmp-tests.tap:923:    # Subtest: fails closed on checksum mismatch and leaves the previous installation untouched\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SCHEMA2_INTEGRATION/failed-long-tmp-tests.tap:924:    ok 2 - fails closed on checksum mismatch and leaves the previous installation untouched\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SCHEMA2_INTEGRATION/failed-long-tmp-tests.tap:960:    # Subtest: does not delete or corrupt working installation during same-version reinstall when package fails self-test\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SCHEMA2_INTEGRATION/failed-long-tmp-tests.tap:961:    ok 6 - does not delete or corrupt working installation during same-version reinstall when package fails self-test\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SCHEMA2_INTEGRATION/failed-long-tmp-tests.tap:1157:    # Subtest: writes and reads durable installation provenance record\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SCHEMA2_INTEGRATION/failed-long-tmp-tests.tap:1158:    ok 1 - writes and reads durable installation provenance record\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SCHEMA2_INTEGRATION/failed-long-tmp-tests.tap:1162:    # Subtest: detects package-manager installations and blocks self-upgrade\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SCHEMA2_INTEGRATION/failed-long-tmp-tests.tap:1163:    ok 2 - detects package-manager installations and blocks self-upgrade\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SCHEMA2_INTEGRATION/failed-long-tmp-tests.tap:1189:    # Subtest: accepts backup paths under HOME with a custom installation prefix\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SCHEMA2_INTEGRATION/failed-long-tmp-tests.tap:1190:    ok 4 - accepts backup paths under HOME with a custom installation prefix\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SCHEMA2_INTEGRATION/failed-long-tmp-tests.tap:1209:    # Subtest: recovers a crash during switching by reverting symlink to source installation\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SCHEMA2_INTEGRATION/failed-long-tmp-tests.tap:1210:    ok 8 - recovers a crash during switching by reverting symlink to source installation\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SCHEMA2_INTEGRATION/failed-long-tmp-tests.tap:1432:    # Subtest: leaves installation untouched when deliberate approval is declined in TUI\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SCHEMA2_INTEGRATION/failed-long-tmp-tests.tap:1433:    ok 4 - leaves installation untouched when deliberate approval is declined in TUI\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/REQ-REL-114-rc10-20261027/README.md:26:| `nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.0.0-rc.10.tar.gz` | `444d0812ad583b7f688890ac8536cb872e92364c977d9fbf298fa0408d98b3e7` |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/REQ-REL-114-rc10-20261027/README.md:31:| `install.sh` | `5620d56ef6f8d637fc102ae2c8ea3b055effbc4069243a2df68b67520b1e2302` |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/REQ-REL-114-rc10-20261027/repro-evidence.json:37:    \"install.sh\": \"5620d56ef6f8d637fc102ae2c8ea3b055effbc4069243a2df68b67520b1e2302\",\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/REQ-REL-114-rc10-20261027/repro-evidence.json:38:    \"nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.0.0-rc.10.tar.gz\": \"444d0812ad583b7f688890ac8536cb872e92364c977d9fbf298fa0408d98b3e7\",\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/handoff-codex-t4-acceptance-2026-10-17.md:40:- **Line 49 (`REQ-QUAL-105` row):** the documented conflict (\"DEC-05 says eight classes, ACCEPTANCE §6.2 lists nine\") is **resolved — nine classes retained** (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-17; SIGTERM/resume is the ninth class). What remains is unchanged: the ACCEPTANCE §6.2 one-line edit (above) and the frozen 9 × 5 execution evidence.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/independent-review-dec17.md:90:Issue 1 resolved (handoff or note covering READINESS.md). Issues 2-4 are one-line wording fixes that could ride along; 5 can be a follow-up.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/HELDOUT_CUSTODY/custody-report-2026-10-18.md:56:| `ho2-js-debug-03` | `setup` commits a one-line `is-buffer` shim (`Buffer.isBuffer`) because the pinned baseline's dependency is unavailable offline; regression runs the repo's full `test/test.js` with mocha globals stubbed | shim is semantically equivalent for Node Buffers; full suite exercised; recorded, accepted |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/publication-gating.md:5:| Scope | v1.0.0 release publication: RC and stable tags, GitHub releases, and release-adjacent GitHub state changes |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-12_LEGACY_POLICY/README.md:7:Fresh GitHub release-list inspection found only alpha.1 and alpha.2, each publishing a Linux x86_64 archive and SHA256SUMS. Public archives downloaded and published archive hashes verified; selected file identities retained in public-release-identities.json. Both contain leading-v VERSION values, no compatibility.json and no MANIFEST.sha256. Local historical tags declare CURRENT_STATE_SCHEMA_VERSION1 and Cargo package version1.2.1; declaration is not an executed binary observation. No legacy executable was run during this inspection. Legacy runtime verification must recognize only verified historical file identities, not a general component-version exception. Config/state schema1 is a bounded eligibility policy, not a claim that the legacy artifacts are v1-qualified.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/README.md:7:| Installer | release asset `install.sh`, SHA-256 `5620d56ef6f8d637fc102ae2c8ea3b055effbc4069243a2df68b67520b1e2302` (verified before the run) |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/README.md:28:`run-rc10-lifecycle.sh` runs one disposable Ubuntu 22.04 / Node 22 container through installer-driven version switches. Each install step calls the published `install.sh` with `NEXUS_VERSION`; this script does **not** exercise the `nexus upgrade` command.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/README.md:51:| Checksum tamper | Installer refused with `SHA-256 verification failed; no installation was changed.`; launcher symlink and synthetic state marker unchanged | [log](ubuntu-22-04-node22-checksum-tamper.log) |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/README.md:57:| Provenance attestation | `gh attestation verify nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.0.0-rc.10.tar.gz -R mikeholownych/nexus-code` exited 0 on the published archive (SHA-256 `444d0812…b3e7`) with a Sigstore bundle; `--format json` returned a 13,989-byte verification result | [log](attestation-rc10.log) |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/README.md:65:`lifecycle/prepare-incompatible-fixture.sh <rc10-archive> <out>` builds a synthetic `v1.0.0-rc.4` release from the published RC10 package (same contents, `compatibility.json` rewritten to declare state schema 1 and the rc.4 archive binding) and writes a local API JSON. `lifecycle/run-incompatible-downgrade.sh` installs RC10 in a container, serves the fixture locally, and asserts the refusal plus an unchanged installation. No published RC declares an older state schema (rc.5–rc.10 all declare 2), which is why the fixture is synthetic.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/README.md:74:cp install.sh /tmp/nexus-install.sh   # release asset v1.0.0-rc.10\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/ubuntu-24-04-node24.doctor.json:136:      \"explanation\": \"The `nexus` launcher on PATH is this packaged installation.\",\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/ubuntu-24-04-node24.doctor.json:138:        \"The nexus launcher resolves to this packaged installation.\"\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/run-rc10-lifecycle.sh:6:installer=/tmp/nexus-install.sh\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/run-rc10-lifecycle.sh:13:  --mount \"type=bind,src=$installer,dst=/tmp/nexus-install.sh,readonly\" \\\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/run-rc10-lifecycle.sh:19:  install() { NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=0 NEXUS_VERSION=\"$1\" sh /tmp/nexus-install.sh; }\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/ubuntu-22-04-node22.doctor.json:136:      \"explanation\": \"The `nexus` launcher on PATH is this packaged installation.\",\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/ubuntu-22-04-node22.doctor.json:138:        \"The nexus launcher resolves to this packaged installation.\"\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/debian-12-node24.doctor.json:136:      \"explanation\": \"The `nexus` launcher on PATH is this packaged installation.\",\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/debian-12-node24.doctor.json:138:        \"The nexus launcher resolves to this packaged installation.\"\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/ubuntu-22-04-node24.doctor.json:136:      \"explanation\": \"The `nexus` launcher on PATH is this packaged installation.\",\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/ubuntu-22-04-node24.doctor.json:138:        \"The nexus launcher resolves to this packaged installation.\"\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-12_PR-12a/validation.md:49:   - Deliberate approval interaction (`requestApproval`) exercised before modifying installation.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-12_PR-12a/validation.md:74:- **Fail-Closed Verification:** Downloaded archives are validated against release `SHA256SUMS` before any extraction or link switching. Tampered files trigger immediate cleanup and leave the existing installation active.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-08_PR-8a/verification.md:8:- HOME/XDG: a fresh temporary HOME was supplied for each build/test command; `CARGO_HOME` and `RUSTUP_HOME` pointed to the existing toolchain installations. The CLI runner created a second per-suite temporary HOME and exposed only the outer temporary HOME as `NEXUS_TEST_REAL_HOME`.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-08_PR-8a/verification.md:10:- Validation: `make test` passed: core 24/24, TUI 240/240, CLI 906/906, and all security lifecycle gates. The first test attempt preceded dependency installation and the required build, so the real-sidecar integration failed; after running the repository's CI setup sequence, the complete suite passed.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/fedora-40-node24.doctor.json:136:      \"explanation\": \"The `nexus` launcher on PATH is this packaged installation.\",\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/fedora-40-node24.doctor.json:138:        \"The nexus launcher resolves to this packaged installation.\"\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-UPGRADE-ATTESTATION-20261025/README.md:51:- `install.sh` still has the original fail-open pattern: it resolves `gh` with `command -v gh` and skips the whole\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/RELEASE-TAKEOVER/authorization-and-handoff.md:11:Authorization is distinct from acceptance. No RC or stable acceptance is granted by this record. Required CI, exact-RC installation/qualification, independent review, human terminal evidence, stable draft verification, protected-branch rules and immutable tags still apply. Failed or absent evidence remains failed or absent. No threshold, supported-platform claim, corpus policy or artifact identity is changed.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/fedora-40-node22.doctor.json:136:      \"explanation\": \"The `nexus` launcher on PATH is this packaged installation.\",\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/fedora-40-node22.doctor.json:138:        \"The nexus launcher resolves to this packaged installation.\"\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/ubuntu-24-04-node22.doctor.json:136:      \"explanation\": \"The `nexus` launcher on PATH is this packaged installation.\",\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/ubuntu-24-04-node22.doctor.json:138:        \"The nexus launcher resolves to this packaged installation.\"\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/debian-12-node22.doctor.json:136:      \"explanation\": \"The `nexus` launcher on PATH is this packaged installation.\",\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/debian-12-node22.doctor.json:138:        \"The nexus launcher resolves to this packaged installation.\"\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/run-rc10-e2-matrix.sh:6:installer=/tmp/nexus-install.sh\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/run-rc10-e2-matrix.sh:35:      --mount \"type=bind,src=$installer,dst=/tmp/nexus-install.sh,readonly\" \\\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/run-rc10-e2-matrix.sh:38:        if output=$(NEXUS_VERSION=\"$NEXUS_VERSION\" sh /tmp/nexus-install.sh 2>&1); then\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/run-rc10-e2-matrix.sh:58:    mounts=(--mount \"type=bind,src=$installer,dst=/tmp/nexus-install.sh,readonly\" --mount \"type=bind,src=$doctor_dir,dst=/evidence\")\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/run-rc10-e2-matrix.sh:69:        NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=0 NEXUS_VERSION=\"$NEXUS_VERSION\" sh /tmp/nexus-install.sh\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/lifecycle/run-checksum-tamper.sh:5:  --mount type=bind,src=/tmp/nexus-install.sh,dst=/tmp/nexus-install.sh,readonly \\\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/lifecycle/run-checksum-tamper.sh:10:    NEXUS_VERSION=v1.0.0-rc.10 sh /tmp/nexus-install.sh\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/lifecycle/run-c