{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T10:03:05.808Z","ordinal":527593,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0db389702a7164cc016ae46b587690819f852ba7f6fc9296ee","status":"completed","call_id":"call_f1daf63855e04e6c850374ab8f489bb9","name":"exec","input":"const r=await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"gh attestation verify --help | sed -n '1,75p'; gh auth status --hostname github.com 2>&1 | sed -E 's/(Token: ).*/\\\\1[redacted]/'\",\"workdir\":\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc14-artifact-verification\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":1200});text(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18c3d-7cdd-71d3-966d-f30f05df4fb0","create_time":1793354584.4798338}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T10:03:05.928Z","ordinal":527594,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18c3d-7cdd-71d3-966d-f30f05df4fb0","session_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","root_turn_id":"01a18c3d-7cdd-71d3-966d-f30f05df4fb0","response_id":"resp_0db389702a7164cc016ae46b55f430819f96d11b3d303fb7c5","usage":{"input_tokens":180936,"cached_input_tokens":179328,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":345,"reasoning_output_tokens":240,"total_tokens":181281},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":5221868,"cached_input_tokens":5191040,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":10260,"reasoning_output_tokens":5892,"total_tokens":5232128},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":9955749822,"cached_input_tokens":9850775040,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":28523622,"reasoning_output_tokens":16771054,"total_tokens":9984273444}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T10:03:07.851Z","ordinal":527595,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18c3d-7cdd-71d3-966d-f30f05df4fb0","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-405b5bdf-1807-490f-aee2-fdf776703f9b","process_id":"18786","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh attestation verify --help | sed -n '1,75p'; gh auth status --hostname github.com 2>&1 | sed -E 's/(Token: ).*/\\1[redacted]/'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/rc14-artifact-verification","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh attestation verify --help | sed -n '1,75p'; gh auth status --hostname github.com 2>&1 | sed -E 's/(Token: ).*/\\1[redacted]/'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"Verify the integrity and provenance of an artifact using its associated\ncryptographically signed attestations.\n\n## Understanding Verification\n\nAn attestation is a claim (i.e. a provenance statement) made by an actor\n(i.e. a GitHub Actions workflow) regarding a subject (i.e. an artifact).\n\nIn order to verify an attestation, you must provide an artifact and validate:\n* the identity of the actor that produced the attestation\n* the expected attestation predicate type (the nature of the claim)\n\nBy default, this command enforces the `https://slsa.dev/provenance/v1`\npredicate type. To verify other attestation predicate types use the\n`--predicate-type` flag.\n\nThe \"actor identity\" consists of:\n* the repository or the repository owner the artifact is linked with\n* the Actions workflow that produced the attestation (a.k.a the\n  signer workflow)\n\nThis identity is then validated against the attestation's certificate's\nSourceRepository, SourceRepositoryOwner, and SubjectAlternativeName\n(SAN) fields, among others.\n\nIt is up to you to decide how precisely you want to enforce this identity.\n\nAt a minimum, this command requires either:\n* the `--owner` flag (e.g. --owner github), or\n* the `--repo` flag (e.g. --repo github/example)\n\nThe more precisely you specify the identity, the more control you will\nhave over the security guarantees offered by the verification process.\n\nIdeally, the path of the signer workflow is also validated using the\n`--signer-workflow` or `--cert-identity` flags.\n\nPlease note: if your attestation was generated via a reusable workflow then\nthat reusable workflow is the signer whose identity needs to be validated.\nIn this situation, you must use either the `--signer-workflow` or\nthe `--signer-repo` flag.\n\nFor more options, see the other available flags.\n\n## Loading Artifacts And Attestations\n\nTo specify the artifact, this command requires:\n* a file path to an artifact, or\n* a container image URI (e.g. `oci://<image-uri>`)\n  * (note that if you provide an OCI URL, you must already be authenticated with\nits container registry)\n\nBy default, this command will attempt to fetch relevant attestations via the\nGitHub API using the values provided to `--owner` or  `--repo`.\n\nTo instead fetch attestations from your artifact's OCI registry, use the\n`--bundle-from-oci` flag.\n\nFor offline verification using attestations stored on disk (c.f. the download command)\nprovide a path to the `--bundle` flag.\n\nWhen you load attestations with `--bundle` or `--bundle-from-oci`, this command\ncompares the `--repo` or `--owner` value only with the repository and owner\nnames recorded in the attestation's certificate when the attestation was\ncreated. It cannot detect whether the repository or owner has since been\nrenamed, or whether a different repository or owner now uses that name. To\nconfirm that an attestation belongs to the repository or owner that currently\nhas the name, omit `--bundle` and `--bundle-from-oci` so that this command\nfetches attestations from the GitHub API.\n\n## Additional Policy Enforcement\n\nGiven the `--format=json` flag, upon successful verification this\ncommand will output a JSON array containing one entry per verified attestation.\n\ngithub.com\n  ✓ Logged in to github.com account mikeholownych (/home/mike/.config/gh/hosts.yml)\n  - Active account: true\n  - Git operations protocol: ssh\n  - Token: [redacted]\n  - Token scopes: 'admin:gpg_key', 'delete:packages', 'gist', 'project', 'read:org', 'repo', 'write:packages'\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":634288498}},"started_at_ms":1793354586216,"completed_at_ms":1793354587851}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T10:03:08.837Z","ordinal":527596,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18c43-62a5-7cd1-80e0-37b5f28475ca","call_id":"call_f1daf63855e04e6c850374ab8f489bb9","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Verify the integrity and provenance of an artifact using its associated\ncryptographically signed attestations.\n\n## Understanding Verification\n\nAn attestation is a claim (i.e. a provenance statement) made by an actor\n(i.e. a GitHub Actions workflow) regarding a subject (i.e. an artifact).\n\nIn order to verify an attestation, you must provide an artifact and validate:\n* the identity of the actor that produced the attestation\n* the expected attestation predicate type (the nature of the claim)\n\nBy default, this command enforces the `https://slsa.dev/provenance/v1`\npredicate type. To verify other attestation predicate types use the\n`--predicate-type` flag.\n\nThe \"actor identity\" consists of:\n* the repository or the repository owner the artifact is linked with\n* the Actions workflow that produced the attestation (a.k.a the\n  signer workflow)\n\nThis identity is then validated against the attestation's certificate's\nSourceRepository, SourceRepositoryOwner, and SubjectAlternativeName\n(SAN) fields, among others.\n\nIt is up to you to decide how precisely you want to enforce this identity.\n\nAt a minimum, this command requires either:\n* the `--owner` flag (e.g. --owner github), or\n* the `--repo` flag (e.g. --repo github/example)\n\nThe more precisely you specify the identity, the more control you will\nhave over the security guarantees offered by the verification process.\n\nIdeally, the path of the signer workflow is also validated using the\n`--signer-workflow` or `--cert-identity` flags.\n\nPlease note: if your attestation was generated via a reusable workflow then\nthat reusable workflow is the signer whose identity needs to be validated.\nIn this situation, you must use either the `--signer-workflow` or\nthe `--signer-repo` flag.\n\nFor more options, see the other available flags.\n\n## Loading Artifacts And Attestations\n\nTo specify the artifact, this command requires:\n* a file path to an artifact, or\n* a container image URI (e.g. `oci://<image-uri>`)\n  * (note that if you provide an OCI URL, you must already be authenticated with\nits container registry)\n\nBy default, this command will attempt to fetch relevant attestations via the\nGitHub API using the values provided to `--owner` or  `--repo`.\n\nTo instead fetch attestations from your artifact's OCI registry, use the\n`--bundle-from-oci` flag.\n\nFor offline verification using attestations stored on disk (c.f. the download command)\nprovide a path to the `--bundle` flag.\n\nWhen you load attestations with `--bundle` or `--bundle-from-oci`, this command\ncompares the `--repo` or `--owner` value only with the repository and owner\nnames recorded in the attestation's certificate when the attestation was\ncreated. It cannot detect whether the repository or owner has since been\nrenamed, or whether a different repository or owner now uses that name. To\nconfirm that an attestation belongs to the repository or owner that currently\nhas the name, omit `--bundle` and `--bundle-from-oci` so that this command\nfetches attestations from the GitHub API.\n\n## Additional Policy Enforcement\n\nGiven the `--format=json` flag, upon successful verification this\ncommand will output a JSON array containing one entry per verified attestation.\n\ngithub.com\n  ✓ Logged in to github.com account mikeholownych (/home/mike/.config/gh/hosts.yml)\n  - Active account: true\n  - Git operations protocol: ssh\n  - Token: [redacted]\n  - Token scopes: 'admin:gpg_key', 'delete:packages', 'gist', 'project', 'read:org', 'repo', 'write:packages'\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18c3d-7cdd-71d3-966d-f30f05df4fb0","create_time":1793354588.837219}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
