{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T10:03:12.118Z","ordinal":527601,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18c3d-7cdd-71d3-966d-f30f05df4fb0","session_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","root_turn_id":"01a18c3d-7cdd-71d3-966d-f30f05df4fb0","response_id":"resp_0db389702a7164cc016ae46b5e64e4819f9457da46d21be439","usage":{"input_tokens":182102,"cached_input_tokens":180864,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":118,"reasoning_output_tokens":31,"total_tokens":182220},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":5403970,"cached_input_tokens":5371904,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":10378,"reasoning_output_tokens":5923,"total_tokens":5414348},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":9955931924,"cached_input_tokens":9850955904,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":28523740,"reasoning_output_tokens":16771085,"total_tokens":9984455664}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T10:03:13.514Z","ordinal":527602,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18c3d-7cdd-71d3-966d-f30f05df4fb0","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-cbc3e515-6329-475b-a839-165045e550f3","process_id":"78034","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh attestation verify --help | rg -n -A5 -B3 'signer-workflow|cert-identity|format'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/rc14-artifact-verification","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh attestation verify --help | rg -n -A5 -B3 'signer-workflow|cert-identity|format'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"33-have over the security guarantees offered by the verification process.\n34-\n35-Ideally, the path of the signer workflow is also validated using the\n36:`--signer-workflow` or `--cert-identity` flags.\n37-\n38-Please note: if your attestation was generated via a reusable workflow then\n39-that reusable workflow is the signer whose identity needs to be validated.\n40:In this situation, you must use either the `--signer-workflow` or\n41-the `--signer-repo` flag.\n42-\n43-For more options, see the other available flags.\n44-\n45-## Loading Artifacts And Attestations\n--\n70-\n71-## Additional Policy Enforcement\n72-\n73:Given the `--format=json` flag, upon successful verification this\n74-command will output a JSON array containing one entry per verified attestation.\n75-\n76-This output can then be used for additional policy enforcement, i.e. by being\n77-piped into a policy engine.\n78-\n--\n109-an artifact, have the build and attestation signing occur within a reusable workflow\n110-whose execution cannot be influenced by input provided through the caller workflow.\n111-\n112:See above re: `--signer-workflow`.\n113-\n114:For more information about output formatting flags, see `gh help formatting`.\n115-\n116-USAGE\n117-  gh attestation verify [<file-path> | oci://<image-uri>] [--owner | --repo] [flags]\n118-\n119-FLAGS\n120-  -b, --bundle string                Path to bundle on disk, either a single bundle in a JSON file or a JSON lines file with multiple bundles\n121-      --bundle-from-oci              When verifying an OCI image, fetch the attestation bundle from the OCI registry instead of from GitHub\n122:      --cert-identity string         Enforce that the certificate's SubjectAlternativeName matches the provided value exactly\n123:  -i, --cert-identity-regex string   Enforce that the certificate's SubjectAlternativeName matches the provided regex\n124-      --cert-oidc-issuer string      Enforce that the issuer of the OIDC token matches the provided value (default \"https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com\")\n125-      --custom-trusted-root string   Path to a trusted_root.jsonl file; likely for offline verification\n126-      --deny-self-hosted-runners     Fail verification for attestations generated on self-hosted runners\n127-  -d, --digest-alg string            The algorithm used to compute a digest of the artifact: {sha256|sha512} (default \"sha256\")\n128:      --format string                Output format: {json}\n129-      --hostname string              Configure host to use\n130-  -q, --jq expression                Filter JSON output using a jq expression\n131-  -L, --limit int                    Maximum number of attestations to fetch (default 30)\n132-      --no-public-good               Do not verify attestations signed with Sigstore public good instance\n133-  -o, --owner string                 GitHub organization to scope attestation lookup by\n134-      --predicate-type string        Enforce that verified attestations' predicate type matches the provided value (default \"https://slsa.dev/provenance/v1\")\n135:  -R, --repo string                  Repository name in the format <owner>/<repo>\n136-      --signer-digest string         Enforce that the digest associated with the signer workflow matches the provided value\n137-      --signer-repo string           Enforce that the workflow that signed the attestation's repository matches the provided value (<owner>/<repo>)\n138:      --signer-workflow string       Enforce that the workflow that signed the attestation matches the provided value ([host/]<owner>/<repo>/<path>/<to>/<workflow>)\n139-      --source-digest string         Enforce that the digest associated with the source repository matches the provided value\n140-      --source-ref string            Enforce that the git ref associated with the source repository matches the provided value\n141:  -t, --template string              Format JSON output using a Go template; see \"gh help formatting\"\n142-\n143-INHERITED FLAGS\n144-  --help   Show help for command\n145-\n146-EXAMPLES\n--\n151-  $ gh attestation verify example.bin --owner github\n152-  \n153-  # Verify an artifact and output the full verification result\n154:  $ gh attestation verify example.bin --owner github --format json\n155-  \n156-  # Verify an OCI image using attestations stored on disk\n157-  $ gh attestation verify oci://<image-uri> --owner github --bundle sha256:foo.jsonl\n158-  \n159-  # Verify an artifact signed with a reusable workflow\n160-  $ gh attestation verify example.bin --owner github --signer-repo actions/example\n161-\n162-LEARN MORE\n163:  Use `gh <command> <subcommand> --help` for more information about a command.\n164-  Read the manual at https://cli.github.com/manual\n165-  Learn about exit codes using `gh help exit-codes`\n166-  Learn about accessibility experiences using `gh help accessibility`\n167-\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":22552596}},"started_at_ms":1793354592491,"completed_at_ms":1793354593514}}
