{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T10:03:35.166Z","ordinal":527622,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18c3d-7cdd-71d3-966d-f30f05df4fb0","session_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","root_turn_id":"01a18c3d-7cdd-71d3-966d-f30f05df4fb0","response_id":"resp_0db389702a7164cc016ae46b7594b8819f9b6a6bcd31360ab4","usage":{"input_tokens":184782,"cached_input_tokens":183552,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":149,"reasoning_output_tokens":34,"total_tokens":184931},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":5955395,"cached_input_tokens":5920384,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":11362,"reasoning_output_tokens":6295,"total_tokens":5966757},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":9956483349,"cached_input_tokens":9851504384,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":28524724,"reasoning_output_tokens":16771457,"total_tokens":9985008073}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T10:03:36.415Z","ordinal":527623,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18c3d-7cdd-71d3-966d-f30f05df4fb0","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-bdeeaed5-a3f2-437d-a733-b9f4b9f6b47f","process_id":"86230","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,65p' quickstart.md; sed -n '115,195p' install.sh; rg -n \"smoke-package|clean install|one-line installer\" docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md quickstart.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/rc14-artifact-verification","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,65p' quickstart.md","name":"quickstart.md","path":"quickstart.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '115,195p' install.sh","name":"install.sh","path":"install.sh"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'smoke-package|clean install|one-line installer' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md quickstart.md","query":"smoke-package|clean install|one-line installer","path":"ACCEPTANCE.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"failed","aggregated_output":"# Nexus Code quickstart\n\nNexus Code is a local coding client. It is separate from the Cloudflare Workers and Artifacts collaboration service in the contest entry.\n\n## Install\n\nOn Linux x86-64 with glibc 2.35 or newer and Node.js 22 or newer:\n\n```sh\ncurl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/main/install.sh | sh\n```\n\nThe installer downloads the matching versioned client archive and `SHA256SUMS` from this repository's GitHub Release, verifies the archive, and installs under `~/.local/lib/nexus`. It adds a `nexus` symlink in `~/.local/bin`; it does not edit shell startup files or use root. If `~/.local/bin` is not in `PATH`, add it yourself:\n\n```sh\nexport PATH=\"$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH\"\n```\n\nWithout `NEXUS_VERSION`, the installer follows the latest stable release. If no stable release has been published yet, the installer exits with a hint to select a prerelease tag from [GitHub Releases](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases). To install a prerelease or pin a version, set `NEXUS_VERSION` to its published tag. The `v1.0.0-rc.1` example below works after that tag appears on [GitHub Releases](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases); before then, replace it with a prerelease tag already listed there:\n\n```sh\ncurl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/main/install.sh | NEXUS_VERSION=v1.0.0-rc.1 sh\n```\n\nFor inspect-before-running, download [install.sh](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/main/install.sh), read it, then run `sh install.sh`.\n\nThe release package includes the TypeScript client, production Node dependencies, `harness-core`, and the Ratatui `nexus-tui` binary. Node is an external runtime prerequisite. Current release support is limited to Linux x86-64/glibc; macOS, Windows, ARM, musl, and other architectures are not claimed.\n\n## Configure an inference endpoint\n\nNexus works with an OpenAI-compatible local endpoint such as LM Studio or vLLM. Start that server and load a model first. For example:\n\n```sh\nmkdir -p \"$HOME/.config/nexus\"\nchmod 700 \"$HOME/.config/nexus\"\ncat > \"$HOME/.config/nexus/config.env\" <<'EOF'\nLOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:1234/v1\nLOCAL_LLM_MODEL=your-loaded-model\nLOCAL_LLM_API_KEY=REDACTED\nEOF\nchmod 600 \"$HOME/.config/nexus/config.env\"\n```\n\nUse your endpoint's actual model ID. Nexus automatically discovers the loaded context window from LM Studio (`/api/v0/models`), llama.cpp (`/props`), vLLM (`/v1/models`), and Ollama (`/api/show`), or you can override it with `--context-limit` (`NEXUS_CONTEXT_LIMIT`). For HTTPS servers using a private certificate authority, set `NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS=/path/to/ca.pem` in `~/.config/nexus/config.env`. Do not put real credentials in a project `.env`, shell history, or this example. See [Local servers](docs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md) for per-server setup and [Cloud providers](docs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md) for cloud provider and credential handling.\n\n## First run\n\nFrom a project directory:\n\n```sh\nnexus doctor\nnexus\n```\n\nEnter a small task, review requested actions, and inspect the reported turn outcome. On a terminal, running `nexus` with no arguments opens the live TUI; in non-interactive environments or with `nexus repl`, it opens the interactive REPL. For non-interactive tasks, run `nexus run \"<task>\"`. Use `nexus --help` and `/help` for implemented commands.\n\n### Folder trust and tool permissions\n\nBy default, Nexus opens in `review` posture, asking for your explicit confirmation before executing shell commands, file modifications, network egress, or test suites. Folder trust is separate: it controls whether project instructions and workspace integrations are loaded.\n\nIf this is your own repository and you want autonomous execution, trust it:\n\n```sh\nnexus trust .\n```\nNEEDS_EXTRACT=1\nif [ -d \"$VERSION_DIR\" ] && [ \"$FORCE\" != \"1\" ]; then\n  if [ -x \"$VERSION_DIR/bin/nexus\" ] && \\\n     [ -x \"$VERSION_DIR/lib/core/harness-core\" ] && \\\n     [ -x \"$VERSION_DIR/lib/core/nexus-tui\" ] && \\\n     [ \"$(cat \"$VERSION_DIR/VERSION\" 2>/dev/null || true)\" = \"$VERSION\" ]; then\n    if [ -f \"$VERSION_DIR/MANIFEST.sha256\" ]; then\n      if (cd \"$VERSION_DIR\" && sha256sum --check --status MANIFEST.sha256 2>/dev/null); then\n        NEEDS_EXTRACT=0\n      fi\n      if [ \"$NEEDS_EXTRACT\" = \"0\" ]; then\n        if ! node - \"$VERSION_DIR/.provenance.json\" \"$ARCHIVE_SHA256\" <<'NODE'\nconst fs = require(\"node:fs\");\nconst [file, archiveSha256] = process.argv.slice(2);\ntry {\n  const record = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(file, \"utf8\"));\n  if (record.archiveSha256 !== archiveSha256) process.exit(1);\n} catch { process.exit(1); }\nNODE\n        then\n          NEEDS_EXTRACT=1\n        fi\n      fi\n    fi\n  fi\nfi\n\nif [ \"$NEEDS_EXTRACT\" = \"1\" ]; then\n  mkdir -p \"$TMP/unpack\"\n  tar -xzf \"$TMP/$ARCHIVE\" -C \"$TMP/unpack\" || fail \"archive extraction failed.\"\n  PACKAGE=\"$TMP/unpack/nexus\"\n  [ -x \"$PACKAGE/bin/nexus\" ] && [ -x \"$PACKAGE/lib/core/harness-core\" ] && [ -x \"$PACKAGE/lib/core/nexus-tui\" ] && [ \"$(cat \"$PACKAGE/VERSION\" 2>/dev/null || true)\" = \"$VERSION\" ] || fail \"release archive is incomplete or has a mismatched version.\"\n  if [ -f \"$PACKAGE/MANIFEST.sha256\" ]; then\n    (cd \"$PACKAGE\" && sha256sum --check --status MANIFEST.sha256) || fail \"release archive failed manifest checksum verification.\"\n  fi\n  PACKAGE_VERSION_OUTPUT=$(\"$PACKAGE/bin/nexus\" --version 2>&1) || fail \"release binary failed its pre-install self-test.\"\n  PACKAGE_VERSION_REPORTED=$(printf '%s\\n' \"$PACKAGE_VERSION_OUTPUT\" | sed -n '1s/[[:space:]].*$//p')\n  [ \"$PACKAGE_VERSION_REPORTED\" = \"$NORMALIZED_VERSION\" ] || fail \"release binary reported version '$PACKAGE_VERSION_REPORTED' instead of '$NORMALIZED_VERSION' during self-test.\"\n  if [ -f \"$PACKAGE/compatibility.json\" ]; then\n    node - \"$PACKAGE/compatibility.json\" \"$VERSION\" \"$ARCHIVE\" <<'NODE' || fail \"release compatibility metadata is invalid or mismatched.\"\nconst fs = require(\"node:fs\");\nconst [file, version, archive] = process.argv.slice(2);\nconst data = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(file, \"utf8\"));\nconst asset = data.platforms?.[\"linux-x86_64\"];\nconst compatible = data.schemaVersion === 1 && data.product === \"nexus-code\" &&\n  data.version === version.replace(/^v/, \"\") &&\n  typeof data.revision === \"string\" && /^[a-f0-9]{7,64}$/i.test(data.revision) &&\n  typeof data.builtAt === \"string\" && !Number.isNaN(Date.parse(data.builtAt)) &&\n  asset?.archive === archive && asset.os === \"linux\" && asset.arch === \"x86_64\" &&\n  data.compatibility && Number.isSafeInteger(data.compatibility.configSchemaVersion) &&\n  Number.isSafeInteger(data.compatibility.stateSchemaVersion) &&\n  Number.isSafeInteger(data.compatibility.minSupportedConfigVersion) &&\n  Number.isSafeInteger(data.compatibility.minSupportedStateVersion) &&\n  data.compatibility.minSupportedConfigVersion <= data.compatibility.configSchemaVersion &&\n  data.compatibility.minSupportedStateVersion <= data.compatibility.stateSchemaVersion;\nif (!compatible) process.exit(1);\nNODE\n  fi\n  # A rename persists the directory entry, not file data: flush the extracted\n  # package before it replaces anything, or a power loss can leave 0-byte files.\n  sync\n  rm -rf \"$VERSION_DIR\"\n  mv \"$PACKAGE\" \"$VERSION_DIR\"\nfi\nnode - \"$VERSION_DIR/compatibility.json\" \"$VERSION\" \"$PREFIX\" \"$VERSION_DIR\" \"$LINK\" \"$ARCHIVE\" \"$ARCHIVE_SHA256\" \"$VERSION_DIR/.provenance.json\" <<'NODE'\nconst fs = require(\"node:fs\");\nconst [metadataPath, version, prefix, installedPath, binPath, archive, archiveSha256, output] = process.argv.slice(2);\nlet metadata = null;\ntry { metadata = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(metadataPath, \"utf8\")); } catch {}\nconst record = {\n  formatVersion: 1,\n  method: \"installer\",\n  product: \"nexus-code\",\n  version,\n  ...(metadata?.revision ? { revision: metadata.revision } : {}),\n  ...(metadata?.builtAt ? { builtAt: metadata.builtAt } : {}),\n  prefix,\n  installedPath,\n  binPath,\n  managed: true,\n  archive,\n","exit_code":1,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":904728020}},"started_at_ms":1793354615510,"completed_at_ms":1793354616415}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T10:03:36.619Z","ordinal":527624,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18c43-cf2b-7b11-b26f-20adb4abb060","call_id":"call_a9589a9a7b094a538051c7c039a87889","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.5 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 1974)\nTotal output lines: 146\n\n# Nexus Code quickstart\n\nNexus Code is a local coding client. It is separate from the Cloudflare Workers and Artifacts collaboration service in the contest entry.\n\n## Install\n\nOn Linux x86-64 with glibc 2.35 or newer and Node.js 22 or newer:\n\n```sh\ncurl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/main/install.sh | sh\n```\n\nThe installer downloads the matching versioned client archive and `SHA256SUMS` from this repository's GitHub Release, verifies the archive, and installs under `~/.local/lib/nexus`. It adds a `nexus` symlink in `~/.local/bin`; it does not edit shell startup files or use root. If `~/.local/bin` is not in `PATH`, add it yourself:\n\n```sh\nexport PATH=\"$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH\"\n```\n\nWithout `NEXUS_VERSION`, the installer follows the latest stable release. If no stable release has been published yet, the installer exits with a hint to select a prerelease tag from [GitHub Releases](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases). To install a prerelease or pin a version, set `NEXUS_VERSION` to its published tag. The `v1.0.0-rc.1` example below works after that tag appears on [GitHub Releases](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases); before then, replace it with a prerelease tag already listed there:\n\n```sh\ncurl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/main/install.sh | NEXUS_VERSION=v1.0.0-rc.1 sh\n```\n\nFor inspect-before-running, download [install.sh](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/main/install.sh), read it, then run `sh install.sh`.\n\nThe release package includes the TypeScript client, production Node dependencies, `harness-core`, and the Ratatui `nexus-tui` binary. Node is an external runtime prerequisite. Current release support is limited to Linux x86-64/glibc; macOS, Windows, ARM, musl, and other architectures are not claimed.\n\n## Configure an inference endpoint\n\nNexus works with an OpenAI-compatible local endpoint such as LM Studio or vLLM. Start that server and load a model first. For example:\n\n```sh\nmkdir -p \"$HOME/.config/nexus\"\nchmod 700 \"$HOME/.config/nexus\"\ncat > \"$HOME/.config/nexus/config.env\" <<'EOF'\nLOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:1234/v1\nLOCAL_LLM_MODEL=your-loaded-model\nLOCAL_LLM_API_KEY=REDACTED\nEOF\nchmod 600 \"$HOME/.config/nexus/config.env\"\n```\n\nUse your endpoint's actual model ID. Nexus automatically discovers the loaded context window from LM Studio (`/api/v0/models`), llama.cpp (`/props`), vLLM (`/v1/models`), and Ollama (`/api/show`), or you can override it with `--context-limit` (`NEXUS_CONTEXT_LIMIT`). For HTTPS servers using a private certificate authority, set `NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS=/path/to/ca.pem` in `~/.config/nexus/config.env`. Do not put real credentials in a project `.env`, shell history, or this example. See [Local servers](docs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md) for per-server setup and [Cloud providers](docs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md) for cloud provider and credential handling.\n\n## First run\n\nFrom a project directory:\n\n```sh\nnexus docto…474 tokens truncated… ] && [ -x \"$PACKAGE/lib/core/harness-core\" ] && [ -x \"$PACKAGE/lib/core/nexus-tui\" ] && [ \"$(cat \"$PACKAGE/VERSION\" 2>/dev/null || true)\" = \"$VERSION\" ] || fail \"release archive is incomplete or has a mismatched version.\"\n  if [ -f \"$PACKAGE/MANIFEST.sha256\" ]; then\n    (cd \"$PACKAGE\" && sha256sum --check --status MANIFEST.sha256) || fail \"release archive failed manifest checksum verification.\"\n  fi\n  PACKAGE_VERSION_OUTPUT=$(\"$PACKAGE/bin/nexus\" --version 2>&1) || fail \"release binary failed its pre-install self-test.\"\n  PACKAGE_VERSION_REPORTED=$(printf '%s\\n' \"$PACKAGE_VERSION_OUTPUT\" | sed -n '1s/[[:space:]].*$//p')\n  [ \"$PACKAGE_VERSION_REPORTED\" = \"$NORMALIZED_VERSION\" ] || fail \"release binary reported version '$PACKAGE_VERSION_REPORTED' instead of '$NORMALIZED_VERSION' during self-test.\"\n  if [ -f \"$PACKAGE/compatibility.json\" ]; then\n    node - \"$PACKAGE/compatibility.json\" \"$VERSION\" \"$ARCHIVE\" <<'NODE' || fail \"release compatibility metadata is invalid or mismatched.\"\nconst fs = require(\"node:fs\");\nconst [file, version, archive] = process.argv.slice(2);\nconst data = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(file, \"utf8\"));\nconst asset = data.platforms?.[\"linux-x86_64\"];\nconst compatible = data.schemaVersion === 1 && data.product === \"nexus-code\" &&\n  data.version === version.replace(/^v/, \"\") &&\n  typeof data.revision === \"string\" && /^[a-f0-9]{7,64}$/i.test(data.revision) &&\n  typeof data.builtAt === \"string\" && !Number.isNaN(Date.parse(data.builtAt)) &&\n  asset?.archive === archive && asset.os === \"linux\" && asset.arch === \"x86_64\" &&\n  data.compatibility && Number.isSafeInteger(data.compatibility.configSchemaVersion) &&\n  Number.isSafeInteger(data.compatibility.stateSchemaVersion) &&\n  Number.isSafeInteger(data.compatibility.minSupportedConfigVersion) &&\n  Number.isSafeInteger(data.compatibility.minSupportedStateVersion) &&\n  data.compatibility.minSupportedConfigVersion <= data.compatibility.configSchemaVersion &&\n  data.compatibility.minSupportedStateVersion <= data.compatibility.stateSchemaVersion;\nif (!compatible) process.exit(1);\nNODE\n  fi\n  # A rename persists the directory entry, not file data: flush the extracted\n  # package before it replaces anything, or a power loss can leave 0-byte files.\n  sync\n  rm -rf \"$VERSION_DIR\"\n  mv \"$PACKAGE\" \"$VERSION_DIR\"\nfi\nnode - \"$VERSION_DIR/compatibility.json\" \"$VERSION\" \"$PREFIX\" \"$VERSION_DIR\" \"$LINK\" \"$ARCHIVE\" \"$ARCHIVE_SHA256\" \"$VERSION_DIR/.provenance.json\" <<'NODE'\nconst fs = require(\"node:fs\");\nconst [metadataPath, version, prefix, installedPath, binPath, archive, archiveSha256, output] = process.argv.slice(2);\nlet metadata = null;\ntry { metadata = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(metadataPath, \"utf8\")); } catch {}\nconst record = {\n  formatVersion: 1,\n  method: \"installer\",\n  product: \"nexus-code\",\n  version,\n  ...(metadata?.revision ? { revision: metadata.revision } : {}),\n  ...(metadata?.builtAt ? { builtAt: metadata.builtAt } : {}),\n  prefix,\n  installedPath,\n  binPath,\n  managed: true,\n  archive,\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18c3d-7cdd-71d3-966d-f30f05df4fb0","create_time":1793354616.6195154}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
