{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T10:05:14.172Z","ordinal":527699,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18c3d-7cdd-71d3-966d-f30f05df4fb0","session_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","root_turn_id":"01a18c3d-7cdd-71d3-966d-f30f05df4fb0","response_id":"resp_0db389702a7164cc016ae46bd87bac819fb7f623c0855ebf97","usage":{"input_tokens":197960,"cached_input_tokens":197376,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":121,"reasoning_output_tokens":16,"total_tokens":198081},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":7689072,"cached_input_tokens":7639936,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":18507,"reasoning_output_tokens":11526,"total_tokens":7707579},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":9958217026,"cached_input_tokens":9853223936,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":28531869,"reasoning_output_tokens":16776688,"total_tokens":9986748895}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T10:05:15.660Z","ordinal":527700,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18c3d-7cdd-71d3-966d-f30f05df4fb0","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-67318b05-11b1-40db-8615-8d353294a081","process_id":"95415","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '85,150p' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md; sed -n '1,100p' docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-07*"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/rc14-artifact-verification","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"sed -n '85,150p' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md; sed -n '1,100p' docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-07*"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"## 3. Gate checklist (G0–G4: automated acceptance IDs)\n\nEvery ACC ID below is defined in the linked spec. The plan for each spec names the test that implements it. Run each check at the lifecycle stage dictated by its acceptance method in §1.1: source-applicable checks before the RC tag; checks requiring the RC archive, attestation, release, or installed package after RC construction; environment-specific checks in their declared environment. Bind every result to the exact source commit and, when artifact-dependent, the RC package digest. A source test or local build does not replace an artifact-bound check, and no G0–G4 ID is complete until all of its applicable checks pass.\n\n| Gate | Acceptance IDs | Spec |\n|---|---|---|\n| Safety | ACC-SAFE-01 to ACC-SAFE-10 | SPEC-01 |\n| Process ownership | ACC-PROC-01 to ACC-PROC-08 (ACC-PROC-07 is the load test, run in E3) | SPEC-02 |\n| Untrusted inputs | ACC-TRUST-01 to ACC-TRUST-09 | SPEC-03 |\n| Continuity | ACC-CONT-01 to ACC-CONT-09 (ACC-CONT-10 is in §8) | SPEC-04 |\n| Inference | ACC-INF-01 to ACC-INF-09 (ACC-INF-10 is in §4) | SPEC-05 |\n| Packaging | ACC-PKG-01 to ACC-PKG-09 | SPEC-06 |\n| Supply chain | ACC-SUP-01 to ACC-SUP-08 (artifact-bound ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08 after RC construction) | SPEC-07 |\n| Persistence | ACC-PER-01 to ACC-PER-07 | SPEC-08 |\n| Governance | ACC-GOV-01 to ACC-GOV-06 | SPEC-09 |\n| Verification | ACC-VER-01 to ACC-VER-09 | SPEC-11 |\n| Upgrade | ACC-UPG-01 to ACC-UPG-14 | SPEC-12 |\n\n\n### 3.1 Acceptance IDs defined in this file\n\nThese are retained commitments from REQUIREMENTS §2 and cross-cutting checks.\n\n| ID | Check | Pass condition |\n|---|---|---|\n| ACC-TUI-STEER | PTY: submit a task; while a tool runs, type steering text and press Enter; also queue a steer before a cancel | Steering is applied at the next step boundary. Unapplied steering is returned to the composer. Nothing is dropped silently (existing `sidecar_steering_diff` plus PTY s6). |\n| ACC-TUI-A11Y | PTY with `NO_COLOR=1` and with `TERM=dumb` at 40×14 and 100×30 | Zero colour SGR codes. Every state is distinguishable by glyph and word. Hints are complete at 40 columns (TUI-10). |\n| ACC-SEC-JAIL | `core/tests` plus harness-core calls with `..`, absolute, symlinked-file, symlinked-dir and symlinked-parent payloads | Every one is refused (C §4 R1 set). |\n| ACC-SEC-B6 | Re-run `docs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/repro/zz_trust_repro.test.ts`. Seeded-secret scan of `~/.nexus` and `.nexus` after a scripted turn. | Zero plaintext seeded secrets in durable stores or outbound bodies. |\n| ACC-PRV-LIVE | `nexus providers verify --provider <p> -m <pinned model> -j` for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06) | `passed: true`. Receipts archived. |\n| ACC-PRV-STANDALONE | §4.2 on the installed RC through the approved stripped proxy, with gateway credentials absent from the child environment | Every required profile completes through the proxy and the absent-gateway boundary holds; receipts archived. |\n| ACC-PLAT | E2 matrix, §7 | All rows pass. |\n| ACC-QUAL-T2 | §6.1 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n| ACC-QUAL-T3 | §6.3 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n| ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n| ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\n| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five terminal environments and three sizes | Waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20. No manual-cell execution or evidence is required, and no result is inferred. Automated §5.1 and scripted PTY §5.2 remain mandatory. |\n\n## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\n\n### 4.1 Clean-HOME procedure\n\n1. `export HOME=$(mktemp -d)`.\n2. Install the RC with the documented command.\n3. Create `~/.config/nexus/config.env` containing only:\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:<proxy>/v1`\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_MODEL=<id as listed by the proxy>`\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY=REDACTED\n\n   No gateway token file, no homelab paths, no `NODE_*` overrides.\n4. Start `node eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs --upstream <gateway> --token-file <operator token> [--emulate <kind>]`. The gateway token stays with the proxy and never reaches the Nexus HOME.\n5. Run `nexus doctor --json` and archive it. It must report the server kind and context source with no `gateway` capability.\n\n### 4.2 Standalone matrix\n\n| Profile | What Nexus sees | Runs | Pass condition |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| P-plain | Bare OpenAI-compatible `/models` and chat. No tokenize, no capacity headers. | Standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 held-out tasks) × 3 runs; T4 classes 1, 3, 4, 7 × 3 | T2 correctness ≥ (gateway-direct T2 correctness on the same tasks − 10 pts). False VERIFIED = 0. T4 truthful = 100%. Context source reported as `client_default` or an operator override, with no error. |\n| P-llamacpp | Emulated llama.cpp `/props` and overflow body | Same tasks × 1 run; plus the forced-overflow case (context limit set to 8k) | Context discovered from `/props`. Overflow gives one compact-and-retry, then success or an actionable error. |\n| P-vllm | Emulated `max_model_len` and vLLM overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `max_model_len` |\n| P-ollama | Emulated `/api/show` and Ollama overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `ollama_show` |\n| Conformance | CI fixtures for llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio and Ollama shapes | CI | All pass (ACC-INF-01, -02, -05) |\n\nACC-INF-10 passes only when every row passes. The release notes state the scope in the form required by DEC-16.\n\n### 4.3 Provider matrix (E5)\n# SPEC-07: Supply chain, compliance and release engineering\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Status | Ready. GitHub attestations for provenance (DEC-09); `cli/dist` untracked (DEC-10). |\n| Release class | **BLOCKER**: third-party notices (license obligation for redistributed binaries). RELEASE-REQUIRED: SBOM, provenance, SECURITY.md, CHANGELOG, CI matrix, gate fail-closed, dist freshness. |\n| Requirements | REQ-REL-107, REQ-REL-108, REQ-REL-109, REQ-REL-110, REQ-REL-111, REQ-REL-112, REQ-REL-113, REQ-REL-114 |\n| Findings | REL-05, REL-06, REL-07, REL-09, REL-13, MNT-01, MNT-02, MNT-03, MNT-05, MNT-06, HIST-07, EVL-007 |\n| Historical requirements | REL-001..004, SCAN-001..005 (Issue #12) |\n| Plan | [PLAN-07](../plans/PLAN-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md) |\n| Acceptance | ACC-SUP-01 to ACC-SUP-08 |\n\n## 1. Problem and evidence\n\n| Finding | What is wrong | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| REL-05 | The release archive contains only the project LICENSE. About 150 Rust crates (MIT/Apache-2.0 and others) are statically linked into `harness-core` and `nexus-tui`, with no attribution. No SBOM is published. | RUNTIME + SOURCE (`scripts/package-linux.sh:22`) |\n| REL-06 | `scripts/generate_sbom.sh` lists direct dependencies only, with versions taken from ranges, not lockfiles. It is not run in release. | SOURCE |\n| REL-07 | The fallback \"RustSec database\" in `scripts/audit_rust_deps.py` is 9 hard-coded advisories, yet it prints \"clean\". The real `cargo audit` runs in CI only because the runner image ships it. | SOURCE + CI log |\n| REL-09 | There is no signature or provenance attestation, and the installer is served from mutable `main`. | SOURCE |\n| REL-13 | CI covers Node 20 only (the developer runs 24.21.0) and a floating stable Rust. There is no `rust-toolchain.toml`, no MSRV, no `engines` field, and no check that `cli/dist` is fresh. | SOURCE + CI log |\n| MNT-01 | `cli/dist` (86 generated files) is tracked. It matches a fresh build today, but nothing enforces that. | MEASUREMENT |\n| MNT-02 | `.gitlab-ci.yml` is dead and divergent. | SOURCE |\n| MNT-03 | `make verify-reproducibility` writes fixed `/tmp` paths and covers dist only. | SOURCE |\n| MNT-05 | Release bodies are \"Full Changelog\" only, and there is no CHANGELOG.md. | RUNTIME |\n| HIST-07 | There is no SECURITY.md vulnerability intake, yet the repository is public and releases are published, so REL-004's patch obligation is live. | SOURCE |\n| EVL-007 | `__pycache__/*.pyc` files are tracked under `experiments/`. | SOURCE |\n\nStrengths to preserve:\n\n- The release is gated on main ancestry and a version match.\n- The full suite runs, including PTY e2e tests.\n- Two package builds are compared with `cmp`.\n- Package and installer smoke tests run.\n- `npm audit` is clean.\n- Builds use `--locked` and `npm ci`.\n\n## 2. Requirements\n\n1. **REQ-REL-107.** Each release ships `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt` inside the archive and as a release asset. It covers 100% of the Cargo.lock packages compiled into the shipped binaries and all production npm packages, with license texts.\n2. **REQ-REL-108.** Each release ships a lockfile-derived SBOM: CycloneDX 1.5 JSON for npm (prod) and Cargo, merged. It is validated by `cyclonedx validate` in CI.\n3. **REQ-REL-109.** Release assets carry verifiable provenance (DEC-09: `actions/attest-build-provenance`). The installer can optionally verify it when `gh` is present. The installer is also published as a release asset, so a tag-pinned installer exists.\n4. **REQ-REL-110.** The vulnerability gate fails closed. `cargo-audit` or `cargo-deny` is installed explicitly in workflows with `--locked`. The toy fallback is removed. A missing tool exits non-zero.\n5. **REQ-REL-111.** The CI matrix covers Node 22 and 24 (DEC-12: Node.js 20 is end of life and unsupported), with a pinned Rust toolchain (`rust-toolchain.toml`) and a declared MSRV (`rust-version`). It includes a `cli/dist` freshness check, with dist untracked per DEC-10. The package declares `\"engines\": { \"node\": \">=22\" }`.\n6. **REQ-REL-112.** SECURITY.md defines the reporting channel, the supported versions and the response targets. CHANGELOG.md is maintained, and the release body is taken from `docs/releases/<tag>.md` (the release fails if that file is missing).\n7. **REQ-REL-113.** Dead CI config is removed, and tracked bytecode is removed and ignored.\n8. **REQ-REL-114.** Cross-machine reproducibility is demonstrated once for the RC: two different runner images with the pinned toolchain produce identical tarballs. This is RELEASE-REQUIRED evidence, not a code change.\n\n## 3. Design\n\n- **Notices.**\n  - Rust: `cargo about generate about.hbs > THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES-rust.txt`, with an `about.toml` license allowlist.\n  - npm: `npx --yes license-checker-rseidelsohn --production --plainVertical` from `cli/`.\n  - `package-linux.sh` concatenates both into the archive root.\n  - `cargo deny check licenses` runs in CI with the same allowlist, so new incompatible licenses fail early.\n- **SBOM.** `npx @cyclonedx/cyclonedx-npm --omit dev` and `cargo cyclonedx --format json`, merged with `cyclonedx merge`. Replace `scripts/generate_sbom.sh` and update `make sbom`.\n- **Provenance.** Add `permissions: id-token: write, attestations: write` to release.yml and a step `actions/attest-build-provenance@v1` with `subject-path` set to the tarball and SHA256SUMS. Docs: `gh attestation verify <tarball> -R mikeholownych/nexus-code`.\n- **CI.** `strategy.matrix.node: [22, 24]` for the test job. Packaging, release and reproducibility builds run on Node 22. Add `cargo install cargo-audit --locked --version <pin>`. Add a step `git diff --exit-code -- cli/dist` after the build.\n\n## 4. Acceptance criteria\n\n| ID | Check |\n|---|---|\n| ACC-SUP-01 | The RC archive contains `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt`. A script asserts that every `name version` in `cargo metadata --locked` for the shipped binaries and in `npm ls --omit=dev --all` appears in it. |\n| ACC-SUP-02 | `cyclonedx validate --input-file sbom.cdx.json` passes. The component count equals the lockfile prod closure (±0). |\n| ACC-SUP-03 | `gh attestation verify` passes for the RC tarball. |\n| ACC-SUP-04 | `PATH` without cargo-audit makes `security_gates.sh` exit non-zero. |\n| ACC-SUP-05 | The CI matrix is green on Node 22 and 24, release and reproducibility packaging use Node 22, and the dist-freshness step is present. |\n| ACC-SUP-06 | SECURITY.md and CHANGELOG.md exist. `gh release view <rc>` body equals `docs/releases/<rc>.md`. |\n| ACC-SUP-07 | `.gitlab-ci.yml` is removed (or marked as a mirror). `git ls-files '*.pyc'` is empty. |\n| ACC-SUP-08 | Cross-runner reproducibility: tarballs built on ubuntu-22.04 and ubuntu-24.04 runners with the pinned toolchain are byte-identical, or the differences are documented and accepted as a DEC-10 follow-up. |\n\n## 5. Dependencies\n\n- DEC-09 and DEC-10 (both resolved).\n- SPEC-06's version sync runs first in the release job.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":92920345}},"started_at_ms":1793354714566,"completed_at_ms":1793354715660}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T10:05:16.354Z","ordinal":527701,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18c45-54c1-71b0-a3e1-9a776e79cf22","call_id":"call_83f80e6d12ae4afea520100a93fea1dd","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 3120)\nTotal output lines: 142\n\n## 3. Gate checklist (G0–G4: automated acceptance IDs)\n\nEvery ACC ID below is defined in the linked spec. The plan for each spec names the test that implements it. Run each check at the lifecycle stage dictated by its acceptance method in §1.1: source-applicable checks before the RC tag; checks requiring the RC archive, attestation, release, or installed package after RC construction; environment-specific checks in their declared environment. Bind every result to the exact source commit and, when artifact-dependent, the RC package digest. A source test or local build does not replace an artifact-bound check, and no G0–G4 ID is complete until all of its applicable checks pass.\n\n| Gate | Acceptance IDs | Spec |\n|---|---|---|\n| Safety | ACC-SAFE-01 to ACC-SAFE-10 | SPEC-01 |\n| Process ownership | ACC-PROC-01 to ACC-PROC-08 (ACC-PROC-07 is the load test, run in E3) | SPEC-02 |\n| Untrusted inputs | ACC-TRUST-01 to ACC-TRUST-09 | SPEC-03 |\n| Continuity | ACC-CONT-01 to ACC-CONT-09 (ACC-CONT-10 is in §8) | SPEC-04 |\n| Inference | ACC-INF-01 to ACC-INF-09 (ACC-INF-10 is in §4) | SPEC-05 |\n| Packaging | ACC-PKG-01 to ACC-PKG-09 | SPEC-06 |\n| Supply chain | ACC-SUP-01 to ACC-SUP-08 (artifact-bound ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08 after RC construction) | SPEC-07 |\n| Persistence | ACC-PER-01 to ACC-PER-07 | SPEC-08 |\n| Governance | ACC-GOV-01 to ACC-GOV-06 | SPEC-09 |\n| Verification | ACC-VER-01 to ACC-VER-09 | SPEC-11 |\n| Upgrade | ACC-UPG-01 to ACC-UPG-14 | SPEC-12 |\n\n\n### 3.1 Acceptance IDs defined in this file\n\nThese are retained commitments from REQUIREMENTS §2 and cross-cutting checks.\n\n| ID | Check | Pass condition |\n|---|---|---|\n| ACC-TUI-STEER | PTY: submit a task; while a tool runs, type steering text and press Enter; also queue a steer before a cancel | Steering is applied at the next step boundary. Unapplied steering is returned to the composer. Nothing is dropped silently (existing `sidecar_steering_diff` plus PTY s6). |\n| ACC-TUI-A11Y | PTY with `NO_COLOR=1` and with `TERM=dumb` at 40×14 and 100×30 | Zero colour SGR codes. Every state is distinguishable by glyph and word. Hints are complete at 40 columns (TUI-10). |\n| ACC-SEC-JAIL | `core/tests` plus harness-core calls with `..`, absolute, symlinked-file, symlinked-dir and symlinked-parent payloads | Every one is refused (C §4 R1 set). |\n| ACC-SEC-B6 | Re-run `docs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/repro/zz_trust_repro.test.ts`. Seeded-secret scan of `~/.nexus` and `.nexus` after a scripted turn. | Zero plaintext seeded secrets in durable stores or outbound bodies. |\n| ACC-PRV-LIVE | `nexus providers verify --provider <p> -m <pinned model> -j` for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06) | `passed: true`. Receipts archived. |\n| ACC-PRV-STANDALONE | §4.2 on the installed RC through the approved stripped proxy, with gateway credentials absent from the child environment | Every required profile completes through the proxy and the absent-gateway boundary holds; receipts archived. |\n| ACC-PLAT | E2 matrix, §7 | All rows pass. |\n| ACC-QUAL-T2 | §6.1 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n| ACC-QUAL-T3 | §6.3 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n| ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n| ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\n| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five terminal environments and three sizes | Waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20. No manual-cell execution or evidence is required, and no result is inferred. Automated §5.1 and scripted PTY §5.2 remain mandatory. |\n\n## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\n\n### 4.1 Clean-HOME procedure\n\n1. `export HOME=$(mktemp -d)`.\n2. Install the RC with the documented command.\n3. Create `~/.config/nexus/config.env` containing only:\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:<proxy>/v1`\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_MODEL=<id as listed by the proxy>`\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY=REDACTED\n\n   No gateway token file, no homelab paths, no `NODE_*` overrides.\n4. Start `node eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs --upstream <gateway> --token-file <operator token> [--emulate <kind>]`. The gateway token stays with the proxy and never reaches the Nexus HOME.\n5. Run `nexus doctor --json` and archive it. It must report the server kind and context source with no `gateway` capability.\n\n### 4.2 Standalone matrix\n\n| Profile | What Nexus sees | Runs | Pass condition |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| P-plain | Bare OpenAI-compatible `/models` and chat. No tokenize, no capacity headers. | Standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 held-out tasks) × 3 runs; T4 classes 1, 3, 4, 7 × 3 | T2 correctness ≥ (gateway-direct T2 correctness on the same tasks − 10 pts). False VERIFIED = 0. T4 truthful = 100%. Context source reported as `client_default` or an operator override, with no error. |\n| P-llamacpp | Emulated llama.cpp `/props` and overflow body | Same tasks × 1 run; plus the forced-overflow case (context limit set to 8k) | Context discovered from `/props`. Overflow gives one compact-and-retry, then success or an actionable error. |\n| P-vllm | Emulated `max_model_len` and vLLM overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `max_model_len` |\n| P-ol…520 tokens truncated…veloper runs 24.21.0) and a floating stable Rust. There is no `rust-toolchain.toml`, no MSRV, no `engines` field, and no check that `cli/dist` is fresh. | SOURCE + CI log |\n| MNT-01 | `cli/dist` (86 generated files) is tracked. It matches a fresh build today, but nothing enforces that. | MEASUREMENT |\n| MNT-02 | `.gitlab-ci.yml` is dead and divergent. | SOURCE |\n| MNT-03 | `make verify-reproducibility` writes fixed `/tmp` paths and covers dist only. | SOURCE |\n| MNT-05 | Release bodies are \"Full Changelog\" only, and there is no CHANGELOG.md. | RUNTIME |\n| HIST-07 | There is no SECURITY.md vulnerability intake, yet the repository is public and releases are published, so REL-004's patch obligation is live. | SOURCE |\n| EVL-007 | `__pycache__/*.pyc` files are tracked under `experiments/`. | SOURCE |\n\nStrengths to preserve:\n\n- The release is gated on main ancestry and a version match.\n- The full suite runs, including PTY e2e tests.\n- Two package builds are compared with `cmp`.\n- Package and installer smoke tests run.\n- `npm audit` is clean.\n- Builds use `--locked` and `npm ci`.\n\n## 2. Requirements\n\n1. **REQ-REL-107.** Each release ships `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt` inside the archive and as a release asset. It covers 100% of the Cargo.lock packages compiled into the shipped binaries and all production npm packages, with license texts.\n2. **REQ-REL-108.** Each release ships a lockfile-derived SBOM: CycloneDX 1.5 JSON for npm (prod) and Cargo, merged. It is validated by `cyclonedx validate` in CI.\n3. **REQ-REL-109.** Release assets carry verifiable provenance (DEC-09: `actions/attest-build-provenance`). The installer can optionally verify it when `gh` is present. The installer is also published as a release asset, so a tag-pinned installer exists.\n4. **REQ-REL-110.** The vulnerability gate fails closed. `cargo-audit` or `cargo-deny` is installed explicitly in workflows with `--locked`. The toy fallback is removed. A missing tool exits non-zero.\n5. **REQ-REL-111.** The CI matrix covers Node 22 and 24 (DEC-12: Node.js 20 is end of life and unsupported), with a pinned Rust toolchain (`rust-toolchain.toml`) and a declared MSRV (`rust-version`). It includes a `cli/dist` freshness check, with dist untracked per DEC-10. The package declares `\"engines\": { \"node\": \">=22\" }`.\n6. **REQ-REL-112.** SECURITY.md defines the reporting channel, the supported versions and the response targets. CHANGELOG.md is maintained, and the release body is taken from `docs/releases/<tag>.md` (the release fails if that file is missing).\n7. **REQ-REL-113.** Dead CI config is removed, and tracked bytecode is removed and ignored.\n8. **REQ-REL-114.** Cross-machine reproducibility is demonstrated once for the RC: two different runner images with the pinned toolchain produce identical tarballs. This is RELEASE-REQUIRED evidence, not a code change.\n\n## 3. Design\n\n- **Notices.**\n  - Rust: `cargo about generate about.hbs > THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES-rust.txt`, with an `about.toml` license allowlist.\n  - npm: `npx --yes license-checker-rseidelsohn --production --plainVertical` from `cli/`.\n  - `package-linux.sh` concatenates both into the archive root.\n  - `cargo deny check licenses` runs in CI with the same allowlist, so new incompatible licenses fail early.\n- **SBOM.** `npx @cyclonedx/cyclonedx-npm --omit dev` and `cargo cyclonedx --format json`, merged with `cyclonedx merge`. Replace `scripts/generate_sbom.sh` and update `make sbom`.\n- **Provenance.** Add `permissions: id-token: write, attestations: write` to release.yml and a step `actions/attest-build-provenance@v1` with `subject-path` set to the tarball and SHA256SUMS. Docs: `gh attestation verify <tarball> -R mikeholownych/nexus-code`.\n- **CI.** `strategy.matrix.node: [22, 24]` for the test job. Packaging, release and reproducibility builds run on Node 22. Add `cargo install cargo-audit --locked --version <pin>`. Add a step `git diff --exit-code -- cli/dist` after the build.\n\n## 4. Acceptance criteria\n\n| ID | Check |\n|---|---|\n| ACC-SUP-01 | The RC archive contains `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt`. A script asserts that every `name version` in `cargo metadata --locked` for the shipped binaries and in `npm ls --omit=dev --all` appears in it. |\n| ACC-SUP-02 | `cyclonedx validate --input-file sbom.cdx.json` passes. The component count equals the lockfile prod closure (±0). |\n| ACC-SUP-03 | `gh attestation verify` passes for the RC tarball. |\n| ACC-SUP-04 | `PATH` without cargo-audit makes `security_gates.sh` exit non-zero. |\n| ACC-SUP-05 | The CI matrix is green on Node 22 and 24, release and reproducibility packaging use Node 22, and the dist-freshness step is present. |\n| ACC-SUP-06 | SECURITY.md and CHANGELOG.md exist. `gh release view <rc>` body equals `docs/releases/<rc>.md`. |\n| ACC-SUP-07 | `.gitlab-ci.yml` is removed (or marked as a mirror). `git ls-files '*.pyc'` is empty. |\n| ACC-SUP-08 | Cross-runner reproducibility: tarballs built on ubuntu-22.04 and ubuntu-24.04 runners with the pinned toolchain are byte-identical, or the differences are documented and accepted as a DEC-10 follow-up. |\n\n## 5. Dependencies\n\n- DEC-09 and DEC-10 (both resolved).\n- SPEC-06's version sync runs first in the release job.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18c3d-7cdd-71d3-966d-f30f05df4fb0","create_time":1793354716.3539526}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
