{"timestamp":"2026-10-30T10:06:21.140Z","ordinal":527754,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18c3d-7cdd-71d3-966d-f30f05df4fb0","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-72ba0f22-53fb-4170-8eff-be1beb8dc804","process_id":"59408","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n '^## 7|^### 7' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md; sed -n '270,330p' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md; sed -n '1,120p' docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/run-rc10-e2-matrix.sh"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/rc14-artifact-verification","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n '^## 7|''^### 7' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md","query":"^## 7|^### 7","path":"ACCEPTANCE.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '270,330p' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md","name":"ACCEPTANCE.md","path":"docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,120p' docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/run-rc10-e2-matrix.sh","name":"run-rc10-e2-matrix.sh","path":"docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/run-rc10-e2-matrix.sh"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"271:## 7. Install, upgrade, rollback, uninstall (ACC-PLAT; E2)\n\n## 7. Install, upgrade, rollback, uninstall (ACC-PLAT; E2)\n\n| Case | Command | Pass condition |\n|---|---|---|\n| Fresh install, each image with Node ≥ 22 | Documented one-line command with `NEXUS_VERSION=<rc>`, then the no-version command after v1.0.0 is published | Installed. `nexus --version` equals the RC. `nexus doctor` shows no version warning and an empty stderr. |\n| No Node / Node 20 | Same | Clear prerequisite message before download or state change. HOME untouched. |\n| Upgrade alpha.2 → RC | Same, with the tag | Symlink swapped. Old version retained. User state intact. |\n| Rollback RC → alpha.2 | Same, with the old tag | Works. |\n| Repair | Delete a file in the version dir, then reinstall | Repaired (REQ-REL-105). Same-version reinstall preserves working files if package fails verification. |\n| Uninstall (documented manual) | Commands from the quickstart | Only Nexus-owned paths removed. `~/.config/nexus` and `~/.nexus` retained. |\n| Checksum tamper | installer-smoke | Refused. The existing install is unchanged. |\n| Attestation | `gh attestation verify <tarball> -R mikeholownych/nexus-code` | PASS |\n| Upgrade self-test failure | `nexus upgrade` (broken candidate package) | Refused. Staging verified before switch; if post-switch verification fails, launcher atomically rolls back to previous target and journal records `rolled_back`. |\n| Upgrade crash recovery | `nexus upgrade --recover` | Idempotent recovery. Cleans incomplete staging, restores unverified launcher symlink, verifies functional installation. |\n| Backup restore | `nexus upgrade --restore-backup <state-backup-directory>` | Snapshot of configuration and complete durable state restored from a recognized private backup directory (`backup.json`, `state/`, optional `config/`), with strict 0600 file / 0700 directory modes. A canonical `config.env.bak.*` path restores configuration only. Arbitrary files and tar archives are rejected. Run it through the stable `nexus` launcher; close existing legacy clients, then keep version-pinned legacy binaries and direct old entry points offline until the durable restore journal is cleared. |\n| Incompatible downgrade | `nexus upgrade --version <v> --allow-downgrade` (incompatible state schema) | Refused fail-closed with actionable state schema explanation. Existing installation unchanged. |\n\n## 8. Independent acceptance (REQ-AGT-110, ACC-CONT-10)\n\nThe reviewer is supplied by the owner (X5) and did not implement the work under review.\n\nThe reviewer receives:\n\n- the RC package;\n- this file;\n- the REQUIREMENTS ledger;\n- SPEC-04;\n- read access to the evidence directory.\n\nThe reviewer performs:\n\n1. An independent re-run of a sample. At minimum:\n   - ACC-SAFE-01, 03, 09;\n   - ACC-PROC-02;\n   - ACC-TRUST-01, 02;\n   - ACC-CONT-01, 03;\n   - ACC-VER-01, 03;\n   - ACC-PKG-01;\n   - 5 random T2 tasks;\n   - 2 T4 classes.\n2. One live long task (≥ 60 steps, ≥ 2 compactions) on the RC through the gateway, including one kill and resume.\n3. A review of the scorer verdict and of contamination handling.\n\n**Output:** `docs/reviews/<date>-v1-rc-independent-acceptance.md` with an ACCEPT, ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS, or REJECT verdict per area. \"Accept with defects\" needs an owner disposition for every defect, and for a blocker area the only acceptable disposition is a fix.\n\n## 9. Contest (separate product; not a client gate)\n\nThe contest submission is complete and judging has concluded. No contest freeze applies (DEC-13 status amendment); post-contest hardening is tracked separately from client v1.0.0 acceptance and is accepted by:\n\n| ID | Check |\n|---|---|\n| CON-A1 | Ordinary maintained package/experiment checks build `agent-collab-worker`. `worker.config.json` has the configured name, and the bundle contains the `/work-state` handler. Do not restore the retired `cloudflare-contest-contract` status check. |\n| CON-A2 | Broker negative tests: caller-supplied env paths and URLs are ignored. A host outside `*.artifacts.cloudflare.net` is refused. |\n| CON-A3 | On a clean VM, `install.sh --fresh` followed by `post-install-qualify.py` passes. |\n| CON-A4 | `sudo -l` for the demo user shows only fixed argv. `sudo setpriv --reuid=0 id` is denied. |\n| CON-A5 | One clean-account `--mode cloudflare --agents real` run, with a committed, redacted run record. |\n| CON-A6 | The video source commits are tagged and published, or the docs state that they are unpublished. |\n\n## 10. Release decision (G6)\n\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# RC10 E2 matrix: negative Node preflight cells and fresh-install/doctor cells\n# across the prepared Ubuntu 22.04/24.04, Debian 12 and Fedora 40 images.\nset -uo pipefail\nhere=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\" && pwd)\"\ninstaller=/tmp/nexus-install.sh\nversion=v1.0.0-rc.10\nexpected_version=\"1.0.0-rc.10 (16ee8ca36438)\"\ninstaller_sha=5620d56ef6f8d637fc102ae2c8ea3b055effbc4069243a2df68b67520b1e2302\nnode24=/home/mike/.local/node-v24.11.1-linux-x64\ndoctor_dir=/tmp/opencode/e2-doctor\nmkdir -p \"$doctor_dir\"\nrm -f \"$doctor_dir\"/*.doctor.json\nchmod 0777 \"$doctor_dir\"\n[ -f \"$installer\" ] || { echo \"missing installer at $installer\" >&2; exit 2; }\nprintf '%s  %s\\n' \"$installer_sha\" \"$installer\" | sha256sum -c -\n[ -x \"$node24/bin/node\" ] || { echo \"missing Node 24 runtime at $node24\" >&2; exit 2; }\n\nplatforms=(ubuntu-22-04 ubuntu-24-04 debian-12 fedora-40)\nnegative_runtimes=(nodenone node12 node20)\npositive_runtimes=(node22 node24)\nfailures=0\nresults=\"$here/results.tsv\"\n: > \"$results\"\nprintf 'cell\\tkind\\tresult\\n' >> \"$results\"\n\nrecord() { printf '%s\\t%s\\t%s\\n' \"$1\" \"$2\" \"$3\" >> \"$results\"; }\n\nfor platform in \"${platforms[@]}\"; do\n  for runtime in \"${negative_runtimes[@]}\"; do\n    image=\"nexus-e2/${platform}-${runtime}:prep-182e8addeee0\"\n    log=\"$here/${platform}-${runtime}.log\"\n    echo \"START ${platform} ${runtime} $(date -u +%FT%TZ)\"\n    if docker run --rm --pull=never --network none \\\n      --mount \"type=bind,src=$installer,dst=/tmp/nexus-install.sh,readonly\" \\\n      --env NEXUS_VERSION=\"$version\" \"$image\" sh -ec '\n        before=$(find \"$HOME\" -mindepth 1 -printf \"%P %y\\n\" | sort | sha256sum | cut -d\" \" -f1)\n        if output=$(NEXUS_VERSION=\"$NEXUS_VERSION\" sh /tmp/nexus-install.sh 2>&1); then\n          echo \"unexpected installer success\"; exit 40\n        fi\n        printf \"%s\\n\" \"$output\"\n        printf \"%s\" \"$output\" | grep -F \"Node.js 22 or newer is required\" >/dev/null\n        after=$(find \"$HOME\" -mindepth 1 -printf \"%P %y\\n\" | sort | sha256sum | cut -d\" \" -f1)\n        test \"$before\" = \"$after\"\n        echo \"preflight=PASS home_unchanged=true\"\n      ' > \"$log\" 2>&1; then\n      echo \"PASS ${platform} ${runtime}\"; record \"${platform}-${runtime}\" negative PASS\n    else\n      echo \"FAIL ${platform} ${runtime}\"; record \"${platform}-${runtime}\" negative FAIL; failures=$((failures+1))\n    fi\n  done\n\n  for runtime in \"${positive_runtimes[@]}\"; do\n    base_runtime=$runtime\n    [ \"$runtime\" = node24 ] && base_runtime=node22\n    image=\"nexus-e2/${platform}-${base_runtime}:prep-182e8addeee0\"\n    log=\"$here/${platform}-${runtime}.log\"\n    mounts=(--mount \"type=bind,src=$installer,dst=/tmp/nexus-install.sh,readonly\" --mount \"type=bind,src=$doctor_dir,dst=/evidence\")\n    [ \"$runtime\" = node24 ] && mounts+=(--mount \"type=bind,src=$node24,dst=/opt/node24,readonly\")\n    echo \"START ${platform} ${runtime} $(date -u +%FT%TZ)\"\n    if docker run --rm --pull=never --network bridge \"${mounts[@]}\" \\\n      --env NEXUS_VERSION=\"$version\" --env NEXUS_CELL=\"${platform}-${runtime}\" \"$image\" sh -ec '\n        if [ -x /opt/node24/bin/node ]; then export PATH=\"/opt/node24/bin:$PATH\"; fi\n        id\n        node --version\n        expected='\"${runtime#node}\"'\n        major=$(node --version | cut -d. -f1 | tr -d v)\n        test \"$major\" = \"$expected\"\n        NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=0 NEXUS_VERSION=\"$NEXUS_VERSION\" sh /tmp/nexus-install.sh\n        export PATH=\"$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH\"\n        version=$(nexus --version)\n        printf \"launcher_version=%s\\n\" \"$version\"\n        test \"$version\" = \"'\"$expected_version\"'\"\n        nexus doctor --json >/tmp/doctor.json 2>/tmp/doctor.err || doctor_rc=$?\n        doctor_rc=${doctor_rc:-0}\n        printf \"doctor_rc=%s doctor_stderr_bytes=%s\\n\" \"$doctor_rc\" \"$(wc -c </tmp/doctor.err)\"\n        cp /tmp/doctor.json \"/evidence/${NEXUS_CELL}.doctor.json\"\n        test ! -s /tmp/doctor.err\n        node -e '\\''const fs=require(\"fs\");const d=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(\"/tmp/doctor.json\",\"utf8\"));if(d.nexusVersion!==\"'\"${expected_version%% *}\"'\")process.exit(1);const f=d.findings||[];for(const id of [\"install.build\",\"engine.binary\"]){const x=f.find(y=>y.id===id);if(!x||x.status!==\"pass\")process.exit(2)}if(f.some(x=>/version/i.test(x.id+\" \"+x.explanation)&&[\"warn\",\"fail\"].includes(x.status)))process.exit(3);'\\''\n        node -e '\\''const d=require(\"/tmp/doctor.json\");for(const f of d.findings||[])console.log(f.status+\"\\t\"+f.id+\"\\t\"+f.explanation);'\\''\n      ' > \"$log\" 2>&1; then\n      echo \"PASS ${platform} ${runtime}\"; record \"${platform}-${runtime}\" positive PASS\n    else\n      echo \"FAIL ${platform} ${runtime}\"; record \"${platform}-${runtime}\" positive FAIL; failures=$((failures+1))\n    fi\n  done\ndone\n\n{\n  printf '{\\n  \"tag\": \"%s\",\\n  \"expectedVersion\": \"%s\",\\n  \"installerSha256\": \"%s\",\\n  \"generatedAt\": \"%s\",\\n  \"images\": [\\n' \"$version\" \"$expected_version\" \"$installer_sha\" \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ)\"\n  first=1\n  for platform in \"${platforms[@]}\"; do\n    for runtime in nodenone node12 node20 node22; do\n      image=\"nexus-e2/${platform}-${runtime}:prep-182e8addeee0\"\n      id=$(docker image inspect --format '{{.Id}}' \"$image\")\n      [ $first -eq 0 ] && printf ',\\n'\n      first=0\n      printf '    {\"cell\": \"%s-%s\", \"image\": \"%s\", \"id\": \"%s\"}' \"$platform\" \"$runtime\" \"$image\" \"$id\"\n    done\n  done\n  printf '\\n  ]\\n}\\n'\n} > \"$here/prepared-images.json\"\n\ncp \"$doctor_dir\"/*.doctor.json \"$here\"/ 2>/dev/null || true\necho \"failures=$failures\"\nexit $((failures > 0 ? 1 : 0))\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":168613553}},"started_at_ms":1793354779970,"completed_at_ms":1793354781140}}
